{"abstract":"Children with congenital heart disease are more likely to receive special educational services in schools and have an increased risk of mental health issues. We explored the lived experiences of parents caring for a child with heart disease and concurrent mental health issues in Denmark. Semi-structured interviews with ten parents (age 39-57 years) to these children (age 5-17 years) were analysed using interpretative phenomenological analysis. Three Group Experiential Themes (GETs) were generated from the analysis: The first GET, Parental roles and caring behaviours, described parental struggles of fulfilling their parenting role ideals and experiences with stigmatization of MHI. GET two, Parental reflections on their illness explanations, portrayed how parents utilize different illness explanations to make sense of their child's MHI. GET three, Differences in access to help and support, captured how the CHD affected overall access to mental health support. The results may inform various topics of importance for health professionals to address in their clinical encounters with these families.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hejl, Julie L.","Hulgaard, Ditte R","Rasmussen, Anne Sofie D","Larsen, Lærke Emilie N","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-772932"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Congenital heart defect","Experience","Mental health issues","Parent","Perspective","Psychiatric disorder","Qualitative Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linking heart and mind lived experiences of parents to children with congenital heart disease and mental health issues","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85205700704","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-772932","identifier":[{"id":"39041634","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85205700704","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-869c2307-5929-4562-9a17-7958b290bbc7"],"keyword":["Congenital heart defect","experience","mental health issues","parent","perspective","psychiatric disorder","qualitative research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFFA4D3E47AAED2A05A1ADBB580DD8DE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Psychiatric Hospital for Children and Adolescents"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Julie L","key":"hejlpau","last":"Hejl","locid":"6352b8da-9131-4a9f-8ce6-939f2b251790","name":"Hejl, Julie L.","name_org":"Hejl, Julie L","orcid":"0000-0002-5060-3112","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ditte R","key":"hulgaardpau","last":"Hulgaard","name":"Hulgaard, Ditte R","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Sofie D","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"30f6f5de-b80f-4daf-ac55-5c985557d3a3","name":"Rasmussen, Anne Sofie D","orcid":"0009-0006-6422-5809","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lærke Emilie N","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Lærke Emilie N","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte U","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","locid":"1e308742-df61-47da-83ce-53d8a7c774c3","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","name_org":"Rask, Charlotte U","orcid":"0000-0002-7426-0353","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39041634"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/13591045241267129","issn":["13591045","14617021"],"issn_org":["13591045"],"journal":"Clinical Child Psychology and Psychiatry","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"e","title":"Clinical Child Psychology and Psychiatry"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205700704"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["E-Published (ahead of print)"]},"sid":["au-869c2307-5929-4562-9a17-7958b290bbc7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Linking heart and mind - lived experiences of parents to children with congenital heart disease and mental health issues","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-772932","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"People with moderate to severe functional impairment may experience shame, self-criticism and isolation, but few psychotherapeutic opportunities are available for this population. Compassion-based therapies facilitate kindness towards one’s own challenges and thus counteract shame and isolation but may be too demanding for people with cognitive impairments. Animals may facilitate support, allow pleasant projections and mediate contact between people, all without much cognitive demand. However, this must be integrated with an actual form of therapy if it is to provide genuine therapeutic benefits. We developed a Rabbit Assisted Compassion Focussed Therapy (RA-CFT) for this population and implemented it in small group settings to further facilitate cohesion and community. This article introduces the main elements of the therapeutic manual, which includes population-adapted tools and eight weekly sessions whose main content is listed. We then summarise from a case study while focussing on participant statements that indicate the formation of a community with and around the rabbits and the therapy. We conclude that RA-CFT is a promising form of therapy for this population but requires sufficient knowledge of both rabbits and the therapeutic elements.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Højholdt, Charlotte May","Sondrup, Camilla Louise Wemmelund","Larsen, Steffi G.","Hansen, Tia G. B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-794412"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animal assisted therapy","Rabbits","dyreassisteret terapi"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Støttepoter, Psykologhuset Echoa, Aalborg"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jeg føler mig ikke alene i det her kaninassisteret compassion fokuseret terapi for mennesker med funktionsnedsættelser","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-794412","ids":["aau-444333c9-b031-4c48-a87d-cfd26dbcf3b0"],"keyword":["Animal Assisted Services","Intervention manual","Rabbits","animal assisted therapy","dyreassisteret terapi","interventionsmanual","kaniner"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8FA8D06C987390FA36724E7F7EC8C7FB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Cognition, Development and Clinical Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Støttepoter, Psykologhuset Echoa, Aalborg"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte May","key":"højholdtpau","last":"Højholdt","locid":"c06728b6-d539-42d9-8940-28cdaa079c2b","name":"Højholdt, Charlotte May","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla Louise Wemmelund","key":"sondruppau","last":"Sondrup","locid":"b7a12053-e5e5-43eb-a3e8-060149aeb6ee","name":"Sondrup, Camilla Louise Wemmelund","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffi G.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Steffi G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tia G. B.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ddcf2848-2f9e-4f0a-a87c-bc7b12ac95f3","name":"Hansen, Tia G. B.","orcid":"0000-0002-8823-5183","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01071211"],"issue":"1","journal":"Psyke & Logos","pages":"182","publisher":"Dansk Psykologisk Forlag","status":"i","title":"Psyke & Logos","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["In Press"]},"sid":["aau-444333c9-b031-4c48-a87d-cfd26dbcf3b0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"“Jeg føler mig ikke alene i det her” – kaninassisteret compassion-fokuseret terapi for mennesker med funktionsnedsættelser","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-794412","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Diffuse large B-cell lymphoma (DLBCL) exhibits striking clinical and biological heterogeneity. Recent studies have identified new subgroups within germinal center B-cell like (GCB) DLBCL, associated with inferior prognosis, irrespective of MYC and BCL2 translocations. We explored the existence of such a DLBCL high-risk subgroup, based on multilevel aberrations, especially focusing on MYC and BCL2. Methods: Tissue samples from 111 DLBCL patients were sequenced with a 90-gene lymphoma panel, followed by integrative analyses combining sequencing data, immunohistochemistry, fluorescent in situ hybridization, and clinical data. Results: We identified a high-risk subgroup in DLBCL defined by: dual immunohistochemical MYC and BCL2 expression (DEL), concurrent MYC and BCL2 translocations (DHL-BCL2), mutations in MYC, CXCR4, or both, and/or BCL2 amplification. The high-risk subgroup constituted 41% of the cohort and included DHL-BCL2, DEL, a GCB subgroup likely representing the recently described GCB subgroups, and a subset of non-GCB patients. In multivariate analysis, high-risk features provided independent predictive value from age and IPI. The 5-year overall survival was 36% in high-risk patients, compared to 76% in non-high-risk patients. Conclusion: We identified a distinct high-risk DLBCL subgroup, characterized by MYC and BCL2 aberrations, beyond conventional DHL-BCL2 and DEL, and irrespective of cell-of-origin, thereby expanding the poor-prognosis group.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Vimalathas, Gayaththri","Lang, Cecilie Steensboe","Green, Tina","Møller, Michael Boe","Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","Hansen, Marcus Høy","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-801668"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vimalathas, Gayaththri"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","BCL2","Biomarkers Tumor genetics","Diffuse large B cell lymphoma","Female","GENES","Gene Rearrangement","Genetic Heterogeneity","High Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","In Situ Hybridization Fluorescence","Lymphoma Large B Cell Diffuse genetics","MYC","Male","Middle Aged","Mutation","Next generation sequencing","Prognosis","Proto Oncogene Proteins c bcl 2 genetics","Proto Oncogene Proteins c myc genetics","Translocation Genetic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"multilevel analysis of myc and bcl000000000002 aberrations in diffuse large b cell lymphoma identifying a high risk patient subgroup across cell of origin using targeted sequencing","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85209820080","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-801668","identifier":[{"id":"39565012","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85209820080","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1224e7d0-58e5-4a68-be2f-4b156bb0b6be"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","BCL2","Biomarkers, Tumor/genetics","Female","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","In Situ Hybridization, Fluorescence","Lymphoma, Large B-Cell, Diffuse/genetics","MYC","Male","Middle Aged","Proto-Oncogene Proteins c-bcl-2/genetics","Proto-Oncogene Proteins c-myc/genetics","Translocation, Genetic","diffuse large B-cell lymphoma","gene rearrangement","genes","genetic heterogeneity","mutation","next-generation sequencing","prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-31A312D6C159B471340712861DD3244F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2025-11-20","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Pathology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gayaththri","key":"vimalathaspau","last":"Vimalathas","locid":"ebe9802e-b5a4-44ea-bc20-0115d3e4996c","name":"Vimalathas, Gayaththri","orcid":"0000-0001-5507-9762","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Steensboe","key":"langpau","last":"Lang","locid":"e7b58303-6e7f-4506-b00e-8d8ef429b573","name":"Lang, Cecilie Steensboe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina Marie","key":"greenpau","last":"Green","locid":"160e8170-39d7-426a-83ad-e470608285aa","name":"Green, Tina","name_org":"Green, Tina Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-4406-9291","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Boe","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"edd876e8-0651-4c8f-8f0f-95f4519e1654","name":"Møller, Michael Boe","orcid":"0000-0003-2041-3630","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Guldborg","key":"nyvoldpau","last":"Nyvold","locid":"ba584c2b-215e-421c-a6e6-c799c1b16b7c","name":"Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","orcid":"0000-0002-0411-7594","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus Høy","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"066dac5b-cbf5-4b70-b136-3e5dd42e4bee","name":"Hansen, Marcus Høy","orcid":"0000-0003-3083-4850","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Stauffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dd2de49b-c3d9-49cb-bb8d-e92119e0b2d1","name":"Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39565012"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ejh.14345","issn":["09024441","09024506"],"issn_org":["09024441"],"issue":"3","journal":"European Journal of Haematology","pages":"469-480","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Haematology","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85209820080"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1224e7d0-58e5-4a68-be2f-4b156bb0b6be"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Multilevel Analysis of MYC and BCL2 Aberrations in Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma : Identifying a High-Risk Patient Subgroup Across Cell-of-Origin Using Targeted Sequencing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-801668","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The practice of weaning at 21 to 28 days of age in conventional pig production poses a challenge to the digestive tract of piglets. Post-weaning challenges like diarrhea, small intestinal villous atrophy, and decreased feed intake (FI) are a consequence of the abrupt change in diet from sow milk to solid feed. The aim of this study was to investigate the effect of benzoic acid (BA) to artificially reared suckling piglets on growth performance, intestinal morphology and change in gene expression in the small intestine (SI). Twenty-seven one-day-old piglets were included in this study, and randomly allocated between three dietary groups. All three groups received milk replacer (MR) throughout the entire experimental period. One group only received MR (CON), one was supplemented with liquid creep feed (LCF) (MRLF) from day 10, and one was supplemented with LCF with 0.5% BA (BEN) from day 10. Piglets were euthanized and post-mortem examinations conducted on days 28 and 29 of the experiment. Small intestinal tissue samples were collected for analysis of morphological parameters and gene expression. Results displayed no effect on growth performance, however, the feed conversion ratio was higher (p < 0.05) for MRLF compared to CON in P2 (days 10-28) and higher (p < 0.05) in MRLF and BEN compared to CON P1+P2 (days 1-28). A tendency (p < 0.10) to an increased villus height in the proximal part of the SI and increased (p < 0.05) villus width in the medial part of the SI were observed for BEN, when compared to CON and MRLF. Furthermore, pathways related to the immune system and metabolism were enriched (Adj. p < 0.05) by BEN in comparison to CON and MRLF. In conclusion, BA did show some potential to enhance the intestinal integrity in the pre-weaning period, and thereby developing a more robust piglet during the peri‑weaning period.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Crone, C. M.","Rasmussen, A. P.","Larsen, C.","Williams, Andrew R.","Eskildsen, M. H.","Christensen, E. M. H.","de Knegt, Leonardo Victor","Williams, Charlotte Amdi","Madsen, Johannes Gulmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810853"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Benzoic acid","Gene expression","Growth performance","Intestinal integrity","Morphology","Suckling piglets"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of benzoic acid supplementation on growth performance and early development of gastrointestinal tract function and immune system in artificially reared suckling piglets","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.livsci.2025.105655","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-810853","identifier":[{"id":"85219728091","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b9bde7dd-4815-4b0f-8b87-a31e93964cf8"],"keyword":["Artificially rearing","Benzoic acid","Gene expression","Growth performance","Intestinal integrity","Morphology","Suckling piglets"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F9DBA0E5DE1B4F7256575E218A5B0073"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/447844900/Effect_of_benzoic_acid_supplementation_on_growth_performance.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.livsci.2025.105655","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"C. M.","key":"cronepau","last":"Crone","name":"Crone, C. M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A. P.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, A. P.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"694ee612-8562-4e50-9a0e-1918acd31784","name":"Larsen, C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A. R.","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","locid":"393f749c-84d9-4245-84f2-1fee6f8d3ead","name":"Williams, Andrew R.","name_org":"Williams, A. R.","orcid":"0000-0002-8231-282X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M. H.","key":"eskildsenpau","last":"Eskildsen","name":"Eskildsen, M. H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"E. M.H.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"f1683526-49d7-4119-bb2f-664278825625","name":"Christensen, E. M. H.","name_org":"Christensen, E. M.H.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"L. V.","key":"deknegtpau","last":"de Knegt","locid":"d43a552f-5a5a-433f-ae53-f4dcba4b26e1","name":"de Knegt, Leonardo Victor","name_org":"de Knegt, L. V.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"amdipau","last":"Amdi","locid":"8057561d-85f5-4717-ba1e-18a709a9f121","name":"Williams, Charlotte Amdi","name_org":"Amdi, C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. G.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"f4b4330e-ca58-4db7-90df-0220335d59f9","name":"Madsen, Johannes Gulmann","name_org":"Madsen, J. G.","orcid":"0000-0001-7528-9521","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.livsci.2025.105655","issn":["18711413","18780490"],"issn_org":["18711413"],"journal":"Livestock Science","paperid":"105655","status":"p","title":"Livestock Science","volume":"294"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219728091"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b9bde7dd-4815-4b0f-8b87-a31e93964cf8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of benzoic acid supplementation on growth performance and early development of gastrointestinal tract function and immune system in artificially reared suckling piglets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-810853","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Clipping artifacts impact the image quality and diagnostic accuracy in ultrasound imaging. This study introduces a post-processing technique designed to eliminate clipping in ultrasound scans acquired using synthetic aperture ultrasound systems (SAUS). It is hypothesized that the proposed method can effectively masks out clipped signals while preserving non-clipped contributions and without a significant loss of image quality. A phantom and an in-vivo rat brain scan were used to test this hypothesis. The analysis of the phantom data showed that the proposed method can be applied to remove mild levels of clipping without a significant loss in contrast and resolution. In fact, when up to 30% of the data was clipped, the loss in resolution after applying clipping removal was lower than 2.5% and the contrast decreased less than 7.9%, when compared with the original non-clipped image. In-vivo results, on the other hand, demonstrated that applying the proposed algorithm effectively removes clipping artifacts while preserving the underlying information. Additionally, it enhances the image's dynamic range by approximately 12%, when compared with the clipped data.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jimenez, Natalia Perez","Bengtsson, Emma Kanchana Ertner","Révész, Eszter Olga","Larsen, Karin","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","Jensen, Jørgen Arendt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819335"],"event":{"end":"2025-02-20","place":"San Diego, us","start":"2025-02-18","title":"Medical Imaging 2025: Ultrasonic Imaging and Tomography","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Artifact","Brain","Clipping","Contrast free","PD","SRI","SURE","Skull","Super resolution","Synthetic aperture","Ultrasound"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clipping removal in synthetic aperture imaging","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/452220851/134121C.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819335","identifier":[{"id":"001482451000037","type":"wos"},{"id":"105004800714","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6f47b9fb-8bb9-408b-9c4b-2ed240f6eed3"],"keyword":["Artifact","Brain","Clipping","Contrast-free","PD","Power Poppler","SRI","SURE","Skull","Super-Resolution","Synthetic Aperture","Transcranial Imaging","Ultrasound"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-2EBB6EFCC203B36F8AC6193C2C19B672"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/452220851/134121C.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Natalia Perez","key":"jimenezpau","last":"Jimenez","locid":"5e2b2cc4-ee6c-4c38-a658-5fcb7fd3767e","name":"Jimenez, Natalia Perez","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Emma Kanchana Ertner","key":"bengtssonpau","last":"Bengtsson","name":"Bengtsson, Emma Kanchana Ertner","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eszter Olga","key":"révészpau","last":"Révész","locid":"e0b13991-a6b3-40cc-83ce-9d3038512855","name":"Révész, Eszter Olga","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karin","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f956493b-d90d-42e7-9a8a-d786830a9d88","name":"Larsen, Karin","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michael Bachmann","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Mehlin","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"0ceca69d-e5cd-43dc-9995-305ac5855c4f","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Mehlin","orcid":"0000-0002-9984-3125","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jørgen Arendt","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Jørgen Arendt","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"boehmpedh","last":"Boehm","name":"Boehm, Christian","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mohammad","key":"mehrmohammadipedh","last":"Mehrmohammadi","name":"Mehrmohammadi, Mohammad","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1117/12.3047400","isbn":["9781510686021"],"issn":["16057422"],"place":"Washington, USA","publisher":"SPIE","series":"Progress in Biomedical Optics and Imaging - Proceedings of SPIE","status":"p","subtitle":"Ultrasonic Imaging and Tomography","title":"Medical Imaging 2025"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004800714"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6f47b9fb-8bb9-408b-9c4b-2ed240f6eed3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Clipping removal in Synthetic Aperture Imaging","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819335","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Periprosthetic knee fracture (PPKF) following total knee arthroplasty (TKA) can be difficult to treat. A PPKF can be treated both operatively and nonoperatively, and the treatment varies between fracture sites. This study aimed to assess the risk of reoperation according to the fracture site and treatment of the PPKF. Method: This study is a nationwide cohort study using register data from 1997 to 2022. Cruciate-retaining or posterior-stabilized primary TKA were identified from the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register. Subsequent PPKFs, fracture treatments, and later reoperations were identified through the International Classification of Diseases, tenth edition (ICD-10) diagnosis and procedure codes in the Danish National Patient Register. In addition, indications for revision total knee arthroplasty (rTKA) in the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register were used to identify PPKFs and the reason for reoperation. Results: We included 1,931 PPKFs (1,494 femoral, 207 patellae, and 230 tibial) with an overall two-year reoperation risk of 20% (95% confidence interval (CI): 18 to 23). Femoral PPKFs had a two-year reoperation risk of 16% (CI: 12 to 22) after nonoperative treatment and 21% (CI: 18 to 24) after operative treatment. Patellar PPKFs had a two-year reoperation risk in five to 17 after nonoperative treatment and 46% (CI: 30 to 69) after operative treatment. Tibial PPKFs had a two-year reoperation risk of 17% (CI: 11 to 27) after nonoperative treatment and 36% (25 to 53) after operative treatment. Conclusions: The overall two-year reoperation risk was 20% (CI: 18 to 23). Operative-treated PPKFs had a higher risk of reoperation across all fracture locations. The highest reoperation risk was found after operatively treated patella and tibial PPKFs (46 and 36%, respectively), and the lowest reoperation risk was found after nonoperative-treated patella PPKFs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Risager, Stefan Kastalag","Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Abrahamsen, Charlotte","Viberg, Bjarke","Odgaard, Anders","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821294"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Risager, Stefan Kastalag"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Knee Fractures","Male","Middle Aged","Periprosthetic knee fracture","Registries","Reoperation","Reoperation statistics numerical data","Total knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reoperations after operatively and non operatively treated periprosthetic knee fractures a nationwide study on 000000000001 000000000931 fractures after primary total knee arthroplasty","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2024.11.010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-821294","identifier":[{"id":"39549884","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85210640990","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-629dbc07-694e-426d-8e74-724a4ff2fb46"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Knee Fractures","Male","Middle Aged","Periprosthetic Fractures/therapy","Registries","Reoperation/statistics & numerical data","Tibial Fractures/therapy","operative versus nonoperative treatment","periprosthetic knee fracture","reoperation","total knee arthroplasty","type of reoperation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D6DF69602C888329120A3BEDBDE851A7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2024.11.010","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290023201/PIIS0883540324012038.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan K.","key":"risagerpau","last":"Risager","locid":"dc21700f-7caf-43ac-901c-5fb66ad42684","name":"Risager, Stefan Kastalag","name_org":"Risager, Stefan K.","orcid":"0000-0001-8157-7001","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine B.","key":"arndtpau","last":"Arndt","locid":"a2513ef2-9214-48ee-b84f-bea6ef1717ac","name":"Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","name_org":"Arndt, Kristine B.","orcid":"0000-0001-8258-7922","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte S.","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"22215dd3-464e-4e62-b19f-71a71e0e1e65","name":"Abrahamsen, Charlotte","name_org":"Abrahamsen, Charlotte S.","orcid":"0000-0002-3700-289X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarke","key":"vibergpau","last":"Viberg","locid":"8cb06beb-80dd-4b2f-bcd7-eb9cba7b9da6","name":"Viberg, Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0001-5169-4282","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39549884"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.arth.2024.11.010","issn":["08835403","15328406"],"issn_org":["08835403"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Arthroplasty","pages":"1622-1628","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Arthroplasty","title_org":"The Journal of Arthroplasty","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85210640990"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-629dbc07-694e-426d-8e74-724a4ff2fb46"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Reoperations After Operatively and Non-Operatively Treated Periprosthetic Knee Fractures : A Nationwide Study on 1,931 Fractures After Primary Total Knee Arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-821294","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This article discusses the methodological concept ‘chains of reasons’, as a conceptual possibility for analysing connections between personal participation and structural conditions in a concrete historical practice. The concept of context is central within psychology but methodologically it is often an open question how to select and focus on the relevant contextual nexuses to a problem. Following subjective reasons as an analytical foundation for tracking relevant conditions provides a possibility for concretising the work with ‘contexts’ and anchoring personal aspects in social practice. This is illustrated through an analysis of unequal possibilities for children’s participation in educational institutions - conceptualised as ‘situated inequality’. Although the analysis exemplifies an analytical round trip into social practices involved in the individual representation of problems at school, the concept is meant as a general contribution to theoretical psychology – highlighting structural conditions through analysis of subjective perspectives in participant’s conduct of everyday live.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830664"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Contextual conditions","Methodology","Participation","Situated inequality","Subjective reasons"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chains of reasons exploring structural conditions by analysing subjective reasons","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-830664","identifier":[{"id":"105002018168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-a5ed7232-31e6-4151-b193-f81de3a1d8e6"],"keyword":["Contextual conditions","Methodology","Participation","Situated inequality","Subjective reasons"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78709962299195B3287D3F7B6C832FE7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, The Danish Centre for Research in Early Childhood Education and Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/09593543251326506","issn":["09593543","14617447"],"issn_org":["09593543"],"issue":"3","journal":"Theory & Psychology","pages":"271-292","status":"p","title":"Theory & Psychology","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002018168"],"sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-a5ed7232-31e6-4151-b193-f81de3a1d8e6"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Chains of reasons : Exploring structural conditions by analysing subjective reasons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830664","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Vores senere praksisforskningsprojekter udforsker ’situeret ulighed’ på tværs af børnelivets forskellige institutionelle sammenhænge – dvs. institutionelle betingelser og sociale dynamikker i hverdagslivet, der er en del af ulighedsskabende processer i praksis. Vores udgangspunkt er, at en sådan udforskning må ske i nært samarbejde med medforskere – dvs. de forskellige mennesker, der befolker den praksis, vi ønsker at vide mere om. Medforskerne er i den sammenhæng ikke ’objekter’ for undersøgelse, intervention eller udvikling, men er involveret i processen med at udforske fælles problemer. Forskningsprocessen må derfor ses som en gensidig læringsproces, der både skaber muligheder for praksisudvikling, viden og teoretisk udvikling. Med udgangspunkt i projekterne, diskuterer vi, hvordan psykologisk praksisforskning med forskellige deltagere, hver med forskellige positioner og perspektiver kan bidrage med indsigt i et felts konflikter og historiske modsætninger og derigennem også med viden om, hvad et problem kan hænge sammen med i hverdagslivets sociale praksis - hvordan vi på baggrund af kvalitativ udforskning og samarbejde med mange forskellige medforskere involveret i et felt kan foretage situerede generaliseringer netop om sammenhænge i det sociale liv.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830671"],"event":{"end":"2025-05-16","place":"Roskilde, dk","start":"2025-05-15","title":"Kvalekonferencen 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"praksisforskning om situeret ulighed om at åbne ulighedens sorte boks","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-830671","ids":["ruc-aa84f127-d9b3-442e-9422-420ee5b59d42"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C6E45A07B1813249D024BADDF2326CFE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, The Danish Centre for Research in Early Childhood Education and Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-aa84f127-d9b3-442e-9422-420ee5b59d42"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Praksisforskning om ’situeret ulighed’ : om at åbne ”ulighedens sorte boks”","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830671","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Artiklen analyserer fritidspædagogers faglighed gennem empirisk forskning i fritidsinstitutioner med observationer fra praksis og citater fra pædagogerne. Den fokuserer på, hvordan fritidspædagoger dagligt arbejder professionelt med at skabe lige deltagelsesmuligheder for børn og forebygge situeret ulighed – en form for ulighed der opstår i specifikke sociale kontekster. Artiklen introducerer begrebet ”fleksibel fokuseret faglighed” for at beskrive den dynamiske og situationsbestemte tilgang, som pædagogerne anvender i deres daglige arbejde. Gennem konkrete eksempler og observationer belyses, hvordan pædagogerne må navigere i komplekse sociale dynamikker og understøtte børns sociale liv og selvforståelse. Artiklen argumenterer for, at pædagogernes professionelle sprog og blik med denne form for faglighed er central for at skabe inkluderende fællesskaber og forebygge social ulighed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Højholt, Charlotte","Mardahl-Hansen, Tilde","Røn Larsen, Maja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830705"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fleksibel fokuseret faglighed hvordan fritidspædagoger arbejder med børns ulige deltagelsesmuligheder","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-830705","ids":["ruc-c925d2f0-c117-49b6-b97f-d7f86e950e2c"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1EF760A9837E164D97F4441D89C5FDD2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Tilde","key":"mardahlhansenpau","last":"Mardahl-Hansen","locid":"681a2367-eec3-469b-a925-ae6720df6462","name":"Mardahl-Hansen, Tilde","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01065386"],"journal":"Unge Paedagoger","pages":"97-109","status":"p","title":"Unge Paedagoger","title_org":"Unge Pædagoger","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-c925d2f0-c117-49b6-b97f-d7f86e950e2c"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Fleksibel fokuseret faglighed : - hvordan fritidspædagoger arbejder med børns (ulige) deltagelsesmuligheder","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830705","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Homecare for neonates has advanced, but combative analysis of contact methods remains unexplored. The aim was to identify predictors of readmission during homecare and to compare home visit, telemedicine or outpatient visit. Methods: This retrospective study included infants receiving homecare from 1 January 2015 to 31 December 2022. Data were obtained from local databases from six neonatal units in Denmark. The medical records of readmitted infants were reviewed. The main outcome were causes and predictors of readmission during homecare. The secondary outcome was exclusive breastfeeding at discharge. Results: The cohort consisted of 4827 infants (boys = 54.0%). The rate of unplanned readmissions was 4.6%. A gestational age (GA) <32 weeks (p-value <0.01) or bronchopulmonary dysplasia (BPD) (p-value <0.01) were predictors of readmission. There was no difference in unplanned readmissions based on contact method (p-value = 0.46 for telemedicine, p-value = 0.11 for outpatient visit). The overall exclusive breastfeeding rate at discharge from homecare was 64.1%. Conclusion: Homecare can be provided for preterm and term infants while establishing oral feeding, with caution on infants with a GA < 32 or BPD. All types of contact methods during homecare investigated can be provided equally in relation to readmission and exclusive breastfeeding.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rosenbaek, Charlotte Hoeyer","Zachariassen, Gitte","Hoest, Bente","Hahn, Gitte Holst","Larsen, Joan Neergaard","Salmonsen, Tenna Gladbo","Horskjær, Malene","Holm, Kristina Garne"],"cuid":["S02-085.71-803698"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rosenbaek, Charlotte Hoeyer"],"keyword":["Breastfeeding","Homecare","Preterm infants","Readmission","neonatal unit"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low readmission rates during neonatal homecare gestational age and bronchopulmonary dysplasia as key predictors","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.17576","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study was supported by a research scholarship from the Novo Nordisk Foundation."],"id":"S02-085.71-803698","identifier":[{"id":"85214398210","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12066913","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39775953","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-5cd878d5-ba00-45db-92be-b76425d2d987","au-52be1cf5-eb8f-4b54-802a-b3bc5743538e"],"keyword":["breastfeeding","homecare","neonatal unit","preterm infants","readmission"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-B20EB26378A88ED5E43B3BE8CE16B9AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.17576","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet, Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Hoeyer","key":"rosenbaekpau","last":"Rosenbaek","name":"Rosenbaek, Charlotte Hoeyer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"zachariassenpau","last":"Zachariassen","name":"Zachariassen, Gitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"hoestpau","last":"Hoest","locid":"cb323d7d-c189-4a9b-a541-f0df335502a8","name":"Hoest, Bente","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Holst","key":"hahnpau","last":"Hahn","name":"Hahn, Gitte Holst","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Joan Neergaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Joan Neergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Tenna Gladbo","key":"salmonsenpau","last":"Salmonsen","locid":"ba8b9fb1-09c9-4f2a-8f33-9a20126c084f","name":"Salmonsen, Tenna Gladbo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"horskjaerpau","last":"Horskjaer","locid":"3eb77c1b-b150-49c4-8baa-23643e75a3a7","name":"Horskjær, Malene","name_org":"Horskjaer, Malene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Garne","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","name":"Holm, Kristina Garne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39775953"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apa.17576","issn":["08035253","08035326"],"issn_org":["08035253"],"issue":"6","journal":"Acta Paediatrica","pages":"1342-1351","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Acta Paediatrica","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214398210"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5cd878d5-ba00-45db-92be-b76425d2d987","au-52be1cf5-eb8f-4b54-802a-b3bc5743538e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Low readmission rates during neonatal homecare: Gestational age and bronchopulmonary dysplasia as key predictors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.71-803698","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose: Over the past decades, childhood cancer survival has increased substantially in Europe, including Denmark. However, families with fewer social resources may have benefitted less from these improvements. In this nationwide register-based study, we assessed associations between parental socioeconomic position (SEP) and 5-year relapse-free survival (RFS) and overall survival (OS) in childhood cancer patients. Material and methods: All children aged <16 years diagnosed with cancer in Denmark between 1998 and 2017 were identified in the Danish Childhood Cancer Registry (N = 3245). Parents, with whom the children resided, were identified, and data on the parents’ education, cohabitation status, affiliation to work market, country of origin, and vital status of the children were obtained through individual-level linkage across Danish nationwide registries. Cox proportional hazards models were used to estimate the association between SEP indicators and 5-year RFS and OS. Results and interpretation: Tendencies towards lower 5-year RFS and OS were observed among children whose parents were unemployed/not in workforce (RFS: HR [hazard ratio] = 1.14, 95% CI [confidence interval]: 0.90–1.45, OS: HR = 1.28, 95% CI: 0.95–1.71) or from non-Western countries (RFS: HR = 1.21 95% CI: 0.96–1.52, OS: HR = 1.44, 95% CI: 1.09–1.90). Results by diagnostic groups revealed particularly low OS for children with non-central nervous system tumors whose parents were from non-Western countries (HR = 1.92, 95% CI: 1.24–2.97). Targeted strategies are needed to promote social equity and ensure optimal diagnosis, care, and management of childhood cancer across social groups.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Stegenborg, Fie","Bek, Mathilde S.","Nilsson, Charlotte J.","Pedersen, Line H.","Scheike, Thomas","Hjalgrim, Lisa L.","Erdmann, Friederike","Schmiegelow, Kjeld","Bidstrup, Pernille","Kenborg, Line","Winther, Jeanette Falck","Larsen, Hanne B.","Dalton, Susanne O."],"cuid":["S02-088.24-793305"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Stegenborg, Fie"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","Leibniz Institute for Prevention Research and Epidemiology","Universitätsmedizin Mainz"],"keyword":["Cancer survival","Childhood cancer","Register based study","Relapse","Social inequality","Socioeconomic position","Socioeconomic status"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socioeconomic characteristics and relapse free and overall survival from childhood cancer a nationwide study based on data from the danish childhood cancer registry","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/1651-226X.2025.42131","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.24-793305","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11808813","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85217357300","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39881602","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-74797a55-9145-4b7f-acfc-16e22e5f1aee","ku-69c93732-040d-4a7d-849a-2200f611bab5"],"keyword":["Childhood cancer","cancer survival","register-based study","relapse","social inequality","socioeconomic position","socioeconomic status"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-80FF7DED769BEA36C1BB4F2330D09F7A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/1651-226X.2025.42131","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/429883997/AO42131.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["National Hospital of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"de","key":"universitätsmedizin mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universitätsmedizin Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for prevention research and epidemiology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Institute for Prevention Research and Epidemiology","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"de","key":"johannes gutenberg university mainz","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Johannes Gutenberg University Mainz","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fie","key":"stegenborgpau","last":"Stegenborg","name":"Stegenborg, Fie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathilde S.","key":"bekpau","last":"Bek","name":"Bek, Mathilde S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte J.","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"573fb3db-41df-4adf-86e6-e5b0c69a43ef","name":"Nilsson, Charlotte Juul","name_org":"Nilsson, Charlotte J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3364-7412","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line H.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Line H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"scheikepau","last":"Scheike","locid":"53de2123-e34e-44a3-945f-265fce28de25","name":"Scheike, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-2148-4740","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisa L.","key":"hjalgrimpau","last":"Hjalgrim","name":"Hjalgrim, Lisa L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Friederike","key":"erdmannpau","last":"Erdmann","name":"Erdmann, Friederike","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","first":"Kjeld","key":"schmiegelowpau","last":"Schmiegelow","locid":"6ce2f948-244d-4f19-82aa-f08a71289674","name":"Schmiegelow, Kjeld","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Pernille","key":"bidstruppau","last":"Bidstrup","locid":"7cef3894-8d41-4b9b-acec-95b1d1b3f890","name":"Bidstrup, Pernille Envold","name_org":"Bidstrup, Pernille","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"kenborgpau","last":"Kenborg","name":"Kenborg, Line","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette F.","key":"wintherpau","last":"Winther","locid":"11ca8ef7-98c5-4eed-9dbe-3b44124f948b","name":"Winther, Jeanette Falck","name_org":"Winther, Jeanette F.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne B.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Hanne B.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Susanne O.","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","name_org":"Dalton, Susanne O.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39881602"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/1651-226x.2025.42131","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"179-187","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217357300"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-74797a55-9145-4b7f-acfc-16e22e5f1aee","ku-69c93732-040d-4a7d-849a-2200f611bab5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Socioeconomic characteristics and relapse-free and overall survival from childhood cancer – a nationwide study based on data from the Danish Childhood Cancer Registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.24-793305","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Incursions and persistence of high pathogenicity avian influenza viruses (HPAIVs) in Europe have resulted in devastating epidemiological seasons in 2020/2021 and 2021/2022 compared to previous seasons. HPAIVs were confirmed in 27 outbreaks in poultry and other captive birds, and in 553 wild birds throughout Denmark. Our data revealed that the viruses detected in Denmark were highly similar to contemporary HPAIVs in other European countries in both seasons. The HPAIVs detected in Denmark belonged to clade 2.3.4.4b and were of different subtypes (H5N1, H5N3, H5N5, and H5N8). Several viruses identified in 2021/2022 were found to be highly similar to those found in the previous season, whereas others were identified as novel viruses. The genetic data combined with epidemiological information on the outbreaks in Denmark were used to explore the most likely route of introduction into each infected poultry production site. In a few cases, the data supported that the outbreaks were caused by between-farm HPAIV transmission. However, the majority of outbreaks in poultry are believed to have been a result of direct or indirect contact with HPAIV-infected wild birds. With a logistic regression model, it was determined that the only significant risk factor for experiencing an outbreak was the poultry production type. Turkey and mallard farms had a significantly higher risk of experiencing an outbreak in comparison to chicken farms. These findings prompt reconsideration of AIV preventative measures limiting HPAIV outbreaks, not only at the wild bird-poultry interface but also due to secondary transmissions between poultry farms.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Liang, Yuan","Boklund, Anette Ella","Larsen, Lars Erik","Breum, Solvej","Giese, Steen","Hammer, Anne Sofie","Kirkeby, Carsten Thure","Krog, Jesper Schak","Liu, Yangfan","Madsen, Jesper Johannes","Therkildsen, Ole Roland","Ovesen, Maibritt Træholt","Quaade, Michelle Lauge","Trebbien, Ramona","Mortensen, Sten","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-803949"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Liang, Yuan"],"keyword":["Avian influenza virus","Phylogeny","Risk Factors","Surveillance","Wild bird"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Fødevarestyrelsen"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"epidemiological and virological investigation of high pathogenicity avian influenza outbreaks in danish poultry during 000000002020 000000002021 and 000000002021 000000002022","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rvsc.2025.105618","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-803949","identifier":[{"id":"105000873647","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40147156","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-2244aa1b-0508-499b-b3ae-d2afd858257b","ku-26d5b091-5f5a-48c3-b105-a354a2282854"],"keyword":["Avian influenza virus","Phylogeny","Risk factors","Surveillance","Wild bird"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B0B74BA0D3A23727E494D55A2582EF05"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451598961/1-s2.0-S003452882500092X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.rvsc.2025.105618","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"