e Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40147156"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.rvsc.2025.105618","issn":["00345288","15322661"],"issn_org":["00345288"],"journal":"Research in Veterinary Science","paperid":"105618","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Research in Veterinary Science","volume":"189"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000873647"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-2244aa1b-0508-499b-b3ae-d2afd858257b","ku-26d5b091-5f5a-48c3-b105-a354a2282854"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Epidemiological and Virological investigation of high pathogenicity avian influenza outbreaks in Danish poultry during 2020/2021 and 2021/2022","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-803949","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"High-intensity interval training (HIIT) has been suggested as an effective treatment approach of childhood obesity. The objective of the present study was to examine intensity, enjoyment, and perceived exertion of a 4x4-minute play-based HIIT program for children and adolescents with obesity. 83 participants (42.2% girls, 12.3±1.5 years, 57.8% boys, 12.0±1.6 years) completed a 12-week intervention comprising three weekly sessions. After nine sessions (weeks 2, 6, and 11), participants rated perceived exertion (RPE) with a Borg scale and enjoyment of activities using the Physical Activity Enjoyment Scale (PACES). Heart rate (HR) was recorded to assess time spent in high- and moderate-intensity. Participants spent more time in high-intensity during strength-based(P=0.004) and running-based(P=0.007) activities compared to ball games, and more time was spent in moderate-intensity during ball games compared to strength-based(P=0.033) and running-based(P=0.028) activities. Overall, boys spent more time in moderate-intensity than girls(P=0.007). Participants rated RPE lower for ball games than for strength-based(P<0.001) and running-based(P<0.001) activities. Boys rated running-based activities more enjoyable than girls(P=0.021). Exercise intensity and RPE vary by activity in HIIT for children and adolescents with obesity. Ball games led to less high-intensity time and were seen as less exhausting. No differences in RPE or enjoyment were found over time.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Simonsen, Morten Bilde","Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær","Bech Pedersen, Jeppe","Christiansen, Stine","Vestergaard, Esben Thyssen","Hagstrøm, Søren","Larsen, Ryan Godsk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-770048"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exercise","Heart Rate","High intensity interval training","Running","Strength training"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intensity and enjoyment of play based hiit in children and adolescents with obesity","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85211003113&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Steno Diabetes Center North Denmark, Trygfonden (Grant No. 149852), Danish Regions (Grant No. R201-A4487), Svend Andersens Foundation and Memorial legatee for Carpenter J\\u00F8rgen Holm and wife Elisa F. Hansen (Grant No. 20094).Thank you to iQniter (Aalborg, Denmark) for lending us the heart rate system. iQniter had no influence on the interpretation of the results."],"id":"S01-000.00-770048","identifier":[{"id":"85211003113","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39472023","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-34f6bf5a-e74f-4f5d-8174-81c1fef2fa61"],"keyword":["Department of Materials and Production, Aalborg University Aalborg Denmark","ball game","exercise","heart rate","high-intensity interval training","running","strength training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DEE4F26B91567058148D05F7861CCF51"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-03-01","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Biomechanics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Center for Mathematical Modelling of Knee Osteoarthritis","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Materials and Production, Physics and Mechanics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Bilde","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"7d1393c0-2905-4e87-9a3d-80cca4dbeee6","name":"Simonsen, Morten Bilde","orcid":"0000-0001-6645-3596","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Nørkjær","key":"eggertsenpau","last":"Eggertsen","locid":"ef704125-8280-4878-8ebc-8f60b38e7782","name":"Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-3425-0839","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Bech","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d2019b6e-fcb3-4c1c-a0d2-34f61f8a98ae","name":"Bech Pedersen, Jeppe","name_org":"Pedersen, Jeppe Bech","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"8322afab-4403-467c-905e-18073e709ec7","name":"Christiansen, Stine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben Thyssen","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Esben Thyssen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"hagstrømpau","last":"Hagstrøm","locid":"fe472f53-6bcd-4587-8287-df1539f689c3","name":"Hagstrøm, Søren","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ryan Godsk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"86d31e60-1de1-4284-a688-596cc17dca1c","name":"Larsen, Ryan Godsk","orcid":"0000-0002-4622-1453","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39472023"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1055/a-2456-4054","issn":["01724622","0943917X"],"issn_org":["01724622"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","pages":"207-216","publisher":"Georg Thieme Verlag","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Medicine","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211003113"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-34f6bf5a-e74f-4f5d-8174-81c1fef2fa61"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Intensity and enjoyment of play-based HIIT in children and adolescents with obesity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-770048","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Newcastle disease (ND) is a notifiable avian disease responsible for several panzootics, which has resulted in the establishment of mandatory vaccination programs against the virus in several countries including Denmark. This study compared the immune response elicited in layers by the standard vaccination program for ND of a Danish commercial egg production facility with a simplified version of the vaccination program. A commercial flock of layers was followed for 77 weeks from hatching to culling. The flock was divided into two groups according to vaccination program and housed separately. One group received the standard vaccination program consisting of a vector vaccine, a live vaccine (administered twice) and an inactivated vaccine (standard vaccination program). The other group received a newly marketed vector vaccine and the inactivated vaccine of the standard vaccination program (simplified vaccination program). Blood samples were collected at regular intervals from 30 randomly selected layers in each group until culling (77 weeks of age) and analysed for ND antibodies by ELISA assays, which measured antibodies against the nucleoprotein or fusion protein, and hemagglutination inhibition tests. Both vaccination programs provided lasting antibodies until 77 weeks. The simplified vaccination program showed significantly higher fusion protein antibodies and a markedly earlier onset of immunity at five weeks of age (97–100 % seroprevalence) than the standard program. The standard vaccination program reached the same seroprevalence at 14 and 24 weeks of age based on fusion protein antibodies and HI titres, respectively. The inactivated vaccine elicited a boost in antibody titres in both groups, however, boosting with the live vaccine used in the standard vaccination program did not result in an increased antibody response. This might indicate that administering of a vector vaccine prior to a live vaccine inhibits the serological response to the live vaccine.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Martiny, Karen","Christensen, Jens Peter","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-800830"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Immunity","LAYERS","Newcastle disease","Vaccination","Vector vaccine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a simplified vaccination program elicits an immune response comparable to a complex standard vaccination program in commercial layers under field conditions","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vetimm.2025.110882","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-800830","identifier":[{"id":"39817996","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85214836663","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-eb073aca-3b33-4dd4-a777-f2a1ad173163"],"keyword":["Attenuated live vaccine","Avian paramyxovirus 1","Immunity","Layers","Newcastle disease","Vaccination","Vector vaccine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8685FA3EFC1C292D2954524130A6FFBC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/430092217/A_simplified_vaccination_program_elicits_an_immune_response_comparable_to_a_complex_standard_vaccination_program_in_commercial_layers_under_field_conditions.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vetimm.2025.110882","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"martinypau","last":"Martiny","locid":"2f168c92-c78b-43da-944e-872121b1cc06","name":"Martiny, Karen","orcid":"0000-0002-7948-1067","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"939fd558-e675-4e66-9601-2a336ebfd5a9","name":"Christensen, Jens Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-6430-9010","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39817996"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vetimm.2025.110882","issn":["01652427","18732534"],"issn_org":["01652427"],"journal":"Veterinary Immunology and Immunopathology","paperid":"110882","status":"p","title":"Veterinary Immunology and Immunopathology","volume":"280"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214836663"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-eb073aca-3b33-4dd4-a777-f2a1ad173163"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A simplified vaccination program elicits an immune response comparable to a complex standard vaccination program in commercial layers under field conditions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-800830","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Malene Charlotte","Krogager, Stinne Gunder Strøm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-805450"],"event":{"end":"2025-08-15","start":"2025-08-13","title":"NordMedia","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social media made me buy it how critical algorithm studies can improve understandings of everyday over consumption in the digital age","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-805450","ids":["aau-be92eda7-30b8-4635-8460-f39bc7075f86"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-98CD31EEFA063100E7C126FF0B8C3C04"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Digital Media in Everyday Life","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Exploring Methods for Participation and Dialogue in Communication Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Mediated Communication","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Green Societies","Aalborg University, [Mission] Improved Wellbeing Among Children And Youth In Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stinne Gunder Strøm","key":"krogagerpau","last":"Krogager","locid":"a62b58cc-8bfa-46d6-8588-004f926d107d","name":"Krogager, Stinne Gunder Strøm","orcid":"0000-0002-3180-0583","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-be92eda7-30b8-4635-8460-f39bc7075f86"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"“Social media made me buy it” : How Critical Algorithm Studies Can Improve Understandings of Everyday Over-Consumption in the Digital Age","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-805450","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Importance:: The spatial and temporal distribution of intracerebral hemorrhage (ICH) recurrence are largely unknown. Objective: To assess timing and location of recurrent ICH events in relation to the index ICH event (adjacent ICH [adjICH] vs remote ICH [remICH]). Design, Setting, and Participants: This cohort study was a pooled analysis of individual cohort studies from 2002 to 2021 among hospital-based European cohorts. Patients with 2 or more clinically distinguishable (≥1 recurrent) small vessel disease-related ICH events were included. Data analysis was performed from December 2023 to December 2024. Exposures: ICH location and underlying small vessel disease type. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was adjICH, defined by anatomical ICH location and side, and the secondary outcome was time to recurrence. Multivariable regression analyses were conducted adjusting for ICH location, cerebral amyloid angiopathy according to Boston 2.0 or simplified Edinburgh criteria, convexity subarachnoid hemorrhage extension, hypertension, and antihypertensive treatment, including an interaction term for hypertension and antihypertensive treatment. Results: Among 733 patients (median [IQR] age, 72.4 [65.2 to 79.0] years; 346 female [47.2%]), there were 1616 ICH events, including 733 index and 883 recurrent ICH events (range, 1 to 6 recurrences) over a median (IQR) follow-up of 2.53 (0.66 to 4.92) years. There were 340 patients (46.4%) with adjICH and 393 patients (53.6%) with remICH. Among recurrent ICH events, there were 476 adjICH events and 407 remICH events. In multivariable regression analyses, lobar index ICH (adjusted odds ratio [aOR], 2.08; 95% CI, 1.32 to 3.27) and cerebral amyloid angiopathy at index ICH (aOR, 2.21; 95% CI, 1.57 to 3.11) were associated with higher odds of adjICH, while cerebellar index ICH was associated with lower odds of adjICH (aOR, 0.25; 95% CI, 0.07 to 0.89). The median (IQR) time to recurrence was 1.25 (0.36 to 3.38) years for adjICH and 2.21 (0.66 to 4.85) years for remICH. Previous lobar or convexity subarachnoid hemorrhage (coefficient, -0.75; 95% CI, -1.25 to -0.25; P =.003), adjICH (coefficient, -0.60; 95% CI, -1.02 to -0.18; P =.005), and the number of previous ICH events (coefficient per 1-event increase, -0.62; 95% CI, -0.93 to -0.32; P <.001) were independently associated with a shorter time to recurrence. Conclusions and relevance: This study found that early recurrence and cerebral amyloid angiopathy were associated with adjICH. These findings suggest that regional, tissue-based factors may facilitate recurrence and that identifying and targeting local vasculopathic changes may represent potential novel treatment targets..","author_count":39,"contributors":["Goeldlin, Martina B.","Fandler-Höfler, Simon","Pezzini, Alessandro","Manikantan, Anusha","Rauch, Janis","Hald, Stine Munk","Kristensen, Mona Løgtholt","Obergottsberger, Lena","Sembill, Jochen A.","Haupenthal, David","Larsen, Kristin Tveitan","Avramiotis, Nikolaos S.","Polymeris, Alexandros A.","Periole, Charlotte","Thiankhaw, Kitti","Rangus, Ida","Puy, Laurent","Pasi, Marco","Morotti, Andrea","Silvestrelli, Giorgio","Giacalone, Giacomo","Paciaroni, Maurizio","Zedde, Marialuisa","Giorli, Elisa","Tassi, Rossana","Delgado-Romeu, Marc","Fischer, Urs","Volbers, Bastian","Hakim, Arsany","Z'Graggen, Werner J.","Nolte, Christian H.","Werring, David J.","Raposo, Nicolas","Engelter, Stefan T.","Kristoffersen, Espen S.","Kuramatsu, Joji","Gattringer, Thomas","Gaist, David","Seiffge, David J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-812653"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Goeldlin, Martina B.","Seiffge, David J."],"country":["Austria","France","Germany","Italy","Norway","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["ASST “Carlo Poma” Mantova","AUSL-IRCCS Reggio Emilia","Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations","Azienda Ospedaliera Spedali Civili di Brescia","Berlin Institute of Health","CHU de Toulouse","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Hospital de la Santa Creu in Sant Pau","Medical University of Graz","Ospedale Sant' Andrea la Spezia","RoMed Klinikum","San Raffaele Scientific Institute","Toulouse University Hospital","Tours University Hospital","UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology","University Hospital Erlangen","University Hospital of Basel","University Hospital of Bern","University Hospital of Ferrara","University Hospital of Parma","University Hospital of Siena","University of Lille","University of Parma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"location and timing of recurrent nontraumatic intracerebral hemorrhage","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-812653","identifier":[{"id":"40029641","type":"pmid"},{"id":"86000584226","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-af370da9-5dfa-498c-bce1-90ac4a12080d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-275D25E4B74D1AACA4C97D36DFFC86FE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ch","key":"university hospital of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University Hospital of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"medical university of graz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical University of Graz","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"ucl queen square institute of neurology","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"UCL Queen Square Institute of Neurology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"university of parma","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Parma","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"university hospital of pa