{"abstract":"Transcription factors carry long intrinsically disordered regions often containing multiple activation domains. Despite numerous recent high-throughput identifications and characterizations of activation domains, the interplay between sequence motifs, activation domains, and regulator binding in intrinsically disordered transcription factor regions remains unresolved. Here, we map sequence motifs and activation domains in an Arabidopsis thaliana NAC transcription factor clade, revealing that although sequence motifs and activation domains often coincide, no systematic overlap exists. Biophysical analyses using NMR spectroscopy show that the long intrinsically disordered region of senescence-associated transcription factor ANAC046 is devoid of residual structure. We identify two activation domain/sequence motif regions, one at each end that both bind a panel of six positive and negative regulator domains from biologically relevant regulators promiscuously. Binding affinities measured using isothermal titration calorimetry reveal a hierarchy for regulator binding of the two ANAC046 activation domain/sequence motif regions defining these as regulatory hotspots. Despite extensive dynamic intramolecular contacts along the disordered chain revealed using paramagnetic relaxation enhancement experiments and simulations, the regions remain uncoupled in binding. Together, the results imply rheostatic regulation by ANAC046 through concentration-dependent regulator competition, a mechanism likely mirrored in other transcription factors with distantly located activation domains.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Due, Amanda D.","Davey, Norman E.","Thomasen, F. Emil","Morffy, Nicholas","Prestel, Andreas","Brakti, Inna","O'Shea, Charlotte","Strader, Lucia C.","Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","Skriver, Karen","Kragelund, Birthe B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820323"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Duke University","The Institute of Cancer Research, London"],"keyword":["Intrinsically disordered region","Isothermal titration calorimetry","Nuclear magnetic resonance","Protein protein interactions","Short Linear Motif","Transcription factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hierarchy in regulator interactions with distant transcriptional activation domains empowers rheostatic regulation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.70142","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-820323","identifier":[{"id":"105005280848","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40371733","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12079402","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-e487b591-98ce-461e-8434-2de41239fef1"],"keyword":["activation domains","intrinsically disordered region","isothermal titration calorimetry","nuclear magnetic resonance","protein–protein interactions","short linear motif","transcription factor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-34E717E5174BE6A86BDD74795E919D52"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pro.70142","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451603020/Protein_Science_-_2025_-_Due_-_Hierarchy_in_regulator_interactions_with_distant_transcriptional_activation_domains_empowers.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Biomolecular Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"the institute of cancer research london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Institute of Cancer Research, London","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"duke university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Duke University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Amanda D.","key":"duepau","last":"Due","locid":"4d38cfe3-4cf2-41c4-b019-583ad6f2fb07","name":"Due, Amanda D.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Norman E.","key":"daveypau","last":"Davey","name":"Davey, Norman E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"F. Emil","key":"thomasenpau","last":"Thomasen","locid":"7605ed5e-b48a-44a0-8c80-556031f27eb1","name":"Thomasen, F. Emil","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Nicholas","key":"morffypau","last":"Morffy","name":"Morffy, Nicholas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"prestelpau","last":"Prestel","locid":"f60090ef-7296-43ef-a98a-713fd09d47fe","name":"Prestel, Andreas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inna","key":"braktipau","last":"Brakti","locid":"9219594a-b795-4630-8bb7-8c4d98eae5d2","name":"Brakti, Inna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"osheapau","last":"O'Shea","locid":"66faa368-fff8-4a0a-8001-73ce7306646f","name":"O'Shea, Charlotte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lucia C.","key":"straderpau","last":"Strader","name":"Strader, Lucia C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kresten","key":"lindorfflarsenpau","last":"Lindorff-Larsen","locid":"be20a4d8-92c4-44b9-9dfb-b6ad6471a58c","name":"Lindorff-Larsen, Kresten","orcid":"0000-0002-4750-6039","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"skriverpau","last":"Skriver","locid":"15d37718-e4b5-4e19-afe1-004e0f73a675","name":"Skriver, Karen","orcid":"0000-0003-2225-4012","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Birthe B.","key":"kragelundpau","last":"Kragelund","locid":"c3a5d42e-5e73-4af3-94f9-22550bb7c499","name":"Kragelund, Birthe B.","orcid":"0000-0002-7454-1761","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40371733"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pro.70142","issn":["09618368","13595040"],"issn_org":["09618368"],"issue":"6","journal":"Protein Science","paperid":"e70142","status":"p","title":"Protein Science","volume":"34"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005280848"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e487b591-98ce-461e-8434-2de41239fef1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hierarchy in regulator interactions with distant transcriptional activation domains empowers rheostatic regulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820323","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD) affects roughly 1 in 3 adults and is a leading cause of liver transplants and liver related mortality. A deeper understanding of disease pathogenesis is essential to assist in developing blood-based biomarkers. Methods: Here, we use data-independent acquisition mass spectrometry to assess disease-state associated protein profiles in human liver, blood plasma, and white adipose tissue (WAT). Results: In liver, we find that MASLD is associated with an increased abundance of proteins involved in immune response and extracellular matrix (ECM) and a decrease in proteins involved in metabolism. Cell type deconvolution of the proteome indicates liver endothelial and hepatic stellate cells are the main source of ECM rearrangements, and hepatocytes are the major contributor to the changes in liver metabolism. In the blood, profiles of several MASLD-associated proteins correlate with expression in WAT rather than liver and so could serve as suitable liver disease predictors in a multi-protein panel marker. Moreover, our proteomics-based logistic regression models perform better than existing methods for predicting MASLD and liver fibrosis from human blood samples. Conclusions: Our comprehensive proteomic analysis deepens the understanding of liver function and MASLD pathology by elucidating key cellular mechanisms and multi-organ interactions, and demonstrates the robustness of a proteomics-based biomarker panel to enhance diagnosis of MASLD and significant fibrosis.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Pedersen, Felix Boel","Akimov, Vyacheslav","Teuchler, Mathias","Terkelsen, Mike Krogh","Wernberg, Charlotte","Larsen, Frederik Tibert","Hallenborg, Philip","Lauridsen, Mette Munk","Krag, Aleksander","Mandrup, Susanne","Ravnskjaer, Kim","Blagoev, Blagoy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821792"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Blagoev, Blagoy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deep proteome profiling of metabolic dysfunction associated steatotic liver disease","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43856-025-00780-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-821792","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11876662","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"86000051058","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40032974","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-e7136ca2-d266-4883-944c-065f9bfb80f3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-38CA79F27A4347AC23A9C160C5BD878E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290537035/s43856-025-00780-3.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s43856-025-00780-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, ATLAS - Center for Functional Genomics and Tissue Plasticity","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Biomedical Mass Spectrometry and Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Felix","key":"boelpau","last":"Boel","locid":"059fd876-56ae-4c33-abd8-6f78949756cb