Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte H.","key":"larsencharlottehpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Charlotte H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Samar M.","key":"christensensamarmpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Samar M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Elnaz","key":"parwaeielnazpau","last":"Parwaei","name":"Parwaei, Elnaz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thordis","key":"thomsenthordispau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"6c1e4246-728c-46eb-9c96-dfd48e4de8bc","name":"Thomsen, Thordis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik F.","key":"thomsenfrederikfpau","last":"Thomsen","name":"Thomsen, Frederik F.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39992553"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11255-025-04415-3","issn":["03011623","15732584"],"issn_org":["03011623"],"issue":"8","journal":"International Urology and Nephrology","pages":"2475-2480","status":"p","title":"International Urology and Nephrology","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219192719"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-154f62fd-b1ea-4e3d-91e1-40f5fdbbd1aa"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Incidence and location of positioning-related injuries in lateral positioning during laparoscopic kidney surgery","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828391","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Lichen sclerosus (LSc) is a chronic inflammatory disease affecting the anogenital area and having malignant potential. Population-based data on the incidence of LSc in men and associated cancer risk are sparse. In the Danish Pathology Register, we identified all men with histologically verified penile LSc 1997–2022 and calculated incidence rates. Through linkage with the Danish Cancer Registry, standardized incidence ratios (SIRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were computed as relative risk estimates of penile squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) and non-penile cancer in men with penile LSc (1978–2019) compared with background population rates. During the study period, the age-standardized incidence rate of penile LSc more than doubled, being 17.9 per 100,000 person-years in the most recent time (2021–2022). The age-specific incidence increased with age and was highest in ages 70–79 years (29.2 per 100,000 person-years). Compared with the general population, men with penile LSc had an increased rate of penile SCC (SIR = 15.5, 95% CI: 12.0–19.5), which increased with follow-up length and younger age at LSc diagnosis. Rates of non-penile cancers were mostly close to unity except for lung cancer (SIR = 0.6, 95% CI: 0.5–0.7). This nationwide study showed an increased incidence of histologically verified penile LSc over the past 26 years. Importantly, men with penile LSc had nearly 16 times higher rate of penile SCC compared with the general population. There was no strong association with the non-penile cancers, except for a lower rate of lung cancer, suggesting that the malignant potential of LSc is caused by local factors rather than a general cancer predisposition.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Stærk, Marianne Gardar","Kaderly Rasmussen, Emma L.","Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Baandrup, Louise","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828983"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Incidence","Penile cancer","Risk"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"histologically verified penile lichen sclerosus incidence in denmark over 000000000026 years and long term risk of penile and non penile cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.35454","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-828983","identifier":[{"id":"105005406486","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12280859","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40251017","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-5df6c557-73d2-42a2-b80e-067e104a96e2"],"keyword":["incidence","non-penile cancer","penile cancer","penile lichen sclerosus","risk"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-CD78193695DA0A5D5FF93202AC4C0B50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.35454","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/460999048/Intl_Journal_of_Cancer_-_2025_-_St_rk_-_Histologically_verified_penile_lichen_sclerosus_Incidence_in_Denmark_over_26_years.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, No speciality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marianne Gardar","key":"stærkpau","last":"Stærk","name":"Stærk, Marianne Gardar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emma L.","key":"kaderlyrasmussenpau","last":"Kaderly Rasmussen","name":"Kaderly Rasmussen, Emma L.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Gerd","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","name":"Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum-Larsen","name":"Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Louise","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","locid":"abccf449-8bed-4f98-bb4d-012134523360","name":"Baandrup, Louise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 4","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40251017"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.35454","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"6","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"1086-1093","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"157"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005406486"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5df6c557-73d2-42a2-b80e-067e104a96e2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Histologically verified penile lichen sclerosus — Incidence in Denmark over 26 years and long-term risk of penile and non-penile cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-828983","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The PERISAFE trial aims to assess the adverse effects associated with an 8-day postoperative treatment with ibuprofen after hip and knee arthroplasties. This paper outlines the detailed statistical analysis plan for the primary data. The PERISAFE trial is a randomized, placebo-controlled, blinded multicentre trial allocating 2904 hip- or knee-arthroplasty patients 1:1 to ibuprofen 400 mg ×3/day or identical placebo ×3/day for 8 days postoperatively. The primary outcome is a composite of death, acute myocardial infarction, stroke, pulmonary embolism, deep venous thrombosis, renal failure, major bleeding, re-operation, gastrointestinal ulcer, or readmission within 90 days postoperatively. Secondary outcomes are hospital-free days within 90 days postoperatively, a composite of ibuprofen and opioid-related adverse reactions based on an 8-day postoperative diary, and health-related quality of life after 90 days postoperatively. All randomized patients who undergo surgery will be included in all analyzes. Binary data will be analyzed using a mixed-effects generalized linear model, count data will be analyzed using the van Elteren test, and continuous data will be analyzed using a mixed-effects linear regression. Additionally, the win ratio will be calculated for the primary outcome. The statistical analyzes will be conducted in accordance with this pre-planned statistical analysis plan with one interim analysis after the inclusion of 1400 patients. All analyzes will be adjusted for site. We expect that the PERISAFE trial will provide high-quality data based on predefined detailed methodology regarding the safety of postoperative treatment with ibuprofen after elective hip and knee arthroplasties.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Laursen, Christina C.W.","Lunn, Troels H.","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Olsen, Markus Harboe","Kappel, Andreas","Jakobsen, Thomas","Pedersen, Niels A.","Thougaard, Thomas","Graungaard, Ben K.","Bjerno, Thomas","Hollænder, Peter B.","Runge, Charlotte","Yilmaz, Müjgan","Eljaja, Salamah B.","Therkelsen, Anne S.N.","Steiness, Joakim","Gasbjerg, Kasper S.","Thybo, Kasper","Lange, Kai H.W.","Brorson, Stig","Varnum, Claus","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Overgaard, Søren","Mathiesen, Ole","Jakobsen, Janus C."],"cuid":["S02-087.50-813367"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Laursen, Christina C.W."],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the adverse effects associated with ibuprofen use after major orthopaedic surgeries a detailed statistical analysis plan for the perisafe randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.70062","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.50-813367","identifier":[{"id":"40433991","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12117996","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105006838302","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-6440d44d-1bf4-402d-8e58-767111cbebe7","sdu-9188c5e7-63cb-4175-9472-a0ecc56e2f10"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A0830D02A087CD223E49886A3B8BB6BE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.70062","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/787205643/Laursen_et_al._2025_The_Adverse_Effects_Associated_With_Ibuprofen_Use_After_Major_Orthopaedic_Surgeries.pdf","version":"Published V