{"abstract":"The Danish prenatal program and genetic testing provide pregnant couples with the opportunity to learn about serious and potentially life-threatening fetal conditions. While invasive diagnostic methods remain the gold standard, advances in non-invasive technologies are emerging as valuable alternatives but they still have reduced resolution. Whole genome sequencing offers much increased resolution but raises challenges related to costs, uncertain findings, and secondary results. Counselling and multidisciplinary collaboration are critical to supporting couples navigating these complex decisions.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Thomsen, Simon Horsholt","Hjortshøj, Tina Duelund","Barbosa, Malou","Laursen, Lone","Larsen, Martin","Hvidbjerg, Marie Skov","Tørring, Pernille","Sperling, Lene","Lund, Ida Charlotte Bay","Andreasen, Lotte","Ernst, Anja","Sunde, Lone","Balslev-Harder, Marie","Petersen, Olav Bjørn","Lou, Stina","Becher, Naja","Vogel, Ida"],"cuid":["S02-087.76-803979"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Vogel, Ida"],"keyword":["Denmark","Female","Fetal Diseases genetics","Genetic Counseling","Genetic Testing methods","Humans","Pregnancy","Prenatal Diagnosis methods","Whole genome sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetik i føtalmedicin","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V12240853","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.76-803979","