{"abstract":"Background: Four influenza pandemics have occurred during the past 100 years, and new variants of influenza viruses will continue to emerge. The nasal mucosa acts as the primary site of exposure to influenza A virus (IAV) infection, but viral recognition and host immune responses in the nasal mucosa are still poorly understood. Objectives: This study aimed to evaluate the utility of non-invasive nasopharyngeal swabs for longitudinal monitoring of mucosal immune responses in pigs experimentally challenged with two swine-adapted and one human-adapted IAV. By tracking antiviral immune responses from disease onset to recovery, we sought to assess the feasibility of this method for capturing dynamic changes in viral load and host responses across different IAV strains. Methods: Forty-two IAV-negative pigs were divided into four groups and housed separately for infection studies. Viral and host RNA from nasopharyngeal swabs was analyzed using microfluidic qPCR, while statistical analysis was performed with a Bayesian approach in R. Additionally, immunohistochemical staining was used to assess MUC5AC expression in the nasal mucosa of infected pigs. Results: RNA was successfully isolated from nasopharyngeal swabs, enabling gene expression analysis to monitor innate immune responses to IAV infection. A classical innate antiviral immune response was demonstrated after the three virus infections including expression of pattern recognition receptors (PRRs), transcription factors, interferons (IFNs), interferon-stimulated genes (ISGs), cytokines, and chemokines. The kinetics and magnitude of immune responses varied between infections, with notable downregulation of mucins following infection with the Danish swine-adapted isolate. Further, the Danish isolate induced a fast but transient IFN-mediated response concurrent with high expression of cytokines and chemokines, while the other swine-adapted Mexican isolate induced a prolonged immune response of ISGs, cytokines, and chemokines. Conclusion: This study highlights the significance of highly translational nasopharyngeal swabs as a non-invasive method for assessing mucosal antiviral immune responses. Utilizing microfluidic mRNA analysis, we gained valuable insights into antiviral mucosal responses across 216 swab samples collected from viral inoculation through recovery in three distinct influenza virus infections.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Glud, Helena Aagaard","Kristensen, Charlotte","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Brogaard, Louise","George, Sophie","Henriksen, Betina Lyngfeldt","Polhaus, Chrysillis Judy Magaard","Trebbien, Ramona","Larsen, Lars E.","Skovgaard, Kerstin"],"cuid":["S02-099.53-804388"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Glud, Helena Aagaard"],"keyword":["Experimental infection","Influenza A virus","Mucosal innate immunity","Nasopharyngeal swabs","Pig model"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tracking mucosal innate immune responses to three influenza a virus strains in a highly translational pig model using nasopharyngeal swabs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/17534259251331385","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.53-804388","identifier":[{"id":"40165394","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11960188","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105002545514","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f7dd8e4d-253f-4f64-9aa6-859dfd4d060a","ku-86ba0fa9-651e-4652-a174-c8f07d7282bd"],"keyword":["Experimental infection","Influenza A virus","Mucosal innate immunity","Nasopharyngeal swabs","Pig model"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F391DAC8C5C75C25568E90850C51EF16"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/17534259251331385","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/448194563/Tracking_mucosal_innate_immune_responses_to_three_influenza_A_virus_strains_in_a_highly_translational_pig_model_using_nasopharyngeal_swabs.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/395881540/laybourn-et-al-2025-tracking-mucosal-innate-immune-responses-to-three-influenza-a-virus-strains-in-a-highly.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine, Section for Medical Biotechnology, Antiviral Immunomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Helena A.","key":"laybournpau","last":"Laybourn","locid":"8237a5ca-c866-413c-a362-165d58455ea0","name":"Glud, Helena Aagaard","name_org":"Laybourn, Helena A.","orcid":"0000-0002-0477-7584","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders G.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bb3513aa-fb20-46ef-ba14-9c150c929cf1","name":"Pedersen, Anders Gorm","name_org":"Pedersen, Anders G.","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-8965","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"brogaardpau","last":"Brogaard","locid":"f00b834e-dca2-4296-86bf-7023304adab8","name":"Brogaard, Louise","orcid":"0000-0003-4571-6822","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sophie","key":"georgepau","last":"George","locid":"40656a28-0c15-447d-9c3d-75697fd23b6b","name":"George, Sophie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Betina L.","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","locid":"92822e1c-7a1c-4605-b3e1-b91f2019d4d3","name":"Henriksen, Betina Lyngfeldt","name_org":"Henriksen, Betina L.","orcid":"0009-0006-6838-9798","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Chrysillis H.","key":"polhauspau","last":"Polhaus","locid":"d7ea1332-60c1-4d67-8b4e-31dd4927c8f4","name":"Polhaus, Chrysillis Judy Magaard","name_org":"Polhaus, Chrysillis H.","orcid":"0000-0001-6877-6233","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kerstin","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c3c3868-b5a3-457b-8b97-9645ad03e405","name":"Skovgaard, Kerstin","orcid":"0000-0001-5663-4879","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40165394"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/17534259251331385","issn":["17432839","17534259"],"issn_org":["17534259"],"journal":"Innate Immunity","pages":"1-15","publisher":"SAGE Publications Ltd","status":"p","title":"Innate Immunity","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002545514"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f7dd8e4d-253f-4f64-9aa6-859dfd4d060a","ku-86ba0fa9-651e-4652-a174-c8f07d7282bd"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tracking mucosal innate immune responses to three influenza A virus strains in a highly translational pig model using nasopharyngeal swabs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.53-804388","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) are recommended for pain treatment after elective hip and knee arthroplasties. However, evidence regarding the incidence of adverse effects with short-term NSAID treatment following surgery is limited. We, therefore, aim to assess the adverse effects with an eight-day postoperative treatment with ibuprofen after elective hip and knee arthroplasties. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: PERISAFE is a randomized, placebo-controlled, blinded multicenter trial with 90-day and one-year follow-up. Eligible patients undergoing elective hip or knee arthroplasty are allocated 1:1 to either ibuprofen 400 mg ×3/day or identical placebo ×3/day for eight days after surgery. The primary outcome is a composite of either death, acute myocardial infarction, stroke, pulmonary embolism, deep venous thrombosis, renal failure, major bleeding, re-operation, gastrointestinal ulcer, or readmission within 90 days postoperatively. Secondary outcomes are hospital-free days within 90 days postoperatively, a composite of ibuprofen and opioid-related adverse reactions based on eight-day postoperative diary, and health related quality of life after 90 days postoperatively. A total of 2904 patients are needed to demonstrate a relative risk reduction of 33% in the placebo group, accepting a risk of type I error of 5% and type II error of 20% and a proportion of serious adverse events in the ibuprofen group of 8%. The primary analysis will be in the modified intention-to-treat population. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The trial is approved by the Danish Medicine Agency and the Research Ethics Committee (EU CT no. 2022-502, 502-32-00). We plan to submit for publication in a major international peer-reviewed journal and present results at scientific meetings.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Laursen, Christina Cleveland Westerdahl","Lunn, Troels Haxholdt","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Therkelsen, Anne Sofie Nautrup","Varnum, Claus","Lange, Kai Henrik Wiborg","Yilmaz, Müjgan","Pedersen, Niels Anker","Kappel, Andreas","Jakobsen, Thomas","Eljaja, Salamah Belal","Thougaard, Thomas","Graungaard, Ben Kristian","Bjerno, Thomas","Beck, Jacob","Runge, Charlotte","Steiness, Joakim","Gasbjerg, Kasper Smidt","Thybo, Kasper Højgaard","Brorson, Stig","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Overgaard, Søren","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Mathiesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-086.04-792763"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Laursen, Christina Cleveland Westerdahl"],"keyword":["Adverse effects","Anti Inflammatory Agents Non Steroidal therapeutic use","Arthroplasty","Arthroplasty Replacement Hip","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee","Double Blind Method","Hip arthroplasty","Humans","Ibuprofen","Ibuprofen therapeutic use","Knee arthroplasty","NSAID","Pain Postoperative drug therapy","Pain treatment","Postoperative Complications epidemiology","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","analgesic treatment","total hip arthroplasty surgery","total knee arthroplasty surgery","unicompartment knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Embargoed Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Capio Gildhøj Private Hospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the adverse effects with ibuprofen after major orthopedic surgeries a protocol for the perisafe randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85216650191&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The PERISAFE trial has received grants from Sygesikring \\u201Cdanmark,\\u201D The Independent Research Fund Denmark, the Zealand Region, the Danish Medical Associations Research Fund, and by Skibsreder Per Henriksen, R. og Hustrus fund. The funding sources have no influence on trial design and will have no influences on data collection, analysis, or reporting."],"id":"S03-086.04-792763","identifier":[{"id":"39887674","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85216650191","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001408864300001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-05d84a4f-dd81-4eb8-bf1f-4cc4824e5104","ku-7cf01493-e179-4b5e-b23e-813a53320dfd","sdu-925b5685-305a-4bd6-bb63-2ab6a0fe008b"],"keyword":["Anti-Inflammatory Agents, Non-Steroidal/therapeutic use","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Hip","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee","Double-Blind Method","Humans","Ibuprofen/therapeutic use","Pain, Postoperative/drug therapy","Postoperative Complications/epidemiology","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","adverse effects","analgesic treatment","arthroplasty","hip arthroplasty","ibuprofen","knee arthroplasty","nsaid","pain treatment","total hip arthroplasty surgery","total knee arthroplasty surgery","unicompartment knee arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2EAF11F3012F171A4402C88D7B38943C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"ea","embargo":"2026-03-01","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"ea","embargo":"2027-01-30","type":"loc","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenha