24,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39887674"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14578","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","paperid":"e14578","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85216650191"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","capio privathospital"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-05d84a4f-dd81-4eb8-bf1f-4cc4824e5104","ku-7cf01493-e179-4b5e-b23e-813a53320dfd","sdu-925b5685-305a-4bd6-bb63-2ab6a0fe008b"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The adverse effects with ibuprofen after major orthopedic surgeries: A protocol for the PERISAFE randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-086.04-792763","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Circulating tumor DNA (ctDNA) has the potential to become a reliable biomarker for identifying minimal residual disease (MRD) and predicting recurrence in patients with non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC) following curative treatment. However, there is a lack of studies that investigate the clinical validity of ctDNA using a tumor-agnostic approach, which can provide significant clinical benefits. METHODS: We analyzed samples from 45 NSCLC patients recruited in a prospective national multicenter study, all of whom had undergone curative treatment. A total of 38 pre-treatment plasma samples and 76 post-treatment plasma samples were examined using a commercially available cancer personalized profiling by deep sequencing (CAPP-seq) strategy, and a tumor-agnostic approach. Post-treatment samples were collected at two distinct landmark time points: Follow-up 1 (0.5-4.5 months post-treatment) and Follow-up 2 (4.5-7.5 months post-treatment). RESULTS: Detectable ctDNA post-treatment was significantly associated with increased risk of tumor recurrence and shorter recurrence-free survival (RFS). Using only a single blood sample taken from Follow-up 2, we correctly identified MRD in 50% of the patients who later experienced recurrence. However, subgroup analysis further revealed that in patients treated with radiotherapy or chemoradiotherapy (CRT), ctDNA detection was significantly linked to shorter RFS in the MRD analysis from Follow-up 2, but not in the MRD analysis from Follow-up 1. CONCLUSION: These findings suggest that post-treatment ctDNA, detected using a tumor-agnostic approach, is a reliable biomarker for predicting recurrence in NSCLC patients following curative treatment. However, the optimal timing for blood sampling to detect MRD appears to depend on the type of curative treatment received.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lærke Rosenlund","Guldbrandsen, Kasper","Ahlborn, Lise Barlebo","Bloch, Martin","Skougaard, Kristin","Albrecht-Beste, Elisabeth","Nellemann, Hanne Marie","Krakauer, Martin","Gørtz, Peter Michael","Fledelius, Joan","Nielsen, Anne Lerberg","Holdgaard, Paw Christian","Nielsen, Søren Steen","Grüner, Julie Marie","Højsgaard, Anette","Petersen, Rene Horsleben","Møller, Lars Borgbjerg","Dahl, Morten","Frank, Malene Støchkel","Ehlers, Jeanette Haar","Saghir, Zaigham","Pøhl, Mette","Borissova, Svetlana","Land, Lotte Holm","Kristiansen, Charlotte","McCulloch, Tine","Mortensen, Lise Saksø","Christophersen, Malene Søby","Hilberg, Ole","Rasmussen, Thor Lind","Simonsen Schwaner, Signe Høyer","Laursen, Christian B","Bodtger, Uffe","Lonsdale, Markus Nowak","Meyer, Christian Niels","Gerke, Oke","Mortensen, Jann","Rasmussen, Torben Riis","Hjorthaug, Karin","Larsen, Klaus Richter","Meldgaard, Peter","Fischer, Barbara Malene","Sorensen, Boe Sandahl"],"cuid":["S04-098.61-822420"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Rosenlund, Lærke","Sorensen, Boe Sandahl"],"keyword":["Curative Therapy","Liquid biopsy","MRD","NSCLC","Time Factors","Tumor agnostic","ctDNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ctdna can detect minimal residual disease in curative treated non small cell lung cancer patients using a tumor agnostic approach","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lungcan.2025.108528","version":"Published Vers