","status":"u"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Unpublished"]},"sid":["aau-08305d89-03c4-4360-9bbf-77f7621c553e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Digital etnografi : At undersøge det digitale hverdagsliv","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-704726","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Several reproductive factors are associated with ovarian cancer risk but the association with survival is less clear. The main aim was to examine the impact of pre-diagnostic reproductive factors on long-term ovarian cancer survival (≥10 years). METHODS: We included all women with epithelial ovarian cancer in Denmark, 1990-2014. Information on reproductive factors and covariates were obtained from nationwide registers. Using pseudo-values, we estimated the absolute and relative 10-year survival probabilities and 95% CIs for each reproductive factor and ovarian cancer overall, restricted to serous tumors and stratified into localized and non-localized tumors. A relative survival probability >1 indicates better survival. Adjusted models considered age, diagnosis year, histology, stage, comorbidity, and income. In a sub-population sensitivity analysis, we also adjusted for residual disease. RESULTS: The cohort comprised 11,870 women. In the adjusted models, pre-diagnostic parity (relative survival probability 1.08, 95% CI 1.01 to 1.16) and endometriosis (relative survival probability 1.17, 95% CI 1.02 to 1.34) increased the likelihood of surviving ≥10 years in women with localized cancer. Previous infertility also improved the 10-year survival in women with localized ovarian cancer (relative survival probability 1.18, 95% CI 1.07 to 1.29) and in women with a non-localized tumor (relative survival probability 1.45, 95% CI 1.15 to 1.84). Pre-diagnostic pelvic inflammatory disease enhanced 10-year survival in women with localized serous (relative survival probability 1.24, 95% CI 1.03 to 1.49) and non-localized cancer (relative survival probability 1.35, 95% CI 1.04 to 1.76). Previous tubal ligation or hysterectomy were not significantly associated with 10-year survival. Adjustment for residual disease did not substantially change estimates, except for parity and pelvic inflammatory disease, where the associations disappeared. CONCLUSION: Pre-diagnostic reproductive factors, such as endometriosis or infertility, were associated with improved long-term survival. However, causality cannot be established in this observational study, and more research to confirm our findings and into potential mechanisms is warranted.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","Baandrup, Louise","Zheng, Guoqiao","Galanakis, Michael","Maltesen, Thomas","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799026"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cohort study","Long term survival","Nationwide","Ovarian cancer","reproductive factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"role of pre diagnostic reproductive factors on long term 000000000010 years or greater survival of epithelial ovarian cancer the extreme study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-799026","identifier":[{"id":"39878280","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85217271965","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1c787468-70d0-423d-bd82-a1d22956701e"],"keyword":["cohort study","long-term survival","nationwide","ovarian cancer","reproductive factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-64EF3FD8A5565269F8E8010848C98E55"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, No speciality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Gerd","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","name":"Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Louise","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","locid":"abccf449-8bed-4f98-bb4d-012134523360","name":"Baandrup, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guoqiao","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Guoqiao","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"galanakispau","last":"Galanakis","name":"Galanakis, Michael","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"maltesenpau","last":"Maltesen","name":"Maltesen, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum-Larsen","name":"Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 4","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39878280"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijgc.2024.100025","issn":["1048891X","15251438"],"issn_org":["1048891X"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Gynecological Cancer","paperid":"100025","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Gynecological Cancer","title_org":"International journal of gynecological cancer : official journal of the International Gynecological Cancer Society","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217271965"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1c787468-70d0-423d-bd82-a1d22956701e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Role of pre-diagnostic reproductive factors on long-term (10 years or greater) survival of epithelial ovarian cancer : The Extreme study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799026","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Rubber accelerators are used in the vulcanization of rubber. However, rubber accelerators for example tetraethylthiuram disulfide (TETD) and zinc diethyldithiocarbamate (ZDEC) may cause contact allergy. Concomitant reactions between ZDEC and TETD have been observed in patients which could be explained by co- or cross-reactivity. Objectives: To investigate cross-reactivity between TETD and ZDEC and vice versa. Methods: Groups of mice were sensitized with TETD or ZDEC based on reported EC3-values. Proliferation of lymphocytes were measured on day 5. To test cross-reactivity, mice were sensitized and challenged 3 weeks later with TETD or ZDEC. The inflammatory response was measured by changes in ear thickness and the proliferative response in CD4+ and CD8+ T cells in the submandibular and cervical draining lymph nodes. Results: Sensitization of mice with doses of ZDEC 3%, TETD 5.6% or TETD 16.2% induced significant increased ear thickness and proliferation of CD4+ and CD8+ T cells. Challenge with ZDEC or TETD in these groups induced significant increased ear thickness. Challenge with ZDEC in mice sensitized to TETD 5.6% or TETD 16.2% induced significant increased proliferation of CD4+ and CD8+ T cells. Conclusions: We show cross-reactivity between TETD and ZDEC. Patients sensitized to TETD or ZDEC should avoid exposure to both ZDEC and TETD.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Kursawe Larsen, Christoffer","Funch, Anders B.","Vaher, Helen","Lohmann, Rebecca Kitt Davidson","Jee, Mia Hamilton","Schwensen, Jakob F.B.","Zachariae, Claus","Svedman, Cecilia","Bergendorff, Ola","Bonefeld, Charlotte Menné","Johansen, Jeanne D"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799066"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital"],"keyword":["Allergic contact dermatitis","Contact allergy","Contact dermatitis","Dermatitis","Immunology","TETD","ZDEC","rubber accelerators"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cross reactivity between thiuram disulfides and dithiocarbamates a study of tetd and zdec using mouse models","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cod.14706","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799066","identifier":[{"id":"39340203","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11710922","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85205295505","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-215ef70e-26e0-4de8-814d-3cd8d3f794b1"],"keyword":["TETD","ZDEC","allergic contact dermatitis","contact allergy","contact dermatitis","dermatitis","dithiocarbamates","immunology","rubber accelerators","thiurams"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-559B237A8D409A50CBDF27142DCF56FE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cod.14706","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/421062764/Cross_reactivity.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Christoffer","key":"kursawelarsenpau","last":"Kursawe Larsen","name":"Kursawe Larsen, Christoffer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Boutrup","key":"funchpau","last":"Funch","locid":"42519d1e-5a5e-4802-a99a-41744f819396","name":"Funch, Anders B.","name_org":"Funch, Anders Boutrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helen","key":"vaherpau","last":"Vaher","locid":"96a33f86-6907-426c-ae91-2adc11f17272","name":"Vaher, Helen","orcid":"0000-0002-8845-0326","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rebecca Kitt Davidson","key":"lohmannpau","last":"Lohmann","name":"Lohmann, Rebecca Kitt Davidson","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mia Hamilton","key":"jeepau","last":"Jee","locid":"c7b909ea-0758-4d76-8930-9a3eaca654e7","name":"Jee, Mia Hamilton","orcid":"0000-0002-1435-4817","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jakob F.B.","key":"schwensenpau","last":"Schwensen","name":"Schwensen, Jakob F.B.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Claus","key":"zachariaepau","last":"Zachariae","locid":"ee5c26db-8a40-4753-b9da-249ffce2b771","name":"Zachariae, Claus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Cecilia","key":"svedmanpau","last":"Svedman","name":"Svedman, Cecilia","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Ola","key":"bergendorffpau","last":"Bergendorff","name":"Bergendorff, Ola","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Menné","key":"bonefeldpau","last":"Bonefeld","locid":"984200fd-eadd-4a8b-a9f0-92d4158657a8","name":"Bonefeld, Charlotte Menné","orcid":"0000-0002-0523-6229","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Jeanne D.","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"2caf86f2-1ce0-4314-835d-46bcfcf4e337","name":"Johansen, Jeanne D","name_org":"Johansen, Jeanne D.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39340203"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cod.14706","issn":["01051873","13966669"],"issn_org":["01051873"],"issue":"2","journal":"Contact Dermatitis","pages":"137-144","status":"p","title":"Contact Dermatitis","volume":"92"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205295505"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-215ef70e-26e0-4de8-814d-3cd8d3f794b1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cross-reactivity between thiuram disulfides and dithiocarbamates. A study of TETD and ZDEC using mouse models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799066","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background Umbilical outpouchings (UOs) in pigs are a multifactorial disease and little is known about effective prevention strategies and risk factors for UO development. UOs are common in Danish pigs and legislation complicates and increases the cost of keeping and raising pigs with UO. Recommendations for preventive measures exist but the scientific evidence behind the recommendations is often lacking. This study´s purpose was to investigate veterinarians’ perspectives on UO pigs´ fitness for transport, the welfare of UO pigs, the significance of UO, risk factors for the development of UO, and the management of pigs with UO. This study´s purpose was to investigate veterinarians’ perspectives on UO pigs´ fitness for transport, the welfare of UO pigs, the significance of UO, risk factors for the development of UO, and the management of pigs with UO. Results The survey received 93 complete responses from veterinarians working within porcine health management. Because of the large proportion of replies from Danish veterinarians, all reporting of results was divided among Danish and non-Danish veterinarians. There were no statistically significant differences between the two groups in the assessment of fitness for transport. Both groups mainly agreed to a series of statements regarding the significance of UO and risk factors for UO development. The management of UO was also similar across the groups except for the use of neonatal antibiotics which was used considerably more in Danish herds. Conclusions Umbilical outpouchings seem to be perceived as a challenge across pork production; affecting the welfare of the individual pig as well as the management of the entire production. There were no significant differences between Danish and non-Danish veterinarians’ assessments of fitness for transport, and almost all the veterinarians agreed that some UO pigs might need special attention and care. Most would also recommend preventive measures. Despite most respondents in this survey working under the laws of the European Union, some were unaware of legislation regarding UO pigs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Marie Louise","Larsen, Inge","Jensen, Tina Birk","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Pedersen, Ken Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-799904"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"umbilical outpouchings in pigs an international survey on fitness for transport welfare and management","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-024-00411-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-799904","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11721061","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39789622","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85218233347","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-8459071d-bdac-4190-8332-e07c2c6b52d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C83789D41ADCE67A6E149661F6257FEA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/427368432/Umbilical_outpouchings_in_pigs.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-024-00411-8","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie-Louise","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d4e731e0-3535-4e5b-92b3-857d21d575fc","name":"Hansen, Marie Louise","name_org":"Hansen, Marie-Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Inge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tina Birk","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Tina Birk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39789622"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40813-024-00411-8","issn":["20555660"],"journal":"Porcine Health Management","paperid":"4","status":"p","title":"Porcine Health Management","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85218233347"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8459071d-bdac-4190-8332-e07c2c6b52d9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Umbilical outpouchings in pigs – an international survey on fitness for transport, welfare and management","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-799904","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: High body mass index (BMI) has been linked to higher risk of complications following implant-based breast reconstruction. However, the impact of increasing BMI within the normal to overweight range (18.5–30 kg/m2) remains underexplored. We aimed to examine the association between BMI and complications and evaluate differences in risk of implant loss between patients undergoing immediate- and delayed reconstruction. Methods: Consecutive patients who underwent implant-based breast reconstruction from 2010–2023 at three plastic surgical departments were analyzed with BMI as a continuous variable. The primary outcome was implant loss stratified by immediate versus delayed reconstruction. Secondary outcomes included implant infection, seroma, hematoma, and mastectomy skin flap necrosis. All outcomes were analyzed with multivariate Cox regression. Results: We included 1847 patients (2631 breasts) with a median BMI of 23.3 kg/m2 (IQR 21.0–25.8, range 17.1–36.9). In patients undergoing immediate reconstruction, BMI was significantly associated with an increased risk of implant loss (P=0.04) but not after delayed reconstruction (P=0.22). Overall, higher BMI was significantly associated with risk of implant infection (P=0.003) and seroma (P<0.001) but not hematoma or mastectomy skin flap necrosis. The absolute risk difference for implant loss between BMI 23 kg/m² (6.2%) and 30 kg/m² (8.2%) was 2.0% (95% CI −2.9 to 6.8) for immediate reconstruction. Conclusion: The small absolute risk differences for complications in patients with BMI between 23 and 30 kg/m² suggest that patients with BMI ≤30 kg/m² should not be discouraged from implant-based breast reconstruction. However, delayed reconstruction may be a safer option for patients with higher BMI.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Weltz, Tim K.","Skautrup, Signe M.","Snog, Maria O.","Wulff, Ida K.K.","Larsen, Andreas","Hemmingsen, Mathilde N.","Jensen, Lisa T.","Andersen, Pia C.L.","Uth, Charlotte C.","Bredgaard, Rikke","Hölmich, Lisbet R.","Krezdorn, Nicco","Vester-Glowinski, Peter","Ørholt, Mathias","Herly, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811556"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Breast implant","Breast reconstruction","Implant based breast reconstruction","Implant infection","Implant loss","body mass index BMI"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"limited impact of body mass index on the risk of postoperative complications after implant based breast reconstruction a retrospective cohort study of 000000001847 patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bjps.2025.02.046","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811556","identifier":[{"id":"40174261","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105001552148","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fcddfe67-e8e7-4356-89e1-ddced091e90d"],"keyword":["Body mass index (BMI)","Breast implant","Breast reconstruction","Implant infection","Implant loss","Implant-based breast reconstruction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1A5C316520F379A5B75C10FF67C60CEF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/447752536/Limited_impact_of_body_mass_index.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bjps.2025.02.046","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark",