Telecare","pages":"1138-1151","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of Telemedicine and Telecare","volume":"31"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85194378182"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0212fb3e-21cd-4739-8e62-af5b88ed81ea","sdu-fdb67cab-11ba-45eb-9bba-3969a7aee7a9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Transforming health care : Investigating Influenzer, a novel telemedicine-supported early discharge program for patients with lower respiratory tract infection: A non-randomized feasibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-822889","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE. Previous findings indicate that patients with myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPN) exhibit elevated levels of inflammatory biomarkers and have a high prevalence of AMD. In this study, we aim to determine whether drusen and systemic inflammation in patients with MPN affect macular sensitivity in the same manner as in patients with AMD. METHODS. The study was conducted as a prospective cross-sectional study. A total of 139 study eyes of 71 patients were included in this study. We measured macular sensitivity using microperimetry and extracted blood samples to evaluate systemic inflammation markers. RESULTS. Multilevel linear mixed-effect analysis did not show any difference in macular sensitivity when comparing eyes of MPN patients with AMD to those without drusen (β = −0.254, P = 0.657). However, higher levels of the complement system fragment C5a were significantly correlated with decreased total macular sensitivity (β = −0.561, P = 0.027), irrespective of the presence of drusen. CONCLUSIONS. We found that high levels of the systemic inflammation marker C5a are associated with reduced macular sensitivity, regardless of the presence of visible degenerative changes in the macular area. These findings suggest an early contribution of the complement system to macular sensitivity.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Gotfredsen, Kathrine","Abou Taha, Andreas","Liisborg, Charlotte","Nielsen, Marie Krogh","Larsen, Morten Kranker","Skov, Vibe","Kjær, Lasse","Hasselbalch, Hans Karl","Sørensen, Torben Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-803232"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Gotfredsen, Kathrine"],"keyword":["Age related macular degeneration","Complement","Microperimetry","Myeloproliferative neoplasms","Systemic inflammation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high levels of c000000000005a are associated with reduced macular sensitivity in patients with myeloproliferative neoplasms","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.66.2.41","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-803232","identifier":[{"id":"39946135","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85217971014","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11827620","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-fad2241b-2c70-432f-9b61-19b9950ba349"],"keyword":["age-related macular degeneration","complement","microperimetry","myeloproliferative neoplasms","systemic inflammation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B88DD22647CA33752B159332C5823D18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1167/iovs.66.2.41","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/284408759/i1552-5783-66-2-41_1739438574.42086.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Ophthalmology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":