{"abstract":"Newcastle disease, a notifiable avian disease, is caused by virulent avian paramyxovirus 1 (APMV-1). In this study, we screened samples collected through the active and passive surveillance for avian influenza virus in Denmark between 2014 and 2022 for APMV-1, detecting 32 APMV-1 in wild and commercial waterfowl. Phylogenetic analysis identified them as class I genotype 1.2 and class II genotype I.2 viruses, all with monobasic fusion (F) cleavage sites (112ERQERL117 and 112GKQGRL117), characterizing them as lentogenic. Nucleotide and amino acid similarities ranged from 95 to 99.8% and 98.2 to 100% for class I viruses and 95.6–99.8% and 98.7–100% for class II viruses. Genetic comparisons of F genes showed divergence from vaccine strains, ruling out vaccine spillover. Selection analysis revealed neutral and negative selection pressures, suggesting limited adaptive evolution. These findings indicate that lentogenic APMV-1 circulated in Denmark from 2014 to 2022 without strong selection pressures driving significant genetic changes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Martiny, Karen","Liang, Yuan","Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Larsen, Lars Erik","Christensen, Jens Peter","Hjulsager, Charlotte K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809736"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lentogenic avian paramyxovirus 000000000001 of both class i and class ii are circulating in danish wild and commercial waterfowl","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44298-025-00108-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809736","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11971311","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40295831","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-510ed38d-6ae0-41e1-84e4-ea72534e1aae"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F442FADA72A0EF2FF465931A5EDAAC7C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44298-025-00108-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/460420922/Lentogenic_avian_paramyxovirus_1_of_both_class_I_and_class_II_are_circulating_in_danish_wild_and_commercial_waterfowl.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Karen","key":"martinypau","last":"Martiny","locid":"2f168c92-c78b-43da-944e-872121b1cc06","name":"Martiny, Karen","orcid":"0000-0002-7948-1067","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuan","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","locid":"15fec07b-8b15-410c-9db2-b2b7fda77736","name":"Liang, Yuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens P.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"939fd558-e675-4e66-9601-2a336ebfd5a9","name":"Christensen, Jens Peter","name_org":"Christensen, Jens P.","orcid":"0000-0002-6430-9010","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte K.","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40295831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s44298-025-00108-x","issn":["29481767"],"journal":"npj Viruses","paperid":"26","status":"p","title":"npj Viruses","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-510ed38d-6ae0-41e1-84e4-ea72534e1aae"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lentogenic avian paramyxovirus 1 of both class I and class II are circulating in Danish wild and commercial waterfowl","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809736","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: The mechanisms behind the association between adult offspring's socioeconomic position and their parents' mortality are not well understood. This study investigates lifestyle-related diseases as a potential mediating pathway between adult offspring's education and parental mortality. Methods: This nationwide register-based cohort study consists of 963,742 older adults aged 65 years between 2000 and 2018. Lifestyle-related diseases were measured between 60 and 65 years and those with prior lifestyle-related diseases were excluded. Natural Effect Models were performed to assess potential mediation through lifestyle-related diseases of the association between offspring's education and parental mortality measured by additive hazard estimates with 95% confidence intervals (CIs). Results: Between 60 and 65 years, 150,501 (15.6%) older adults were diagnosed with lifestyle-related diseases and 149,647 (15.5%) died during follow-up. Compared with having offspring with long education, short education was associated with 631 (95% CI: 555; 707) and 581 (95% CI: 525; 638) additional deaths per 100,000 person-years for women and men, respectively, of which 15.4% (95% CI: 9.0; 21.6) and 16.8% (95% CI: 14.6; 18.9) were mediated by lifestyle-related diseases. The corresponding numbers for medium education were 276 (95% CI: 205; 347) and 299 (95% CI: 255; 343) with 26.2% (95% CI: 12.0; 40.6) and 27.6% (95% CI: 25.1; 31.8) mediated by lifestyle-related diseases. Conclusions: Lifestyle-related diseases accounted for 15-28% of the association between offspring's education and parental mortality for both men and women.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Sloth, Mathilde Marie Brünnich","Neble Larsen, Emma","Mathisen, Jimmi","Nilsson, Charlotte Juul","Osler, Merete","Jørgensen, Terese Sara Høj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-810036"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adult offspring s education and parental mortality a nationwide cohort study of the mediating role of lifestyle related diseases","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-810036","identifier":[{"id":"38523257","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105003549801","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6c76992d-e390-4632-bbbe-bba4dfdecf0a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-ED97BFF11D119FBE4CBCB6183EB7EE30"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mathilde M B","key":"slothpau","last":"Sloth","locid":"0ba0a0a4-eda3-4067-a5b0-a4c7104b1b19","name":"Sloth, Mathilde Marie Brünnich","name_org":"Sloth, Mathilde M B","orcid":"0000-0003-2261-8779","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Emma","key":"neblelarsenpau","last":"Neble Larsen","locid":"88f57d3a-31ac-451d-99b2-88c8966ec86d","name":"Neble Larsen, Emma","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jimmi","key":"mathisenpau","last":