{"abstract":"Home sampling of saliva is noninvasive, easy, and convenient, especially for multiple sampling. Such samples are therefore appropriate for the measurement of melatonin, a biomarker for circadian dysregulation. However, home sampling is restricted by access to appropriate storage conditions. This study, therefore, evaluated the effect of common storage conditions on the stability of melatonin in synthetic fiber swabs employed for home sampling. Saliva was provided by healthy volunteers during daytime, pooled and subsequently divided into fractions, each spiked with different amounts of melatonin. Synthetic fiber swabs were allowed to accumulate saliva from these fractions followed by storage at room temperature, 4 °C or −20 °C for 24, 48 or 72 h. The melatonin levels were analyzed employing a commercial ELISA assay. Differences in concentrations at each storage condition were evaluated with a two-way repeated measures ANOVA followed by a Tukey multiple comparison test. Samples were significantly more stable at −20 °C compared to room temperature and 4 °C, irrespective of the storage duration. However, no significant decrease from baseline was observed for samples stored at either 4 °C or −20 °C after 72 h. In comparison, a significant decrease was observed at room temperature after just 24 h. In conclusion, storage at −20 °C may be considered the gold standard for synthetic fiber swabs for quantification of salivary melatonin. However, storage at 4 °C ensures stability for 72 h while also ensuring convenience for home sampling. It is therefore our recommendation that such home samples are refrigerated, transported cold and centrifuged within 72 h of collection.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Anton, Jennifer","Larsen, Charlotte S.","Gudmundsson, Majken","Bak, Lasse Kristoffer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-819907"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomarkers","Circadian rhythm","Enzyme Linked Immunosorbent Assay","Melatonin","Saliva"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of storage conditions on the stability of salivary melatonin in synthetic fiber swabs for home sampling","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00365513.2025.2487987","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-819907","identifier":[{"id":"40208215","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105002592080","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ae42a96d-8627-4403-88cd-ecc8200dd2ad"],"keyword":["Melatonin","biomarkers","circadian rhythm","enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay","saliva"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-93FB3C56576C1C3B1FB2B48008AFB97E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/452220773/The_effects_of_storage_conditions_on_the_stability_of_salivary_melatonin_in_synthetic_fiber_swabs_for_home_sampling.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00365513.2025.2487987","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy, Teaching"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jennifer","key":"antonpau","last":"Anton","locid":"da00ea08-6878-4337-a9de-455828eb4509","name":"Anton, Jennifer","orcid":"0000-0001-8466-7205","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Charlotte S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Majken","key":"gudmundssonpau","last":"Gudmundsson","name":"Gudmundsson, Majken","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lasse K.","key":"bakpau","last":"Bak","locid":"6e8b5c5f-965a-4702-90a2-bcf49dc53fc1","name":"Bak, Lasse Kristoffer","name_org":"Bak, Lasse K.","orcid":"0000-0003-0784-7864","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40208215"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365513.2025.2487987","issn":["00365513","0085591X"],"issn_org":["00365513"],"issue":"3","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","pages":"180-183","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical & Laboratory Investigation","title_org":"Scandinavian Journal of Clinical and Laboratory Investigation","volume":"85"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002592080"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ae42a96d-8627-4403-88cd-ecc8200dd2ad"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of storage conditions on the stability of salivary melatonin in synthetic fiber swabs for home sampling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-819907","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aim: Homecare for neonates has advanced, but combative analysis of contact methods remains unexplored. The aim was to identify predictors of readmission during homecare and to compare home visit, telemedicine or outpatient visit. Methods: This retrospective study included infants receiving homecare from 1 January 2015 to 31 December 2022. Data were obtained from local databases from six neonatal units in Denmark. The medical records of readmitted infants were reviewed. The main outcome were causes and predictors of readmission during homecare. The secondary outcome was exclusive breastfeeding at discharge. Results: The cohort consisted of 4827 infants (boys = 54.0%). The rate of unplanned readmissions was 4.6%. A gestational age (GA) <32 weeks (p-value <0.01) or bronchopulmonary dysplasia (BPD) (p-value <0.01) were predictors of readmission. There was no difference in unplanned readmissions based on contact method (p-value = 0.46 for telemedicine, p-value = 0.11 for outpatient visit). The overall exclusive breastfeeding rate at discharge from homecare was 64.1%. Conclusion: Homecare can be provided for preterm and term infants while establishing oral feeding, with caution on infants with a GA < 32 or BPD. All types of contact methods during homecare investigated can be provided equally in relation to readmission and exclusive breastfeeding.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rosenbaek, Charlotte Hoeyer","Zachariassen, Gitte","Hoest, Bente","Hahn, Gitte Holst","Larsen, Joan Neergaard","Salmonsen, Tenna Gladbo","Horskjaer, Malene","Holm, Kristina Garne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-821212"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rosenbaek, Charlotte Hoeyer"],"keyword":["Breast Feeding statistics numerical data","Breastfeeding","Denmark","Female","Gestational Age","Home Care Services statistics numerical data","Homecare","Humans","Infant Newborn","Infant Premature","Male","Patient Readmission statistics numerical data","Preterm infants","Readmission","Retrospective Studies","neonatal unit"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low readmission rates during neonatal homecare gestational age and bronchopulmonary dysplasia as key predictors","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.17576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-821212","identifier":[{"id":"39775953","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12066913","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85214398210","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-48569a84-b660-4b9f-90db-64ef6c7b6262"],"keyword":["Breast Feeding/statistics & numerical data","Bronchopulmonary Dysplasia/therapy","Denmark","Female","Gestational Age","Home Care Services/statistics & numerical data","Humans","Infant, Newborn","Infant, Premature","Male","Patient Readmission/statistics & numerical data","Retrospective Studies","breastfeeding","homecare","neonatal unit","preterm infants","readmission"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-6-B20EB26378A88ED5E43B3BE8CE16B9AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290896299/Acta_Paediatrica_-_2025_-_Rosenbaek_-_Low_readmission_rates_during_neonatal_homecare_Gestational_age_and_bronchopulmonary.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.17576","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Hoeyer","key":"rosenbaekpau","last":"Rosenbaek","locid":"8b846e0c-9c12-40cb-b29f-8ac01669784c","name":"Rosenbaek, Charlotte Hoeyer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"zachariassenpau","last":"Zachariassen","locid":"8635ed4a-eab3-41b6-adc3-a54ff1f0ce67","name":"Zachariassen, Gitte","orcid":"0000-0003-4440-2362","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bente","key":"hoestpau","last":"Hoest","name":"Hoest, Bente","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Holst","key":"hahnpau","last":"Hahn","name":"Hahn, Gitte Holst","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Joan Neergaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Joan Neergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tenna Gladbo","key":"salmonsenpau","last":"Salmonsen","name":"Salmonsen, Tenna Gladbo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene","key":"horskjaerpau","last":"Horskjaer","name":"Horskjaer, Malene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina Garne","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"2393dc89-d60b-4c86-a140-60e6deeb7dab","name":"Holm, Kristina Garne","orcid":"0000-0002-2730-1167","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39775953"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apa.17576","issn":["08035253","08035326"],"issn_org":["08035253"],"issue":"6","journal":"Acta Paediatrica","pages":"1342-1351","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Acta Paediatrica","title_org":"Acta Paediatrica, International Journal of Paediatrics","volume":"114"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214398210"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-48569a84-b660-4b9f-90db-64ef6c7b6262"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Low readmission rates during neonatal homecare : Gestational age and bronchopulmonary dysplasia as key predictors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-821212","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Denne artikel undersøger, hvordan forskningsdeltagelse i hverdagsliv og fællesskaber blandt mennesker, som hjælpesystemerne kategoriserer som i udsathed kan skabe nuanceret viden om oplevelser og erfaringer med hjælpesystemer. Med udgangspunkt i deltagerobservation som metodisk greb og gennem længerevarende feltarbejde i tre forskellige forskningsprojekter, stilles der skarpt på forskernes deltagerpositioner og deltagelse som skabende for både empiri og analyse. Artiklen viser, hvordan deltagerobservation – forstået som både sanselig, situativ og relationel praksis – kan bidrage til tykke beskrivelser, der rummer erfaringer og perspektiver, som ikke altid kan indfanges gennem interview eller sprog alene. Gennem eksempler fra feltarbejdet belyses forskellige deltagelsespositioner, og hvordan disse påvirker relationer, observationer og fortolkninger. Artiklen argumenterer for, at deltagerobservation ikke blot er en metode til dataindsamling, men også en måde at forstyrre og nuancere gængse forståelser i forsknings- og hjælpesystemer. Derved bliver det muligt at indfange og påvirke betydningsfulde indsigter, der kan kvalificere fremtidig socialfaglig praksis.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Løvstad, Charlotte Vange","Nørgaard, Astrid Kidde Larsen","Jørgensen, Gert Hoberg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-822070"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co research","Feltarbejde","Forskningsmetode","Socialt arbejde og sociale forhold","feltvandring","medforskning"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvordan ser hverdagslivet ud fra din side at vandre med intuitivt og situativt","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/site.v1i4.158007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-822070","ids":["via-44b97d03-e508-4dab-b1bf-b563dc7ec679"],"keyword":["Socialt arbejde og sociale forhold","co-research","feltarbejde","feltvandring","forskningsmetode","intuitivt","medforskning","positioner i feltarbejde","roller i feltarbejde","situativt","videnskab og Hjælp"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69323183D0764DF6FC09971C717110CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/site/article/view/158007/200164","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/site.v1i4.158007","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for pædagogik og dannelse, Forsk.center for pædagogik og deltagelse"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Vange","key":"løvstadpau","last":"Løvstad","locid":"9f3cb2da-29ee-41cc-b40c-e0b923987633","name":"Løvstad, Charlotte Vange","orcid":"0000-0001-6428-4258","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid Kidde Larsen","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"55bd85c3-5b83-438e-91db-1246474d0cc7","name":"Nørgaard, Astrid Kidde Larsen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gert Hoberg","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"6141af77-b58a-4cf4-8559-63e9253e5ec0","name":"Jørgensen, Gert Hoberg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/site.v1i4.158007","issn":["27949427"],"issue":"4","journal":"Tidsskrift for Social Innovation & Transformativ Entreprenørska