{"abstract":"The Danish healthcare system is currently undergoing a transformation towards increased use of virtual healthcare services. In this review, we propose a structured risk-stratified model to delineate the differences between homecare, homemonitoring, and hospital-at-home, while discussing their current status and addressing barriers hindering the widespread adoption and scaling of home-based care incl. technological limitations, regulatory complexities, and cultural considerations. We advocate for establishing a national central support function to expedite the shift towards home-based care.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Fischer, Thea Kølsen","Sandreva, Tatjana","Larsen, Maria Normand","Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","Lund Christensen, Maria","Svane, Jeff Kirk","Kidholm, Kristian","Demuth von Sydow, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-084.91-804534"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Fischer, Thea Kølsen"],"keyword":["Denmark","Home Care Services","Home Care Services Hospital Based","Humans","Telemedicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behandling monitorering og indlæggelse i hjemmet","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V02240158","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-084.91-804534","identifier":[{"id":"39323246","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85204941033","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-aa365aba-7612-4006-bde2-23cd7c8afb2d","sdu-1636bcc6-c214-4b7c-b752-2eeb1ca9ca20"],"keyword":["Denmark","Home Care Services","Home Care Services, Hospital-Based","Humans","Telemedicine"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-22A3C6C3EF0D793E74B4FAB8BA131CBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/281833222/V02240158_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/V02240158","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446775077/V02240158_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Global Health Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of CIMT - Centre for Innovative Medical Technology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Thea Kølsen","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"97c4bf8d-8bd1-470b-8e0b-91eb4faf7703","name":"Fischer, Thea K.","name_org":"Fischer, Thea Kølsen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tatjana","key":"sandrevapau","last":"Sandreva","name":"Sandreva, Tatjana","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Normand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Maria Normand","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Kjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"cc76ec55-14ab-429b-ac2e-5ec2cd6ccc04","name":"Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-7405-4373","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thyge Lynghøj","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"lundchristensenpau","last":"Lund Christensen","name":"Lund Christensen, Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maria Lund","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Maria Lund","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeff Kirk","key":"svanepau","last":"Svane","name":"Svane, Jeff Kirk","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian","key":"kidholmpau","last":"Kidholm","locid":"38a02804-c94a-4706-b5a4-de0795e5970e","name":"Kidholm, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-1037-6514","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"demuthvonsydowpau","last":"Demuth von Sydow","name":"Demuth von Sydow, Charlotte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Demuth","key":"vonsydowpau","last":"von Sydow","name":"von Sydow, Charlotte Demuth","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39323246"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/v02240158","issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"2","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","paperid":"V02240158","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"187"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-aa365aba-7612-4006-bde2-23cd7c8afb2d","sdu-1636bcc6-c214-4b7c-b752-2eeb1ca9ca20"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Behandling, monitorering og indlæggelse i hjemmet","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.91-804534","year":2025,"yearsub":2025}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose: The NIELS trial will examine if inhomogeneous dose-escalated radiotherapy up to a mean dose of 80 Gy in 40 fractions (fx), twice-daily delivered (BID), for patients with limited disease small cell lung cancer can improve overall survival. Because of the inherent risks of dose-escalation, pre-trial QA is particularly important. This study aims to examine the feasibility of the NIELS trial planning approach in a multicenter setting. Materials and methods: The NIELS trial will randomize patients between standard dose radiotherapy (60 Gy/40fx BID) and inhomogeneous dose-escalated radiotherapy (up to 80 Gy/40fx BID). Five representative patient cases were distributed to seven Nordic centers for pre-trial QA planning of a standard and an escalated dose plan. Targets for escalation were primary tumor (GTVp) and involved lymph nodes (GTVn). We evaluated inter-center variation in achievable dose-escalation and doses to organs at risk (OAR). Results: All targets could be escalated beyond the standard dose, with a median mean dose of 79.6 Gy [76.9–81.0] and 75.8 Gy [68.3–81.1] for GTVp and GTVn. Some targets could not be fully escalated due to OAR proximity. Three separate breaches of mandatory OAR constraints were observed in 35 escalated dose plans. There was a statistical difference in mean lung dose between standard and escalated plans, though clinically small, with a median inter-patient difference of 0.3 Gy. There were no differences in mean doses to the heart and esophagus. Conclusion: Inhomogeneous dose-escalation as planned in the NIELS trial is feasible, and the dose-escalation can be performed respecting the OAR constraints in a multi-center setting.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Linde, Sara","Møller, Ditte Sloth","Linaa, Mai Britt","Appelt, Ane","Almhagen, Erik","Hofland, Kenneth F.","Knap, Marianne Marquard","Kristiansen, Charlotte","Land, Lotte H.","Larsen, Christina","Levin, Nina","Lindberg, Karin","Lund, Mikkel D.","Merring-Mikkelsen, Lars","Nielsen, Tine B.","Ottosson, Wiviann","Persson, Gitte F.","Sand, Hella M.B.","Suppli, Morten H.","Villegas, Fernanda","Schmidt, Hjørdis Hjalting","Szejniuk, Weronika M.","Hoffmann, Lone"],"cuid":["S04-100.00-822391"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Linde, Sara"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","St. Olav University Hospital","St. Olavs Hospital - University Hospital Trondheim","St. Olavs University Hospital (Trondheim)","University of Leeds"],"keyword":["Dose Fractionation","Quality assurance","Radiotherapy","Radiotherapy Dosage","Radiotherapy planning","Small cell"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"design and pre trial dose planning quality assurance of the nordic trial of inhomogeneous dose escalated radiotherapy for patients with limited disease small cell lung cancer niels","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.radonc.2025.110946","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-100.00-822391","identifier":[{"id":"40409366","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005944990","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-93fc08a1-9b03-4c3e-8edd-74e2a112b8a2","au-04fd1847-c61