{"abstract":"The content of phenolic compounds in chocolate depends on the processing of the cocoa from bean to bar. The aim of this study was to determine the fate of phenolic compounds and theobromine in cocoa beans during roasting at different temperatures. Based on a screening of 12 cocoa bean sorts, three beans (NM, NCC, and NB) with initial high total phenolic content (TPC) were selected for the roasting trial (100 and 150°C up to 20 min). The concentration of three major flavonoids ((−)-catechin, (−)-epicatechin and procyanidin B2) and one methylxanthine (theobromine) were evaluated in both raw and roasted beans. Results showed changes in the concentration of flavonoids and theobromine during roasting. Roasting at 150°C for 15 min was optimal for maintaining high flavonoid levels while reducing theobromine levels. However, sensory evaluation on final product is needed to confirm whether the suggested roasting condition would also result in a final product with pleasant sensory properties.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hermund, Ditte Baun","Larsen, Louise Kirstein","Trangbæk, Sara Riegels","Madsen, Quoc-Khanh Rose-Marie Therese","Sørensen, Ann-Dorit Moltke","Kaya, Jacob","Jacobsen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789447"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hermund, Ditte Baun"],"keyword":["Antioxidants","Food processing","Phenolic compounds","Quality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Mellow Chocolate"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fate of flavonoids and theobromine in cocoa beans during roasting effect of time and temperature","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/aocs.12853","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-789447","identifier":[{"id":"85193926400","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e8d8fa40-cd9c-4c92-b883-a8969349afbc"],"keyword":["Antioxidants","Food processing","Phenolic compounds","Quality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6FA96E745EC3B3177B0D5EE70AD3DEE8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386884134/J_Americ_Oil_Chem_Soc_-_2024_-_Hermund_-_Fate_of_flavonoids_and_theobromine_in_cocoa_beans_during_roasting_Effect_of_time_2_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/aocs.12853","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Bioactives – Analysis and Application"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Mellow Chocolate"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ditte B.","key":"hermundpau","last":"Hermund","locid":"04c563e9-6f7b-4599-b51f-8b231fbbe3e5","name":"Hermund, Ditte Baun","name_org":"Hermund, Ditte B.","orcid":"0000-0002-8265-2867","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise Kirstein","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Louise Kirstein","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Riegels","key":"trangbækpau","last":"Trangbæk","name":"Trangbæk, Sara Riegels","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Quoc-Khanh Rose-Marie Therese","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Quoc-Khanh Rose-Marie Therese","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ann-Dorit Moltke","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"dd7b7dae-3650-43cb-850c-ac4189bf0125","name":"Sørensen, Ann-Dorit Moltke","orcid":"0000-0001-9349-1221","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"kayapau","last":"Kaya","name":"Kaya, Jacob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"36158d7c-a1ce-4b85-a240-93c6218ea6be","name":"Jacobsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3540-9669","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/aocs.12853","issn":["0003021X","15589331"],"issn_org":["0003021X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of the American Oil Chemists' Society","pages":"35-45","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Oil Chemists' Society","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85193926400"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e8d8fa40-cd9c-4c92-b883-a8969349afbc"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fate of flavonoids and theobromine in cocoa beans during roasting : Effect of time and temperature","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789447","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose — Periprosthetic knee fractures (PPKFs) can be a serious complication after total knee arthroplasty (TKA). We aimed to compare patient-reported outcome (PRO) scores reported between 1 and 4 years after PPKF with a matched uncomplicated TKA control group. Methods — This nationwide cross-sectional matched cohort study included 372 TKA patients with a PPKF occur-ring from 2019 to 2022 and a control group of 878 uncomplicated TKA patients matched by age, time since TKA, and sex. The study population was derived from the Danish National Patient Register. The patients received questionnaires regarding knee function, quality of life, pain and satisfaction in 2023. The questionnaires included Oxford Knee Score (OKS), the Forgotten Joint Score (FJS), and the EQ-5D-5L Index. Results — The response rate was 48%. Mean OKS was 7 (confidence interval [CI] 5–9) points lower after a PPKF with a score of 30 (standard deviation [SD] 11) in the PPKF group vs 37 (SD 11) in the control group. The FJS was 13 (CI 7–19) points lower after a PPKF with a score of 50 (SD 30) in the PPKF group vs 63 (SD 30) in the control group. Mean EQ-5D-5L Index scores were 0.17 (CI 0.12–0.22) lower after a PPKF with a score of 0.68 (SD 0.25) in the PPKF group vs 0.85 (SD 0.25) in the control group. Additional analysis of patients who completed PROMs 1–2 years compared with 3–4 years after PPKF showed better PRO scores after 3–4 years with an OKS of 32 (SD 12) vs 27 (SD 12), FJS 55 (SD 32) vs 43 (SD 32), and EQ-5D-5L Index of 0.74 (SD 0.34) vs 0.60 (SD 0.34). Conclusion — Following PPKF, patients reported worse knee function, more pain, lower satisfaction, and poorer quality of life than those with uncomplicated TKAs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Risager, Stefan Kastalag","Viberg, Bjarke","Abrahamsen, Charlotte","Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Odgaard, Anders","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-803147"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Risager, Stefan Kastalag"],"keyword":["Arthroplasty","Fractures","Knee","Osteoarthrosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient reported outcome 000000000001 to 000000000004 years after periprosthetic knee fracture a nationwide cross sectional matched study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2025.43083","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-803147","identifier":[{"id":"40029097","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11868926","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"86000328374","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f02dd58b-c0bf-47cf-b853-905da328090c"],"keyword":["Arthroplasty","Fractures","Knee","Osteoarthrosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1C1E33320A1ABBEBAE5098BD315ABD36"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/285990427/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2025.43083","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan Kastalag","key":"risagerpau","last":"Risager","locid":"dc21700f-7caf-43ac-901c-5fb66ad42684","name":"Risager, Stefan Kastalag","orcid":"0000-0001-8157-7001","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarke","key":"vibergpau","last":"Viberg","locid":"8cb06beb-80dd-4b2f-bcd7-eb9cba7b9da6","name":"Viberg, Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0001-5169-4282","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Skov","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"22215dd3-464e-4e62-b19f-71a71e0e1e65","name":"Abrahamsen, Charlotte","name_org":"Abrahamsen, Charlotte Skov","orcid":"0000-0002-3700-289X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Bollerup","key":"arndtpau","last":"Arndt","locid":"a2513ef2-9214-48ee-b84f-bea6ef1717ac","name":"Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","orcid":"0000-0001-8258-7922","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40029097"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/17453674.2025.43083","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"209-216","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","volume":"96"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-86000328374"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-f02dd58b-c0bf-47cf-b853-905da328090c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patient-reported outcome 1 to 4 years after periprosthetic knee fracture : a nationwide cross-sectional matched study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-803147","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In 2018, a single detection of a novel reassortant swine influenza A virus (swIAV) was made in Denmark. The hemagglutinin (HA) of the virus was from the H1N1 pandemic 2009 (H1N1pdm09) lineage and the neuraminidase (NA) from the H1N1 Eurasian avian-like swine lineage (H1N1av). By 2022, the novel reassortant virus (H1pdm09N1av) constituted 27% of swIAVs identified through the Danish passive swIAV surveillance program. Sequencing detected two H1pdm09N1av genotypes; Genotype 1 contained an entire internal gene cassette of H1N1pdm09 origin, Genotype 2 differed by carrying an NS gene segment of H1N1av origin. The internal gene cassette of Genotype 2 became increasingly dominant, not only in the H1pdm09N1av population, but also in other Danish enzootic swIAV subtypes. Phylogenetic analysis of the HA genes from H1pdm09N1av viruses revealed a monophyletic source, a higher substitution rate compared to other H1N1pdm09 viruses and genetic differences with human seasonal and other swine adapted H1N1pdm09 viruses. Correspondingly, H1pdm09N1av viruses were antigenically distinct from human H1N1pdm09 vaccine viruses. Both H1pdm09N1av genotypes transmitted between ferrets by direct contact, but only Genotype 1 was capable of efficient aerosol transmission. The rapid spread of H1pdm09N1av viruses in Danish swine herds is concerning for swine and human health. Their zoonotic threat is highlighted by the limited pre-existing immunity observed in the human population, aerosol transmission in ferrets and the finding that the internal gene cassette of Genotype 2 was present in the first two zoonotic influenza infections ever detected in Denmark.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia","George, Sophie","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Trebbien, Ramona","Krog, Jesper Schak","Ciucani, Marta Maria","Langerhuus, Sine Nygaard","DeBeauchamp, Jennifer","Crumpton, Jeri Carol","Hibler, Taylor","Webby, Richard J.","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818971"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","St. Jude Children’s Research Hospital"],"keyword":["Influenza A virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-AAF","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rapid surge of reassortant a h000000000001n000000000001 influenza viruses in danish swine and their zoonotic potential","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/22221751.2025.2466686","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818971","identifier":[{"id":"85219500018","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39945729","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11849018","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-44168ac8-9b36-4c2d-9eda-52ae009e4634"],"keyword":["H1pdm09N1av","Influenza A virus","novel reassortant virus","swine influenza surveillance","zoonotic potential"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-99CE8A9155EC789526708E731CF1A634"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/454320335/Rapid_surge_of_reassortant_A_H1N1_influenza_viruses_in_Danish_swine_and_their_zoonotic_potential.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/22221751.2025.2466686","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish agriculture food council","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-AAF","l3nl":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","l3nn":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","namevar":["Danish Agriculture & Food Council"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-AAF","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"st jude children s research hospital","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"St. Jude Children’s Research Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sophie","key":"georgepau","last":"George","locid":"40656a28-0c15-447d-9c3d-75697fd23b6b","name":"George, Sophie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marta Maria","key":"ciucanipau","last":"Ciucani","name":"Ciucani, Marta Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Sine Nygaard","key":"langerhuuspau","last":"Langerhuus","name":"Langerhuus, Sine Nygaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jennifer","key":"debeauchamppau","last":"DeBeauchamp","name":"DeBeauchamp, Jennifer","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jeri Carol","key":"crumptonpau","last":"Crumpton","name":"Crumpton, Jeri Carol","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Taylor","key":"hiblerpau","last":"Hibler","name":"Hibler, Taylor","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Richard J.","key":"webbypau","last":"Webby","name":"Webby, Richard J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39945729"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/22221751.2025.2466686","issn":["22221751"],"issue":"1","journal":"Emerging Microbes and Infections","paperid":"2466686","status":"p","title":"Emerging Microbes and Infections","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85219500018"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Danish Agriculture & Food Council","Governmental Institutions","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-44168ac8-9b36-4c2d-9eda-52ae009e4634"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Rapid surge of reassortant A(H1N1) influenza viruses in Danish swine and their zoonotic potential","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818971","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Forskningsprojektet peger samlet set på, at det vi kalder den ”fleksible fokuserede fritidspædagogiske faglighed” repræsenterer nogle veje at gå i det fritidspædagogiske arbejde, som handler om udvikling af børns adgang til børnefællesskaber og bidrag til udvikling af fælles aktiviteter snarere end individorienterede indsatser, der har til formål at kompensere for fx børns sociale baggrund. Dermed kobler vi en optagethed af almen pædagogisk faglighed og ulighed i børnelivet. I stedet for alene at rette blikket mod det enkelte barns livshistoriske ”rygsæk”, tager fritidspædagogen pædagogisk udgangspunkt i en konkret udforskning og analyse af et ”nu-og-her” for at finde frem til, hvad det er for konkrete problemer forskellige børn bakser med, hvilke udfordrende betingelser, der har betydning her – og hvilke konkrete muligheder, der kan skabes for at udvikle løsninger, der er bæredygtige for både de enkelte børn, børnefællesskaberne og den samlede praksis på tværs af skole og SFO. Denne særlige fritidspædagogiske faglighed retter altså et udforskende blik mod, hvad der er på spil i de aktuelle børnefællesskaber, hvilke betingelser dette stiller for forskellige børns deltagelse, og hvordan man pædagogisk kan skabe deltagelsesmuligheder. Projektet peger desuden på, at denne faglige tilgang kan komme under pres, når der er tids- og ressourcemæssig knaphed. Når den nødvendige kollektive og tværfaglige udforskning og tilrettelæggelsesmæssige fleksibilitet begrænses, stiger risikoen for individuel problemudpegning og deraf følgende indskrænkning af nogle børns deltagelsesmuligheder og adgang til nødvendige sociale ressourcer. På baggrund af projektets samlede materiale identificeres en række temaer, der kendetegner fritidspædagogisk faglighed og dens betingelser i forhold til at arbejde med ulighedsproblematikker.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte","Mardahl-Hansen, Tilde","Sylvest-Berg, Rebekka"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-820793"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Børneperspektiver","Fritidspædagogik","Situeret ulighed"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fritidspædagogik og situeret ulighed viden om hvordan pædagogisk faglighed skaber deltagelsesmuligheder for børn på tværs af fritid og skole","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://bupl.dk/sites/default/files/2025-05/Fritidsp%C3%A6dagogik%20og%20situeret%20ulighed.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-820793","ids":["ruc-5eb8af03-8ff2-4479-9f22-a86d19664868"],"keyword":["Børneperspektiver","Fritidspædagogik","Situeret ulighed"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5BC9A707218E897DA53A2C50F1A374FF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://bupl.dk/sites/default/files/2025-05/Fritidsp%C3%A6dagogik%20og%20situeret%20ulighed.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, The Danish Centre for Research in Early Childhood Education and Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Tilde","key":"mardahlhansenpau","last":"Mardahl-Hansen","locid":"681a2367-eec3-469b-a925-ae6720df6462","name":"Mardahl-Hansen, Tilde","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Rebekka","key":"sylvestbergpau","last":"Sylvest-Berg","locid":"e37ac92c-7c3f-48ed-9a09-cc7ae9503eab","name":"Sylvest-Berg, Rebekka","orcid":"0009-0007-4958-9361","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"34","publisher":"Roskilde Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-5eb8af03-8ff2-4479-9f22-a86d19664868"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Fritidspædagogik og Situeret Ulighed : Viden om hvordan pædagogisk faglighed skaber deltagelsesmuligheder for børn på tværs af fritid og skole","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-820793","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The assessment of polysaccharide responsiveness via vaccination is pivotal in the evaluation of patients for primary immunodeficiency. However, the applicability of current guidelines provided by the American Academy of Allergy, Asthma & Immunology (AAAAI) has been subject to scrutiny. METHODS: We conducted a prospective study involving 120 healthy Danish adult blood donors. Antibodies targeting pneumococcal capsular polysaccharide serotypes were quantified using a multianalyte bead immunoassay before and four to eight weeks post-vaccination. Polysaccharide responsiveness in donors was assessed according to AAAAI guidelines. RESULTS: Remarkably, only a minority of participants (2.5%) demonstrated a normal polysaccharide response per AAAAI criteria. This finding prompted us to advocate for an alternative approach based on percentile rankings relative to a reference population. Polysaccharide Responsiveness Percentile (PRP) was not significantly associated with age, sex, vaccine batch, or the duration between vaccination and antibody measurements in our cohort supporting its robustness, generalizability, and potential for standardized clinical application. CONCLUSION: Our study unveils significant limitations of the AAAAI guidelines, highlighting the imperative for a more robust and adaptable approach. By introducing a novel PRP assessment method, we aim to enhance the accuracy and reliability of immune function evaluations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fogsgaard, Stine Fischer","Todaro, Sonia","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824988"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Fogsgaard, Stine Fischer"],"keyword":["Adult","Antibodies Bacterial blood","Antibody deficiency","Clinical guidelines","Diagnostic vaccination","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pneumococcal Vaccines","Pneumococcal Vaccines immunology","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Primary immunodeficiency","Prospective Studies","Streptococcus pneumoniae immunology","Vaccination","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reassessing polysaccharide responsiveness unveiling limitations of current guidelines and introducing the polysaccharide responsiveness percentile approach","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105011695960","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-824988","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12296993","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40711631","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105011695960","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-454a52f9-d235-4bd6-a993-45aa9c45bb4c"],"keyword":["Adult","Antibodies, Bacterial/blood","Antibody deficiency","Clinical guidelines","Diagnostic vaccination","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pneumococcal Vaccines/immunology","Pneumococcal vaccines","Polysaccharide responsiveness percentile","Polysaccharides, Bacterial/immunology","Practice Guidelines as Topic","Primary immunodeficiency","Prospective Studies","Streptococcus pneumoniae/immunology","Vaccination","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-1F5E1B4EA6574FB960CFD367B24F2653"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Infectious Diseases"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Fischer","key":"fogsgaardpau","last":"Fogsgaard","name":"Fogsgaard, Stine Fischer","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Sonia","key":"todaropau","last":"Todaro","name":"Todaro, Sonia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Schade","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2435cb82-03bd-498b-909d-1ef0e99443fe","name":"Larsen, Carsten Schade","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sværke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Magnus Bernth","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a67e0021-e11c-47a3-93dd-8f3783ad755a","name":"Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth","orcid":"0000-0002-5004-7822","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40711631"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s10875-025-01915-w","issn":["02719142","15732592"],"issn_org":["02719142"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Clinical Immunology","paperid":"115","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Immunology","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105011695960"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-454a52f9-d235-4bd6-a993-45aa9c45bb4c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Reassessing Polysaccharide Responsiveness: : Unveiling Limitations of Current Guidelines and Introducing the Polysaccharide Responsiveness Percentile Approach","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-824988","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Previous results on the association between statin use and risk of ovarian cancer (OC) are inconsistent, warranting further investigation. This study aims to examine the association between statin use and risk of OC in a large study population. METHODS: Based on two nationwide nested case-control studies utilizing data from Danish and Swedish high-quality registries, we identified 11,874 OC cases who were individually matched on age to 474,960 controls using risk-set sampling. Conditional logistic regression was performed separately on the country-specific data to calculate odds ratios (ORs) and corresponding 95 % confidence intervals (CIs) for the association between statin use and risk of OC. Country-specific estimates were combined based on a fixed-effect assumption. Furthermore, we examined potential effect modifications by a priori selected OC risk factors on the association between statin use and OC risk. RESULTS: We found no overall association between statin use and risk of OC (OR = 0.96; 95 % CI: 0.91-1.01); neither with duration nor intensity of use. However, statin use was associated with a decreased risk of OC in subsets of women with endometriosis (OR = 0.70; 95 % CI: 0.53-0.91), and nulliparous women (OR = 0.86; 95 % CI: 0.79-0.93). CONCLUSION: We found an effect modification of some known ovarian cancer risk factors on the association between statin use and risk of OC. In women with endometriosis, and in nulliparous women, respectively, statin use was associated with a decreased risk of OC, suggesting statins may have potential as a preventive measure.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bouazzi, Meyya","Zheng, Guoqiao","Wang, Jiangrong","Baandrup, Louise","Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Sundström, Karin","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-828461"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Case Control Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Endometriosis epidemiology","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl CoA Reductase Inhibitors therapeutic use","Menopause","Middle Aged","Ovarian Neoplasms epidemiology","Parity","Pregnancy","Registries","Risk Factors","Sweden epidemiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of statins and risk of ovarian cancer evidence on effect modification by parity menopause and endometriosis from nationwide nested case control studies","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-828461","identifier":[{"id":"40499207","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105007549241","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-1e94dc37-6a55-464e-9498-1b35f75683a7"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Case-Control Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Endometriosis/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Hydroxymethylglutaryl-CoA Reductase Inhibitors/therapeutic use","Menopause","Middle Aged","Ovarian Neoplasms/epidemiology","Parity","Pregnancy","Registries","Risk Factors","Sweden/epidemiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E05BE365EEEA3A2331BC5140FB6FA7E5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"