ermann","name":"Zimmermann, Alina","rank":283,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"zimmermannchristianpau","last":"Zimmermann","name":"Zimmermann, Christian","rank":284,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 32","corresponding":null,"first":"Justin J J","key":"vanderhooftjustinjjpau","last":"van der Hooft","name":"van der Hooft, Justin J J","rank":285,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"127","corresponding":null,"first":"Roger G","key":"liningtonrogergpau","last":"Linington","name":"Linington, Roger G","rank":286,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tilmann","key":"webertilmannpau","last":"Weber","locid":"06d96037-a8c4-4fba-bdbf-1319696e8ef5","name":"Weber, Tilmann","orcid":"0000-0002-8260-5120","rank":287,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marnix H","key":"medemamarnixhpau","last":"Medema","name":"Medema, Marnix H","rank":288,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39657789"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkae1115","issn":["03051048","13624962"],"issn_org":["03051048"],"issue":"D1","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Nucleic Acids Research","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85214414411"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eccbb6d6-0c8c-4faa-9eda-43a1a0ca2ceb","dtu-c42004d1-89ba-429d-9fbe-2452d786266c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"MIBiG 4.0 : advancing biosynthetic gene cluster curation through global collaboration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.74-785232","year":2025,"yearsub":2025}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Approximately 60-70% of all stroke incidents are categorised as mild. Although individuals with mild stroke manage most basic occupations independently, the consequences of mild stroke are multifaceted and might impact both the person with mild stroke and their partner’s lives, as well as the dynamics of the couples’ relationship and occupations. Purpose: To gain insight into the experience of the adjustment of occupations in couple dyads following mild stroke up to 1 year after the stroke. Methods: The study employed a qualitative longitudinal approach using ethnographically inspired fieldwork and joint interviews; a phenomenological-hermeneutical approach was used to interpret the data. Findings: One main theme, When life throws you a curve ball, and three interrelated subthemes, Feeling relieved yet concerned, Modification of shared and individual occupations, and New shared everyday life priorities were identified. Conclusion: Both persons in the dyad experienced a modification of shared and individual occupations. The couples were more engaged in co-occupations than before, and often these co-occupations were adjusted to accommodate the needs of the person with stroke. It is suggested that, in some cases, a mild stroke event can lead to a disruption and reconstruction of occupational identities for both individuals in the couple dyad.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Stina Meyer","Ytterberg, Charlotte","Johansson, Sverker","Thybæk- Hansen, Signe","Minet, Lisbeth Rosenbek"],"cuid":["S02-096.89-814163"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Stina Meyer"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute"],"keyword":["Couples","Hermeneutic phenomenology","Mild stroke","Occupational identity","Occupational science"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"when life throws you a curve ball a longitudinal couple dyad experience of adjustment of occupations following mild stroke","src":["sdu","ucl"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14427591.2024.2430381","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.89-814163","identifier":[{"id":"85211504707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7a14a9cb-48c0-4573-94fb-906dcd431ad1","ucl-43dc3881-0a2c-4dc3-ab74-a57adb641210"],"keyword":["Occupational science","co-occupation","couples","hermeneutic phenomenology","mild stroke","occupational identity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-64B257BD73DA06376FB14F8867894F2B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/292912266/When_life_throws_you_a_curve_ball_A_longitudinal_couple_dyad_experience_of_adjustment_of_occupations_following_mild_stroke.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14427591.2024.2430381","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Sundhed, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Center for Person-Centred Rehabilitation","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of CIMT - Centre for Innovative Medical Technology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Meyer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8f543caf-2ac2-46be-a40d-28a4477afc3a","name":"Larsen, Stina Meyer","orcid":"0000-0001-5836-370X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"ytterbergpau","last":"Ytterberg","locid":"4fb99d6a-9c7b-48c3-9b56-1dce87fbead6","name":"Ytterberg, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3704-8887","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sverker","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Sverker","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe","key":"thybækhansenpau","last":"Thybæk-Hansen","locid":"01e450fb-638e-498a-abda-d4a38f585902","name":"Thybæk-Hansen, Signe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth","key":"rosenbekminetpau","last":"Rosenbek Minet","locid":"a5aaf3a3-cbf8-4709-8cda-f2d14a3e1d2b","name":"Rosenbek Minet, Lisbeth Kirstine","name_org":"Rosenbek Minet, Lisbeth","orcid":"0000-0001-6179-5183","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/14427591.2024.2430381","issn":["14427591"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Occupational Science","pages":"258-271","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Journal of Occupational Science","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211504707"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7a14a9cb-48c0-4573-94fb-906dcd431ad1","ucl-43dc3881-0a2c-4dc3-ab74-a57adb641210"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College"],"title":"“When life throws you a curve ball”: A longitudinal couple dyad experience of adjustment of occupations following mild stroke","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.89-814163","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background Multidisciplinary lifestyle interventions for children with obesity in Denmark often include recommendations regarding physical activity, but no structured exercise program. We hypothesized that adding high-intensity interval training (HIIT) to a multidisciplinary lifestyle intervention would improve BMI z-score (primary outcome), waist circumference, blood pressure, and health-related quality of life (HRQOL). Methods This randomized controlled trial included 173 children and adolescents with obesity. Participants were allocated to 12-months lifestyle intervention (N = 83), or 12-month lifestyle intervention accompanied by a 12-week HIIT program (N = 90). HIIT consisted of three weekly sessions and included activities eliciting intensities >85% of maximal heart rate. Results Attendance rate for the 3-months HIIT intervention was 68.0 ± 23.2%. Dropout was lower in HIIT compared to control at three months (7.8% vs. 20.5%) and 12 months (26.5% vs 48.2%). Changes in BMI z-score did not differ between HIIT and control at 3 months (Mean Difference (MD): 0.01, 95% confidence interval (CI): −0.09; 0.12, P = 0.82) or 12 months (MD: 0.06, CI: −0.07;0.19, P = 0.34). Across randomization, BMI z-score was reduced by 0.11 (CI: 0.17; 0.06, P < 0.01) at 3 months and 0.20 (CI: 0.26;0.14, P < 0.01) at 12 months. At 3 months, HIIT experienced a greater increase in HRQOL of 2.73 (CI: 0.01;5.44, P = 0.05) in PedsQL Child total-score and 3.85 (CI: 0.96; 6.74, P < 0.01) in psychosocial health-score compared to control. At 12 months, PedsQL Child physical-score was reduced by 6.89 (CI: 10.97; 2.83, P < 0.01) in HIIT compared to control. No group differences or changes over time were found for waist circumference or blood pressure. Conclusion Adding a 12-week HIIT program did not further augment the positive effects of a 12-month lifestyle intervention on BMI z-score. Adding HIIT improved HRQOL after 3 months, but reduced HRQOL at 12 months. Implementation of HIIT in community-based settings was feasible and showed positive effects on adherence to the lifestyle intervention.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær","Larsen, Ryan Godsk","Duch, Kirsten","Simonsen, Morten Bilde","Christensen, Cecilie Brøns","Warner, Tine Caroc","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Handberg, Aase","Stjernholm, Theresa","Vestergaard, Esben Thyssen","Hagstrøm, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-099.36-803835"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility and efficacy of adding high intensity interval training to a multidisciplinary lifestyle intervention in children with obesity a randomized controlled trial pediatrics","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41366-024-01645-w","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The project was supported by Steno Diabetes Center North Denmark, Trygfonden (Grant No. 149852), Danish Regions (Grant No. R201-A4487), A.P. Moller Foundation (Grant No. 17-L-0393), Beckett Foundation (Grant No. 17-2-1655), Svend Andersens Foundation and Memorial legatee for Carpenter J\\u00F8rgen Holm and wife Elisa F. Hansen (Grant No. 20094). We thank iQniter (Aalborg, Denmark) for lending us the heart rate system. iQniter had no influence on the interpretation of the results."],"id":"S02-099.36-803835","identifier":[{"id":"39390066","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85206387885","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ced0506c-d63d-4d50-bc3b-3c81783e9a4f","au-182bf1aa-4f5c-4a5f-b476-13643c18cd8c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EB2E0C7A48B7C3A0E655186E75F464B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/766084092/Eggertsen_et_al._2025_._Feasibility_and_efficacy_of_adding_high-intensity_interval_training_to_a_multidisciplinary_lifestyle_intervention_in_children_with_obesity_a_randomized_controlled_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41366-024-01645-w","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Paediatrics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Steno Diabetes Center North Denmark","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Nørkjær","key":"eggertsenpau","last":"Eggertsen","locid":"ef704125-8280-4878-8ebc-8f60b38e7782","name":"Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-3425-0839","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ryan Godsk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"86d31e60-1de1-4284-a688-596cc17dca1c","name":"Larsen, Ryan Godsk","orcid":"0000-0002-4622-1453","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"duchpau","last":"Duch","locid":"952b4bf9-4968-4e9f-8f30-204e8c36d539","name":"Duch, Kirsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten Bilde","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"7d1393c0-2905-4e87-9a3d-80cca4dbeee6","name":"Simonsen, Morten Bilde","orcid":"0000-0001-6645-3596","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Brøns","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"e0ac8b0e-b41d-4c12-95ab-9ea6401333eb","name":"Christensen, Cecilie Brøns","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine Caroc","key":"warnerpau","last":"Warner","locid":"d4d62017-5154-4023-a5b3-6303991937c3","name":"Warner, Tine Caroc","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Brøndum","key":"frøkjærpau","last":"Frøkjær","locid":"6e553b4c-cf1d-452b-963c-94942485d472","name":"Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","orcid":"0000-0001-8722-0070","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aase","key":"handbergpau","last":"Handberg","locid":"aba86271-7a2f-4bb7-83d0-426af197b6e5","name":"Handberg, Aase","orcid":"0000-0001-5719-203X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Theresa","key":"stjernholmpau","last":"Stjernholm","locid":"4b647d95-10f5-4d97-831b-dea3529fcc92","name":"Stjernholm, Theresa","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esben Thyssen","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"2cbff962-cbb0-43fa-8fc3-648dc685070a","name":"Vestergaard, Esben Thyssen","orcid":"0000-0003-4263-1815","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"hagstrømpau","last":"Hagstrøm","locid":"fe472f53-6bcd-4587-8287-df1539f689c3","name":"Hagstrøm, Søren","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39390066"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41366-024-01645-w","issn":["03070565","14765497"],"issn_org":["03070565"],"issue":"2","journal":"International Journal of Obesity","pages":"269-277","paperid":"53","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Obesity","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206387885"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ced0506c-d63d-4d50-bc3b-3c81783e9a4f","au-182bf1aa-4f5c-4a5f-b476-13643c18cd8c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Feasibility and efficacy of adding high-intensity interval training to a multidisciplinary lifestyle intervention in children with obesity—a randomized controlled trial : Pediatrics","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.36-803835","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: The combination of a reduction in the Danish hospital bed count, the shortage of hospital staff and demographic changes challenges the Danish hospital capacity. This was further highlighted during the COVID-19 pandemic when hospitals worldwide were overwhelmed by infected patients requiring acute hospital care. To address these challenges, a hospital-at-home (HaH) programme offers an alternative to conventional in-hospital admission. Furthermore, HaH has the potential to improve patient outcomes, reduce costs and increase patient satisfaction. However, few studies have evaluated HaH in a Scandinavian setting, and this article describes the protocol for a randomised controlled trial (RCT) comparing an HaH model with continued conventional in-hospital admission. The main aim of the trial is to evaluate physical activity level and mental wellbeing in patients admitted at home compared with conventionally admitted patients. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: 110 clinically stable patients from two internal medical wards at Nordsjaellands Hospital in Denmark will be included and randomised in a ratio of 1:1 to either continued conventional in-hospital admission (control group) or virtual HaH model (intervention group). The control group will receive standard hospital treatment, and the intervention group will be transferred home for continued treatment (eg, intravenous antibiotics or oxygen treatment). The primary outcome measures are physical activity assessed using daily step count (during the first 24 hours after inclusion, as an intermediary indicator of the risk of adverse events) and treatment satisfaction (assessed using a patient satisfaction survey). Secondary outcome measures are adverse events of special interest, escalation of care, readmission rate postdischarge (30 days and 90 days), mortality (associated and 7 days, 30 days and 90 days postdischarge), process data (eg, the number of teleconsultations) and a health economic evaluation. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The study was approved by the Danish Research Ethics Committees (no. 2303051) and the Danish Medicines Agency (CIV-23-03-042542) and will be monitored by the Copenhagen University Hospital Good Clinical Practice unit. Results will be published in peer-reviewed journals and presented at relevant national and international conferences. We also plan to communicate the results to relevant stakeholders in the Danish healthcare system. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT05920304.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Maria Normand","Dreisig, Tatjana Sandreva","Rasmussen, Maja Kjaer","Christensen, Maria Lund","Bjerregaard, Daniel","Von Sydow, Charlotte Demuth","Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","Fischer, Thea K."],"cuid":["S02-099.86-814006"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Maria Normand"],"keyword":["Administration","COVID 19 epidemiology","Clinical Protocols","Denmark epidemiology","Exercise","Female","Hospitalization","Humans","Patient Satisfaction","Public health","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","SARS CoV 2","Telemedicine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"telemedicine supported hospital at home for acutely admitted patients at nordsjaellands hospital denmark a study protocol for a randomised controlled trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2024-098287","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.86-814006","identifier":[{"id":"40374231","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105005336407","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12083328","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-37bf7772-2a62-4fc3-ad9a-39041028a1e3","sdu-7279fb0b-8407-4e2f-b4ff-34a4414e07c7"],"keyword":["Administration","COVID-19/epidemiology","Clinical Protocols","Denmark/epidemiology","Exercise","Female","Home Care Services, Hospital-Based/organization & administration","Hospitalization","Humans","Patient Satisfaction","Public health","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","SARS-CoV-2","Telemedicine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-78DBFEFFC7B922E6EC865BE26FFB4F0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2024-098287","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/451438820/e098287.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290025032/e098287.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of CIMT - Centre for Innovative Medical Technology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Global Health Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Normand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Maria Normand","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tatjana Sandreva","key":"dreisigpau","last":"Dreisig","name":"Dreisig, Tatjana Sandreva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Kjaer","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"cc76ec55-14ab-429b-ac2e-5ec2cd6ccc04","name":"Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","name_org":"Rasmussen, Maja Kjaer","orcid":"0000-0002-7405-4373","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Lund","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Maria Lund","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Daniel","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","name":"Bjerregaard, Daniel","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Demuth","key":"vonsydowpau","last":"Von Sydow","name":"Von Sydow, Charlotte Demuth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thyge Lynghøj","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Thea","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"97c4bf8d-8bd1-470b-8e0b-91eb4faf7703","name":"Fischer, Thea K.","name_org":"Fischer, Thea","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40374231"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2024-098287","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"5","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e098287","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005336407"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-37bf7772-2a62-4fc3-ad9a-39041028a1e3","sdu-7279fb0b-8407-4e2f-b4ff-34a4414e07c7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Telemedicine-supported hospital-at-home for acutely admitted patients at Nordsjaellands Hospital, Denmark : A study protocol for a randomised controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.86-814006","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: The population-based Inter99 cohort has contributed extensively to our understanding of effects of a systematic screening and lifestyle intervention, as well as the multifactorial aetiology of type 2 diabetes (T2D) and cardiovascular disease. To understand causes, trajectories and patterns of early and overt cardiometabolic disease manifestations, we will perform a combined clinical deep phenotyping and registry follow-up study of the now 50-80 years old Inter99 participants. METHODS AND ANALYSIS: The Inter99 cohort comprises individuals aged 30-60 years, who lived in a representative geographical area of greater Copenhagen, Denmark, in 1999. Age-stratified and sex-stratified random subgroups were invited to participate in either a lifestyle intervention (N=13 016) or questionnaires (N=5264), while the rest served as a reference population (N=43 021). Of the 13 016 individuals assigned to the lifestyle intervention group, 6784 (52%) accepted participation in a baseline health examination in 1999, including screening for cardiovascular risk factors and prediabetic conditions. In total, 6004 eligible participants, who participated in the baseline examination, will be invited to participate in the deep phenotyping 20-year follow-up clinical examination including measurements of anthropometry, blood pressure, arterial stiffness, cardiometabolic biomarkers, coronary artery calcification, heart rate variability, heart rhythm, liver stiffness, fundus characteristics, muscle strength and mass, as well as health and lifestyle questionnaires. In a subsample, 10-day monitoring of diet, physical activity and continuous glucose measurements will be performed. Fasting blood, urine and faecal samples to be stored in a biobank. The established database will form the basis of multiple analyses. A main purpose is to investigate whether low birth weight independent of genetics, lifestyle and glucose tolerance predicts later common T2D cardiometabolic comorbidities. ETHICS AND DISSEMINATION: The study was approved by the Medical Ethics Committee, Capital Region, Denmark (H-20076231) and by the Danish Data Protection Agency through the Capital Region of Denmark's registration system (P-2020-1074). Informed consent will be obtained before examinations. Findings will be disseminated in peer-reviewed journals, at conferences and via presentations to stakeholders, including patients and public health policymakers. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: NCT05166447.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Bjørnsbo, Kirsten Schroll","Brøns, Charlotte","Aadahl, Mette","Kampmann, Freja Bach","Friis Bryde Nielsen, Camilla","Lundbergh, Bjørn","Christensen, Rasmus Wibaek","Kårhus, Line Lund","Madsen, Anja Lykke","Hansen, Christian Stevns","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","Suetta, Charlotte","Kjaer, Michael","Grarup, Niels","Kanters, Jørgen K.","Larsen, Michael","Køber, Lars","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Loos, Ruth J.F.","Hansen, Torben","Linneberg, Allan","Vaag, Allan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721417"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Skåne University Hospital","University of California San Francisco"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cardiovascular Diseases prevention control","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2 epidemiology","Follow Up Studies","Glucose","Humans","Middle Aged","Registries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protocol for the combined cardiometabolic deep phenotyping and registry based 000000000020 year follow up study of the inter000000000099 cohort","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078501","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721417","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10826573","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38286704","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184011808","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a7f818c8-f801-44f3-9713-f89c44ed44c9"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cardiovascular Diseases/prevention & control","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2/epidemiology","Follow-Up Studies","Glucose","Humans","Middle Aged","Registries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2518AA96A2731A4847F2961873AE748E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381240948/e078501.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078501","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centre, Gentofte, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Rheumatology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of california san francisco","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California San Francisco","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten Schroll","key":"bjørnsbokirstenschrollpau","last":"Bjørnsbo","name":"Bjørnsbo, Kirsten Schroll","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte","key":"brønscharlottepau","last":"Brøns","name":"Brøns, Charlotte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Mette","key":"aadahlmettepau","last":"Aadahl","locid":"019b268b-8dff-4a10-91f6-07730c29d39b","name":"Aadahl, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-5904-9747","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Freja Bach","key":"kampmannfrejabachpau","last":"Kampmann","name":"Kampmann, Freja Bach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla","key":"friisbrydenielsencamillapau","last":"Friis Bryde Nielsen","name":"Friis Bryde Nielsen, Camilla","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bjørn","key":"lundberghbjørnpau","last":"Lundbergh","name":"Lundbergh, Bjørn","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus Wibaek","key":"christensenrasmuswibaekpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Rasmus Wibaek","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Lund","key":"kårhuslinelundpau","last":"Kårhus","name":"Kårhus, Line Lund","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anja Lykke","key":"madsenanjalykkepau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Anja Lykke","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christian Stevns","key":"hansenchristianstevnspau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Christian Stevns","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardkirstenpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Niklas Rye","key":"jørgensenniklasryepau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"3dc68a95-e26c-4b82-a4f0-7548313f8045","name":"Jørgensen, Niklas Rye","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Charlotte","key":"suettacharlottepau","last":"Suetta","locid":"26af20c6-3c1b-4b5a-aa41-bf3e1598e2b0","name":"Suetta, Charlotte","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Michael","key":"kjaermichaelpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"7937b8ab-7820-4d25-982f-1d2f58b033a3","name":"Kjaer, Michael","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Niels","key":"grarupnielspau","last":"Grarup","locid":"824a7159-a059-4de1-bf3f-e116ef59e0de","name":"Grarup, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5526-1070","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Jørgen","key":"kantersjørgenkpau","last":"Kanters","locid":"f544654f-76ab-44f6-a780-d0a011eb7341","name":"Kanters, Jørgen K.","name_org":"Kanters, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-3267-4910","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenmichaelpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Lars","key":"køberlarspau","last":"Køber","locid":"e3f0c57c-605a-431a-9c63-2213c46621e6","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Klaus Fuglsang","key":"kofoedklausfuglsangpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ruth","key":"loosruthjfpau","last":"Loos","locid":"abd47200-05e5-4557-b3da-3de36ac78586","name":"Loos, Ruth J.F.","name_org":"Loos, Ruth","orcid":"0000-0002-8532-5087","rank":20,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Torben","key":"hansentorbenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":21,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Allan","key":"linnebergallanpau","last":"Linneberg","locid":"09da8aa6-fd95-4ace-a2f1-19f38d7d3f9e","name":"Linneberg, Allan","orcid":"0000-0002-0994-0184","rank":22,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 5 6","first":"Allan","key":"vaagallanpau","last":"Vaag","locid":"4b68020d-63cf-4701-ad10-cbc4845d0f1c","name":"Vaag, Allan","rank":23,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38286704"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078501","issn":["20446055"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMJ Open","paperid":"e078501","status":"p","title":"BMJ Open","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184011808"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a7f818c8-f801-44f3-9713-f89c44ed44c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protocol for the combined cardiometabolic deep phenotyping and registry-based 20-year follow-up study of the Inter99 cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721417","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: The effectiveness and safety of computed tomography (CT) and invasive coronary angiography (ICA) in different age groups is unknown. OBJECTIVE: To determine the association of age with outcomes of CT and ICA in patients with stable chest pain. DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: The assessor-blinded Diagnostic Imaging Strategies for Patients With Stable Chest Pain and Intermediate Risk of Coronary Artery Disease (DISCHARGE) randomized clinical trial was conducted between October 2015 and April 2019 in 26 European centers. Patients referred for ICA with stable chest pain and an intermediate probability of obstructive coronary artery disease were analyzed in an intention-to-treat analysis. Data were analyzed from July 2022 to January 2023. INTERVENTIONS: Patients were randomly assigned to a CT-first strategy or a direct-to-ICA strategy. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: MACE (ie, cardiovascular death, nonfatal myocardial infarction, or stroke) and major procedure-related complications. The primary prespecified outcome of this secondary analysis of age was major adverse cardiovascular events (MACE) at a median follow-up of 3.5 years. RESULTS: Among 3561 patients (mean [SD] age, 60.1 [10.1] years; 2002 female [56.2%]), 2360 (66.3%) were younger than 65 years, 982 (27.6%) were between ages 65 to 75 years, and 219 (6.1%) were older than 75 years. The primary outcome was MACE at a median (IQR) follow-up of 3.5 (2.9-4.2) years for 3523 patients (99%). Modeling age as a continuous variable, age, and randomization group were not associated with MACE (hazard ratio, 1.02; 95% CI, 0.98-1.07; P for interaction = .31). Age and randomization group were associated with major procedure-related complications (odds ratio, 1.15; 95% CI, 1.05-1.27; P for interaction = .005), which were lower in younger patients. CONCLUSIONS AND RELEVANCE: Age did not modify the effect of randomization group on the primary outcome of MACE but did modify the effect on major procedure-related complications. Results suggest that CT was associated with a lower risk of major procedure-related complications in younger patients. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT02400229.","author_count":50,"contributors":["Bosserdt, Maria","Serna-Higuita, Lina M","Feuchtner, Gudrun","Merkely, Bela","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Benedek, Theodora","Donnelly, Patrick","Rodriguez-Palomares, José","Erglis, Andrejs","Štechovský, Cyril","Šakalyte, Gintare","Adic, Nada Cemerlic","Gutberlet, Matthias","Dodd, Jonathan D","Diez, Ignacio","Davis, Gershan","Zimmermann, Elke","Kepka, Cezary","Vidakovic, Radosav","Francone, Marco","Ilnicka-Suckiel, Malgorzata","Plank, Fabian","Knuuti, Juhani","Faria, Rita","Schröder, Stephen","Berry, Colin","Saba, Luca","Ruzsics, Balazs","Rieckmann, Nina","Kubiak, Christine","Hansen, Kristian Schultz","Müller-Nordhorn, Jacqueline","Szilveszter, Bálint","Sigvardsen, Per E","Benedek, Imre","Orr, Clare","Valente, Filipa Xavier","Zvaigzne, Ligita","Suchánek, Vojtech","Jankauskas, Antanas","Adic, Filip","Woinke, Michael","Hensey, Mark","Lecumberri, Iñigo","Thwaite, Erica","Laule, Michael","Kruk, Mariusz","Kragelund, Charlotte","Hove, Jens Dahlgaard","Larsen, Linnea"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731527"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["DISCHARGE Trial Group"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Czechia","Finland","Germany","Hungary","Ireland","Italy","Latvia","Lithuania","Poland","Romania","Serbia","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Alb Fils Kliniken, Göppingen","All Global Affiliations","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Cardiomed Medical Center","Clinical Hospital Center Zemun","Free University of Berlin","George Emil Palade University of Medicine, Pharmacy, Science and Technology of Targu Mures","Hospital de Basurto","Humboldt University of Berlin","Innsbruck Medical University","Leipzig Uni