{"abstract":"AIM: The objective of this registry study is to assess the utilization of pharmacogenomic (PGx) drugs among patients with chronic kidney disease (CKD). METHODS: This study was a retrospective study of patients affiliated with the Department of Nephrology, Aalborg University Hospital, Denmark in 2021. Patients diagnosed with CKD were divided into CKD without dialysis and CKD with dialysis. PGx prescription drugs were retrieved from the Patient Administration System. Actionable dosing guidelines (AG) for specific drug-gene pairs for CYP2D6, CYP2C9, CYP2C19 and SLCO1B1 were retrieved from the PharmGKB homepage. RESULTS: Out of 1241 individuals, 25.5% were on dialysis. The median number of medications for each patient was 9 within the non-dialysis group and 16 within the dialysis group. Thirty-one distinct PGx drugs were prescribed. Altogether, 76.0% (943 individuals) were prescribed at least one PGx drug and the prevalence of prescriptions of PGx drugs was higher in the dialysis group compared to the non-dialysis group. The most frequently prescribed drugs with AG were metoprolol, pantoprazole, atorvastatin, simvastatin and warfarin. CONCLUSION: This study demonstrated that a substantial proportion of patients with CKD are exposed to drugs or drug combinations for which there exists AG related to PGx of CYP2D6, CYP2C19, CYP2C9 and SLCO1B1.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Westergaard, Niels","Baltzer Houlind, Morten","Christrup, Lona Louring","Juul-Larsen, Helle Gybel","Strandhave, Charlotte","Olesen, Anne Estrup"],"cuid":["S03-091.49-724405"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Westergaard, Niels"],"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease","Dialysis","Drug gene interactions","Drug use","Pharmacogenomics","Polypharmacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of drugs with pharmacogenomics pgx based dosing guidelines in a danish cohort of persons with chronic kidney disease both on dialysis and not on dialysis perspectives for prescribing optimization","src":["aau","ku","pha"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13985","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Morten Baltzer Houlind was supported personally by postdoctoral fellowships from the Capital Region's Research Foundation for Health Research (grant A6882 and A7140) and the BRIDGE Translational Excellence Program at the Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, University of Copenhagen, Denmark (grant NNF20SA0064340). Funding information"],"id":"S03-091.49-724405","identifier":[{"id":"85184239554","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38308569","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f7ff9dc2-8030-4716-b12d-66e209109c57","ku-41be3711-bacd-4050-bb6a-e26e20b7f3a8","pha-b58f4a73-7511-4557-8d33-296d2a70d840"],"keyword":["chronic kidney disease","dialysis","drug use","drug–gene interactions","pharmacogenomics","polypharmacy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-D2FEC5B927FC69DC32A1736902B3E10A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/687373004/Westergaard_et_al._2024_._Use_of_drugs_with_pharmacogenomics_PGx_-based_dosing_guidelines_in_a_Danish_cohort_of_persons_with_chronic_kidney_disease_both_on_dialysis_and_not_on_dialysis_-_Perspectives_for_prescribing_optimization.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13985","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/387738383/Basic_Clin_Pharma_Tox_2024_Westergaard_Use_of_drugs_with_pharmacogenomics_PGx_based_dosing_guidelines_in_a_Danish.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Drug Design and Pharmacology, Translational and Clinical Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Nephrology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg Universitetshospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"westergaardpau","last":"Westergaard","locid":"724878cd-d318-4aec-a0a7-bdb6af7bd8c4","name":"Westergaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-2663-8040","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Morten","key":"baltzerhoulindpau","last":"Baltzer Houlind","locid":"c8b3768d-e73e-4235-8c47-f4fb4f7b15ae","name":"Houlind, Morten Baltzer","name_org":"Baltzer Houlind, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lona Louring","key":"christruppau","last":"Christrup","locid":"acf7258c-1e63-48a1-9bef-d6b6c5b8eeca","name":"Christrup, Lona Louring","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Gybel","key":"juullarsenpau","last":"Juul-Larsen","name":"Juul-Larsen, Helle Gybel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"strandhavepau","last":"Strandhave","locid":"feb4dbf8-66b0-460a-b66d-8878cfc661b0","name":"Strandhave, Charlotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Estrup","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"88951454-410c-4411-aeab-9706f3e3351c","name":"Olesen, Anne Estrup","orcid":"0000-0001-9365-1918","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38308569"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.13985","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"4","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"531-542","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","title_org":"Basic and Clinical Pharmacology and Toxicology","volume":"134"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184239554"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f7ff9dc2-8030-4716-b12d-66e209109c57","ku-41be3711-bacd-4050-bb6a-e26e20b7f3a8","pha-b58f4a73-7511-4557-8d33-296d2a70d840"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AB University College Absalon","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Use of drugs with pharmacogenomics (PGx)-based dosing guidelines in a Danish cohort of persons with chronic kidney disease, both on dialysis and not on dialysis: Perspectives for prescribing optimization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.49-724405","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Acromegaly is associated with increased morbidity and mortality if left untreated. The therapeutic options include surgery, medical treatment, and radiotherapy. Several guidelines and recommendations on treatment algorithms and follow-up exist. However, not all recommendations are strictly evidence-based. To evaluate consensus on the treatment and follow-up of patients with acromegaly in the Nordic countries. Methods: A Delphi process was used to map the landscape of acromegaly management in Denmark, Sweden, Norway, Finland, and Iceland. An expert panel developed 37 statements on the treatment and follow-up of patients with acromegaly. Dedicated endocrinologists (n = 47) from the Nordic countries were invited to rate their extent of agreement with the statements, using a Likert-type scale (1−7). Consensus was defined as ≥80% of panelists rating their agreement as ≥5 or ≤3 on the Likert-type scale. Results: Consensus was reached in 41% (15/37) of the statements. Panelists agreed that pituitary surgery remains first line treatment. There was general agreement to recommend first-generation somatostatin analog (SSA) treatment after failed surgery and to consider repeat surgery. In addition, there was agreement to recommend combination therapy with first-generation SSA and pegvisomant as second- or third-line treatment. In more than 50% of the statements, consensus was not achieved. Considerable disagreement existed regarding pegvisomant monotherapy, and treatment with pasireotide and dopamine agonists. Conclusion: This consensus exploration study on the management of patients with acromegaly in the Nordic countries revealed a relatively large degree of disagreement among experts, which mirrors the complexity of the disease and the shortage of evidence-based data.","author_count":52,"contributors":["Arlien-Søborg, Mai Christiansen","Dal, Jakob","Heck, Ansgar","Krag, Kirstine Stochholm","Husted, Eigil","Feltoft, Claus Larsen","Rasmussen, Åse Krogh","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Andreassen, Mikkel","Klose, Marianne Christina","Nielsen, Torben Leo","Andersen, Marianne Skovsager","Christensen, Louise Lehmann","Krogh, Jesper","Jarlov, Anne","Bollerslev, Jens","Nermoen, Ingrid","Oksnes, Marianne","Dahlqvist, Per","Olsson, Tommy","Berinder, Katarina","Hoybye, Charlotte","Petersson, Maria","Akerman, Anna karin","Wahlberg, Jeanette","Ekman, Bertil","Engstrom, Britt Eden","Johannsson, Gudmundur","Ragnarsson, Oskar","Olsson, Daniel","Sigurjónsdóttir, Helga Ágústa","Fougner, Stine Lyngvi","Matikainen, Niina","Vehkavaara, Satu","Metso, Saara","Jaatinen, Pia","Hämäläinen, Päivi","Rintamäki, Reeta","Yliaska, Iina","Immonen, Heidi","Mäkimattila, Sari","Cederberg-Tamminen, Henna","Viukari, Marianna","Nevalainen, Pasi","Nuutila, Pirjo","Schalin-Jäntti, Camilla","Burman, Pia","Jørgensen, Jens Otto Lunde"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-751635"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Arlien-Søborg, Mai C.","Arlien-Søborg, Mai Christiansen"],"country":["Finland","Iceland","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Akershus University Hospital","All Global Affiliations","AstraZeneca","AstraZeneca Sweden","AstraZeneca UK","Faculty of Medicine and Health","Haukeland University Hospital","Helsinki University Central Hospital","Helsinki University Hospital","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Kuopio University Hospital","Landspitali University Hospital","Linköping University","Lund University","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Oslo University Hospital","Oulu University Hospital","Sahlgrenska University Hospital","Skåne University Hospital","St. Olav University Hospital","St. Olavs Hospital - University Hospital Trondheim","St. Olavs University Hospital (Trondheim)","Tampere University Hospital","The National University Hospital of Iceland","Turku University Central Hospital","Turku University Hospital","Umeå University","University Hospital Umeå","University Hospital of North Norway","University Hospital of Tampere","University Hospital of Umeå","University of Gothenburg","University of Iceland","University of Oslo","University of Oulu","University of Turku","Uppsala University","Uppsala University Hospital","Örebro University","Örebro University Hospital"],"keyword":["Acromegaly","Acromegaly therapy","Consensus","Delphi","Delphi Technique","Dopamine agonist","Growth hormone","Human Growth Hormone therapeutic use","Humans","Insulin Like Growth Factor I","Scandinavian and Nordic Countries epidemiology","Somatostatin","Somatostatin analogs derivatives","Surveys and Questionnaires","growth hormone receptor antagonist"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acromegaly management in the nordic countries a delphi consensus survey","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cen.15095","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Jens Otto Lunde J\\u00F8rgensen and Jakob Dal have received unrestricted research grants and lecture fees from Pfizer and IPSEN. Mai C. Arlien\\u2010S\\u00F8borg has received lecture fees from Pfizer. Daniel Olsson has served as a consultant for Ipsen, Pfizer, Novo Nordisk, and Sandoz; has received research grants from Sandoz and Pfizer; and is an employee at AstraZeneca as of 30 August 2021. This work was supported by an unrestrict