e":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Radio4","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-02fa8867-616d-458c-9d45-3381ffe482a9"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Anonym sladder på nettet er andet end bare ondskab","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-725362","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Income inequality affects population health and wellbeing negatively. In Greenland, health inequality has been shown to exist among social groups, regionally and according to urbanization, and between Inuit and migrants from Denmark. The purpose of the study was to compare the changes in health inequality from 1993 to 2018 according to three measures of social position, i.e. a socioeconomic measure (household assets), a measure of urbanization and a composite sociocultural index. We hypothesized that social inequality in health increased parallel to the increasing economic inequality in Greenland. The sample was based on four population health surveys conducted among the Inuit in Greenland in 1993, 2005–2010, 2014 and 2018. The total number of interviews was 9024 and the total number of individuals interviewed was 5829, as participants were invited to several surveys as part of a cohort. As statistical measure of social disparity we used the slope index of inequality (SII) adjusted for age and sex. Analyses were performed with daily smoking, suicidal thoughts and obesity as health outcomes. Daily smoking was most prevalent among participants with low social position whereas obesity was most prevalent among participants with high social position. With household assets as indicator of social position, the results showed high and increasing social inequality for both daily smoking and obesity. Social inequality for daily smoking increased over time also for urbanization and the sociocultural index. The hypothesis that social inequality increased over time was thus confirmed for daily smoking and obesity but not for suicidal thoughts. With the results from the present study there is solid evidence to guide prevention and health care towards social equality in health.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bjerregaard, Peter","Svartá, Durita Lyngsø","Ottendahl, Charlotte Brandstrup","Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-734316"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Bjerregaard, Peter"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Grønlands Universitet"],"keyword":["Greenland","Health disparities","Inuit","Social inequality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increasing health inequality among inuit in greenland from 000000001993 to 000000002018 different patterns for household assets urbanization and a sociocultural index as indicators of social position","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssmph.2024.101635","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-734316","identifier":[{"id":"38486800","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85186999287","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10937147","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-dcd4ef1b-a2be-4ed5-b612-fd03b698f95e"],"keyword":["Greenland","Health disparities","Inuit","Social inequality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B0823602AEEB3EB6E530CF74C8DD2CAA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/257114337/1-s2.0-S2352827324000351-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssmph.2024.101635","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Center for Public health in Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"grønlands universitet","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Grønlands Universitet","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","locid":"ef4a2fa7-9735-4b1e-a4fa-b1272def2cfc","name":"Bjerregaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7153-8447","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Durita Lyngsø","key":"svartápau","last":"Svartá","locid":"7d14a946-3c39-479f-9e88-0b5c3061f8e5","name":"Svartá, Durita Lyngsø","orcid":"0000-0002-8931-8386","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Brandstrup","key":"ottendahlpau","last":"Ottendahl","locid":"9e2ae085-ebf8-4688-b8cf-c257c5458aca","name":"Ottendahl, Charlotte Brandstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-9285-3099","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Viskum Lytken","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3ee738b1-09d1-4886-9ddf-67ca132997fe","name":"Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken","orcid":"0000-0002-6245-4222","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38486800"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ssmph.2024.101635","issn":["23528273"],"journal":"SSM - Population Health","paperid":"101635","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"SSM - Population Health","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186999287"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-dcd4ef1b-a2be-4ed5-b612-fd03b698f95e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Increasing health inequality among Inuit in Greenland from 1993 to 2018 : Different patterns for household assets, urbanization and a sociocultural index as indicators of social position","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-734316","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Denne artikel bidrager til diskussioner om specialpædagogiske faglighed med udgangspunkt i teori om børns hverdagsliv, læring og udvikling sammen med andre børn og på tværs af deres forskellige livssammenhænge. Der redegøres for begreber til at inspirere en situeret specialpædagogisk faglighed i hverdagslivets fleksibelt fokuserede udforskning omkring børns perspektiver, livsførelse og deltagelsesmuligheder. Derudover diskuteres den pointe at særlige kategorier for vanskeligheder kan komme til at dominere, så vi ikke får øje på, hvad børn selv er rettet mod og på deres til tider vanskelige og ulige betingelser for at deltage og bidrage til de læringsfællesskaber, de lærer og udvikler sig igennem. Endelig analyseres det, hvordan disse vanskelige betingelser kan hænge sammen med forskellige sociale forhold, her særlig samarbejde mellem børnenes voksne og dynamikker i børnenes læringsfællesskaber.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-755149"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"situeret specialpædagogik om at arbejde med børns ulige deltagelsesmuligheder","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-755149","ids":["ruc-037a82ce-0e6a-4f6f-9ae5-d1fd95a6a4f2"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-70E15154B247A5250AC2B59C159E9A20"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, The Danish Centre for Research in Early Childhood Education and Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Else Bengaard","key":"skibstedpedh","last":"Skibsted","name":"Skibsted, Else Bengaard","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Merete","key":"munkholmpedh","last":"Munkholm","name":"Munkholm, Merete","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788750064800"],"pages":"76-93","publisher":"Akademisk Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"tæt på levet skoleliv","title":"Specialpædagogik i et inkluderende perspektiv"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-037a82ce-0e6a-4f6f-9ae5-d1fd95a6a4f2"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Situeret Specialpædagogik : Om at arbejde med børns ulige deltagelsesmuligheder","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-755149","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: According to the theory of lipitoxicity, ectopic fat deposition (i.e., storage of triglycerides in non-adipose tissues, such as muscle, liver, pancreas) can lead to inflammation, insulin resistance and beta-cell dysfunction (1, 2). A previous study reported greater fat deposition in skeletal muscle and liver in children with obesity compared to their lean counterparts (3). However, the role of weight status (obesity vs. normal weight) on pancreatic fat deposition in children is yet unclear. In addition, little is known about the roles of sex and physical activity level in modulating ectopic fat deposition in children. We tested the hypotheses that children with obesity exhibit greater fat deposition in psoas muscle, liver, and pancreas compared to children with normal weight, matched for age and sex. We also investigated if sex and physical activity level modulate fat deposition in these organs. Methods: 3T MR scanning with multi-echo Dixon imaging was used to acquire proton density fat fraction (PDFF) maps in 48 children (9-16 years; 33 boys, 15 girls) with obesity (body mass index, BMI > 90 percentile for age and sex) and in 30 age-matched children with normal weight (18 boys, 12 girls). From the PDFF maps, liver, psoas muscle and pancreas were outlined to obtain fat fraction in each specific organ. To assess physical activity level, participants wore a 3-axis accelerometer on the thigh for seven consecutive days. Daily minutes spent in sedentary, light, moderate and vigorous intensity were quantified. Fat fractions and physical activity categories were analyzed using 2-way (group, sex) repeated measures ANOVA. Associations between physical activity level and fat fractions were explored using Pearson’s correlation. Results: Compared to normal weight, children with obesity showed higher fat fraction in liver (6.3±6.9% vs. 1.7±0.7; p<0.001), psoas (2.8±1.6% vs. 1.1±0.6%; p<0.001) and pancreas (4.9±2.8% vs. 1.7±0.7%; p<0.001) with no effects or interactions of sex. Daily minutes spent in moderate (29.0±13.7 vs. 43.1±19.5; p<0.001) and vigorous (8.2±7.6 vs. 21.9 ±13.2; p<0.001) intensity were lower in children with obesity compared with normal weight, with no effects or interactions of sex. Daily minutes of moderate-to-vigorous intensity was inversely associated with fat fraction in liver (r=-0.27, p<0.05), psoas (r=-0.34, p<0.01), and pancreas (r=-0.50, p<0.01). Conclusion: Children with obesity exhibited greater fat deposition in liver, psoas muscle and pancreas compared to their lean counterparts. While sex did not play a role in modulating fat deposition, time spent in moderate-to-vigorous intensity activities were inversely associated with fat fraction in each organ. Future studies are required to 1) elucidate biomarkers that can identify children who display a critical amount of ectopic fat deposition, and 2) explore interventions effective in reducing ectopic fat deposition in children with obesity.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Larsen, Ryan Godsk","Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær","Madsen, Jonas Gelardi","Brønd, Jan C.","Handberg, Aase","Vestergaard, Esben T.","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Hagstrøm, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-756977"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-04","place":"Newcastle-upon-Tyne, gb","start":"2024-07-02","title":"Physiology in Focus 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of ectopic fat deposition between children with and without obesity influence of sex and physical activity level","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.physoc.org/abstracts/comparison-of-ectopic-fat-deposition-between-children-with-and-without-obesity-influence-of-sex-and-physical-activity-level/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-756977","ids":["aau-86801b43-9acb-4a76-8f6a-4ac253cbd0b5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C9CC887FDD838FF1150FF11F669DFA73"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.physoc.org/abstracts/comparison-of-ectopic-fat-deposition-between-children-with-and-without-obesity-influence-of-sex-and-physical-activity-level/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, ExerciseTech"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ryan Godsk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"86d31e60-1de1-4284-a688-596cc17dca1c","name":"Larsen, Ryan Godsk","orcid":"0000-0002-4622-1453","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Nørkjær","key":"eggertsenpau","last":"Eggertsen","locid":"ef704125-8280-4878-8ebc-8f60b38e7782","name":"Eggertsen, Charlotte Nørkjær","orcid":"0000-0002-3425-0839","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Gelardi","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"5eb9d835-18e4-48bd-b475-aac451c533d9","name":"Madsen, Jonas Gelardi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan C.","key":"brøndpau","last":"Brønd","name":"Brønd, Jan C.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aase","key":"handbergpau","last":"Handberg","locid":"aba86271-7a2f-4bb7-83d0-426af197b6e5","name":"Handberg, Aase","orcid":"0000-0001-5719-203X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Esben T.","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","name":"Vestergaard, Esben T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Brøndum","key":"frøkjærpau","last":"Frøkjær","locid":"6e553b4c-cf1d-452b-963c-94942485d472","name":"Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","orcid":"0000-0001-8722-0070","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"hagstrømpau","last":"Hagstrøm","locid":"fe472f53-6bcd-4587-8287-df1539f689c3","name":"Hagstrøm, Søren","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"154-155","status":"p","subtitle":"Abstracts","title":"Physiology in Focus 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-86801b43-9acb-4a76-8f6a-4ac253cbd0b5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparison of ectopic fat deposition between children with and without obesity : Influence of sex and physical activity level","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-756977","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We demonstrate record fast horizontal radial plume mapping (HRPM) of nitrous oxide (N2O) emissions, enabled by a quantum-cascade laser (QCL) and an open-path direct absorption spectroscopy operating around the 4.5 μm wavelength. The high signal-to-noise ratio of the system yields an atmospheric N2O sensor with a remarkable sensitivity of 25 ppt at 1 Hz update rate as assessed through Allan deviation analysis. The excellent sensitivity translates into significantly increased measurement rates (0.2−2 kHz) of column-integrated N2O concentrations. This is complemented by swift horizontal beam-scanning to multiple reflectors positioned in a 4 × 4 grid over a 735 m2 probed area. Consequently, we achieve HRPM over the probed area with scan times as short as 9 s, marking a substantial 60-fold improvement compared to a recent benchmark in the field. The exceptional data update rate of our QCL based sensor, coupled with the rapid beam-scanning capabilities, lays the foundation for real-time generation of HRPM tomographic maps of gas concentration with scan cycles on the order of 1 s. This presents a powerful tool for expedited gas leak source localization, as well as understanding the spatial dynamics of area source emissions.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rodrigo, Peter John","Larsen, Henning Engelbrecht","Ashik, A. S.","Vechi, Nathalia T.","Kissas, Konstantinos","Fredenslund, Anders Michael","Scheutz, Charlotte","Pedersen, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759088"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rodrigo, Peter John"],"keyword":["Laser spectroscopy","Nitrous oxide"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast horizontal radial plume mapping of n sub 000000000002 sub o using open path absorption spectroscopy with a quantum cascade laser","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2024.120510","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759088","identifier":[{"id":"85190246616","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-66f0aaab-45b3-4e82-b2ee-e45cbf645036"],"keyword":["Gas mapping","Laser spectroscopy","Nitrous oxide","Standoff sensing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5D53DA74EAA9E6465BDD1DDF67A9506D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/357650024/1-s2.0-S1352231024001857-main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.atmosenv.2024.120510","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Electrical and Photonics Engineering, Optical Sensor Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter John","key":"rodrigopau","last":"Rodrigo","locid":"a8472768-87a5-415c-9bd7-a4901227ab0b","name":"Rodrigo, Peter John","orcid":"0000-0003-0819-2361","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"8725bc79-f382-439a-a827-540045c3eaf5","name":"Larsen, Henning Engelbrecht","name_org":"Larsen, Henning E.","orcid":"0000-0002-7715-8899","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.S.","key":"ashikpau","last":"Ashik","locid":"7e4617a8-1284-4629-8056-45795513aaa0","name":"Ashik, A. S.","name_org":"Ashik, A.S.","orcid":"0000-0002-6543-4702","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nathalia Thygsen","key":"vechipau","last":"Vechi","locid":"fea10dd7-921d-4625-9473-1096030038e2","name":"Vechi, Nathalia T.","name_org":"Vechi, Nathalia Thygsen","orcid":"0000-0002-7287-7616","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Konstantinos","key":"kissaspau","last":"Kissas","locid":"485f7f90-cf3b-4c60-8aef-da2ce81fe467","name":"Kissas, Konstantinos","orcid":"0000-0003-3869-7248","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Michael","key":"fredenslundpau","last":"Fredenslund","locid":"31c0d967-33a7-4b71-b520-f4a8645f1088","name":"Fredenslund, Anders Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-5196-688X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"scheutzpau","last":"Scheutz","locid":"48fe2850-fdc6-4282-9b97-ac5773419e5c","name":"Scheutz, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-2218-5934","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"0b6b3886-7ff9-4e3e-b906-32bd135d8aa1","name":"Pedersen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-7238-489X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.atmosenv.2024.120510","issn":["13522310","18782442"],"issn_org":["13522310"],"journal":"Atmospheric Environment","paperid":"120510","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Atmospheric Environment","volume":"328"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85190246616"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-66f0aaab-45b3-4e82-b2ee-e45cbf645036"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Fast horizontal radial plume mapping of N<sub>2</sub>O using open-path absorption spectroscopy with a quantum-cascade laser","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759088","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Evidence on how to improve daily physical activity (PA) levels following total knee arthroplasty (TKA) or medial uni-compartmental knee arthroplasty (mUKA) by motivational feedback is lacking. Moreover, it is unknown whether a focus on increased PA after discharge from the hospital improves rehabilitation, physical function, and quality of life. The aim of this randomized controlled trial (RCT) nested in a prospective cohort is (a) to investigate whether PA, physical function, and quality of life following knee replacement can be increased using an activity monitoring device including motivational feedback via a patient app in comparison with activity monitoring without feedback (care-as-usual), and (b) to investigate the potential predictive value of PA level prior to knee replacement for the length of stay, return to work, and quality of life. METHODS: The study is designed as a multicenter, parallel-group, superiority RCT with balanced randomization (1:1) and blinded outcome assessments. One hundred and fifty patients scheduled for knee replacement (TKA or mUKA) will be recruited through Odense University Hospital, Denmark, Vejle Hospital, Denmark and Herlev/Gentofte Sygehus, Denmark. Patients will be randomized to either 12 weeks of activity monitoring and motivational feedback via a patient app by gamification or 'care-as-usual,' including activity monitoring without motivational feedback. The primary outcome is the between-group change score from baseline to 12-week follow-up of cumulative daily accelerometer counts, which is a valid proxy for average objectively assessed daily PA. DISCUSSION: Improving PA through motivational feedback following knee replacement surgery might improve post-surgical function, health-related quality of life, and participation in everyday life. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov, ID: NCT06005623. Registered on 2023-08-22. TRIAL STATUS: Recruiting.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Skov, Cecilie Dollerup","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Wiil, Uffe Kock","Varnum, Claus","Schmal, Hagen","Myhre Jensen, Charlotte","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-766164"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Skov, Cecilie Dollerup"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Freiburg"],"keyword":["Aged","App","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee","Denmark","Exercise","Female","Humans","Knee osteoarthritis","Male","Middle Aged","Motivation","Motivational Feedback","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life","RCT","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Recovery of Function"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of motivational feedback on levels of physical activity and quality of life by activity monitoring following knee arthroplasty surgery protocol for a randomized controlled trial nested in a prospective cohort knee activity","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-024-07878-0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-766164","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11448174","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39358699","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85205526798","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8fa8b59e-a705-49d4-a5a9-5de302f9ceb7"],"keyword":["Aged","App","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee","Denmark","Exercise","Female","Humans","Knee arthroplasty surgery","Knee osteoarthritis","Male","Middle Aged","Motivation","Motivational feedback","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life","RCT","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Recovery of Function"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A7456E57C4CC045CF8E10ECD4530E005"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/272897549/s12891-024-07878-0.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-024-07878-0","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Dollerup","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"62ddb8a5-b21c-4ec6-8fcc-3923a7a1db0c","name":"Skov, Cecilie Dollerup","orcid":"0000-0002-6063-7113","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Uffe Kock","key":"wiilpau","last":"Wiil","locid":"3c3acba0-f147-4923-8d16-48599c4bf797","name":"Wiil, Uffe Kock","orcid":"0000-0001-6898-4083","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"varnumpau","last":"Varnum","locid":"0f639544-4ebc-467c-a15b-3c049a26f62f","name":"Varnum, Claus","orcid":"0000-0002-0625-5691","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hagen","key":"schmalpau","last":"Schmal","name":"Schmal, Hagen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Myhre","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a084c1c8-fe75-45d5-93f8-3c37b71b732b","name":"Myhre Jensen, Charlotte","name_org":"Jensen, Charlotte Myhre","orcid":"0000-0002-7058-4641","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39358699"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12891-024-07878-0","issn":["14712474"],"journal":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","paperid":"778","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","volume":"25"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205526798"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8fa8b59e-a705-49d4-a5a9-5de302f9ceb7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of motivational feedback on levels of physical activity and quality of life by activity monitoring following knee arthroplasty surgery-protocol for a randomized controlled trial nested in a prospective cohort (Knee-Activity)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-766164","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: ActiMotus, a thigh-accelerometer-based software used for the classification of postures and movements (PaMs), has shown high accuracy among adults and school-aged children; however, its accuracy among younger children and potential differences between sexes are unknown. This study aimed to evaluate the accuracy of ActiMotus to measure PaMs among children between 3 and 14 years and to assess if this was influenced by the sex or age of children. METHOD: Forty-eight children attended a structured ~1-hour data collection session at a laboratory. Thigh acceleration was measured using a SENS accelerometer, which was classified into nine PaMs using the ActiMotus software. Human-coded video recordings of the session provided the ground truth. RESULTS: Based on both F1 scores and balanced accuracy, the highest levels of accuracy were found for lying, sitting, and standing (63.2-88.2%). For walking and running, accuracy measures ranged from 48.0 to 85.8%. The lowest accuracy was observed for classifying stair climbing. We found a higher accuracy for stair climbing among girls compared to boys and for older compared to younger age groups for walking, running, and stair climbing. CONCLUSIONS: ActiMotus could accurately detect lying, sitting, and standing among children. The software could be improved for classifying walking, running, and stair climbing, particularly among younger children.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Charlotte Lund","Hendry, Danica","Thomas, George","Beynon, Amber","Stearne, Sarah Michelle","Zabatiero, Juliana","Davey, Paul","Larsen, Jon Roslyng","Rohl, Andrew Lloyd","Straker, Leon","Campbell, Amity"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-781830"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["ARC Centre of Excellence for the Digital Child","All Global Affiliations","Curtin University","University of Queensland"],"keyword":["Accelerometry methods","Adolescent","Child","Child Preschool","Female","Humans","Male","Movement physiology","Nye teknologier","Posture physiology","Running physiology","Software","Walking physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of the actimotus software to accurately classify postures and movements in children aged 000000000003 000000000014","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s24206705","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-781830","identifier":[{"id":"85207443502","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39460185","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11510827","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["nfa-d123d2a7-dbbf-40b2-8d3b-9a691df5026c"],"keyword":["Accelerometry/methods","Adolescent","Child","Child, Preschool","Female","Humans","Male","Movement/physiology","Nye teknologier","Posture/physiology","Running/physiology","Software","Walking/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E485FBE9722A7CB8B10F54CF410E5D3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/s24206705","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"curtin university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Curtin University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"au","key":"arc centre of excellence for the digital child","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"ARC Centre of Excellence for the Digital Child","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Queensland","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-W