{"abstract":"Influenza A viruses (IAVs) originate from wild birds but have on several occasions jumped host barriers and are now also circulating in humans and mammals. The IAV host receptors (glycans with galactose linked to a sialic acid (SA) in an α2,3 or α2,6 linkage) are crucial host factors restricting inter-species transmission. In general, avian-origin IAVs show a preference for SA-α2,3 (avian receptor), whereas IAVs isolated from humans and pigs prefer SA-α2,6 (human receptor). N-acetylneuraminic acid (Neu5Ac) and N-glycolylneuraminic acid (Neu5Gc) are the two major SAs. Neu5Ac is expressed in all species, whereas Neu5Gc is only expressed in a limited number of domestic species such as pigs and horses, but not in humans. Despite that previous studies have shown that the IAV host receptor distribution appears to be similar in pigs and humans, none of these studies have investigated the expression of Neu5Gc-α2,6 in situ in porcine tissues. Thus, the aim of this study was to elucidate the distribution of IAV host receptors expressed in the porcine respiratory tract and relate the expression to the viral tropism of diverse host-adapted IAVs. The IAV receptor (SA-α2,3 and SA-α2,6) distribution and the presence of specifically Neu5Gc-α2,6 in the porcine nasal, tracheal, and lung tissues was investigated by lectin histochemistry. Furthermore, IAV immunohistochemistry was performed on tissues from pigs experimentally infected with IAVs, either adapted to pigs or humans, to investigate the significance of the IAV host receptors and the tropism of the diverse host-adapted IAVs. We document for the first time the expression of the avian receptor on the surface of the porcine nasal mucosa and an equal expression of Neu5Ac-α2,6 and Neu5Gc-α2,6 on the surface of the tracheal epithelium and alveoli. In all IAV-infected pigs, we found a low amount of IAV-positive cells in the trachea despite a high expression of the human receptor. Cumulatively, these findings suggest that optimal IAV replication involves a complex interplay between the viruses and their host receptors and that there might be other less clearly defined host factors that determine the site of replication.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kristensen, Charlotte","Larsen, Lars Erik","Trebbien, Ramona","Jensen, Henrik Elvang"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719204"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Influenza A virus","Pigs","Receptor","Sialic acid"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the avian influenza a virus receptor sa α000000000002 000000000003 gal is expressed in the porcine nasal mucosa sustaining the pig as a mixing vessel for new influenza viruses","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.virusres.2023.199304","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-719204","identifier":[{"id":"38142890","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85181827716","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10793167","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-084e6b84-ee71-42de-b21e-b16948ff1f6f"],"keyword":["Experimental infections","Host tropism","Influenza A virus","Pigs","Receptor","Sialic acid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A28D8EFDAE68F29DB25A5DD5736795EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.virusres.2023.199304","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381842590/The_avian_influenza_A_virus_receptor_SA_2_3_Gal_is_expressed_in_the_porcine_nasal_mucosa_sustaining_the_pig_as_a_mixing_vessel_for_new_influenza_viruses.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38142890"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.virusres.2023.199304","issn":["01681702","09212590"],"issn_org":["01681702"],"journal":"Virus Research","paperid":"199304","status":"p","title":"Virus Research","volume":"340"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85181827716"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-084e6b84-ee71-42de-b21e-b16948ff1f6f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The avian influenza A virus receptor SA-α2,3-Gal is expressed in the porcine nasal mucosa sustaining the pig as a mixing vessel for new influenza viruses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719204","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Patients with autoimmune disease may have impaired cancer survival. The aim was to investigate the association between autoimmune disease and ovarian cancer survival. Methods: From the Extreme study, we included women diagnosed with epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC) in Denmark during 1990–2014 (n = 11,870). Information on exposure and covariates was retrieved from nationwide registries. Using pseudo-values, we estimated absolute and relative 5- and 10-year survival probabilities with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) for autoimmune diseases combined and for the four most common individual disorders in our study population, namely type 1 diabetes, rheumatoid arthritis, Graves' disease, and inflammatory bowel disease. Results: The overall 5- and 10-year absolute survival probabilities were 35% and 24%, respectively, in women with EOC without autoimmune disease. Autoimmune diseases combined was not significantly associated with survival among women with EOC (5-year adjusted relative survival probability = 1.01, 95% CI: 0.94–1.09; 10-year adjusted relative survival probability = 0.90, 95% CI: 0.81–1.00). However, stratification by disease stage showed an impaired 10-year survival in women with autoimmune disease and a localized EOC (relative survival probability = 0.86, 95% CI: 0.76–0.97). None of the individual autoimmune diseases were statistically significantly associated with EOC survival. Conclusions: Only among women with localized EOC, there seemed to be a long-term survival loss associated with a history of autoimmune disease. In contrast, no significant association between a history of autoimmune disease and survival was observed in women with nonlocalized EOC where the survival is already low.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","Kjaer, Susanne K.","Galanakis, Michael","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Maltesen, Thomas","Baandrup, Louise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719576"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autoimmune disease","Cohort study","Long term survival","Nationwide","Ovarian cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"history of autoimmune disease and long term survival of epithelial ovarian cancer the extreme study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-719576","identifier":[{"id":"85183053810","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38246041","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-23c4d81a-b525-4af6-8e9c-74e3c9895655"],"keyword":["Autoimmune disease","Cohort study","Long-term survival","Nationwide","Ovarian cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-64912EC48EA28A2B4C01D2FA958533D0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Gerd","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","name":"Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"galanakispau","last":"Galanakis","name":"Galanakis, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum-Larsen","name":"Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"maltesenpau","last":"Maltesen","locid":"079f181f-c4c5-401e-8190-0da5c869f53b","name":"Maltesen, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","name":"Baandrup, Louise","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38246041"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ygyno.2023.12.024","issn":["00908258","10956859"],"issn_org":["00908258"],"journal":"Gynecologic Oncology","status":"p","title":"Gynecologic Oncology","volume":"182"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183053810"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-23c4d81a-b525-4af6-8e9c-74e3c9895655"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"History of autoimmune disease and long-term survival of epithelial ovarian cancer : The extreme study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719576","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Det kan man faktisk, hvis man bruger information fra vores nabolande og tager højde for sygdomstilfælde tæt på Danmarks grænser.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjær, Lene Jung","Boklund, Anette","Kirkeby, Carsten","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-731167"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kan man forudsige fugleinfluenza i danmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://videnskab.dk/kultur-samfund/kan-man-forudsige-fugleinfluenza-i-danmark/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-731167","ids":["ku-54275d40-b4d8-4f08-86fd-293c54083643"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4F6C10953BDFE416BC014199B3F387A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://videnskab.dk/kultur-samfund/kan-man-forudsige-fugleinfluenza-i-danmark/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Animal Welfare and Disease Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Jung","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"b93ddd14-b340-4550-b3cf-eb9473b0d716","name":"Kjær, Lene Jung","orcid":"0000-0001-9659-4672","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette Ella","key":"boklundpau","last":"Boklund","locid":"b56cee2e-0320-4c3d-a360-6dc1f5b2ee67","name":"Boklund, Anette","name_org":"Boklund, Anette Ella","orcid":"0000-0001-6359-3403","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"kirkebypau","last":"Kirkeby","locid":"ea24c9a4-7aa6-40f3-9afb-0af19f1e962d","name":"Kirkeby, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-9292-5526","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["ku-54275d40-b4d8-4f08-86fd-293c54083643"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Kan man forudsige fugleinfluenza i Danmark?","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-731167","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Umbilical outpouchings (UOs) are common in Danish pigs. Neonatal antibiotics are therefore used with the hope of reducing umbilical infections and subsequently UOs. However, the effect of neonatal antibiotics on preventing UO has been the subject of mixed conclusions, and secondly, treating all animals with antibiotics might exacerbate the development of antimicrobial resistance. This study analysed the effects of different treatments on the prevalence of umbilical outpouchings and mortality from birth to nursery unit. All treatment was on the day of birth. The groups were: a negative control group, an antibiotic group receiving amoxicillin, and an experimental group where the piglets had their umbilical cord disinfected with chlorhexidine, followed by tying and clipping, and lastly, injection with meloxicam. The pigs were examined six weeks after weaning, and all pigs that died during the study were autopsied. Results: There were 5494 pigs divided across the three groups. There were no statistically significant differences in UO prevalence between the groups: control 3.9%, antibiotic 4.2%, and experimental 4.0% (p = 0.87). The only variable affecting the prevalence of UOs in this study was sex with females being at higher risk. There were no statistically significant differences in mortality between the groups from birth until departure from the nursery unit: control 22.9%, antibiotic 21%, and experimental 21.4% (p = 0.33). The variables affecting mortality were sex, intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR), birth weight, and cross fostering. Males had higher odds of dying, as had piglets recorded with some degree of IUGR. Also, low birth weight increased the odds of dying for all weight quartiles compared to the fourth (the heaviest piglets > 1.6 kg), as well as cross fostering increased the odds ratio of dying. Conclusions: This study found no significant differences in the prevalence of UOs and mortality following different treatments at birth. The study showed that the prevalence of UO and mortality was not reduced following the administration of amoxicillin or meloxicam in combination with disinfection and tying of the umbilical cord.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Marie Louise","Larsen, Inge","Jensen, Tina Birk","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Pedersen, Ken Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-732472"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Amoxicillin","Antibiotics","Chlorhexidine","Disinfection","NSAID","Pigs","Prevention","Umbilical outpouchings"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevention of umbilical outpouchings and mortality in pigs meloxicam tying cutting and chlorhexidine versus amoxicillin or no treatment a clinical field trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-024-00358-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-732472","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10874036","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85185286783","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38365774","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d2135115-5b94-4fd7-a787-16956c50e7f9"],"keyword":["Amoxicillin","Antibiotics","Chlorhexidine","Disinfection","Meloxicam","NSAID","Pigs","Prevention","Umbilical outpouchings"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-09EFD1E27942E2564422287AAB31DAC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385219185/s40813_024_00358_w.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-024-00358-w","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Ø-Vet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Louise","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d4e731e0-3535-4e5b-92b3-857d21d575fc","name":"Hansen, Marie Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"82b09bf9-73d5-4c71-a3c1-01e66b0e9ebe","name":"Larsen, Inge","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-2241","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tina Birk","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Tina Birk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38365774"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40813-024-00358-w","issn":["20555660"],"journal":"Porcine Health Management","paperid":"10","status":"p","title":"Porcine Health Management","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85185286783"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","ø-vet a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d2135115-5b94-4fd7-a787-16956c50e7f9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prevention of umbilical outpouchings and mortality in pigs : Meloxicam, tying, cutting, and chlorhexidine versus amoxicillin or no treatment? A clinical field trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-732472","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Use of menopausal hormone therapy (MHT) prior to an epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC) diagnosis has been suggested to be associated with improved survival. In a recent nationwide cohort study, we found that prediagnostic long-term MHT use, especially estrogen therapy (ET), was associated with improved long-term survival in women with nonlocalized EOC. Our aim was to investigate the influence of prediagnostic MHT use on long-term survival among women with localized EOC in the same nationwide study. Our study cohort comprised all women aged 50 years or older with an EOC diagnosis in Denmark 2000–2014 (n = 2097) identified from the Extreme study. We collected information on usage of systemic ET and estrogen plus progestin therapy (EPT) from the Danish National Prescription Registry. By using pseudo-values, 5- and 10-year absolute and relative survival probabilities were estimated with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) while adjusting for histology, comorbidity, and income. Relative survival probabilities >1 indicate better survival. The 5-year absolute survival probabilities were 61% and 56%, respectively, among women who were nonusers and users of prediagnostic MHT, whereas these numbers were 46% and 41%, respectively, regarding 10-year survival. Use of MHT was not significantly associated with an improved 5- or 10-year survival in women with localized EOC (5-year relative survival probability = 0.95, 95% CI: 0.89–1.02; 10-year relative survival probability = 0.92, 95% CI: 0.84–1.02). Similar findings were seen for systemic ET or EPT use. Our findings do not suggest a positive benefit from prediagnostic MHT use on long-term survival of localized EOC.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Duus, Alberte Hjorth","Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","Baandrup, Louise","Zheng, Guoqiao","Galanakis, Michael","Maltesen, Thomas","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Mørch, Lina S.","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-738922"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Long term survival","Menopausal hormone therapy","Ovarian cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prediagnostic use of menopausal hormone therapy and long term survival of localized epithelial ovarian cancer the extreme study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-738922","identifier":[{"id":"38532545","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85189549465","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-35452527-f0ce-42c1-86c1-1e9dd4e14d94"],"keyword":["long-term survival","menopausal hormone therapy","ovarian cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A9E8896A10D2D2FEE528EDDD1660EDFB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alberte Hjorth","key":"duuspau","last":"Duus","name":"Duus, Alberte Hjorth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Gerd","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","name":"Hannibal, Charlotte Gerd","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Louise","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","locid":"abccf449-8bed-4f98-bb4d-012134523360","name":"Baandrup, Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Guoqiao","key":"zhengpau","last":"Zheng","name":"Zheng, Guoqiao","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"galanakispau","last":"Galanakis","name":"Galanakis, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"maltesenpau","last":"Maltesen","name":"Maltesen, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum-Larsen","name":"Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lina S.","key":"mørchpau","last":"Mørch","name":"Mørch, Lina S.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38532545"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.34936","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"19-26","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"155"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189549465"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-35452527-f0ce-42c1-86c1-1e9dd4e14d94"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Prediagnostic use of menopausal hormone therapy and long-term survival of localized epithelial ovarian cancer : The Extreme study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-738922","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Population-based data on the epidemiology of vulvar lichen sclerosus (LS) are sparse and only few prospective studies have investigated the malignant potential of the disease. We used the nationwide Danish Pathology Registry to first assess the incidence of biopsy-verified vulvar LS in the period 1997–2022 and second to examine the incidence of vulvar high-grade squamous precancer and squamous cell carcinoma (SCC) in women with biopsy-verified vulvar LS (1978–2019) compared with that expected in the general female population. For the latter aim, we computed standardized incidence ratios (SIRs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs). During our study period, the age-standardized incidence rate of vulvar LS increased from 5.0 (1997–1998) to 35.7 (2021–2022) per 100,000 person-years. Compared with the general female population, women with biopsy-verified vulvar LS had significantly increased rates of vulvar high-grade squamous precancer (SIR = 8.5; 95% CI: 7.2–10.0) and SCC (SIR = 16.2; 95% CI: 14.2–18.4). The SIRs of vulvar high-grade squamous precancer and SCC did not vary substantially according to length of follow-up. This nationwide and population-based study shows a 7-fold increase in the incidence of biopsy-verified vulvar LS since 1997. Data also show that women with biopsy-verified vulvar LS have 8.5 and 16 times higher than expected incidence of vulvar high-grade squamous precancer and SCC, respectively. The substantially increased incidence of vulvar high-grade squamous precancer and SCC following LS is important in relation to the clinical management and follow-up of LS patients.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Baandrup, Louise","Hannibal, Charlotte G.","Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747798"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Incidence","Lichen sclerosus","Risk","Vulvar cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biopsy verified vulvar lichen sclerosus incidence trends 000000001997 000000002022 and increased risk of vulvar squamous precancer and squamous cell carcinoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.34927","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747798","identifier":[{"id":"85189105747","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38517074","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-3560833e-3aeb-4699-ad29-0bf2592a5c3b"],"keyword":["incidence","lichen sclerosus","risk","vulvar cancer","vulvar precancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2FD23B083CF1A23C6B4046542BB8074C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.34927","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/394987113/Intl_Journal_of_Cancer_2024_Baandrup_Biopsy_verified_vulvar_lichen_sclerosus_Incidence_trends_1997_2022_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Louise","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","locid":"abccf449-8bed-4f98-bb4d-012134523360","name":"Baandrup, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte G.","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","name":"Hannibal, Charlotte G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum-Larsen","name":"Hertzum-Larsen, Rasmus","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1 4","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","name_org":"Kjær, Susanne K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38517074"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.34927","issn":["00207136"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"501-507","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"155"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85189105747"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hosp