{"abstract":"This article presents comprehensive validation of specific sea state parameters (SSPs) and synthetic aperture radar (SAR)-derived wind speeds ( ${{u}_{\\text{SAR}}}$ ). The article introduces a novel approach to retrieving roughness length ( ${{z}_0}$ ) based on wave steepness, following the retrieval of the short wavelengths necessary to estimate ${{z}_0}$ . The SAR onboard the Sentinel-1 (S1) satellite that was used specifically in the interferometric wide swath mode (IW) data. The data were processed using the extended version of CWAVE (CWAVE_EX) algorithm for SSPs and CMOD5 for ${{u}_{\\text{SAR}}}$ . CWAVE_EX was developed especially for coastal waters; the processing chain includes steps for SAR image denoising and eliminating image artifacts. SAR S-1 data inherently exhibit a substantial azimuthal cutoff length due to the data's high satellite altitude and SAR IW resolution. That complicates the retrieving of short wavelengths prevalent in coastal zones and needed to retrieve ${{z}_0}$ . The article focuses on the coastal seas of the USA, benefiting from the presence of an extensive network of ocean buoys for validation purposes. The complete SAR S1 A/B archive from 2014 to 2022 was first processed to retrieve SSPs and ${{u}_{\\text{SAR}}}$ . The validation for significant wave height ( ${{H}_s}$ ), second moment wave period ( ${{T}_{m2}}$ ), and ${{u}_{\\text{SAR}}}$ was performed using in-situ measurements with about 6000 collocations. ${{H}_s}$ and ${{T}_{m2}}$ were compared against the corresponding parameters from hindcast spectral numerical model data with about 380 000 collocations. The comparisons between the retrieved ${{H}_s}$ and ${{T}_{m2}}$ against the in-situ observations and hindcast wave model data yielded a root mean square error (RMSE) of 0.46–0.50 m and 0.9–1.1 s. The RMSE of ${{u}_{\\text{SAR}}}$ against in-situ observation was about 2 m/s with a bias of 0.78 m/s. The estimated ${{z}_0}$ values from satellite-driven wave parameters were highly correlated with the ${{z}_0}$ estimated from the in-situ observations, with an RMSE of 0.04 × 10 −3 m and a bias of −0.01 × 10 −3 m. The article highlights the possibility of using SAR remote sensing data for global mapping of ${{z}_0}$ , including coastal effects of local variability in sea state and wind field gustiness.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Owda, Abdalmenem","Pleskachevsky, Andrey","Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","Badger, Merete","Cavar, Dalibor","Hasager, Charlotte Bay"],"cuid":["S02-091.67-768051"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Owda, Abdalmenem"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Aerospace Center","German Aerospace Center (DLR)"],"keyword":["Air sea interaction","Extended version of CWAVE CWAVE EX","Geophysical model function","Geophysical model function GMF","Integrated sea state parameter SSP","JONSWAP","Joint North Sea Wave Project JONSWAP","Neutral stratified wind","Roughness length","SAR","Synthetic aperture radar SAR"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of sar based sea state parameters and roughness length derivation over the coastal seas of the united states","src":["cbs","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/JSTARS.2024.3393862","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.67-768051","identifier":[{"id":"85192173945","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["cbs-1d8a4b64-4a4c-4bd6-adf5-a8f398dc85d5","dtu-539218df-99f4-49d6-a4c7-c0ab1a5c403b"],"keyword":["Air-sea interaction","CWAVE_EX","Extended version of CWAVE (CWAVE_EX)","Geophysical model function","Geophysical model function (GMF)","Integrated sea state parameter","Integrated sea state parameter (SSP)","JONSWAP","Joint North Sea Wave Project (JONSWAP)","Neutral stratified wind","Roughness length","SAR","Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DB8FE85C591139685A9BBCF0FBAAC59F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/110672379/Evaluation_of_SAR-Based_Sea_State_Parameters_and_Roughness_Length_Derivation_Over_the_Coastal_Seas_of_the_USA.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/JSTARS.2024.3393862","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/361354121/Evaluation_of_SAR-Based_Sea_State_Parameters_and_Roughness_Length_Derivation_Over_the_Coastal_Seas_of_the_USA.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind and Energy Systems","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Wind and Energy Systems, Wind Energy Systems Division"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"german aerospace center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Aerospace Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Educational Development and Quality"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Abdalmenem","key":"owdapau","last":"Owda","locid":"4bda8a00-62bb-4ece-972b-47264959f08e","name":"Owda, Abdalmenem","orcid":"0000-0002-7758-533X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrey","key":"pleskachevskypau","last":"Pleskachevsky","name":"Pleskachevsky, Andrey","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Xiaoli Guo","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"b4f442ea-5cb6-4979-b106-e210895b35d8","name":"Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","name_org":"Larsen, Xiaoli Guo","orcid":"0000-0001-8696-0720","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Merete","key":"badgerpau","last":"Badger","locid":"0493bb98-dd30-4b8d-8540-c3889c8a4e55","name":"Badger, Merete","orcid":"0000-0002-2072-8619","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dalibor","key":"cavarpau","last":"Cavar","locid":"f6a40a2d-351c-4e22-bd26-dccb90c92040","name":"Cavar, Dalibor","orcid":"0000-0003-1446-2866","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"hasagerpau","last":"Hasager","locid":"cf82626c-41b3-42c5-b289-42b5f2dc6f1f","name":"Hasager, Charlotte Bay","name_org":"Hasager, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-2124-5651","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/jstars.2024.3393862","issn":["19391404","21511535"],"issn_org":["19391404"],"journal":"IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Applied Earth Observations and Remote Sensing","pages":"9415-9428","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"IEEE Journal of Selected Topics in Applied Earth Observations and Remote Sensing","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85192173945"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-1d8a4b64-4a4c-4bd6-adf5-a8f398dc85d5","dtu-539218df-99f4-49d6-a4c7-c0ab1a5c403b"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Evaluation of SAR-based Sea State Parameters and Roughness Length Derivation over the Coastal Seas of the United States","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.67-768051","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Older patients receiving antineoplastic treatment face challenges such as frailty and reduced physical capacity and function. This systematic review and meta-analysis aimed to evaluate the effects of exercise interventions on physical function outcomes, health-related quality of life (QoL), and symptom burden in older patients above 65 years with hematological malignancies undergoing antineoplastic treatment. This review adheres to Cochrane guidelines, with the literature searches last updated on 27 March 2024, including studies with patients above 18 years. Screening of identified studies, data extraction, risk of bias, and GRADE assessments were performed independently by two authors. Meta-analyses evaluated the impact of exercise, considering advancing age. Forty-nine studies contributed data to the meta-analyses. Five studies included patients with a mean age above 60 years, and none included only patients above 60. Exercise interventions had moderate to small positive effects on QoL global (SMD 0.34, 95% CI [0.04–0.64]) and physical function (SMD 0.29, 95% CI [0.12–0.45]). Age did not explain the variability in exercise effects, except for physical function (slope 0.0401, 95% CI [0.0118–0.0683]) and pain (slope 0.0472, 95% CI [0.01–0.09]), which favored younger patients. Exercise interventions improve physical function and QoL and reduce symptoms in adults with hematological malignancies undergoing antineoplastic treatment; however, the influence of age remains inconclusive.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Jarden, Mary","Lindholm, Sofie Tscherning","Kaldan, Gudrun","Grønset, Charlotte","Larsen, Rikke Faebo","Larsen, Anders Thyge Steen","Engedal, Mette Schaufuss","Mikkelsen, Marta Kramer","Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","Vinther, Anders","Abildgaard, Niels","Tolver, Anders","Juhl, Carsten Bogh"],"cuid":["S02-092.36-762002"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Jarden, Mary"],"keyword":["Aerobic capacity","Exercise","Health related quality of life","Hematological malignancy","Older patients","Physical function","Strength","Symptoms"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"limited evidence for the benefits of exercise in older adults with hematological malignancies a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers16172962","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.36-762002","identifier":[{"id":"39272820","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85203659997","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11393877","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-816c0599-9201-4b29-9196-b0d20a037b87","sdu-f5ca6ea8-ff7e-4373-8abf-9200a6846cd6"],"keyword":["aerobic capacity","exercise","health-related quality of life","hematological malignancy","older patients","physical function","strength","symptoms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DDF6DFC164C1203CB76FDB29B9200322"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers16172962","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/405558064/cancers_16_02962.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/272511071/cancers-16-02962.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Haematology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Haematology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Mary","key":"jardenmarypau","last":"Jarden","locid":"f716d3db-6f75-41b0-94a0-884f7dcd1259","name":"Jarden, Mary","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sofie Tscherning","key":"lindholmsofietscherningpau","last":"Lindholm","name":"Lindholm, Sofie Tscherning","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie","key":"tscherninglindholmsofiepau","last":"Tscherning Lindholm","name":"Tscherning Lindholm, Sofie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gudrun","key":"kaldangudrunpau","last":"Kaldan","name":"Kaldan, Gudrun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte","key":"grønsetcharlottepau","last":"Grønset","name":"Grønset, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"larsenrikkefaebopau","last":"Faebo Larsen","locid":"bf1f2354-216f-47ed-ac3a-92021a7f2e24","name":"Larsen, Rikke Faebo","name_org":"Faebo Larsen, Rikke","orcid":"0000-0003-3444-2774","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders Thyge Steen","key":"larsenandersthygesteenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anders Thyge Steen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mette Schaufuss","key":"engedalmetteschaufusspau","last":"Engedal","name":"Engedal, Mette Schaufuss","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"schaufussengedalmettepau","last":"Schaufuss Engedal","name":"Schaufuss Engedal, Mette","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marta Kramer","key":"mikkelsenmartakramerpau","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Marta Kramer","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marta","key":"kramermikkelsenmartapau","last":"Kramer Mikkelsen","name":"Kramer Mikkelsen, Marta","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Dorte","key":"nielsendortelisbetpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8bd14092-b1da-4f24-b4db-d31d38f5f1b7","name":"Nielsen, Dorte Lisbet","name_org":"Nielsen, Dorte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"vintheranderspau","last":"Vinther","name":"Vinther, Anders","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"abildgaardnielspau","last":"Abildgaard","locid":"595418b9-29f8-4fd3-8663-1b32eab3451a","name":"Abildgaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-6852-2014","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Anders","key":"tolveranderspau","last":"Tolver","name":"Tolver, Anders","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten","key":"juhlcarstenboghpau","last":"Bogh Juhl","locid":"9381fad1-5721-4b98-ac99-7df1c6e4d837","name":"Juhl, Carsten Bogh","name_org":"Bogh Juhl, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-8456-5364","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39272820"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/cancers16172962","issn":["20726694"],"issue":"17","journal":"Cancers","paperid":"2962","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Cancers","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85203659997"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-816c0599-9201-4b29-9196-b0d20a037b87","sdu-f5ca6ea8-ff7e-4373-8abf-9200a6846cd6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Limited Evidence for the Benefits of Exercise in Older Adults with Hematological Malignancies : A Systematic Review and Meta-Analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.36-762002","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Three trace elements in human bones permit the delineation of temporal and social variability among medieval to early modern Danes in what they ate (strontium, Sr) and whether they lived in an urban or non-urban setting (lead, Pb; copper, Cu). The chemical composition of bones from 332 children (5 to 12 years old) buried in 51 Danish cemeteries was estimated through Inductively Coupled Plasma Mass Spectrometry (ICP-MS). Children provide a local chemical signal because they were less likely than adults to have moved from one place to another. There was no age effect on trace element concentrations. Geographical variability in trace element concentrations was highly localized, so the three elements, individually or collectively, cannot be used to identify where in Denmark people originated. Diets and exposure to sources of Pb and Cu, however, did not remain constant over time. Trace element concentrations show that the life experiences of people from towns differed from their rural counterparts. While most apparent with Pb and Cu, it is also true of Sr until urban and rural diets converged in the early modern period.Keywords: Historic Denmark; Bioavailable trace elements; Social variation; Temporal variation; Human skeletons; ICP-MS","author_count":39,"contributors":["Boldsen, Jesper Lier","Dangvard Pedersen, Dorthe","Milner, George R.","Kristensen, Vicki Rytoft Lillegaard","Skytte, Lilian","Møller, Stig Bergmann","Sarauw, Torben Birk","Andersen, Charlotte Boje Hilligsø","Larsen, Lars Agersnap","Hyldgaard, Inger Marie","Klingenberg, Mette","Larsen, Lars Krants","Mollerup, Lene","Seberg, Lone","Bentsen, Lars Christian","Søvsø, Morten","Kristensen, Tenna","Christensen, Jakob Tue","Heide, Poul Baltzer","Nørgaard, Lone C.","Uldum, Otto","Engberg, Niels","Simonsen, Rikke","Dahlstrøm, Hanna","Langkilde, Jesper","Wickman, Niels","Hansen, Palle Birk","Wille-Jørgensen, Dorthe","Stjernqvist, Kasper Wurr","Rasmussen, Anders","Rasmussen, Kaare Lund"],"cuid":["S02-096.40-735605"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Boldsen, Jesper Lier"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Anthropology, Pennsylvania State University, USA","The Pennsylvania State University"],"keyword":["Human Skeletons","ICP MS","Social variation","Temporal variation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"],"OT":["Roskilde Museum"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variation in bioavailable lead copper and strontium concentrations in human skeletons from medieval to early modern denmark","src":["kum","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaa.2024.101587","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Many institutions granted access to the skeletal remains examined here, as detailed in Table 1 and the Supplemental Information . This research was supported by a grant from DFF – FKK: 6107-00284B."],"id":"S02-096.40-735605","identifier":[{"id":"85186598072","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kum-4f82d25d-066c-4fde-8f89-352051280904","sdu-8c0a8a75-ac1d-435d-8abe-87424821d21d"],"keyword":["Bioavailable trace elements","Historic Denmark","Human skeletons","ICP-MS","Social variation","Temporal variation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E566CF4C6A355558584D6EA848FFCF96"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaa.2024.101587","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearc