{"abstract":"It is well known that N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor encephalitis (NMDARE) can be triggered by infectious encephalitis such as herpes simplex virus 1 encephalitis (HSE). However, the incidence of post-HSE NMDARE in Denmark is unknown. We reviewed literature cases and compared these to retrospectively identified cases of post-HSE NMDARE in Denmark, using a national cohort database of autoimmune encephalitis (AE) and two regional databases of infectious encephalitis patients. We identified 80 post-HSE NMDARE cases in the literature, 66% being children, who more often presented movement disorders, decreased consciousness, and sleep disturbances compared to adults. Eight patients with post-HSE NMDARE were identified from the national cohort database of AE, none being children. Forty-four HSE patients were identified from the regional infectious encephalitis databases. Of these, 16 (36%) fulfilled the Graus criteria for probable/definite NMDARE, and eight (18%) presented a prolonged/relapsing disease course. Ten (23%) were tested for AE during hospitalization. Six (14%) had leftover cerebrospinal fluid available for retrospective autoantibody testing. One out of these six patients (17%) harbored NMDARE antibodies. Thus, in total, nine post-HSE NMDARE patients have been identified in Denmark from 2009 to 2021. Comparing the adult Danish patients to the literature, Danish patients were older, but the clinical phenotype and paraclinical findings were similar. Overall, the incidence of adult post-HSE NMDARE in the Region of Southern Denmark was 0.17 per million people per year and only 7% of adult HSE patients in the region were diagnosed with post-HSE NMDARE. Our findings suggest that adult patients are still underdiagnosed and the absence of pediatric cases diagnosed with post-HSE NMDARE in Denmark is highly concerning.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Magnussen, Anna Søgaard","Aaberg-Jessen, Charlotte","Belhouche, Nadia Zeeberg","Thybo, Alberte","Hovet, Siv Tonje Faret","Larsen, Lykke","Nilsson, Anna Christine","Blaabjerg, Morten","Nissen, Mette Scheller"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-761052"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nissen, Mette Scheller"],"keyword":["Autoimmune encephalitis","Viral encephalitis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"post herpetic anti nmdar encephalitis in denmark current status and future challenges","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines12091953","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-761052","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11429063","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85205055583","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39335467","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-8577d31e-c65c-4a72-952e-b8c00a729f14"],"keyword":["N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor encephalitis","autoimmune encephalitis","herpes simplex virus 1 Encephalitis","post-viral autoimmune encephalitis","viral encephalitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51B58AB9E64E7E8A2671051D8D7B8D7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/270230667/biomedicines-12-01953-v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines12091953","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"925dfab0-2757-4e05-a98b-07abaa125613","name":"Magnussen, Anna Søgaard","name_org":"Søgaard, Anna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Aaberg","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"1498c754-add7-41ce-90c9-1e24c1265a50","name":"Aaberg-Jessen, Charlotte","name_org":"Poulsen, Charlotte Aaberg","orcid":"0000-0003-1407-7976","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia Zeeberg","key":"belhouchepau","last":"Belhouche","locid":"29b6c72e-0678-40d6-8388-903cd82b45d6","name":"Belhouche, Nadia Zeeberg","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alberte","key":"thybopau","last":"Thybo","locid":"1d2939ed-dc57-4672-af96-5c24f73815e0","name":"Thybo, Alberte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Siv Tonje Faret","key":"hovetpau","last":"Hovet","locid":"a8f90727-5057-4722-94b8-a7eca897c205","name":"Hovet, Siv Tonje Faret","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lykke","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f4fd0451-0508-4d78-8726-1e63c7620925","name":"Larsen, Lykke","orcid":"0000-0002-4113-4182","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"81fc45b9-6c7e-44aa-8c4f-7c02ef163a1c","name":"Nilsson, Anna Christine","name_org":"Nilsson, Christine","orcid":"0000-0001-7885-8400","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"blaabjergpau","last":"Blaabjerg","locid":"2f89b837-7700-412e-a8da-141258f1673f","name":"Blaabjerg, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-6007-1861","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Scheller","key":"nissenpau","last":"Nissen","locid":"1e773fc7-1dc8-40da-bff0-b867bafe0440","name":"Nissen, Mette Scheller","orcid":"0000-0002-3512-3479","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39335467"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/biomedicines12091953","issn":["22279059"],"issue":"9","journal":"Biomedicines","paperid":"1953","publisher":"MDPI","status":"p","title":"Biomedicines","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205055583"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8577d31e-c65c-4a72-952e-b8c00a729f14"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Post-Herpetic Anti-NMDAR Encephalitis in Denmark: Current Status and Future Challenges","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-761052","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Poor mental health among youth in Greenland is a major challenge, childhood conditions are critical for mental health later in life. The study aimed to examine the clustering of childhood conditions by considering risk and protective factors for mental health among youth and young adults in Greenland and to explore the relationship between these clusters and mental health outcomes in youth. The study included 565 participants aged 15–34 living in Greenland. Seven indicators including childhood adversities (ACEs), childhood residence, language, and cultural indicators (protective factors) were used to define clusters via latent class analysis (LCA). The associations between clusters and mental health outcomes (satisfaction with life (Cantrill’s ladder), self-esteem, self-efficacy, loneliness, psychological distress (General Health Questionnaire) and mental illness (Kessler 6)) were assessed by logistic regression. Four clusters were identified through LCA. While most participants reported positive childhoods, 40% (in two clusters) experienced ACEs. The two clusters differed as more participants in one cluster had experienced protective factors than the other. ACEs were associated with increased odds of negative aspects of mental health in youth. However, participants who faced high levels of adversity and few protective factors also had reduced odds of positive aspects of mental health in youth.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ottendahl, Charlotte Brandstrup","Bjerregaard, Peter","Svartá, Durita Lyngsø","Sørensen, Ivalu","Olesen, Ingelise","Nielsen, Martine Stecher","Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765968"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ottendahl, Charlotte Brandstrup"],"country":["Greenland","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Grønlands Universitet","Norwegian University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Childhood conditions","Greenland","Inuit","Mental health","Risk and protective factors","Youth"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"childhood conditions and mental health among youth and young adults in greenland a latent class analysis","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/22423982.2024.2400397","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765968","identifier":[{"id":"85204418992","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11407376","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39283055","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-2f4abbdc-80eb-4ec8-8f73-e0f3fd8e65a0"],"keyword":["Childhood conditions","Greenland","Inuit","mental health","risk and protective factors","youth"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F58F3B3F1862180084522CA1A5E7E1E9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/22423982.2024.2400397","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/272668169/Childhood_conditions_and_mental_health_among_youth_and_young_adults_in_Greenland_a_latent_class_analysis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Center for Public health in Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"grønlands universitet","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Grønlands Universitet","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"norwegian university of science and technology","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian University of Science and Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Brandstrup","key":"ottendahlpau","last":"Ottendahl","locid":"9e2ae085-ebf8-4688-b8cf-c257c5458aca","name":"Ottendahl, Charlotte Brandstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-9285-3099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","locid":"ef4a2fa7-9735-4b1e-a4fa-b1272def2cfc","name":"Bjerregaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7153-8447","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Durita Lyngsø","key":"svartápau","last":"Svartá","locid":"7d14a946-3c39-479f-9e88-0b5c3061f8e5","name":"Svartá, Durita Lyngsø","orcid":"0000-0002-8931-8386","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ivalu Katajavaara","key":"seidlerpau","last":"Seidler","locid":"5e19e227-e860-49db-af28-67b29e038c9c","name":"Sørensen, Ivalu","name_org":"Seidler, Ivalu Katajavaara","orcid":"0000-0002-4956-6326","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingelise","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Ingelise","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Martine Stecher","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Martine Stecher","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Viskum Lytken","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3ee738b1-09d1-4886-9ddf-67ca132997fe","name":"Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken","orcid":"0000-0002-6245-4222","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39283055"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/22423982.2024.2400397","issn":["12399736","22423982"],"issn_org":["12399736"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Circumpolar Health","paperid":"2400397","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Circumpolar Health","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204418992"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2f4abbdc-80eb-4ec8-8f73-e0f3fd8e65a0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Childhood conditions and mental health among youth and young adults in Greenland : a latent class analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765968","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Periprosthetic knee fractures (PPKFs) following total knee arthroplasty (TKA) are uncommon, but potentially serious injuries. We analyze the risk and risk factors for a PPKF in standard primary TKA patients who have osteoarthritis and a minimally (cruciate-retaining TKAs without a femoral box cut) or posterior-stabilized TKA. In addition, we report the risk for patients who have other underlying knee disorders and/or a higher level of TKA constraint. Methods: All primary TKAs were identified from the Danish National Patient Register and the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register using data between 1997 and 2022. Subsequent fractures were identified through the International Classification of Diseases diagnosis code, Nordic Medico-Statistical Committee procedure code, or indication for revision TKA. Results: We included 120,642 standard primary TKA patients who had 1,659 PPKFs. The cumulated proportions were 0.4% (95% confidence interval (CI) 0.3 to 0.4) at 2 years 0.8% (0.7 to 0.8) at 5 years. At 10 years, the cumulated proportion was 1.7% (1.6 to 1.8), with 1.3% in the femur, 0.2% in the patella, and 0.2% in the tibia. Significant risk factors were (hazard ratio [HR] [95% CI]); ipsilateral hip arthroplasty (2.3 [2.0 to 2.6]); women (2.1 [1.8 to 2.4]), osteoporosis (1.4 [1.2 to 1.7]); age 80+ (1.4 [1.3 to 1.6]), uncemented TKA (1.3 (1.1 to 1.5) and Charlson Comorbidity Index score 3+ (1.4 [1.1 to 1.8]). An additional 22,624 primary TKA patients who had other underlying knee disorders and/or a higher level of implant constraint were included with 633 PPKFs. The 10-year cumulated proportions were 8.3% (95% CI 6.9 to 9.8) when the underlying disorder was a previous fracture, 2.8% (2.2 to 3.5) for rheumatic disorders, and 5.2% (2.6 to 10.6) for osteonecrosis. In patients who had condylar constrained knees, it was 6.9% (5.1 to 9.4), and 12.4% (8.0 to 16.04) for hinges. Conclusions: In standard primary TKA patients, the 10-year cumulated proportion of PPKFs was 1.7%, and ipsilateral hip arthroplasty, women, osteoporosis, advanced age, uncemented TKA and higher Charlson Comorbidity Index increased the risk. Higher risks were observed in non-osteoarthritis patients and/or patients who had a higher level of TKA constraint.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Risager, Stefan Kastalag","Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Abrahamsen, Charlotte","Viberg, Bjarke","Odgaard, Anders","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765990"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Risager, Stefan Kastalag"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged 80 and over","Arthroplasty Replacement Knee adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Epidemiology","Female","Femoral Fractures surgery","Humans","Knee Fractures","Knee Prosthesis adverse effects","Male","Middle Aged","Osteoarthritis Knee surgery","Periprosthetic Fractures epidemiology","Periprosthetic knee fracture","Registries","Reoperation statistics numerical data","Risk","Risk Factors","Total knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk and epidemiology of periprosthetic knee fractures after primary total knee arthroplasty a nationwide cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2024.05.033","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765990","identifier":[{"id":"85195387995","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38759816","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-3725e78c-e1e7-4a4b-88c2-99e154eedb43"],"keyword":["Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Arthroplasty, Replacement, Knee/adverse effects","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Femoral Fractures/surgery","Humans","Knee Fractures","Knee Prosthesis/adverse effects","Male","Middle Aged","Osteoarthritis, Knee/surgery","Periprosthetic Fractures/epidemiology","Registries","Reoperation/statistics & numerical data","epidemiology","periprosthetic knee fracture","risk","risk factors","total knee arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8521E42BFA3600C87270917B501A985E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/272743119/1-s2.0-S0883540324004807-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.arth.2024.05.033","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stefan K.","key":"risagerpau","last":"Risager","locid":"dc21700f-7caf-43ac-901c-5fb66ad42684","name":"Risager, Stefan Kastalag","name_org":"Risager, Stefan K.","orcid":"0000-0001-8157-7001","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine B.","key":"arndtpau","last":"Arndt","locid":"a2513ef2-9214-48ee-b84f-bea6ef1717ac","name":"Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","name_org":"Arndt, Kristine B.","orcid":"0000-0001-8258-7922","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"22215dd3-464e-4e62-b19f-71a71e0e1e65","name":"Abrahamsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-3700-289X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjarke","key":"vibergpau","last":"Viberg","locid":"8cb06beb-80dd-4b2f-bcd7-eb9cba7b9da6","name":"Viberg, Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0001-5169-4282","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38759816"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.arth.2024.05.033","issn":["08835403","15328406"],"issn_org":["08835403"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Arthroplasty","pages":"2615-2620","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Arthroplasty","title_org":"The Journal of Arthroplasty","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195387995"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3725e78c-e1e7-4a4b-88c2-99e154eedb43"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Risk and Epidemiology of Periprosthetic Knee Fractures After Primary Total Knee Arthroplasty : A Nationwide Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765990","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"From a social practice perspective and in collaboration with professionals we explore situated inequality, and in the paper, we will discuss and exemplify theoretical development in relation to the concept of participation and conflictual collaboration. How can we understand unequal possibilities of participation in societal institutions of education? We want to shift the psychological focus on inequality from issues outside societal institutions for children and young people (intergenerational transmission, family relationships, social background) to how the involved are dealing with social conflicts and historical contradictions within these institutions. This conceptual turn emphasises possibilities of participation in social situations and leads to a concept of ’situated inequality’ – but what is meant by ‘participation’ and ‘participation possibilities’? How can we observe social possibilities for participation and not just individual children, and how can we work professionally with the way children and their adults make up conditions for the participation of one another? Different professionals across children’s lives simultaneously have common tasks in relation to the children and different areas of responsibility and perspectives on the issues surrounding the children. The collaboration between professionals is thus both necessary and conflictual. To strengthen the conditions of children’s conduct of everyday lives across contexts, we need to conceptualise ‘conflicts’ as related to collaboration on common but still contradictory matter. In the everyday life of educational institutions, different considerations must be reconciled every day through a flexible and exploring ‘conflictual collaboration’.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-782448"],"event":{"end":"2024-05-24","place":"Belgrade, rs","start":"2024-05-20","title":"20th Conference of the International Society for Theoretical Psychology","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Children s perspectives","Conflictual collaboration","Educational psychology","Participation","Situated inequality"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"situated inequality and participation in the institutions of children s everyday lives","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-782448","ids":["ruc-37594cd5-a670-4ca9-b0aa-91b93a3c6109"],"keyword":["Children's perspectives","Conflictual Collaboration","Educational Psychology","Participation","Situated inequality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6225296A6EFCF55F0B7C48E8C6F9A31F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, The Danish Centre for Research in Early Childhood Education and Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-37594cd5-a670-4ca9-b0aa-91b93a3c6109"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Situated Inequality and Participation in the Institutions of Children's Everyday Lives","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-782448","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Umbilical outpouchings (UO) are common in Danish weaners. In slaughter pigs UOs consist of various pathological diagnoses; however, no studies have assessed the pathology in weaners from randomly selected herds, nor the agreement between clinical examination findings and post-mortem results. The primary objective was to estimate the prevalence of UO-related clinical findings in weaners before euthanasia and the pathologic macroscopic findings after euthanasia. A secondary objective was to assess the agreement between the size of the UO, the presence of ulcers, and the diagnosis before and after euthanasia. Pigs were selected for euthanasia and included in the study because the individual farmer believed the pigs were already unfit for transport, would not make it to slaughter, or would become unsellable. Results: In total 214 weaners euthanized due to UOs were examined both clinically and post-mortem. Clinically 65.4% of the UOs were large (≥ 11 cm) and 52.3% were unreducible. In the autopsy 78.5% of the UOs were large, and 54.2% had ulcers on their UO. The most prevalent pathological diagnoses were hernia (36.4%), hernia combined with cysts/abscesses (30.8%), cysts (11.7%), and abscesses (11.2%). Adhesions were found in 32.7%, haemorrhage in 22.7%, incarcerated intestines in 8.9%, and connective tissue related to the UO in 51.9% of the pigs post-mortem. The agreement between the size of the UO in the clinical examination and post-mortem was good, as was the sensitivity and specificity for detecting ulcers in the clinical examination compared to post-mortem. Conclusion: Hernias were the most common pathological diagnosis in weaners euthanized due to UOs, and many pigs had complications related to their UO such as ulcers, adhesions, haemorrhage, or incarcerated intestines—all conditions that could impact the pig’s welfare. The presence of connective tissue in the UO in more than half of the pigs indicated that many of the UOs had been present for an extended period. Clinical identification of the umbilical ring is difficult, but the clinical examination is useful for determining the size of the UO and the presence or absence of an ulcer, both critical factors when assessing a pig’s welfare and fitness for transport. Clinical examination, however, has limited value in determining the aetiology of UOs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hansen, Marie Louise","Larsen, Inge","Jensen, Tina Birk","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Pedersen, Ken Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-790710"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Hernia","Pathology","Pig","Sustainability","Umbilical outpouching","Weaner","Welfare"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"clinical and pathological characteristics in 000000000214 danish weaners euthanized because of umbilical outpouchings","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-024-00401-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-790710","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11583573","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85209751704","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39578918","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9b004d06-48ed-45e5-b4e9-6926145ba3f8"],"keyword":["Hernia","Pathology","Pig","Sustainability","Umbilical outpouching","Weaner","Welfare"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-36DAF2D5749A2829B908CAED62D9534E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-024-00401-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/419823455/Clinical_a