{"abstract":"Objective: To evaluate the feasibility and prophylactic effect of psilocybin as well as its effects on hypothalamic functional connectivity (FC) in patients with chronic cluster headache (CCH). Background: CCH is an excruciating and difficult-to-treat disorder with incompletely understood pathophysiology, although hypothalamic dysfunction has been implicated. Psilocybin may have beneficial prophylactic effects, but clinical evidence is limited. Methods: In this small open-label clinical trial, 10 patients with CCH were included and maintained headache diaries for 10 weeks. Patients received three doses of peroral psilocybin (0.14 mg/kg) on the first day of weeks five, six, and seven. The first 4 weeks served as baseline and the last 4 weeks as follow-up. Hypothalamic FC was determined using functional magnetic resonance imaging the day before the first psilocybin dose and 1 week after the last dose. Results: The treatment was well tolerated. Attack frequency was reduced by mean (standard deviation) 31% (31) from baseline to follow-up (pFWER = 0.008). One patient experienced 21 weeks of complete remission. Changes in hypothalamic–diencephalic FC correlated negatively with a percent change in attack frequency (pFWER = 0.03, R = −0.81), implicating this neural pathway in treatment response. Conclusion: Our results indicate that psilocybin may have prophylactic potential and implicates the hypothalamus in possible treatment response. Further clinical studies are warranted.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Madsen, Martin K.","Petersen, Anja Sofie","Stenbæk, Dea Siggaard","Sørensen, Inger Marie","Schiønning, Harald","Fjeld, Tobias","Nykjær, Charlotte H.","Larsen, Sara Marie Ulv","Grzywacz, Maria","Mathiesen, Tobias","Klausen, Ida L.","Overgaard-Hansen, Oliver","Brendstrup-Brix, Kristoffer","Linnet, Kristian","Johansen, Sys Stybe","Fisher, Patrick M.","Jensen, Rigmor Højland","Knudsen, Gitte Moos"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716466"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Knudsen, Gitte M."],"keyword":["Cluster headache","Functional connectivity","Functional magnetic resonance imaging","Hypothalamus","Psilocin","Psilocybin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cch attack frequency reduction after psilocybin correlates with hypothalamic functional connectivity","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263877654/head.14656.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was sponsored by Augustinusfonden (grant number: 18‐0317), Rigshospitalet's Research Council (grant numbers: R130‐A5324 and R214‐A9447), Innovation Fund Denmark (NeuroPharm, grant number: 4108‐00004B), and Lundbeck Foundation through Danish Neurological Society."],"id":"S02-100.00-716466","identifier":[{"id":"38238974","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85182653955","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-9b5bb2ec-e58c-431e-b4fd-16dac0436413","sdu-797211ef-cc14-465b-a81e-e893afe47d99"],"keyword":["cluster headache","functional connectivity","functional magnetic resonance imaging","hypothalamus","psilocin","psilocybin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB18BCE054DB0EAD183BF25A8CB20635"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/263877654/head.14656.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Neurology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Psychology, Department of Psychology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin K.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"a4145e7a-1e90-4151-91f4-d0c07b3b23b1","name":"Madsen, Martin Korsbak","name_org":"Madsen, Martin K.","orcid":"0000-0001-8836-1844","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anja Sofie","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","name":"Petersen, Anja Sofie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Dea S.","key":"stenbækpau","last":"Stenbæk","locid":"cbc45555-3350-4362-8b59-29f8ca64d575","name":"Stenbæk, Dea Siggaard","name_org":"Stenbæk, Dea S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inger Marie","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Inger Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Harald","key":"schiønningpau","last":"Schiønning","name":"Schiønning, Harald","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tobias","k