{"abstract":"Association between alcohol intake and atrioventricular block is rare. This case describes a previously healthy 27-year-old man experiencing syncopes preceded by moderate alcohol intake. An implantable loop recorder demonstrated episodes of total atrioventricular block coinciding with an additional syncope after alcohol intake, resulting in pacemaker implantation. (Level of Difficulty: Intermediate.)","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","Stephansen, Charlotte","Mølgaard, Henning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-274715"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Sanne Bøjet"],"keyword":["Alcohol","Bradycardia","Cardiac pacemaker"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"syncope and total atrioventricular block associated with alcohol consumption in a healthy young man","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccas.2023.101771","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-274715","identifier":[{"id":"85148664105","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37077444","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10106993","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-fec3b9f1-04d9-4c11-9459-b379521ad7c9"],"keyword":["alcohol","bradycardia","cardiac pacemaker"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F3F37F7F82515B6DBC6491F6487DF87"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jaccas.2023.101771","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne Bøjet","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"15c7c979-5236-47ec-b92e-a4a5992b2d1e","name":"Larsen, Sanne Bøjet","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"stephansenpau","last":"Stephansen","locid":"bc398e00-bb58-4ef9-b28a-70f693ee6928","name":"Stephansen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-3272-2115","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"mølgaardpau","last":"Mølgaard","locid":"601d1640-0a48-4ffb-99fa-e4686f780aa2","name":"Mølgaard, Henning","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37077444"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jaccas.2023.101771","issn":["26660849"],"journal":"JACC: Case Reports","paperid":"101771","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Case Reports","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85148664105"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fec3b9f1-04d9-4c11-9459-b379521ad7c9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Syncope and Total Atrioventricular Block Associated With Alcohol Consumption in a Healthy Young Man","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-274715","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background : Adverse reactions to wheat-containing skin care products have been linked to food allergy development. Objectives : To determine the role of skin barrier dysfunction and inflammation in sensitization to gluten-derived hydrolysates via the skin in Brown Norway rats with and without oral tolerance to wheat. Methods : Skin barrier defect was induced by mechanical disruption, and skin inflammation was induced by topical application of SLS or MC903. Unmodified, enzyme hydrolyzed, or acid hydrolyzed gluten products were applied to the skin 3 times per week for 5 weeks. Subsequently, rats were orally gavaged with unmodified gluten. Results : Wheat-naïve rats were readily sensitized to gluten hydrolysates via the skin. Skin barrier defect and skin inflammation had little effect on the skin sensitization and hydrolysate-specific IgE levels. Oral administration of unmodified gluten promoted the production of unmodified gluten-specific IgE in rats sensitized via the skin. Sensitization through intact skin, disrupted skin barrier, or inflamed skin was unable to break tolerance to unmodified gluten in rats on a wheat-containing diet. Conclusions : Mechanical skin barrier disruption and skin inflammation play a limited role in experimental skin sensitization to gluten-derived hydrolysates.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Jeppe Madura","Ballegaard, Anne-Sofie Ravn","Dominguez, Angela Serrano","Kristoffersen, Nanna Jordahn","Maryniak, Natalia Zofia","Locke, Arielle Vallee","Kazemi, Sahar","Epstein, Michelle","Madsen, Charlotte Bernhard","Bøgh, Katrine Lindholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-328343"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bøgh, Katrine Lindholm"],"country":["Austria"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Medical University of Vienna"],"keyword":["Animal model","Food allergy","Gluten","Skin inflammation","Skin sensitization","Wheat"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of skin inflammation barrier dysfunction and oral tolerance in skin sensitization to gluten derived hydrolysates in a rat model","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cod.14233","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-328343","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10091953","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85140214024","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36221232","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-4ff1cf6c-bb41-49ca-8782-5d78c8f8a940"],"keyword":["Animal model","Food allergy","Gluten","Oral tolerance","Skin barrier dysfunction","Skin inflammation","Skin sensitization","Wheat"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86CC6352E8E28EF32456855F23C41982"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/305589566/Contact_Dermatitis_2022_Larsen_The_role_of_skin_inflammation_barrier_dysfunction_and_oral_tolerance_in_skin.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cod.14233","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Food Allergy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"at","key":"medical university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical University of Vienna","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Madura","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fe5aeb36-c03b-49e1-9e39-31127e951953","name":"Larsen, Jeppe Madura","orcid":"0000-0003-1492-0708","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Sofie Ravn","key":"ballegaardpau","last":"Ballegaard","locid":"6e19ac48-6dd5-40c9-a7de-6705b99346bf","name":"Ballegaard, Anne-Sofie Ravn","orcid":"0000-0001-9925-5983","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Angela Serrano","key":"dominguezpau","last":"Dominguez","name":"Dominguez, Angela Serrano","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Jordahn","key":"kristoffersenpau","last":"Kristoffersen","locid":"afeaa93b-dfb0-40be-9ce8-5c79771815ae","name":"Kristoffersen, Nanna Jordahn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Natalia Zofia","key":"maryniakpau","last":"Maryniak","locid":"3c1e2408-fa55-4277-bd35-3811b4619bc2","name":"Maryniak, Natalia Zofia","orcid":"0000-0003-1121-4285","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Arielle Vallee","key":"lockepau","last":"Locke","name":"Locke, Arielle Vallee","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sahar","key":"kazemipau","last":"Kazemi","name":"Kazemi, Sahar","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"epsteinpau","last":"Epstein","name":"Epstein, Michelle","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Bernhard","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"5def08bb-cc87-455f-9c7e-5b0d7877a338","name":"Madsen, Charlotte Bernhard","orcid":"0000-0002-9086-7120","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Katrine Lindholm","key":"bøghpau","last":"Bøgh","locid":"69dcdef2-7e2a-4c8c-966b-dd14c90e6419","name":"Bøgh, Katrine Lindholm","orcid":"0000-0002-5266-0372","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36221232"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/cod.14233","issn":["01051873","13966669"],"issn_org":["01051873"],"issue":"2","journal":"Contact Dermatitis","pages":"109-119","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Contact Dermatitis","volume":"88"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140214024"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4ff1cf6c-bb41-49ca-8782-5d78c8f8a940"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The role of skin inflammation, barrier dysfunction, and oral tolerance in skin sensitization to gluten-derived hydrolysates in a rat model","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-328343","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Neural differentiation, synaptic transmission, and action potential propagation depend on membrane sphingolipids, whose metabolism is tightly regulated. Mutations in the ceramide transporter CERT (CERT1), which is involved in sphingolipid biosynthesis, are associated with intellectual disability, but the pathogenic mechanism remains obscure. Here, we characterize 31 individuals with de novo missense variants in CERT1. Several variants fall into a previously uncharacterized dimeric helical domain that enables CERT homeostatic inactivation, without which sphingolipid production goes unchecked. The clinical severity reflects the degree to which CERT autoregulation is disrupted, and inhibiting CERT pharmacologically corrects morphological and motor abnormalities in a Drosophila model of the disease, which we call ceramide transporter (CerTra) syndrome. These findings uncover a central role for CERT autoregulation in the control of sphingolipid biosynthetic flux, provide unexpected insight into the structural organization of CERT, and suggest a possible therapeutic approach for patients with CerTra syndrome.","author_count":85,"contributors":["Gehin, Charlotte","Lone, Museer A","Lee, Winston","Capolupo, Laura","Ho, Sylvia","Adeyemi, Adekemi M","Gerkes, Erica H","Stegmann, Alexander Pa","López-Martín, Estrella","Bermejo-Sánchez, Eva","Martínez-Delgado, Beatriz","Zweier, Christiane","Kraus, Cornelia","Popp, Bernt","Strehlow, Vincent","Gräfe, Daniel","Knerr, Ina","Jones, Eppie R","Zamuner, Stefano","Abriata, Luciano A","Kunnathully, Vidya","Moeller, Brandon E","Vocat, Anthony","Rommelaere, Samuel","Bocquete, Jean-Philippe","Ruchti, Evelyne","Limoni, Greta","Van Campenhoudt, Marine","Bourgeat, Samuel","Henklein, Petra","Gilissen, Christian","van Bon, Bregje W","Pfundt, Rolph","Willemsen, Marjolein H","Schieving, Jolanda H","Leonardi, Emanuela","Soli, Fiorenza","Murgia, Alessandra","Guo, Hui","Zhang, Qiumeng","Xia, Kun","Fagerberg, Christina","Beier, Christoph Patrick","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Valenzuela, Irene","Fernández-Álvarez, Paula","Xiong, Shiyi","Śmigiel, Robert","López-González, Vanesa","Armengol, Lluís","Morleo, Manuela","Selicorni, Angelo","Torella, Annalaura","Blyth, Moira","Cooper, Nicola S","Wilson, Valerie","Oegema, Renske","Herenger, Yvan","Garde, Aurore","Bruel, Ange-Line","Tran Mau-Them, Frederic","Maddocks, Alexis Br","Bain, Jennifer M","Bhat, Musadiq A","Costain, Gregory","Kannu, Peter","Marwaha, Ashish","Champaigne, Neena L","Friez, Michael J","Richardson, Ellen B","Gowda, Vykuntaraju K","Srinivasan, Varunvenkat M","Gupta, Yask","Lim, Tze Y","Sanna-Cherchi, Simone","Lemaitre, Bruno","Yamaji, Toshiyuki","Hanada, Kentaro","Burke, John E","Jakšić, Ana Marija","McCabe, Brian D","De Los Rios, Paolo","Hornemann, Thorsten","D'Angelo, Giovanni","Gennarino, Vincenzo A"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671604"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Gehin, Charlotte"],"country":["Canada","China","France","Germany","Italy","Japan","Netherlands","Poland","Russia","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam Institute for Global Health and Development (AIGHD)","Berlin Institute of Health","Birmingham Women’s Hospital","Central South University","Columbia University","Department of Medical Genetics, University Children's Hospital, Belgrade, Serbia.","Hospital Clinico Universitario Virgen de la Arrixaca","Institute for Biochemistry and Molecular Cell Biology","Leipzig University","Leipzig University Hospital","Maastricht University Medical Center+","Medical University of South Carolina","Moscow Engineering Physics Institute","National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases","National Institute of Genetics, Japan","Radboud University Medical Center","Royal Hospital for Sick Children, Edinburgh","Te