McCabe, Brian D","rank":81,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Paolo","key":"delosriospau","last":"De Los Rios","name":"De Los Rios, Paolo","rank":82,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"35","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"hornemannpau","last":"Hornemann","name":"Hornemann, Thorsten","rank":83,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giovanni","key":"dangelopau","last":"D'Angelo","name":"D'Angelo, Giovanni","rank":84,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Vincenzo A","key":"gennarinopau","last":"Gennarino","name":"Gennarino, Vincenzo A","rank":85,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36976648"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1172/jci165019","issn":["00219738","15588238"],"issn_org":["00219738"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Clinical Investigation","paperid":"e165019","publisher":"American Society for Clinical Investigation","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Investigation","title_org":"The Journal of Clinical Investigation","volume":"133"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159733545"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-48346282-4246-4625-976e-36b3724e611d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"CERT1 mutations perturb human development by disrupting sphingolipid homeostasis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671604","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To investigate the effects of the “11 for Health” programme on musculoskeletal fitness. Methods: A total of 108 Danish children aged 10–12 years participated in the study, with 61 children in the intervention group (IG, 25 girls and 36 boys) and 47 children in the control group (CG, 21 girls and 26 boys). Measurements were conducted before and after an 11-week intervention consisting of twice-weekly 45-min football training sessions for IG or continuation of normal Physical Education program for CG. Whole-body dual X-ray absorptiometry was conducted for evaluation of leg and total bone mineral density as well as bone, muscle and fat mass. Standing Long Jump and Stork balance tests were employed to assess musculoskeletal fitness and postural balance. Results: During the 11-week study period, leg bone mineral density as well as leg lean body mass increased more (p < 0.05) in the intervention group (IG) compared to the control group (CG) (0.021 ± 0.019 vs 0.014 ± 0.018 g/cm2 and 0.51 ± 0.46 vs 0.32 ± 0.35 kg, respectively). Moreover, body fat percentage decreased more in IG than in CG (−0.6 ± 0.1 vs 0.1 ± 0.1 %-points, p < 0.05). No significant between-group differences were found in bone mineral content. Stork balance test performance increased more in IG than in CG (0.5 ± 2.6 vs −1.5 ± 4.4 s, p < 0.05), whereas no between-group differences were found in jump performance. Conclusions: The school-based football programme, 11 for Health, with twice-weekly 45-min training sessions over 11 weeks improves various, but not all evaluated parameters related to musculoskeletal fitness in 10–12-yr-old Danish school children.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Malte Nejst","Terracciano, Alessia","Møller, Trine Kjeldgaard","Aggestrup, Charlotte Sandager","Buono, Pasqualina","Krustrup, Peter","Castagna, Carlo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671969"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Malte Nejst"],"country":["China","Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CEINGE-Biotecnologie Avanzate","Department of Movement Sciences and Wellness, University Parthenope, Napoli, Italy.","Italian Football Federation","Shanghai University of Sport","University of Exeter","Università di Urbino"],"keyword":["Bone health","Bone mineral density","Children","Physical activity","Soccer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an 000000000011 week school based health education through football programme improves musculoskeletal variables in 000000000010 000000000012 yr old danish school children","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bonr.2023.101681","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The Nordea Foundation (Nordea-fonden), the Danish Football Association (DBU) and Aase and Ejnar Danielsens Foundation."],"id":"S01-000.00-671969","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10176027","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37187574","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85153969769","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-f8d3965c-c340-4074-8e5b-cdcb0d31f970"],"keyword":["Bone health","Bone mineral density","Children","Football program","Physical activity","Soccer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A8A2B394BF86E03862567E0F72B269B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/229145012/1_s2.0_S2352187223000293_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bonr.2023.101681","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affn