{"abstract":"In 2021 and 2022, clade 2.3.4.4b H5Nx high pathogenicity avian influenza viruses were detected in one harbor seal and in one adult and three fox cubs in Denmark. The viruses were closely related to contemporary viruses found in Europe, and some had obtained amino acid substitutions related to mammalian adaptation. Notably, the virus distribution appeared to have been different in the infected fox cubs, as one exclusively tested positive for the presence of HPAIV in the brain and the other two only in the lung. Collectively, these findings stress the need for increased disease surveillance of wild and farmed mammals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Liang, Yuan","Hjulsager, Charlotte K.","Jensen, Tim Kåre","Hammer, Anne Sofie Vedsted","Ovesen, Maibritt Træholt","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702178"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Denmark","Influenza A virus","Mammals","Wild birds","high pathogenicity avian influenza"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of high pathogenicity avian influenza h000000000005nx viruses from a wild harbor seal and red foxes in denmark 000000002021 and 000000002022 characterization of high pathogenicity avian influenza h000000000005nx viruses from a wild harbor seal and red foxes in denmark 000000002021 and 000000002022","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/irv.13208","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-702178","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10577164","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37850154","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85174452986","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-b0fa7740-9053-4ee7-ba1f-f2dd2321a8b8"],"keyword":["Denmark","high pathogenicity avian influenza","influenza A virus","mammals","wild birds"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D2CAC90F31232B0FA44797FC0CF93620"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/382374585/Influenza_Resp_Viruses_2023_Liang_Characterization_of_high_pathogenicity_avian_influenza_H5Nx_viruses_from_a_wild.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/irv.13208","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Yuan","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","locid":"15fec07b-8b15-410c-9db2-b2b7fda77736","name":"Liang, Yuan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte K.","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tim K.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e66d0e73-452c-4e91-83ad-a8ad31a94b0e","name":"Jensen, Tim Kåre","name_org":"Jensen, Tim K.","orcid":"0000-0002-8048-4695","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne Sofie V.","key":"hammerpau","last":"Hammer","locid":"d86de80d-40da-4128-b0d2-55a9f244b129","name":"Hammer, Anne Sofie Vedsted","name_org":"Hammer, Anne Sofie V.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maibritt T.","key":"ovesenpau","last":"Ovesen","locid":"f8414b3f-6585-4570-b0ed-44167000400d","name":"Ovesen, Maibritt Træholt","name_org":"Ovesen, Maibritt T.","orcid":"0009-0004-1521-6717","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37850154"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/irv.13208","issn":["17502640","17502659"],"issn_org":["17502640"],"issue":"10","journal":"Influenza and Other Respiratory Viruses","paperid":"e13208","status":"p","title":"Influenza and Other Respiratory Viruses","title_org":"Influenza and other Respiratory Viruses","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174452986"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b0fa7740-9053-4ee7-ba1f-f2dd2321a8b8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterization of high pathogenicity avian influenza H5Nx viruses from a wild harbor seal and red foxes in Denmark, 2021 and 2022 : Characterization of high pathogenicity avian influenza H5Nx viruses from a wild harbor seal and red foxes in Denmark, 2021 and 2022","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-702178","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Beginning January of 2020, COVID-19 cases detected in Arctic countries triggered government policy responses to stop transmission and limit caseloads beneath levels that would overwhelm existing healthcare systems. This review details the various restrictions, health mandates, and transmission mitigation strategies imposed by governments in eight Arctic countries (the United States, Canada, Greenland, Norway, Finland, Sweden, Iceland, and Russia) during the first year of the COVID-19 pandemic, through 31 January 2021s31 January 2021. We highlight formal protocols and informal initiatives adopted by local communities in each country, beyond what was mandated by regional or national governments. This review documents travel restrictions, communications, testing strategies, and use of health technology to track and monitor COVID-19 cases. We provide geographical and sociocultural background and draw on local media and communications to contextualise the impact of COVID-19 emergence and prevention measures in Indigenous communities in the Arctic. Countries saw varied case rates associated with local protocols, governance, and population. Still, almost all regions maintained low COVID-19 case rates until November of 2020. This review was produced as part of an international collaboration to identify community-driven, evidence-based promising practices and recommendations to inform pan-Arctic collaboration and decision making in public health during global emergencies.","author_count":23,"contributors":["Peterson, Malory","Akearok, Gwen Healey","Cueva, Katie","Lavoie, Josée G.","Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken","Jóhannsdóttir, Lára","Cook, David","Nilsson, Lena Maria","Rautio, Arja","Timlin, Ulla","San Sebastián, Miguel","Gladun, Elena","Rink, Elizabeth","Broderstadt, Ann Ragnhild","Dagsvold, Inger","Siri, Susanna","Ottendahl, Charlotte Brandstrup","Olesen, Ingelise","Zatseva, Larisa","Young, Rebecca Ipiaqruk","Chaliak, Ay’aqulluk Jim","Ophus, Emily","Stoor, Jon Petter A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713578"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Peterson, Malory"],"country":["Canada","Finland","Greenland","Iceland","Norway","Russia","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Grønlands Universitet","Montana State University","Qaujigiartiit Health Research Centre","Tyumen State University","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","Umeå University","University of Alaska","University of Iceland","University of Manitoba","University of Oulu"],"keyword":["Epidemic","First Nations","Health Policy","Indigenous","Infectious diseases","Inuit"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"public health restrictions directives and measures in arctic countries in the first year of the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/22423982.2023.2271211","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["for this project was provided by the Government of Canada."],"id":"S01-000.00-713578","identifier":[{"id":"85175376490","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37898999","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10997298","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-0c79ef71-95b1-496d-b0fc-46538e3b3c3c"],"keyword":["Epidemic","Indigenous","Inuit","first nations","health policy","infectious diseases","remote health services, community"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C430F9F49465B4AF1B9D03ED25254347"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/22423982.2023.2271211","version":"Publis