International Journal of Circumpolar Health","paperid":"2271211","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Circumpolar Health","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175376490"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0c79ef71-95b1-496d-b0fc-46538e3b3c3c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Public health restrictions, directives, and measures in Arctic countries in the first year of the COVID-19 pandemic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713578","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This overview presents 10 Ph.D. projects that illustrate the breadth of Scandinavian rhetorical research. Among them are projects on specific conceptualizations in the field of rhetoric such as accusations, anger, the body, and voice in writing; projects on the rhetoric of groups, organizations and social movements such as the EU, LGBTQ+ minorities, and climate activists; projects that capture public debates, for example on forestry and climate change; didactic projects, and projects entertaining new methods and methodologies for rhetorical research, such as computer assisted big data analysis and participatory rhetorical criticism. This representation of 10 diverse emerging scholars from 6 Scandinavian universities gives a taste of the contemporary rhetorical research scene in Denmark, Sweden, and Norway.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Bruhn, Tommy","Villadsen, Lisa Storm","Schou Therkildsen, Louise Therese","Nørremark, Rebekka Lykke","Olsen, Frederik Appel","Skovbo Moser, Kira","Larsen, Jon Martin","Härgestam, Klara","Hidle, Charlotte","Dehlie Glædesdahl, Anne","Keitum Fisker, Thore","Hviid Broberg, Frida"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-753052"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Kristiania University College","University of Gothenburg","University of Oslo","Örebro University"],"keyword":["Activist research","Manifestos","Participatory action research"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scandinavian emerging scholars and their ph d projects an overview","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY",