 Strøm","key":"krogagerpau","last":"Krogager","locid":"a62b58cc-8bfa-46d6-8588-004f926d107d","name":"Krogager, Stinne Gunder Strøm","orcid":"0000-0002-3180-0583","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Trandberg","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b1c9a10c-1b8a-4e8d-bd09-6928c1ad939f","name":"Jensen, Martin Trandberg","orcid":"0000-0002-6624-5065","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonatan","key":"leerpau","last":"Leer","locid":"11a6fffa-6ac2-40bd-a9dd-45fa1f92f0e5","name":"Leer, Jonatan","orcid":"0000-0002-9068-8835","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2646cc82-85a9-48c4-b85c-9223914f8a66"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"#greenliving: Studying sustainability practices in young adults’ digital everyday lives","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-061175","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Periprosthetic joint infection (PJI) of the knee is associated with extended hospital stay, high doses of antibiotics, lengthy rehabilitation, and pain. Standard treatment is a two-stage procedure comprising two surgeries and two hospitalizations. To facilitate exploration of patients’ perspectives, the qualitative study presented here was an adjunct to a Danish randomized controlled trial comparing one-stage and two-stage revision surgery. Aim: To explore patient experiences, before, during and after hospitalization and surgical treatment with one- or two-stage revision for PJI of the knee. Material and methods: Qualitative, semi-structured telephone interviews were conducted with 10 individuals who had undergone either one- or two-stage revision because of PJI. Thematic analysis was employed. Results: The essence of the findings was that the infection was a transition point in a possible life-changing illness. The three themes representing this comprised: 1) physical, 2) psychological, and 3) social implications. Each theme is further illuminated with subthemes. Conclusions: Infection is a transition point in a possible life changing illness. Late diagnosis and delayed treatment are major issues. Individuals suffer from pain, weight loss, fatigue, and reduced mobility as well as dependency on family members, leading to psychological challenges including depression. Implications for clinical practice: Patients with PJI of the knee could be better informed, educated and involved before and during treatment. Information is needed not only about the physical consequences, but also the psychological and social consequences. More patient involvement and inter-professional and care sector coordination is important when caring for patients with PJI.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rowland, Tina","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Santy-Tomlinson, Julie","Myhre Jensen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-589254"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Myhre Jensen, Charlotte"],"keyword":["Patient experience","Qualitative study","Revision"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a qualitative study of patients experiences before during and after surgical treatment for periprosthetic knee joint infection i assumed it had to be like that","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijotn.2022.100992","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-589254","identifier":[{"id":"85146356055","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36630741","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-382d8829-c5ab-4b87-ad0d-f6519c23141d"],"keyword":["Knee periprosthetic joint infection","Patient experience","Qualitative study","Revision"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52D38B291146F8189DBFE76C9E7FED0A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijotn.2022.100992","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/219180770/1_s2.0_S1878124122000727_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denma