aththri","key":"vimalathaspau","last":"Vimalathas","locid":"ebe9802e-b5a4-44ea-bc20-0115d3e4996c","name":"Vimalathas, Gayaththri","orcid":"0000-0001-5507-9762","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilie Steensboe","key":"langpau","last":"Lang","locid":"e7b58303-6e7f-4506-b00e-8d8ef429b573","name":"Lang, Cecilie Steensboe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"066dac5b-cbf5-4b70-b136-3e5dd42e4bee","name":"Hansen, Marcus Høy","name_org":"Hansen, Marcus","orcid":"0000-0003-3083-4850","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Guldborg","key":"nyvoldpau","last":"Nyvold","locid":"ba584c2b-215e-421c-a6e6-c799c1b16b7c","name":"Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","orcid":"0000-0002-0411-7594","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Boe","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"edd876e8-0651-4c8f-8f0f-95f4519e1654","name":"Møller, Michael Boe","orcid":"0000-0003-2041-3630","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Stauffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dd2de49b-c3d9-49cb-bb8d-e92119e0b2d1","name":"Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e4610f05-443a-4e94-9018-bd9c498d4c3e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"EXPLORING DIFFERENTIAL MUTATIONAL DISTRIBUTION BY TARGETED SEQUENCING IN A R-CHOP TREATED COHORT OF DIFFUSE LARGE B-CELL LYMPHOMA PATIENTS","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-685445","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: This study aimed to assess the diagnostic yield of prenatal genetic testing using trio whole exome sequencing (WES) and trio whole genome sequencing (WGS) in pregnancies with fetal anomalies, comparing the results to conventional chromosomal microarray (CMA) analysis. METHODS: A total of 40 pregnancies with fetal anomalies or increased nuchal translucency (NT≥5mm) were included between the 12th and 21st week of gestation. Trio WES/WGS and CMA were performed on all cases. RESULTS: The trio WES/WGS analysis increased the diagnostic yield by 25% in cases with negative CMA results. Furthermore, all six chromosomal aberrations identified by CMA were independently detected by WES/WGS analysis. In total, 16 out of 40 cases obtained a genetic sequence variant, copy number variant or aneuploidy explaining the phenotype, resulting in an overall WES/WGS diagnostic yield of 40%. WES analysis provided a more reliable identification of mosaic sequence variants than WGS due to higher sequencing depth. CONCLUSION: Prenatal WES/WGS proved to be powerful diagnostic tools for fetal anomalies, surpassing the diagnostic yield of CMA. They have the potential to serve as standalone methods for prenatal diagnosis. The study highlighted the limitations of WGS in accurately detecting mosaic variants, which is particularly relevant when analyzing chorionic villus samples. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Miceikaite, Ieva","Fagerberg, Christina","Brasch-Andersen, Charlotte","Tørring, Pernille M","Kristiansen, Britta Schlott","Hao, Qin","Sperling, Lene","Ibsen, Mette H.","Löser, Katrin","Bendsen, Eske Alf","Ousager, Lilian Bomme","Larsen, Martin Jakob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-691036"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Miceikaite, Ieva"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comprehensive prenatal diagnostics exome versus genome sequencing","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pd.6402","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-691036","identifier":[{"id":"85164179809","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37355983","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-46f48efb-81d4-4069-b3d6-97566b23eb11"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C76D346799A22B6C9A516D76631D8CBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/238322232/Prenatal_Diagnosis_2023_Miceikaite.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/pd.6402","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ieva","key":"miceikaitepau","last":"Miceikaite","locid":"eb4ddff7-556f-465a-87af-2d89e65de326","name":"Miceikaite, Ieva","orcid":"0000-0002-5188-7647","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"fagerbergpau","last":"Fagerberg","locid":"93aebc29-7681-4e3d-b613-867bd3a7eb65","name":"Fagerberg, Christina","orcid":"0000-0002-5206-4327","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"braschandersenpau","last":"Brasch-Andersen","locid":"3fe4d15d-5f04-4ec0-87b8-000b5f993ed1","name":"Brasch-Andersen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4273-0047","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Mathiesen","key":"torringpau","last":"Torring","locid":"10a81f84-d21d-4217-9a6a-aeafde837db6","name":"Tørring, Pernille M","name_org":"Torring, Pernille Mathiesen","orcid":"0000-0002-7303-7619","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Britta Schlott","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"189c4bc0-f563-4cb9-a29d-3993cea6d4db","name":"Kristiansen, Britta Schlott","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Qin","key":"haopau","last":"Hao","locid":"98418102-5519-4eff-86e6-d7373f0b82d3","name":"Hao, Qin","orcid":"0000-0002-6775-2181","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"sperlingpau","last":"Sperling","locid":"d93276e2-5dab-4099-a4d6-36b2952473ba","name":"Sperling, Lene","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Holm","key":"ibsenpau","last":"Ibsen","locid":"dfa3a09a-37e4-4093-bacb-f9225661e37f","name":"Ibsen, Mette H.","name_org":"Ibsen, Mette Holm","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrin","key":"löserpau","last":"Löser","locid":"04e97ea8-fe80-497a-a2bf-83da4733d4be","name":"Löser, Katrin","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eske Alf","key":"bendsenpau","last":"Bendsen","locid":"cb00f9c2-b0bd-4fc7-8c7a-dfb8c6d27ff5","name":"Bendsen, Eske Alf","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lilian Bomme","key":"ousagerpau","last":"Ousager","locid":"58559d8d-61ee-42b3-aeac-cfd62bdf9b70","name":"Ousager, Lilian Bomme","orcid":"0000-0001-9936-2201","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Jakob","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7cfc93bc-88f4-48fa-86de-6b0147dc2825","name":"Larsen, Martin Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-4107-8771","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37355983"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/pd.6402","issn":["01973851","10970223"],"issn_org":["01973851"],"issue":"9","journal":"Prenatal Diagnosis","pages":"1132-1141","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"Prenatal Diagnosis","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164179809"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-46f48efb-81d4-4069-b3d6-97566b23eb11"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comprehensive prenatal diagnostics : Exome versus genome sequencing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-691036","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Diffuse large B cell lymphoma (DLBCL) is the most common lymphoma in the western world. It is highly heterogeneous with a variable clinical course, but curable with chemo-immunotherapy in up to 70% of all cases. The lymphoma presents in lymph nodes and/or extranodal lymphoid tissue, and the diagnosis is based on invasive procedures for histopathologic evaluation. METHODS: In this technical study, we evaluated cell-free DNA (cfDNA) from blood plasma to detect clonal B cells in patients with DLBCL using rearranged immunoglobulin heavy chain gene as targets by next-generation sequencing. Clonal B cell sequences and frequencies were determined from blood plasma cfDNA and cellular DNA from matched excised lymphoma tissues and mononuclear cells isolated from diagnostic bone marrow and blood samples from 15 patients. RESULTS: We showed that identical clonal rearrangements could be detected in blood plasma and excised lymphoma tissue and that plasma cfDNA was superior in detecting clonal rearrangements compared to blood or bone marrow-derived cellular DNA. CONCLUSION: These findings consolidate the role of blood plasma as a reliable and easily accessible source for detecting neoplastic cells in DLBCL.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Højlund, Elisabeth Luna","Cédile, Oriane","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","Vimalathas, Gayaththri","Møller, Michael Boe","Hansen, Marcus Høy","Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697231"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg"],"keyword":["B Lymphocytes pathology","Bone Marrow pathology","Cell Free Nucleic Acids","Diffuse large B cell lymphoma DLBCL","High Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Lymphoma Large B Cell Diffuse diagnosis","Next generation sequencing NGS","cell free DNA cfDNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cell free dna for detection of clonal b cells in diffuse large b cell lymphoma by sequencing","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ijlh.14116","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-697231","identifier":[{"id":"85162894501","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37350020","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-95ab27d6-d3e3-45ec-bf56-ae0cc603ff0e"],"keyword":["B-Lymphocytes/pathology","Bone Marrow/pathology","Cell-Free Nucleic Acids","High-Throughput Nucleotide Sequencing","Humans","Lymphoma, Large B-Cell, Diffuse/diagnosis","cell-free DNA (cfDNA)","diffuse large B cell lymphoma (DLBCL)","immunoglobulin heavy chain (IgH) sequencing","matched tissue samples","next generation sequencing (NGS)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-87A61A33C20FAFBAE260B8AAB9E18AA9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/239959683/Int_J_Lab_Hematology_2023_H_jlund.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/ijlh.14116","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research Unit OPEN (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Haematology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth Luna","key":"højlundpau","last":"Højlund","name":"Højlund, Elisabeth Luna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Oriane","key":"cédilepau","last":"Cédile","locid":"b2e3be48-c899-40b9-b01d-2bd23278dcf1","name":"Cédile, Oriane","orcid":"0000-0002-6632-8039","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Stauffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"dd2de49b-c3d9-49cb-bb8d-e92119e0b2d1","name":"Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","orcid":"0000-0002-8418-6708","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gayaththri","key":"vimalathaspau","last":"Vimalathas","locid":"ebe9802e-b5a4-44ea-bc20-0115d3e4996c","name":"Vimalathas, Gayaththri","orcid":"0000-0001-5507-9762","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Boe","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"edd876e8-0651-4c8f-8f0f-95f4519e1654","name":"Møller, Michael Boe","orcid":"0000-0003-2041-3630","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marcus Høy","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"066dac5b-cbf5-4b70-b136-3e5dd42e4bee","name":"Hansen, Marcus Høy","orcid":"0000-0003-3083-4850","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Guldborg","key":"nyvoldpau","last":"Nyvold","locid":"ba584c2b-215e-421c-a6e6-c799c1b16b7c","name":"Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","orcid":"0000-0002-0411-7594","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37350020"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/ijlh.14116","issn":["17515521","1751553X"],"issn_org":["17515521"],"issue":"5","journal":"International Journal of Laboratory Hematology","pages":"735-742","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Laboratory Hematology","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162894501"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-95ab27d6-d3e3-45ec-bf56-ae0cc603ff0e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cell-free DNA for detection of clonal B cells in diffuse large B cell lymphoma by sequencing","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-697231","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Synthetic corticosteroids are widely used due to their anti-inflammatory and immunosuppressant effects. Their use has been associated with venous thromboembolism, but it is unknown whether thromboembolism has a causal relationship with corticosteroid treatment. In a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in normal to overweight healthy men, the effect of the corticosteroid prednisolone on haemostasis using either 50 mg prednisolone or matching placebo once daily for ten days was investigated. The primary outcome was a change from baseline in the viscoelastic measurement maximal amplitude of clot in kaolin-activated thromboelastography (TEG). Changes from baseline in other TEG measurements, D-dimer, von Willebrand factor (VWF) antigen, and ristocetin cofactor activity (RCo), antithrombin, protein C, prothrombin, fibrinogen, INR, APTT, and platelet count were secondary outcomes. Thirty-four men participated in this study. Compared to placebo, prednisolone treatment did not affect maximal amplitude of clot (difference −0.77 (95% confidence interval (CI) −2.48, 0.94) mm, p = 0.37, missing: n = 2), but it altered VWF antigen (28%, p = 0.0004), VWF:RCo (19%, p = 0.0006), prothrombin (5%, p = 0.05), protein C (31%, p < 0.0001), antithrombin (5%, p = 0.013), and fibrinogen (−15%, p = 0.004). Thus, prednisolone treatment did not alter TEG-assessed maximal amplitude of clot, despite that it affected prothrombotic markers (increased prothrombin, VWF antigen, VWF:RCo, prothrombin, and decreased fibrinogen) and increased antithrombotic markers (protein C and antithrombin).","author_count":10,"contributors":["Kamstrup, Peter","Rastoder, Ema","Hellmann, Pernille Høgh","Sivapalan, Pradeesh","Larsen, Emil List","Vestbo, Jørgen","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Goetze, Jens P.","Knop, Filip K.","Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701504"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Manchester"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Glucocorticoids","Haemostasis","Healthy Volunteers","Randomised controlled trial","Thromboelastography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["Allergi-Og Lungeklinikken Vanløse"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of 000000000010 day treatment with 000000000050 mg prednisolone once daily on haemostasis in healthy men a randomised placebo controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines11072052","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701504","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10377059","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85175109648","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37509691","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2f54547a-8e33-4ac4-a7b9-45c2dbad80d1"],"keyword":["biomarkers","glucocorticoids","haemostasis","healthy volunteers","randomised controlled trial","thromboelastography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A1297A5418E40DB1CAD6EACA9FC71762"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/biomedicines11072052","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/373470277/Effect_of_10_Day_Treatment.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Allergi-Og Lungeklinikken Vanløse"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of manchester","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Manchester","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Respiratory Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"kamstruppau","last":"Kamstrup","name":"Kamstrup, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ema","key":"rastoderpau","last":"Rastoder","name":"Rastoder, Ema","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille Høgh","key":"hellmannpau","last":"Hellmann","name":"Hellmann, Pernille Høgh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pradeesh","key":"sivapalanpau","last":"Sivapalan","name":"Sivapalan, Pradeesh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emil List","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Emil List","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Jørgen","key":"vestbopau","last":"Vestbo","name":"Vestbo, Jørgen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Charlotte Suppli","key":"ulrikpau","last":"Ulrik","locid":"ea578010-4d8b-498b-b9d0-8f3d8cc424df","name":"Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Jens P.","key":"goetzepau","last":"Goetze","locid":"980bceaf-dbf3-4f7a-a8d7-0a8e81b638b2","name":"Goetze, Jens P.","orcid":"0000-0001-6356-3829","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Filip Krag","key":"knoppau","last":"Knop","locid":"ce6eaad9-59f8-4ecf-8a1e-388a74734f6a","name":"Knop, Filip K.","name_org":"Knop, Filip Krag","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Jens Ulrik Stæhr","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"d9593acd-d6ae-4a83-a7c8-64bc2ea541ac","name":"Jensen, Jens Ulrik Stæhr","orcid":"0000-0003-4036-0521","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37509691"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/biomedicines11072052","issn":["22279059"],"issue":"7","journal":"Biomedicines","pages":"1-14","paperid":"2052","status":"p","title":"Biomedicines","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175109648"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2f54547a-8e33-4ac4-a7b9-45c2dbad80d1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of 10-Day Treatment with 50 mg Prednisolone Once-Daily on Haemostasis in Healthy Men—A Randomised Placebo-Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701504","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Information regarding deaths caused by poisoning or adverse effects of medication in Danish persons not using illicit narcotic drugs (PNUIDs) is sparse. To characterize aetiology, demographics, and death scene, we reviewed all legal autopsies performed at Aarhus University from 2017 to 2019 and isolated 96 deaths caused by medications in PNUIDs. Suicides caused by medication overdose accounted for 38%. Opioids and psychotropic medications were the main cause of death in 48% and 35% of the 96 cases, respectively. Morphine, tramadol, and quetiapine were the most commonly involved individual medications. A single medication caused death in 50% of cases, and multiple substances were involved in 50%. The median total number [interquartile range] of detected medications was 5 [4–6], with a higher number in females (5 [4–7]) than males (4 [2–5]), p = 0.009. Median age was 51 [42.5–61.5] years, and 57% were female. Scene of death most frequently involved a body on a bed or couch in the decedent's own home (72%). In conclusion, opioids and psychotropic medications dominated by morphine, tramadol and quetiapine most frequently caused medication-related deaths in PNUIDs. Monitoring this type of death may yield important knowledge to direct prophylactic initiatives regarding medication use and prescription.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj","Ahmed, Hafsa","Rædkjær, Mathias","Hasselstrøm, Jørgen Bo","Larsen, Maiken Kudahl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-707480"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj"],"keyword":["Clinical toxicology","Forensic toxicology","Medication","Opioids","Psychiatry","Psychopharmacology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"deaths caused by medication in persons not using illicit narcotic drugs an autopsy study from western denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13808","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-707480","identifier":[{"id":"36281709","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85141354489","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10092188","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-44526eac-d393-4350-bc54-c154f2207d41"],"keyword":["clinical toxicology","forensic toxicology","medication","opioids","psychiatry","psychopharmacology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1420E06978AD65260EB8A3E56C06F158"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/409607548/Basic_Clin_Pharma_Tox_-_2022_-_Andersen_-_Deaths_caused_by_medication_in_persons_not_using_illicit_narcotic_drugs_An.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/bcpt.13808","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Retskemisk"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte U.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"d9de514e-16a5-468a-96aa-7dce1995a898","name":"Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj","name_org":"Andersen, Charlotte U.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Hafsa","key":"ahmedpau","last":"Ahmed","name":"Ahmed, Hafsa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mathias","key":"rædkjærpau","last":"Rædkjær","locid":"4395f86a-dd3a-45de-86a1-64d1175b7a5c","name":"Rædkjær, Mathias","orcid":"0000-0002-8515-5268","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen B.","key":"hasselstrømpau","last":"Hasselstrøm","locid":"c4351988-ff77-42bc-9a7a-5a329fe8d98b","name":"Hasselstrøm, Jørgen Bo","name_org":"Hasselstrøm, Jørgen B.","orcid":"0000-0002-5928-9238","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Maiken K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5dec5e73-3ad6-468f-8ee7-4fa887c20851","name":"Larsen, Maiken Kudahl","name_org":"Larsen, Maiken K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36281709"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/bcpt.13808","issn":["17427835"],"issue":"1","journal":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","pages":"111-119","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd","publisher_org":"Wiley-Blackwell Publishing Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Basic & Clinical Pharmacology & Toxicology","title_org":"Basic and Clinical Pharmacology and Toxicology","volume":"132"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141354489"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-44526eac-d393-4350-bc54-c154f2207d41"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Deaths caused by medication in persons not using illicit narcotic drugs : An autopsy study from Western Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-707480","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND-AIM Chronic kidney disease (CKD) is a significant public health issue, affecting millions of individuals worldwide. Comorbidities and polypharmacy challenge appropriate treatment of patients with CKD. The Cytochrome P450 (CYP450) drug-metabolizing enzymes play a pivotal role in metabolizing a substantial portion of the prescribed drugs in patients with CKD. Genes responsible for encoding the CYP450 enzyme family exhibit high levels of polymorphism, which result in variations in enzyme activity levels, consequently leading to variations in drug responses and potential side effects. The objective of this registry study is to assess the utilization of PGx drugs among patients with CKD and to explore the potential of integrating PGx-based decision-making into clinical practice. METHODS This study was a retrospective study of patients affiliated to the Department of Nephrology, Aalborg University Hospital in The North Denmark Region during 2021. Inclusion criteria was a diagnosis of CKD according to the ICD-10. Patients were divided into 1) CKD without dialysis 2) CKD with dialysis. PGx prescription drugs were retrieved from the Patient Administration System (PAS) including demographic data. Actionable dosing guidelines for specific gene-drug pairs for CYP2D6, CYP2C9, CYP2C19 and SLCO1B1were retrieved from the PharmGKB homepage. RESULTS Out of 1241 individuals, 25.5% were on dialysis. The median number of medications for each patient was 9 within the non-dialysis group, and 16 within the dialysis group. In total, 31 distinct PGx drugs were prescribed, representing 13 different subgroups at the ATC level 3. Altogether, 76.0% (943 individuals) were prescribed between 1 and 6 PGx drugs and the prevalence of prescriptions of PGx drugs was higher the dialysis group compared to the non-dialysis group. The most frequently prescribed drugs with actionable dosing guidelines were metoprolol, pantoprazole, atorvastatin, simvastatin, warfarin, clopidogrel, and tramadol. The most frequent dyad was the combination of atorvastatin and metoprolol, and the most frequent triad was the combination of pantoprazole, metoprolol, and atorvastatin, both with prevalence of about 4%. CONCLUSIONS This study demonstrated that a substantial proportion of patients with CKD are exposed to drugs or drug combinations for which there exists actionable dosing guidelines related to PGx of CYP2D6, CYP2C19, CYP2C9, and SLCO1B1. These findings underscore the clinical potential of assessing and accounting for genotypic variations and drug-drug interactions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Westergaard, Niels","Houlind, Morten Baltzer","Christrup, Lona Louring","Juul-Larsen, Helle Gybel","Strandhave, Charlotte","Olesen, Anne Estrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713142"],"event":{"end":"2023-10-28","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2023-10-25","title":"7th ESPT Congress","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-AB","DI-UC-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-AB"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of drugs with pharmacogenomics pgx based dosing guidelines in a danish cohort of persons with chronic kidney disease both on dialysis and not on dialysis perspectives for prescribing optimization","src":["pha"],"src-code":["DI-UC-AB"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-713142","ids":["pha-87c9b3b0-ce42-4a9b-ae64-2dff989dec98"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-75F3C666571CDF52914C08893BD2FD42"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"university college absalon","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-AB","l3nl":"University College Absalon","l3nn":"University College Absalon","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University College Absalon","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Absalon, Direktionen - Slagelse, Sundhed, Social og Engineeringområdet, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-AB","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"westergaardpau","last":"Westergaard","locid":"724878cd-d318-4aec-a0a7-bdb6af7bd8c4","name":"Westergaard, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-2663-8040","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Baltzer","key":"houlindpau","last":"Houlind","name":"Houlind, Morten Baltzer","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lona Louring","key":"christruppau","last":"Christrup","name":"Christrup, Lona Louring","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Gybel","key":"juullarsenpau","last":"Juul-Larsen","name":"Juul-Larsen, Helle Gybel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"strandhavepau","last":"Strandhave","name":"Strandhave, Charlotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Estrup","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Anne Estrup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","All University Colleges","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University College Absalon","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["pha-87c9b3b0-ce42-4a9b-ae64-2dff989dec98"],"src":["AB University College Absalon"],"title":"Use of drugs with Pharmacogenomics (PGx)-Based Dosing Guidelines in a Danish Cohort of Persons with Chronic Kidney Disease, Both on Dialysis and Not on Dialysis: Perspectives for Prescribing Optimization","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713142","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: There are significant differences in the densities of resident specialists in gynaecology (RSGs) in various regions of Denmark. It is unclear whether this disparity affects gynaecological patients' experience of the referral process and whether it differs in terms of their socioeconomic status (SES). OBJECTIVE: To examine gynaecological patients' experiences of the referral process to an RSG concerning RSG density and patients' SES. DESIGN: Cross-sectional questionnaire and registry-based study. SETTING: In Denmark, general practitioners (GPs) serve as gatekeepers of secondary care and are responsible for referrals to resident specialists as well as inpatient and outpatient hospital care. SUBJECTS: A total of 2917 patients who consulted an RSG participated in this study. MAIN OUTCOME MEASUREMENTS: Patients' experiences of referral to an RSG, waiting times, involvement, and how they experienced the referral process. RESULTS: Patients who lived in the highest density RSG region were referred to an RSG more promptly after the onset of symptoms, had to visit their GP less frequently to obtain a referral to the RSG, and rarely received a gynaecological examination by their GP compared with those living in regions with lower RSG densities. Moreover, their waiting times were shorter, and more often, the patients themselves proposed to be referred to an RSG. The findings show that RSG density had a greater impact on women's experiences than SES. CONCLUSION: To allow equal access to specialist care, RSG density must be equal across all regions in the country.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Laschke, Alexander","Blaakær, Jan","Jensen, Charlotte Floridon","Larsen, Mette Bach"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713563"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Laschke, Alexander"],"keyword":["Gatekeeping","Gynaecology","Health Services Accessibility","Health equity","Referral and Consultation","Secondary Care"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Gynækologisk Klinik Holbæk"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differences in the referral process from general practice to resident specialists in gynaecology depending on density of specialists and patients socioeconomic status","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2023.2268663","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-713563","identifier":[{"id":"85174149108","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37837435","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-099755f3-c31b-4ded-8c2e-926b22149d02"],"keyword":["Gatekeeping","gynaecology","health equity","health services accessibility","referral and consultation","secondary care"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B731A23DADD5EE5A2866B470EFC3C71C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/252584642/Differences_in_the_referral_process_from_general_practice_to_resident_specialists_in_gynaecology_depending_on_density_of_specialists_and_patients_soc.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/02813432.2023.2268663","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Speciallægeselskabet Alexander Laschke ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Gynækologisk Klinik Holbæk"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regionshospitalet Randers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander D L","key":"laschkepau","last":"Laschke","locid":"6b0a6a80-9955-4152-be22-f966da19e165","name":"Laschke, Alexander","name_org":"Laschke, Alexander D L","orcid":"0000-0003-2348-6747","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"blaakærpau","last":"Blaakær","locid":"1a4149d9-2f14-46a8-882f-702c626338f5","name":"Blaakær, Jan","orcid":"0000-0003-3726-0589","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Floridon","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Charlotte Floridon","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette Bach","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Mette Bach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37837435"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/02813432.2023.2268663","issn":["02813432","15027724"],"issn_org":["02813432"],"issue":"4","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Primary Health Care","pages":"435-444","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Primary Health Care","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174149108"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","speciallægeselskabet alexander laschke aps"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-099755f3-c31b-4ded-8c2e-926b22149d02"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Differences in the referral process from general practice to resident specialists in gynaecology depending on density of specialists and patients' socioeconomic status","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713563","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A virus (IAV) is an RNA virus that causes respiratory disease in a wide range of mammals including humans and pigs. Cav1.2 is a specific voltage-dependent calcium channel (VDCC) important for the internalization of IAV and VDCC inhibitors can decrease IAV disease severity in mice. In this paper, the distribution pattern of a range of VDCCs by immunohistochemistry and Cav1.2 by in situ hybridization in the porcine respiratory tract is documented for the first time. Furthermore, we showed co-localization of VDCC-positive and IAV-positive cells in experimentally infected pigs. These findings provide new perspectives on the IAV internalization process and pave the way for further research investigating the effect of VDDC inhibitors on the IAV infection dynamics in pigs, which could have relevance to humans too.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kristensen, Charlotte","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Trebbien, Ramona","Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-722171"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"co localization of influenza a virus and voltage dependent calcium channels provides new perspectives on the internalization process in pigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44298-023-00009-x","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-722171","ids":["ku-e256088e-793e-42b9-9f35-70f0ebef52b4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C01998E44BA9254E0745448BDF72F72B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381842438/Co_localization_of_influenza_A_virus_and_voltage_dependent_calcium_channels_provides_new_perspectives_on_the_internalization_process_in_pigs.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44298-023-00009-x","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"39624808-4517-44fd-b288-2be379b5cf1a","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik E.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","name_org":"Jensen, Henrik E.","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s44298-023-00009-x","issn":["29481767"],"journal":"npj Viruses","paperid":"8","status":"p","title":"npj Viruses","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e256088e-793e-42b9-9f35-70f0ebef52b4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Co-localization of influenza A virus and voltage-dependent calcium channels provides new perspectives on the internalization process in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-722171","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Insufficient prenatal nutrition can affect fetal development and lead to intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR). The aim of this study was to investigate hepatic transcriptional responses and innate immune function in piglets suffering from IUGR compared to normal-sized piglets at 3 days of age and explore whether the provision of an energy-rich supplement at birth could modulate these parameters. Methods: A total of 68 piglets were included in the study. Peripheral blood mononuclear cells were harvested for LPS stimulation, and organs were harvested post-mortem to quantify relative weights. Liver tissue was utilized for RNA sequencing coupled with gene-set enrichment analysis. Results: IUGR resulted in increased expression of genes such as PDK4 and substantial alterations in transcriptional pathways related to metabolic activity (e.g., citric acid and Krebs cycles), but these changes were equivalent in piglets given an energy-rich supplement or not. Transcriptomic analysis and serum biochemistry suggested altered glucose metabolism and a shift toward oxidation of fatty acids. IUGR piglets also exhibited suppression of genes related to innate immune function (e.g., CXCL12) and pathways related to cell proliferation (e.g., WNT and PDGF signaling). Moreover, they produced less IL-1β in response to LPS stimulation and had lower levels of blood eosinophils than normal-sized piglets. Discussion: Taken together, our results indicate that IUGR results in early-life alterations in metabolism and immunity that may not be easily restored by the provision of exogenous energy supplementation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Williams, Charlotte Amdi","Larsen, C.","Jensen, Karen M.R.","Ørgård Tange, Esther","Sato, Helena","Williams, Andrew R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739605"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fetal Development","Intrauterine growth restriction","LPS challenge","Liver metabolism","Physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intrauterine growth restriction in piglets modulates postnatal immune function and hepatic transcriptional responses independently of energy intake","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphys.2023.1254958","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739605","identifier":[{"id":"37916220","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85175077072","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10617784","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a47c4e7d-7e95-47b1-96a3-84326ff6fcad"],"keyword":["LPS challenge","energy supplement","fetal development","intrauterine growth restriction","liver metabolism","physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-44A647BD9BC0DE1A3EA8C643FE73AD70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/391499994/fphys_14_1254958.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fphys.2023.1254958","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"amdipau","last":"Amdi","locid":"8057561d-85f5-4717-ba1e-18a709a9f121","name":"Williams, Charlotte Amdi","name_org":"Amdi, C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"694ee612-8562-4e50-9a0e-1918acd31784","name":"Larsen, C.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"K. M. R.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"c959ab50-d836-44a1-83c4-31844a72ed13","name":"Jensen, Karen M.R.","name_org":"Jensen, K. M. R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"E. Ø.","key":"tangepau","last":"Tange","locid":"10cdfc91-9046-4805-9f0a-9f0fbb247614","name":"Ørgård Tange, Esther","name_org":"Tange, E. Ø.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"H.","key":"satopau","last":"Sato","locid":"8deef930-0334-43e9-a7d0-a7074e9030e6","name":"Sato, Helena","name_org":"Sato, H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A. R.","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","locid":"393f749c-84d9-4245-84f2-1fee6f8d3ead","name":"Williams, Andrew R.","name_org":"Williams, A. R.","orcid":"0000-0002-8231-282X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37916220"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fphys.2023.1254958","issn":["1664042X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Physiology","paperid":"1254958","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Physiology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175077072"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a47c4e7d-7e95-47b1-96a3-84326ff6fcad"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Intrauterine growth restriction in piglets modulates postnatal immune function and hepatic transcriptional responses independently of energy intake","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739605","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Women with prior gestational diabetes face a highly increased risk of type 2 diabetes and are difficult to recruit for follow-up care, possibly due to a loss of professional support in the care pathway. This study aimed to explore Danish health professionals’ experiences of the challenges in the care pathway for women with prior gestational diabetes, the obstacles to continuity of care, and the possibility of better preventing type 2 diabetes. Qualitative semi-structured interviews with twelve health care professionals were conducted. The interviews were analyzed using inductive content analysis. The study follows the COREQ-checklist. The findings are organized into five main categories. The conclusions indicate that gestational diabetes is easily overlooked due to a lack of information sharing and continuity across health care delivery systems. Creating a management plan and engaging general practice nurses as designated health professionals may improve the care pathway and better prevent type 2 diabetes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ottesen, Anna Camilla","Nørgaard Plougmann, Stine","Hyldgaard Nielsen, Jane","Larsen Rasmussen, Rikke","Overgaard, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-091.75-008141"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ottesen, Anna Camilla"],"keyword":["Continuity of Patient Care","Continuity of care","Diabetes","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Diabetes mellitus","General practice","Gestational","Gestational diabetes mellitus","Public health","Public health nursing","Qualitative Research","disease health science and nursing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"potential improvements to women s care pathways after gestational diabetes a qualitative study","src":["aau","ucn"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://journals.sagepub.com/eprint/3PEG65MRN9ZBBIZSKD94/full","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/20571585221100237","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-091.75-008141","identifier":[{"id":"85206954855","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a84d34ea-84c8-4170-8c68-04fbe1177cf2","ucn-e141884d-32ac-49c2-b1e7-12199893a7ba"],"keyword":["Gestational diabetes Mellitus","continuity of care","continuity of patient care","diabetes","diabetes mellitus","diabetes mellitus type 2","disease, health science and nursing","general practice","gestational","public health","public health nursing","qualitative research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-934F47B2F1FD5680603E51B63133B4B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://journals.sagepub.com/eprint/3PEG65MRN9ZBBIZSKD94/full","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/20571585221100237","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen Aalborg","Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Sygeplejerskeuddannelsen Hjørring og Thisted"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Public Health and Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna Camilla","key":"ottesenpau","last":"Ottesen","locid":"21987693-01aa-444d-9473-726fd41bc3b6","name":"Ottesen, Anna Camilla","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Nørgaard","key":"plougmannpau","last":"Plougmann","locid":"b2d58909-9b37-47ed-9c72-68b0f70eb565","name":"Plougmann, Stine Nørgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Hyldgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"eae86023-3897-4f92-b4ce-6378fc86abd6","name":"Nielsen, Jane Hyldgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-2815-3984","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"larsenrasmussenpau","last":"Larsen Rasmussen","locid":"e96fe96e-f863-405d-b59d-4801409543f7","name":"Larsen Rasmussen, Rikke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"5f4b4ed5-6a98-4b94-9c0d-91e11cb0f9a9","name":"Overgaard, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-3370-2338","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/20571585221100237","issn":["20571585","20571593"],"issn_org":["20571585"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nordic Journal of Nursing Research","pages":"1-9","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Nursing Research","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206954855"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University College of Northern Denmark","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a84d34ea-84c8-4170-8c68-04fbe1177cf2","ucn-e141884d-32ac-49c2-b1e7-12199893a7ba"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","UCN University College of Northern Denmark"],"title":"Potential Improvements to Women’s Care Pathways After Gestational Diabetes : A Qualitative Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.75-008141","year":"2023","yearsub":2023}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: One in four pregnancies end in a pregnancy loss. Although the effect on couples is well documented, evidence-based treatments and prediction models are absent. Fetal aneuploidy is associated with a higher chance of a next successful pregnancy compared with euploid pregnancy loss in which underlying maternal conditions might be causal. Ploidy diagnostics are therefore advantageous but challenging as they require collection of the pregnancy tissue. Cell-free fetal DNA (cffDNA) from maternal blood has the potential for evaluation of fetal ploidy status, but no large-scale validation of the method has been done. METHODS: In this prospective cohort study, women with a pregnancy loss were recruited as a part of the Copenhagen Pregnancy Loss (COPL) study from three gynaecological clinics at public hospitals in Denmark. Women were eligible for inclusion if older than 18 years with a pregnancy loss before gestational age 22 weeks (ie, 154 days) and with an intrauterine pregnancy confirmed by ultrasound (including anembryonic sac), and women with pregnancies of unknown location or molar pregnancies were excluded. Maternal blood was collected while pregnancy tissue was still in situ or within 24 h after pregnancy tissue had passed and was analysed by genome-wide sequencing of cffDNA. Direct sequencing of the pregnancy tissue was done as reference. FINDINGS: We included 1000 consecutive women, at the time of a pregnancy loss diagnosis, between Nov 12, 2020, and May 1, 2022. Results from the first 333 women with a pregnancy loss (recruited between Nov 12, 2020, and Aug 14, 2021) were used to evaluate the validity of cffDNA-based testing. Results from the other 667 women were included to evaluate cffDNA performance and result distribution in a larger cohort of 1000 women in total. Gestational age of fetus ranged from 35-149 days (mean of 70·5 days [SD 16·5], or 10 weeks plus 1 day). The cffDNA-based test had a sensitivity for aneuploidy detection of 85% (95% CI 79-90) and a specificity of 93% (95% CI 88-96) compared with direct sequencing of the pregnancy tissue. Among 1000 cffDNA-based test results, 446 (45%) were euploid, 405 (41%) aneuploid, 37 (4%) had multiple aneuploidies, and 112 (11%) were inconclusive. 105 (32%) of 333 women either did not manage to collect the pregnancy tissue or collected a sample classified as unknown tissue giving a high risk of being maternal. INTERPRETATION: This validation of cffDNA-based testing in pregnancy loss shows the potential and feasibility of the method to distinguish euploid and aneuploid pregnancy loss for improved clinical management and benefit of future reproductive medicine and women's health research. FUNDING: Ole Kirks Foundation, BioInnovation Institute Foundation, and the Novo Nordisk Foundation.","author_count":43,"contributors":["Schlaikjær Hartwig, Tanja","Ambye, Louise","Gruhn, Jennifer R.","Petersen, Jesper Friis","Wrønding, Tine","Amato, Letizia","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Ji, Boyang","Bro-Jørgensen, Maiken Hemme","Werge, Lene","Petersen, Mette Marie Babiel Schmidt","Brinkmann, Clara","Petersen, Julie Birch","Dunø, Morten","Bache, Iben","Herrgård, Markus J.","Jørgensen, Finn Stener","Hoffmann, Eva R.","Nielsen, Henriette Svarre","Hartwig, Tanja Schlaikjær","Freiesleben, Nina la Cour","Bliddal, Sofie","Søndergaard, Therese Juhlin","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Sørensen, Erik","Larsen, Margit Anita Hørup","Herregård, Markus J.","Chan, Andrew Chi Ho","Kolte, Astrid Marie","Westergaard, David","þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Stefánsson, Kári","Jónsson, Hákon","Magnússon, Ólafur","Steinthorsdottir, Valgerdur","Schmidt, Lone","Kristiansen, Karsten","Kamstrup, Pia Rørbæk","Nyegaard, Mette","Krog, Maria Christine","Løkkegaard, Ellen","Bredkjær, Helle Ejdrup","Wilken-Jensen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-094.13-005502"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["COPL consortium"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["BioInnovation Institute"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cell free fetal dna for genetic evaluation in copenhagen pregnancy loss study copl a prospective cohort study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/423927953/AM_AM2_AM3_AM4_merged_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-094.13-005502","identifier":[{"id":"85149715335","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36739882","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-71680817-4e75-4218-8aa5-eb2b74c614d2","ku-008c6cad-106e-4668-a3c3-5ba33b9373b4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D809A774E757DD4CAEF7DC838103091F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/423927953/AM_AM2_AM3_AM4_merged_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Molecular Aging Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"