0-f5da-4a58-a903-8b13233542bf"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The effect of traditional diet on glucose homoeostasis in carriers and non-carriers of a common TBC1D4 variant in Greenlandic Inuit : a randomised crossover study.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.91-716513","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background Real-life evidence on prevalence and management of severe asthma is limited. Nationwide population registries across the Nordic countries provide unique opportunities to describe prevalence and management patterns of severe asthma at population level. In nationwide register data from Sweden, Norway and Finland, we examined the prevalence of severe asthma and the proportion of severe asthma patients being managed in specialist care. Methods This is a cross-sectional study based on the Nordic Dataset for Asthma Research (NORDSTAR) research collaboration platform. We identified patients with severe asthma in adults (aged ⩾18 years) and in children (aged 6–17 years) in 2018 according to the European Respiratory Society/American Thoracic Society definition. Patients managed in specialist care were those with an asthma-related specialist outpatient contact (only available in Sweden and Finland). Results Overall, we identified 598 242 patients with current asthma in Sweden, Norway and Finland in 2018. Among those, the prevalence of severe asthma was 3.5%, 5.4% and 5.2% in adults and 0.4%, 1.0%, and 0.3% in children in Sweden, Norway and Finland, respectively. In Sweden and Finland, 37% and 40% of adult patients with severe asthma and two or more exacerbations, respectively, were managed in specialist care; in children the numbers were 56% and 41%, respectively. Conclusion In three Nordic countries, population-based nationwide data demonstrated similar prevalence of severe asthma. In children, severe asthma was a rare condition. Notably, a large proportion of patients with severe asthma were not managed by a respiratory specialist, suggesting the need for increased recognition of severe asthma in primary care.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Hansen, Susanne","von Bülow, Anna","Sandin, Patrik","Ernstsson, Olivia","Janson, Christer","Lehtimäki, Lauri","Kankaanranta, Hannu","Ulrik, Charlotte","Aarli, Bernt Bøgvald","Wahl, Hanna Fues","Geale, Kirk","Tang, Sheila Tuyet","Wolf, Maija","Larsen, Tom","Altraja, Alan","Backman, Helena","Kilpeläinen, Maritta","Viinanen, Arja","Ludviksdottir, Dora","Kauppi, Paula","Sverrild, Asger","Lehmann, Sverre","Backer, Vibeke","Yasinska, Valentyna","Skjold, Tina","Karjalainen, Jussi","Bossios, Apostolos","Porsbjerg, Celeste"],"cuid":["S02-098.70-666477"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Susanne"],"country":["Estonia","Finland","France","Iceland","Norway","Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Haukeland University Hospital","Karolinska Institutet","Landspitali University Hospital","Novartis","Novartis Finland","Novartis Norge","Novartis Norway AS","Quantify Research","Sanofi","Seinajoki Central Hospital","Tampere University","Umeå University","University of Bergen","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki","University of Iceland","University of Tartu","University of Turku","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prevalence and management of severe asthma in the nordic countries findings from the nordstar cohort","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/23120541.00687-2022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.70-666477","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10068510","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37020835","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85153731153","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c51d