 M.","rank":73,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Konrad","key":"neumannkonradpau","last":"Neumann","name":"Neumann, Konrad","rank":74,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 42","first":"Henryk","key":"dregerhenrykpau","last":"Dreger","name":"Dreger, Henryk","rank":75,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Matthias","key":"riefmatthiaspau","last":"Rief","name":"Rief, Matthias","rank":76,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"43","first":"John","key":"daneshjohnpau","last":"Danesh","name":"Danesh, John","rank":77,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Melanie","key":"estrellamelaniepau","last":"Estrella","name":"Estrella, Melanie","rank":78,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Maria","key":"bosserdtmariapau","last":"Bosserdt","name":"Bosserdt, Maria","rank":79,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"41","first":"Peter","key":"martuspeterpau","last":"Martus","name":"Martus, Peter","rank":80,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"37","first":"Jonathan D.","key":"doddjonathandpau","last":"Dodd","name":"Dodd, Jonathan D.","rank":81,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 42 44 45","first":"Marc","key":"deweymarcpau","last":"Dewey","name":"Dewey, Marc","rank":82,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37725834"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2337/dc23-0710","issn":["01495992"],"issn_org":["19355548"],"issue":"11","journal":"Diabetes Care","pages":"2015-2023","status":"p","title":"Diabetes Care","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175357819"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3e2c2df4-9ce2-4cd8-991a-c9b393cd212a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computed Tomography Versus Invasive Coronary Angiography in Patients With Diabetes and Suspected Coronary Artery Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719963","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Currently, SARS-CoV-2 have been detected in farmed mink in 13 different countries. Due to the high susceptibility and transmissibility among mink, great concerns of mink serving as a reservoir to generate novel variants with unknown virulence and antigenic properties arose. These concerns have consequently resulted in entire mink productions being culled and banned. This study investigates the post-vaccination antibody response in the Canadian farmed mink vaccinated with a commercial Index spike protein-based vaccine, approved for use in cats, and compares the antibody response to that observed post infection in Danish farmed mink. Blood samples were obtained from 50 mink at the Canadian Centre for Fur Animal Research (CCFAR), Dalhousie University (Truro, Canada). The sera were initially analyzed for antibodies by enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay (ELISA), and selected sera was subsequently tested in a virus neutralization tests. The levels of neutralizing antibodies were evaluated for an ancestral D614G strain and a recent circulating SARS-CoV-2 variant of concern (Omicron BA.4). The results revealed that the vaccine induced a strong antibody response in mink by reaching antibody titer levels of up to 1:12800 in the ELISA. Moreover, high levels of neutralizing antibodies were obtained, and despite the great level of genetic differences between the ancestral and Omicron BA.4 strains, the vaccinated mink showed high levels of cross-reacting neutralizing antibodies. Interestingly, the antibody levels towards SARS-CoV-2 in the Canadian vaccinated mink were significantly higher than observed in recently SARS-CoV-2 infected Danish mink and equal to anamnestic responses following re-infection. In conclusion, the vaccine used in the Canadian farmed mink was able to induce a strong and broad-reacting antibody response in mink, which could limit the spread of SARS-CoV-2 in farmed mink and thereby reduce the risk of mink serving as a SARS-CoV-2 reservoir for human infections.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hansen, Line Gram","Larsen, Lars Erik","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","Miar, Younes","Lassuniére, Ria","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Ryt-Hansen, Pia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739188"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dalhousie University"],"keyword":["Antibody response","Cross protection","Mink","Neogale vison","SARS CoV 2","Vaccination"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of the sars cov 000000000002 post vaccination antibody response in canadian farmed mink","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.10.073","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-739188","identifier":[{"id":"37932134","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85175869721","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-60294411-f0bc-49fb-9fe8-21a2d0ee070c"],"keyword":["Antibody response","Cross-protection","Mink","Neogale vison","SARS-CoV-2","Vaccination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-842A9E8E6CBA4F49D5B7F4D6A46CC621"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/390194228/1_s2.0_S0264410X23012884_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.10.073","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"dalhousie university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Dalhousie University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Line Gram","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"11549d14-c45d-43b0-923a-f08c66e86bce","name":"Hansen, Line Gram","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas Bruun","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Younes","key":"miarpau","last":"Miar","name":"Miar, Younes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ria","key":"lassuniérepau","last":"Lassuniére","name":"Lassuniére, Ria","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Sværke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37932134"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vaccine.2023.10.073","issn":["0264410X","13552732"],"issn_org":["0264410X"],"issue":"49","journal":"Vaccine","pages":"7387-7394","status":"p","title":"Vaccine","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175869721"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-60294411-f0bc-49fb-9fe8-21a2d0ee070c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigation of the SARS-CoV-2 post-vaccination antibody response in Canadian farmed mink","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739188","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Increasing age and providing liquid creep feed could potentially increase the solid feed intake in pre-weaning piglets, which may in turn promote gut maturation and post-weaning feed intake, possibly lessening the severity of the growth-check associated with the suckling-to-weaning transition. Therefore, this study aimed to investigate if feeding dry- versus liquid creep feed (DF vs. LF) and weaning in week 4 or 5 (4W or 5W) could accelerate maturational changes to the small intestines of pre-weaning piglets by increasing digestive and absorptive capacity. In a 2 × 2 factorial study the effect of weaning age (WA) and feeding strategy (FS) on weaning weight, pre-weaning accumulated gain (AG), and average daily gain was measured for 12 923 piglets. A subpopulation of 15 piglets from each treatment group (4WDF, 4WLF, 5WDF and 5WLF; n = 60) were sacrificed to assess the effects of WA and FS on weight of digestive organs, activity of maltase, lactase and sucrase, and gene expression level of sodium-glucose linked transporter 1 (SGLT-1), glucose transporter 2 (GLUT2) and peptide transporter 1 (PepT1) in the proximal part of the small intestine (SI). No interactions were found but average weaning weight was affected by WA (P < 0.001) and FS (P < 0.001), where 5W were heavier than 4W and LF were heavier than DF. Correspondingly, the average daily gain (ADG) was affected by both WA (P = 0.003) and FS (P < 0.001). Only WA affected the relative weight of the digestive organs, where stomach weight, weight of SI and colon weight were heavier in 5W piglets compared to 4W. Lactase activity tended to decrease with age (P = 0.061), but there was no difference in the activity of maltase or sucrase between any of the treatment groups. Similarly, there was no differences in gene expression level of SGLT1, GLUT2 or PepT1 between neither the two ages nor feeding strategies. In conclusion, both WA and FS affect weaning weight and weight gain of piglets in the pre-weaning period.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Lyderik, Kimmie Kyed","Madsen, Johannes Gulmann","Larsen, C.","Pedersen, M. L.M.","Kjeldsen, N. J.","Williams, Andrew R.","Hedemann, M. S.","Williams, Charlotte Amdi"],"cuid":["S02-088.00-685870"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Amdi, C."],"keyword":["Creep feed","Digestive capacity","Enzyme activity","Gut maturation","Nutrient transporter"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an increased weaning age and liquid feed enhances weight gain compared to piglets fed dry feed pre weaning","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.animal.2023.100801","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.00-685870","identifier":[{"id":"37121161","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85153800940","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-23d512d0-7487-4ed4-9809-35aa01fbf62a","ku-9a9a5c6b-bda8-451b-87d5-0bac1b287cc7"],"keyword":["Creep feed","Digestive capacity","Enzyme activity","Gut maturation","Nutrient transporter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5058BDB9542CCD1DA45AA999FD240424"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.animal.2023.100801","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/346257781/1_s2.0_S1751731123000976_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/337778427/Lyderik_2023_An_increased_weaning_age.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIVET Gut and host health (GHH)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"K. K.","key":"lyderikpau","last":"Lyderik","locid":"2ffd6bc0-87d7-4835-aa38-ebb7ca63492e","name":"Lyderik, Kimmie Kyed","name_org":"Lyderik, K. K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. G.","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"f4b4330e-ca58-4db7-90df-0220335d59f9","name":"Madsen, Johannes Gulmann","name_org":"Madsen, J. G.","orcid":"0000-0001-7528-9521","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"694ee612-8562-4e50-9a0e-1918acd31784","name":"Larsen, C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M. L.M.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, M. L.M.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"N. J.","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, N. J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"A. R.","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","locid":"393f749c-84d9-4245-84f2-1fee6f8d3ead","name":"Williams, Andrew R.","name_org":"Williams, A. R.","orcid":"0000-0002-8231-282X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M. S.","key":"hedemannpau","last":"Hedemann","locid":"9969d51d-789b-4f72-bff0-5eba8a1dce4f","name":"Hedemann, Mette Skou","name_org":"Hedemann, M. S.","orcid":"0000-0002-1164-4405","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"amdipau","last":"Amdi","locid":"8057561d-85f5-4717-ba1e-18a709a9f121","name":"Williams, Charlotte Amdi","name_org":"Amdi, C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37121161"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.animal.2023.100801","issn":["17517311","1751732X"],"issn_org":["17517311"],"issue":"5","journal":"Animal","paperid":"100801","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Animal","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153800940"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-23d512d0-7487-4ed4-9809-35aa01fbf62a","ku-9a9a5c6b-bda8-451b-87d5-0bac1b287cc7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An increased weaning age and liquid feed enhances weight gain compared to piglets fed dry feed pre-weaning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.00-685870","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The objective was to study the effects of weaning in week 5 (W5) vs. week 4 (W4), as well as liquid (LF) vs. dry feed (DF), on growth performance, disaccharidase activity and nutrient transporter expression after weaning. The experiment included 12,923 pigs fed LF or DF in the pre-weaning period and a subpopulation of 15 pigs from each group, W4DF, W4LF, W5DF and W5LF, which were weighed and euthanized five days after weaning. The proximal part of the small intestine was analyzed for maltase, lactase and sucrase activity and the expression of SGLT-1, GLUT-2 and PepT-1. Pigs fed LF displayed less maltase activity (2100 vs. 2729 U/mg protein, p < 0.05) but an increased expression of SGLT-1 (∆Ct: 5.22 vs. 6.21, p = 0.01). Pigs weaned in W5 were heavier than those weaned in W4 (9.35 vs. 7.11 kg BW, p ≤ 0.05), and pigs fed LF were heavier than those fed DF (8.55 vs. 7.91 kg BW, p ≤ 0.05) five days after weaning in the subpopulation. LF pigs (21.8 kg) were heavier than DF pigs (20.6 kg) (SE 0.108, p < 0.0001), and W4 pigs (21.0 kg) were lighter than W5 pigs (21.5 kg) (SE 0.108, p = 0.01) at nine weeks. LF increased weight gain in the early post-weaning period and at nine weeks, although this was apparently not explained by accelerated gut maturation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lyderik, Kimmie Kyed","Zhang, Xuwen","Larsen, C.","Kjeldsen, Niels Jørgen","Pedersen, Marie Louise Madelung","Hedemann, Mette Skou","Williams, Andrew R.","Williams, Charlotte Amdi","Madsen, Johannes Gulmann"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-692122"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Madsen, Johannes Gulmann"],"keyword":["Absorption","Enzyme activity","Growth performance","Liquid feed","Piglets","Weaning"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of weaning age and creep feed type on growth performance and gut maturation in weaned piglets","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ani13111851","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-692122","identifier":[{"id":"37889763","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85163138604","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10251834","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f5157fe1-7885-4a0f-aee9-4fde95d5c46c","ku-10a75961-46cf-470f-b9ac-a64d6f65caed"],"keyword":["absorption","enzyme activity","growth performance","liquid feed","piglets","weaning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-757A6F46DE508BAEAFBECA02136F3258"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ani13111851","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/359242202/animals_13_01851_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES Innovation"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIVET Gut and host health (GHH)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kimmie Kyed","key":"lyderikpau","last":"Lyderik","locid":"2ffd6bc0-87d7-4835-aa38-ebb7ca63492e","name":"Lyderik, Kimmie Kyed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xuwen","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Xuwen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"694ee612-8562-4e50-9a0e-1918acd31784","name":"Larsen, C.","name_org":"Larsen, Christina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Niels Jørgen","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","name":"Kjeldsen, Niels Jørgen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie Louise Madelung","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Marie Louise Madelung","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Skou","key":"hedemannpau","last":"Hedemann","locid":"9969d51d-789b-4f72-bff0-5eba8a1dce4f","name":"Hedemann, Mette Skou","orcid":"0000-0002-1164-4405","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andrew Richard","key":"williamspau","last":"Williams","locid":"393f749c-84d9-4245-84f2-1fee6f8d3ead","name":"Williams, Andrew R.","name_org":"Williams, Andrew Richard","orcid":"0000-0002-8231-282X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte","key":"amdipau","last":"Amdi","locid":"8057561d-85f5-4717-ba1e-18a709a9f121","name":"Williams, Charlotte Amdi","name_org":"Amdi, Charlotte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Johannes Gulmann","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"f4b4330e-ca58-4db7-90df-0220335d59f9","name":"Madsen, Johannes Gulmann","orcid":"0000-0001-7528-9521","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37889763"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ani13111851","issn":["20762615"],"issue":"11","journal":"Animals","paperid":"1851","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Animals","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163138604"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f5157fe1-7885-4a0f-aee9-4fde95d5c46c","ku-10a75961-46cf-470f-b9ac-a64d6f65caed"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effects of Weaning Age and Creep Feed Type on Growth Performance and Gut Maturation in Weaned Piglets","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-692122","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Around 500,000 Danes are suffering from urinary incontinence, and stress urinary incontinence and urgency urinary incontinence, alone or mixed, are the most common types. Diagnostic workup is similar for all types of urinary incontinence (men and women) and can be done by the GP. Most conservative interventions can be commenced by the GP. In complicated or treatment-resistant cases and when surgery is needed, referral to a urologic or gynaecological department can be necessary, as argued in this review.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Juhl, Caroline Sollberger","Andersen, Margrethe","Larsen, Robert S.","Graugaard-Jensen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S03-089.74-784788"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Juhl, Caroline Sollberger"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"urininkontinens","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/620147686/Juhl_et_al._2023_._Urininkontinens.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-089.74-784788","identifier":[{"id":"37057702","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85152372404","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-25a5aa95-e484-4b19-9efd-6bbfc3f1cc3d","au-17c1c87f-2be6-4d99-916c-c4d5eafc489d","sdu-26a5249f-6704-4b39-b5ef-5fce5a5a9a5e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-E4C6516F3094221C7F623F5D2966E3FB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/417809040/Urininkontinens.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/620147686/Juhl_et_al._2023_._Urininkontinens.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/urininkontinens-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/266299804/V10220594_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Gynaecology and Obstetrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Urology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital Central and West Jutland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Urology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline Sollberger","key":"juhlpau","last":"Juhl","locid":"8f4fd2bb-3b9a-4c66-80e5-69d265bea47e","name":"Juhl, Caroline Sollberger","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Margrethe","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"efdea963-9655-4d7f-adc2-94e84851e83d","name":"Andersen, Margrethe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert S.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Robert S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"graugaardjensenpau","last":"Graugaard-Jensen","locid":"740c7306-3f0b-4be4-b183-eae93d5b2b5a","name":"Graugaard-Jensen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-2441-1790","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37057702"],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"7A","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"688-692","paperid":"V10220594","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"185"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160423349"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-25a5aa95-e484-4b19-9efd-6bbfc3f1cc3d","au-17c1c87f-2be6-4d99-916c-c4d5eafc489d","sdu-26a5249f-6704-4b39-b5ef-5fce5a5a9a5e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Urininkontinens","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-089.74-784788","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to provide information about immunity against COVID-19 along with risk factors and behavior among employees in day care facilities and preschools (DCS) in Denmark. In collaboration with the Danish Union of Pedagogues, during February and March 2021, 47,810 members were offered a point-of-care rapid SARS-CoV-2 antibody test (POCT) at work and were invited to fill in an electronic questionnaire covering COVID-19 exposure. Seroprevalence data from Danish blood donors (total Ig enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay [ELISA]) were used as a proxy for the Danish population. A total of 21,018 (45%) DCS employees completed the questionnaire and reported their POCT result {median age, 44.3 years (interquartile range [IQR], [32.7 to 53.6]); females, 84.1%}, of which 20,267 (96.4%) were unvaccinated and included in analysis. A total of 1,857 (9.2%) participants tested seropositive, significantly higher than a seroprevalence at 7.6% (risk ratio [RR], 1.2; 95% confidence interval [CI], 1.14 to 1.27) among 40,541 healthy blood donors (median age, 42 years [IQR, 28 to 53]; males, 51.3%). Exposure at work (RR, 2.9; 95% CI, 2.3 to 3.6) was less of a risk factor than exposure within the household (RR, 12.7; 95% CI, 10.2 to 15.8). Less than 25% of participants reported wearing face protection at work. Most of the participants expressed some degree of fear of contracting COVID-19 both at work and outside work. SARS-CoV-2 seroprevalence was slightly higher in DCS staff than in blood donors, but possible exposure at home was associated with a higher risk than at work. DCS staff expressed fear of contracting COVID-19, though there was limited use of face protection at work. IMPORTANCE Identifying at-risk groups and evaluating preventive interventions in at-risk groups is imperative for the ongoing pandemic as well as for the control of future epidemics. Although DCS staff have a much higher risk of being infected within their own household than at their workplace, most are fearful of being infected with COVID-19 or bringing COVID-19 to work. This represents an interesting dilemma and an important issue which should be addressed by public health authorities for risk communication and pandemic planning. This study design can be used in a strategy for ongoing surveillance of COVID-19 immunity or other infections in the population. The findings of this study can be used to assess the need for future preventive interventions in DCS, such as the use of personal protective equipment.","author_count":39,"contributors":["Fogh, Kamille","Eriksen, Alexandra R. R.","Larsen, Tine Graakjær","Hasselbalch, Rasmus B.","Bundgaard, Henning","Scharff, Bibi F. S. S.","Nielsen, Susanne D.","Jørgensen, Charlotte S.","Erikstrup, Christian","Østergaard, Lars","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Andersen, Berit","Nielsen, Henrik","Johansen, Isik S.","Wiese, Lothar","Hindhede, Lotte","Mikkelsen, Susan","Sækmose, Susanne G.","Aagaard, Bitten","Holm, Dorte K.","Harritshøj, Lene","Simonsen, Lone","Fischer, Thea K.","Folke, Fredrik","Lippert, Freddy","Ostrowski, Sisse R.","Benfield, Thomas","Mølbak, Kåre","Ethelberg, Steen","Koch, Anders","Vangsted, Anne-Marie","Krause, Tyra Grove","Fomsgaard, Anders","Ullum, Henrik","Skov, Robert","Iversen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S05-098.37-005817"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","corresponding_author":["Fogh, Kamille"],"keyword":["Adult","Antibodies","Antibodies Viral","COVID 19 epidemiology","Child Day Care Centers","Child Preschool","Covid 19","Cross Sectional Studies","Day Care Medical","Denmark epidemiology","Employee","Faculty","Female","Humans","Kindergarten","Male","Point of care test","Risk Factors","SARS CoV 2","School","Schools","Seroepidemiologic Studies","Seroprevalence","Staff","day care facilities","surveillance study"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a cross sectional study of sars cov 000000000002 antibodies and risk factors for seropositivity in staff in day care facilities and preschools in denmark","src":["aau","au","ku","ruc","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-RUC","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/spectrum.04174-22","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S05-098.37-005817","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9927135","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85148114069","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36546864","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-77e38116-cf38-4495-aa26-eb61da156b99","au-86d3ec0c-bfd0-46b6-a5bc-f20eb4ad6e16","ku-d9b7bd1e-9f3b-4425-a86e-dfab5a04ba87","ruc-2305a9ec-adba-4137-a7bc-6dadbfc0e4bf","sdu-6970388d-8294-4828-a717-c6f65d30b736"],"keyword":["Adult","Antibodies, Viral","COVID-19","COVID-19/epidemiology","Child Day Care Centers","Child, Preschool","Cross-Sectional Studies","Day Care, Medical","Denmark/epidemiology","Faculty","Female","Humans","Male","Risk Factors","SARS-CoV-2","Schools","Seroepidemiologic Studies","antibodies","day care facilities","employee","kindergarten","point-of-care test","school","seroprevalence","staff","surveillance study"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-8-647EBF000D0CB046EED41CCBDB924F22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/336130282/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"