{"abstract":"Functional antibody deficiency is clinically assessed from antibody responses to vaccination. However, diagnostic vaccination is complex and may fail in practice. We hypothesized that the levels of naturally occurring antibodies against galactose-α-1,3-galactose (αGal) may represent alternative markers of functional antibody capacity. We included data from 229 patients with suspected primary immunodeficiency in a retrospective study. Antibody levels against αGal and twelve pneumococcal serotypes were determined with solid-phase immunoassays. Pneumococcal vaccinations and treatment with normal human immunoglobulin were assessed from medical records. Anti-αGal antibody levels correlated positively with anti-pneumococcal antibody levels measured before and after pneumococcal vaccination. Contrary to the anti-pneumococcal antibody levels, the anti-αGal antibody level showed potential for predicting subsequent immunoglobulin treatment - a marker of disease severity. Naturally occurring antibodies may reflect the functional capacity tested by diagnostic vaccination but add more useful clinical data. The clinical utility of this easy test should be evaluated in prospective studies.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth","Hansen, Anette Tarp","Söderström, Anna","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Larsen, Carsten Schade","Sørensen, Uffe B Skov","Thiel, Steffen","Petersen, Mikkel Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-137658"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth"],"keyword":["Antibodies Bacterial","Galactose","Humans","Immunoglobulin G","Pneumococcal Vaccines","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Vaccination"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a low level of naturally occurring antibodies associates with functional antibody deficiency","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clim.2022.109070","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-137658","identifier":[{"id":"35779828","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85133724369","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0e875af8-4fca-4b08-83d1-4b6b6e39d186"],"keyword":["Antibodies, Bacterial","Galactose","Humans","Immunoglobulin G","Pneumococcal Vaccines","Primary Immunodeficiency Diseases","Prospective Studies","Retrospective Studies","Vaccination"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-821DF61597F00D67104C8373814A7B70"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/346315470/A_low_level_of_naturally_occurring_antibodies_associates_with_functional_antibody_deficiency.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clim.2022.109070","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Immunology","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Magnus","key":"bernthjensenpau","last":"Bernth Jensen","locid":"a67e0021-e11c-47a3-93dd-8f3783ad755a","name":"Jensen, Jens Magnus Bernth","name_org":"Bernth Jensen, Jens Magnus","orcid":"0000-0002-5004-7822","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette Tarp","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"3eb73e87-6896-4583-9059-70692403d5cd","name":"Hansen, Anette Tarp","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"söderströmpau","last":"Söderström","locid":"57354c14-6f75-4d01-ad21-cc24b97b913c","name":"Söderström, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sværke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Schade","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2435cb82-03bd-498b-909d-1ef0e99443fe","name":"Larsen, Carsten Schade","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe B","key":"skovsørensenpau","last":"Skov Sørensen","locid":"6e354ce6-4d20-45ed-9336-2958dd4344c3","name":"Sørensen, Uffe B Skov","name_org":"Skov Sørensen, Uffe B","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steffen","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"beb49137-797f-4a6a-841c-340818b6f472","name":"Thiel, Steffen","orcid":"0000-0002-4817-155X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Steen","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"188d68ce-6256-4b77-b3a7-2d24490ed74a","name":"Petersen, Mikkel Steen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35779828"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clim.2022.109070","issn":["15216616","15217035"],"issn_org":["15216616"],"journal":"Clinical Immunology","paperid":"109070","publisher":"Academic Press Inc.","status":"p","title":"Clinical Immunology","volume":"241"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133724369"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0e875af8-4fca-4b08-83d1-4b6b6e39d186"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A low level of naturally occurring antibodies associates with functional antibody deficiency","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-137658","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and Objectives: Pain management in children is often inadequate, and the single most common painful procedure in children who are hospitalized is needle procedures. Virtual reality (VR) has been shown to decrease anxiety and pain in children undergoing painful procedures primarily in children from the age of 7 years. Our aim for this study is to investigate patient satisfaction and pain reduction by using a three-dimensional VR interactive game as a distraction in 4–7 years old children during venous cannulation. Methods: In this randomized clinical trial, we enrolled 106 children aged 4–7 years who were scheduled for venous cannulation. Patients assigned to the control group were adherent to standard of care, including topical numbing cream, positioning, and distraction in this group by games of choice on a tablet/smartphone. In the study group, children were adherent to standard of care and were distracted by an interactive VR game. Primary outcomes were patient satisfaction and the procedural pain assessed by using Wong–Baker Faces Pain Rating Scale; secondary outcomes were the procedural time and any adverse events. Results: We found an overall high level of patient satisfaction with our regime of topical numbing cream, positioning, and distraction. The primary outcome of pain during the procedure was median 20 mm (IQR 0–40) and 20 mm (IQR 0–55) (Wong–Baker 0–100 mm) in the VR group and the control group, respectively (difference: 0 mm, 95%CI: 0–20, p =.19). No significant difference was found in procedural times. The number of adverse effects was low, with no significant difference between the two groups. Conclusions: VR distraction is an acceptable form of distraction for children 4–7 years old when combined with topical numbing cream and positioning during preoperative venous cannulation. No difference was found between VR- and smartphone/tablet distraction.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Thybo, Kasper H.","Friis, Susanne M.","Aagaard, Gitte","Jensen, Claus Sixtus","Dyekjær, Charlotte Drejdal","Jørgensen, Casper Haslund","Walther-Larsen, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-273581"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Walther-Larsen, Søren"],"keyword":["Children","Distraction","Procedural pain"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a randomized controlled trial on virtual reality distraction during venous cannulation in young children","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14120","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-273581","identifier":[{"id":"85135850744","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9545199","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35898121","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-fcd5cf4e-cbaf-4b58-9d0b-1616fd8449e7"],"keyword":["children","distraction","procedural pain"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-23E610FC0EAAF9F091A91AF2BFEDCA2C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/330981530/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2022_Thybo_A_randomized_controlled_trial_on_virtual_reality_distraction_during_venous.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14120","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Paediatrics","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Research Center for Emergency Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper H.","key":"thybopau","last":"Thybo","name":"Thybo, Kasper H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne M.","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","name":"Friis, Susanne M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte","key":"aagaardpau","last":"Aagaard","name":"Aagaard, Gitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus S.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"fc10d75e-f4d9-4fd3-8791-a6cb072ad508","name":"Jensen, Claus Sixtus","name_org":"Jensen, Claus S.","orcid":"0000-0001-5416-7744","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte D.","key":"dyekjærpau","last":"Dyekjær","locid":"c1a0e475-8e07-4c10-8320-288b6a2d8f8e","name":"Dyekjær, Charlotte Drejdal","name_org":"Dyekjær, Charlotte D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper Haslund","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgense