h Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8b59dd76-c2ba-476d-a3d8-40e84647c459"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Research to support CO<sub>2</sub> storage in existing O&amp;G fields","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-346137","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Quantification of the relative ellipsoid zone reflectivity (rEZR) might be a structural surrogate parameter for an early disease progression in the context of age-related macular degeneration (AMD). Within the European multicenter, cross-sectional MACUSTAR study, we have devised an automatic approach to determine the mean rEZR [arbitrary units, AU] at two independent visits in SD-OCT volume scans in study participants. Linear mixed-effects models were applied to analyze the association of AMD stage and AMD associated high-risk features including presence of pigmentary abnormalities, reticular pseudodrusen (RPD), volume of the retinal-pigment-epithelial–drusenoid-complex (RPEDC) with the rEZR. Intra-class correlation coefficients (ICC) were determined for rEZR reliability analysis. Within the overall study cohort (301 participants), we could observe decreased rEZR values (coefficient estimate ± standard error) of − 8.05 ± 2.44 AU (p = 0.0011) in the intermediate and of − 22.35 ± 3.28 AU (p < 0.0001) in the late AMD group. RPD presence was significantly associated with the rEZR in iAMD eyes (− 6.49 ± 3.14 AU; p = 0.0403), while there was a good ICC of 0.846 (95% confidence interval: 0.809; 0.876) in the overall study cohort. This study showed an association of rEZR with increasing disease severity and the presence of iAMD high-risk features. Further studies are necessary to evaluate the rEZR’s value as a novel biomarker for AMD and disease progression.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Saßmannshausen, Marlene","Behning, Charlotte","Isselmann, Ben","Schmid, Matthias","Finger, Robert P.","Holz, F. G.","Schmitz-Valckenberg, Steffen","Pfau, Maximilian","Agostini, H.","Altay, L.","Atia, R.","Bandello, F.","Basile, P. G.","Behning, C.","Belmouhand, Mohamed","Berger, M.","Binns, A.","Boon, C. J.F.","Böttger, M.","Bouchet, C.","Brazier, J. E.","Butt, T.","Carapezzi, C.","Carlton, J.","Carneiro, A.","Charil, A.","Coimbra, R.","Cozzi, M.","Crabb, D. P.","Cunha-Vaz, J.","Dahlke, C.","de Sisternes, L.","Dunbar, H.","Finger, R. P.","Fletcher, E.","Floyd, H.","Francisco, C.","Gutfleisch, M.","Hogg, R.","Holz, F. G.","Hoyng, C. B.","Kilani, A.","Krätzschmar, J.","Kühlewein, L.","Larsen, Michael","Leal, S.","Lechanteur, Y. T.E.","Luhmann, U. F.O.","Lüning, A.","Marques, I."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-411461"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["MACUSTAR Consortium"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Portugal","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["AIBILI Association for Innovation and Biomedical Research on Light and Image (AIBILI)","All Global Affiliations","Bayer AG","Belfast Health and Social Care Trust","Carl Zeiss SMT AG","Centre hospitalier national d'ophtalmologie des Quinze-Vingts","City, University of London","F. Hoffmann-La Roche","Fondation Voir et Etendre","Gloucestershire Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust","Hospital Center São João","Leiden University","National Institutes of Health","Novartis","Radboud University Nijmegen","St. Franziskus-Hospital Münster","Ulm University","University College London","University of Bonn","University of Cologne","University of Freiburg","University of Milan","University of Sheffield","University of Tübingen","University of Utah","Vita-Salute San Raffaele University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relative ellipsoid zone reflectivity and its association with disease severity in age related macular degeneration a macustar study report","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-022-18875-5","version":"Publish