{"abstract":"Prediagnostic use of menopausal hormone therapy (MHT) has been suggested to be associated with improved survival of epithelial ovarian cancer (EOC). We investigated the potential long-term survival benefit of prediagnostic MHT use in women ≥50 years with nonlocalized EOC using the Extreme study including all women in Denmark registered with nonlocalized EOC during 2000 to 2014 (N = 3776). We obtained individual-level information on prediagnostic use of systemic estrogen therapy (ET) and estrogen plus progestin therapy (EPT) from the National Prescription Registry and estimated absolute and relative 5- and 10-year survival probabilities with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) using pseudo-values, taking into account histology, comorbidity, income and residual disease. Among women not having used prediagnostic MHT, 5- and 10-year absolute survival probabilities were 19% and 11%, respectively. Compared to MHT nonusers, prediagnostic systemic ET use for 3 to 4 years and ≥ 5 years was associated with 1.43 (95% CI: 1.01-2.02) and 1.22 (95% CI: 0.96-1.55) times higher 5-year survival probabilities, respectively. Ten-year survival probabilities were also increased but not statistically significantly. Among prediagnostic EPT users, increased 5-year (1.14, 95% CI: 0.85-1.53) and 10-year (1.38, 95% CI: 0.91-2.08) survival probabilities were observed after use for 3 to 4 years compared to MHT nonuse, whereas EPT use for ≥5 years was not associated with long-term survival of nonlocalized EOC. Our findings may suggest a better long-term survival of nonlocalized EOC in women having used long-term prediagnostic ET. However, the statistical precision of our results did not allow firm conclusions and more studies are needed.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Baandrup, Louise","Galanakis, Michael","Hannibal, Charlotte G.","Dehlendorff, Christian","Hertzum‐larsen, Rasmus","Mørch, Lina S.","Kjaer, Susanne K."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446714"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term survival of nonlocalized epithelial ovarian cancer among women using menopausal hormone therapy prior to diagnosis the extreme study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.34171","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446714","identifier":[{"id":"85133725120","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9541581","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35716136","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-59099281-6fdb-42a5-a4a6-ef90f5d6179a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EBDE9B638AB454741927A622D412081B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ijc.34171","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/325752293/Long_term_survival_of_nonlocalized_epithelial.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"baandruppau","last":"Baandrup","name":"Baandrup, Louise","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"galanakispau","last":"Galanakis","name":"Galanakis, Michael","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte G.","key":"hannibalpau","last":"Hannibal","name":"Hannibal, Charlotte G.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"dehlendorffpau","last":"Dehlendorff","name":"Dehlendorff, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus","key":"hertzumlarsenpau","last":"Hertzum‐larsen","name":"Hertzum‐larsen, Rasmus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lina S.","key":"mørchpau","last":"Mørch","name":"Mørch, Lina S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Susanne K.","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"1c671dbc-6a27-49fd-ba11-6d26a9a07047","name":"Kjaer, Susanne K.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35716136"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ijc.34171","issn":["00207136"],"issn_org":["08986924"],"issue":"9","journal":"International Journal of Cancer","pages":"1512-1522","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cancer","volume":"151"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133725120"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-59099281-6fdb-42a5-a4a6-ef90f5d6179a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long‐term survival of nonlocalized epithelial ovarian cancer among women using menopausal hormone therapy prior to diagnosis: The extreme study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446714","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Based on an ongoing research-project about \"Leisure time pedagogy and situated inequality\", we present the theoretical framework for understanding inequality in school as related to concrete social dynamics in the everyday life among both children and different professionals. By empirical examples, we illustrate how inequality relates to social situations and nexuses across children's compound everyday life contexts. Observations of situations in children's everyday school life illustrate how children together maneuver in double agendas related to social dynamics, academic tasks, collaboration, friendships, competition, conflicts, performance, etc. Including this acknowledgement of the signification of children's access to collaboration with other children points to methodological challenges. These are among other things related to exploring the social dynamics in communities from the perspectives of the children and to explore social - structural and historical - conditions in their concrete meanings to subjects and their everyday life. We will propose the concept of reasons - and not just reasons but what we term 'chains of reasons' as a methodological possibility for exploring structural conditions from the perspectives of the subjects living them. This has significances to how we move within our fieldwork and move our research according to the subjective reasons. When children's unequal conditions for taking part in school life are explored as 'wicked problems' in the sense that they relate to other problems, we must move our research - extend it into new contexts. In this way we work analytical and explorative with 'chains of reasons' as pointing to conditions of the problems and guiding the focus of exploration. In the research project, we conduct participatory observations in the life contexts of the children and in the working contexts of the professionals -- such as meetings, interdisciplinary collaboration and conflicts. Also, we conduct interviews with the involved and arrange research collaboration with the professionals. The theoretical basis for this exploration is a practice and subject oriented critical psychology with a focus on children's development of conduct of everyday life.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-567126"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-21","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2022-09-19","title":"2nd International CHILDLIFE Conference","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Children s perspectives","Education","Leisure time","Situated inequality"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"situated inequality in education how to explore children s conditions for participation from the perspective of subjective reasons","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-567126","ids":["ruc-a54a104e-cbc8-4e76-9a3a-5f4fcb774ed0"],"keyword":["Children's perspectives","Education","Leisure time","chains of reasons","situated inequality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-598C16ADA842F583C6E6AF5746A15697"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-a54a104e-cbc8-4e76-9a3a-5f4fcb774ed0"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Situated inequality in education : How to explore children’s conditions for participation from the perspective of subjective reasons","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-567126","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
