{"abstract":"This paper analyses what makes young adults feel insecure when they use social media to socialise and connect with peers. In a broader sense, the paper discusses what it means to grow up in a digitalized world with social media at the heart of youth life. The analysis is based on a two-year online ethnography conducted on Jodel, an anonymous location based social media app. The paper focuses on Jodel users’ anonymous disclosures about their social media related insecurities – shedding light on discourses related to social media practices that are often hidden or neglected in interview studies. The analysis finds that it is often the affordances of the platforms or design choices of apps such as Instagram, Snapchat or Tinder that lead to feelings of insecurity or uncertainty in relational maintenance or in the forming of new relationships. Because of the platforms, young adults sometimes find it difficult to know why peers behave like they do online, resulting in unfounded worries and feelings of insecurity.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Malene Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-105985"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"social media insecurities in everyday life among young adults an ethnography of anonymous jodel disclosures","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23865/ntpk.v8.4071","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-105985","ids":["aau-c0dccccd-fef7-44fe-a7ca-53f8fefe6509"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E6B2FD7E0D180C2D015822601F24F6DB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/489570899/NTPK_4071_Web.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.23865/ntpk.v8.4071","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Digital Media in Everyday Life","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Exploring Methods for Participation and Dialogue in Communication Research","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Mattering: Centre for Discourse & Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.23865/ntpk.v8.4071","issn":["23875739"],"journal":"Nordisk tidsskrift for pedagogikk og kritikk","pages":"298-313","publisher":"Cappelen Damm Akademisk","status":"p","title":"Nordisk tidsskrift for pedagogikk og kritikk","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c0dccccd-fef7-44fe-a7ca-53f8fefe6509"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Social media insecurities in everyday life among young adults - an ethnography of anonymous Jodel disclosures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-105985","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The current status of postoperative delirium (POD) risk in selected orthopedic elective surgery cohorts is unclear. The influence of fast-track surgery, in combination with regional anesthetic nerve blocks, BIS-monitoring and modernized patient trajectories, may well reduce POD risk, even in an elderly population. Methods: An observational cohort, screening for postoperative delirium using the Nu-DESC (Nursing-Delirium Screening Scale) in 879 consecutive elective orthopedic surgery patients. Nu-DESC rating at 4 preset time points; preoperatively, at emergence, at post-anesthesia care unit (PACU) admittance, at PACU discharge. Results: Overall, 6 of the (n=) 879 participants (0.68%) scored ≥2 Nu-DESC points when interviewed at PACU discharge. These were distributed amongst surgical categories as follows; Knee (0.0%), Hip (2 out of 227 = 0.88%), Shoulder (0 out of 70 = 0%), Minor Lumbar Spine (1 out of 226 = 0.44%), and Major Lumbar spine (3 out of 129 = 2.3%). 3.98% of all patients scored ≥2 NuDESC at PACU arrival. Though there was a significant overrepresentation of general anesthesia patients among ≥2 NuDESC, these select patients were not related to BIS-monitoring or Ketamine infusion, and inversely correlated to spinal anesthesia and regional anesthetic nerve blocks. Discussion: We report a lower-than anticipated incidence of POD-related ≥2 NuDESC scores at PACU discharge in a selected, elective orthopedic surgery cohort, but still a significant incidence at PACU arrival. Modern anesthesia management and techniques may help lower clinical POD in the elderly patient. Keywords: Postoperative delirium; Delirium score; orthopedic surgery; fast-track; patient pathways; regional anesthesia","author_count":12,"contributors":["Andreasen, Andreas Porsborg","Clemmesen, Louise","Madsen, Helle","Larsen, Christine L.","Nørgaard, Lotte Cecilie","Johansen, Iben N.","Skovbjerg, Mai H.","Ryhammer, Pia Katarina","Runge, Charlotte","Vestergaard, Trine Astrup Bech","Radtke, Finn M.","Larsen, Jens Rolighed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-263683"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low postoperative delirium risk after elective orthopedic fast track procedures","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.39127/2021/JRAPM:1000114","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-263683","ids":["au-eb64b467-72df-40c6-899b-52a021a9f7de"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-CC6967341AD305C9D18754EC29AF44B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.39127/2021/JRAPM:1000114","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University (AU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Regional Hospital of Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Region Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Porsborg","key":"andreasenandreasporsborgpau","last":"Andreasen","name":"Andreasen, Andreas Porsborg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie Louise","key":"clemmesenlouisepau","last":"Clemmesen","locid":"ea2925c3-0124-4309-9571-f0667949af07","name":"Clemmesen, Louise","name_org":"Clemmesen, Marie Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"madsenhellepau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Helle","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine L.","key":"larsenchristinelpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Christine L.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte Cecilie","key":"nørgaardlottececiliepau","last":"Nørgaard","name":"Nørgaard, Lotte Cecilie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben N.","key":"johansenibennpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Iben N.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mai H.","key":"skovbjergmaihpau","last":"Skovbjerg","name":"Skovbjerg, Mai H.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pia K.","key":"ryhammerpiakatarinapau","last":"Ryhammer","locid":"f6470443-165f-49a5-82f1-0d7b81c784aa","name":"Ryhammer, Pia Katarina","name_org":"Ryhammer, Pia K.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"rungecharlottepau","last":"Runge","locid":"eca83862-b388-4479-bc0b-c8a670ae52e9","name":"Runge, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-9480-2490","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Astrup Bech","key":"vestergaardtrineastrupbechpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"613d71b5-4e07-4f8b-b2e1-2351c3972869","name":"Vestergaard, Trine Astrup Bech","orcid":"0009-0004-8605-6108","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn M.","key":"radtkefinnmpau","last":"Radtke","name":"Radtke, Finn M.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Rolighed","key":"larsenjensrolighedpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"485143af-239d-407f-96e4-f045733fa8c8","name":"Larsen, Jens Rolighed","orcid":"0000-0003-0694-0135","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.39127/2021/jrapm:1000114","issn":["26617390"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Regional Anesthesia & Pain Medicine","pages":"1-4","paperid":"114","status":"p","title":"Journal of Regional Anesthesia & Pain Medicine","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-eb64b467-72df-40c6-899b-52a021a9f7de"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Low Postoperative Delirium Risk after Elective Orthopedic Fast-Track Procedures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-263683","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Multijunction solar cells in a tandem configuration could further lower the costs of electricity if crystalline Si (c-Si) is used as the bottom cell. However, for direct monolithic integration on c-Si, only a restricted number of top and bottom cell architectures are compatible, due to either epitaxy or high-temperature constraints, where the interface between subcells is subject to a trade-off between transmittance, electrical interconnection, and bottom cell degradation. Using polySi/SiOx passivating contacts for Si, this degradation can be largely circumvented by tuning the polySi/SiOx stacks to promote gettering of contaminants admitted into the Si bottom cell during the top cell synthesis. Applying this concept to the low-cost top cell chalcogenides Cu2ZnSnS4 (CZTS), CuGaSe2 (CGSe), and AgInGaSe2 (AIGSe), fabricated under harsh S or Se atmospheres above 550 °C, we show that increasing the heavily doped polySi layer thickness from 40 to up to 400 nm prevents a reduction in Si carrier lifetime by 1 order of magnitude, with final lifetimes above 500 μs uniformly across areas up to 20 cm2. In all cases, the increased resilience was correlated with a 99.9% reduction in contaminant concentration in the c-Si bulk, provided by the thick polySi layer, which acts as a buried gettering layer in the tandem structure without compromising the Si passivation quality. The Si resilience decreased as AIGSe > CGSe > CZTS, in accordance with the measured Cu contamination profiles and higher annealing temperatures. An efficiency of up to 7% was achieved for a CZTS/Si tandem, where the Si bottom cell is no longer the limiting factor.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hajijafarassar, Alireza","Martinho, Filipe Mesquita Alves","Larsen, Jes","Saini, Nishant","Shearer, Denver","Moro, Marcos V","Stulen, Fredrik","Grini, Sigbjørn","Engberg, Sara Lena Josefin","Stamate, Eugen","Schou, Jørgen","Vines, Lasse","Canulescu, Stela","Platzer-Björkman, Charlotte","Hansen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316132"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Chalcogenides","Si","TOPCon","Tandem"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gettering in polysi siox passivating contacts enables si based tandem solar cells with high thermal and contamination resilience","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/337907679/Paper_Chalcogenide_Si_tandems_v2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316132","identifier":[{"id":"85127846625","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35297597","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-26f0c8b4-d4aa-49f4-b824-82c9676d4240"],"keyword":["Chalcogenides","Gettering","Si","TOPCon","Tandem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BD4892313BC770F5D9C96A8CBB46D835"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/337907679/Paper_Chalcogenide_Si_tandems_v2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","coun