},{"affno":"13","first":"Krzysztof","key":"smietankapau","last":"Smietanka","name":"Smietanka, Krzysztof","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"grundpau","last":"Grund","name":"Grund, Christian","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"beerpau","last":"Beer","name":"Beer, Martin","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Timm","key":"harderpau","last":"Harder","name":"Harder, Timm","rank":30,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35726917"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/mbio.00609-22","issn":["21507511","21612129"],"issn_org":["21612129"],"issue":"4","journal":"mBio","paperid":"e0060922","status":"p","title":"mBio","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85137124851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0a7fe757-9ded-46af-a613-46ba0630ec8f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Has Epizootic Become Enzootic? Evidence for a Fundamental Change in the Infection Dynamics of Highly Pathogenic Avian Influenza in Europe, 2021","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-399728","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Purpose We investigated schoolteachers’ emotional reactions to COVID-19 and mental health during three phases of the COVID-19 pandemic. We further analyzed if teachers, who belonged to a COVID-19 risk group, had more emotional reactions and poorer mental health than “non-risk” groups. Methods We collected questionnaire data in May, June, and November–December 2020 and used data from 2665 teachers at public schools (871 individuals participated in all three surveys). Participants reported their fear of infection, fear of transmission of infection to their home or pupils, perceived burnout and stress, and worries about their ability to manage the working conditions. We included information about COVID-19 risk group status, gender, age, organization of teaching (physical presence or remote teaching), and the pupils’ grade. We estimated prevalence ratios and took repeated measures into account. Results Emotional reactions and poor mental health increased signifcantly with 27–84% from May to November–December 2020. Teachers, who were particularly vulnerable to the adverse consequences of COVID-19, had the highest prevalence of fear of infection and poor mental health. Conclusion Teachers play a crucial role in a society’s response to a pandemic. Yet, the dual role of teaching and virus control along with concerns regarding the health consequences of an infection may contribute to the observed increase in emotional reactions to COVID-19 and poor mental health.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","Christensen, Karl Bang","Fuglsang, Nina Vibe","Larsen, Inge","Nilsson, Charlotte Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-447454"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Longitudinal Studies","Mental health","Occupational health","School Teachers"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danmarks Lærerforening"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effect of covid 000000000019 on schoolteachers emotional reactions and mental health longitudinal results from the class study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8522178/pdf/420_2021_Article_1806.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-447454","identifier":[{"id":"000708377500002","type":"wos"},{"id":"34661723","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8522178","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85117200579","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5a55a594-3b10-47b4-80e3-180a0755a3d7"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Longitudinal studies","Mental health","Occupational health","School teachers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BA911F24364C354597B57BED107D91A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8522178/pdf/420_2021_Article_1806.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danmarks Lærerforening"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","locid":"266b247f-d127-46ae-a6ab-aa16c3f010b9","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0002-4298-1420","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karl Bang","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"850a805f-c580-4858-822c-8e5c72ac780c","name":"Christensen, Karl Bang","orcid":"0000-0003-4518-5187","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nina Vibe","key":"fuglsangpau","last":"Fuglsang","name":"Fuglsang, Nina Vibe","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Inge","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Juul","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"573fb3db-41df-4adf-86e6-e5b0c69a43ef","name":"Nilsson, Charlotte Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-3364-7412","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34661723"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00420-021-01806-8","issn":["03400131","14315777"],"issn_org":["03400131"],"issue":"4","journal":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","pages":"855-865","status":"p","title":"International Archives of Occupational and Environmental Health","volume":"95"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117200579"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5a55a594-3b10-47b4-80e3-180a0755a3d7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effect of COVID-19 on schoolteachers' emotional reactions and mental health: longitudinal results from the CLASS study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-447454","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Influenza D virus (IDV) was first described in 2011 and has been found to mainly circulate among cattle and swine populations worldwide. Nasal swab samples were collected from 100 Danish calf herds (83 dairy and 17 veal herds) from 2018–2020. Influenza D virus was detected in 12 of the herds. Samples with the lowest cycle quantification value were selected for full genome sequencing. A hemagglutinin-esterase fusion (HEF) gene sequence from a Danish IDV collected in 2015 was also included in this study. Phylogenetic analysis showed that viruses from seven of the IDV-positive herds belonged to the D/OK lineage and clustered together in the HEF tree with the IDV collected in 2015. Viruses from the four other herds belonged to the D/660 lineage, where three of the viruses clustered closely together, while the fourth virus was more phylogenetically distant in all gene segments. The high level of genetic similarity between viruses from two different herds involved in calf trading suggests that transmission occurred through the movement of calves. This study is, to our knowledge, the first to describe the characterization of IDV in calves in Denmark.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Liang, Yuan","Otten, Nina Dam","Hjulsager, Charlotte K.","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460690"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bovine","Calves","Denmark","Influenza D virus","PCR","Phylogeny","Sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of influenza d virus in danish calves","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v14020423","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460690","identifier":[{"id":"35216016","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85125181392","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8880214","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-7094a98a-421e-4396-8e23-12fde09697b9"],"keyword":["Bovine","Calves","Denmark","Influenza D virus","PCR","Phylogeny","Sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-53C4D4B248E9F696FC4CD4117795202A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v14020423","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/307375992/viruses_14_00423.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole B.","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"ed85c101-c8e6-403b-ba93-39e95e23e68d","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","name_org":"Goecke, Nicole B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Yuan","key":"liangpau","last":"Liang","locid":"15fec07b-8b15-410c-9db2-b2b7fda77736","name":"Liang, Yuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina D.","key":"ottenpau","last":"Otten","locid":"f1cce97d-bec1-4cad-9ad9-ccfaf09822b6","name":"Otten, Nina Dam","name_org":"Otten, Nina D.","orcid":"0000-0003-1004-1474","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte K.","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte K.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35216016"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/v14020423","issn":["19994915"],"issue":"2","journal":"Viruses","paperid":"423","status":"p","title":"Viruses","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85125181392"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7094a98a-421e-4396-8e23-12fde09697b9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characterization of Influenza D Virus in Danish Calves","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-460690","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Children live their everyday life together in and across different contexts such as families, schools and leisure time institutions. In our recent research, we have explored how unequal conditions in educational institutions are related to children’s different possibilities of participation in children’s communities as well as to collaborative and conflictual processes among different participants (Different professionals, parents and children) across children’s different life contexts. In both research and professional practice, inequality is often understood as related to social inheritance and intergenerational transmission of social and economic family background. However, statistical and qualitative studies challenge such predictable causality. To understand processes of inequality in educational institutions, we need to analyse them as more specifically related to children’s access to social resources within the institutions, and this access relates to concrete situated collaboration and conflicts among different participants here – children, teachers, parents, pedagogues and psychologists. Based on an ongoing research-project about “Leisure time pedagogy and situated inequality”, we present the theoretical framework for understanding inequality as related to concrete social dynamics in the everyday life among both children and different professionals. By empirical examples, we illustrate how inequality relates to social situations and nexuses across children’s compound everyday life contexts. This acknowledgement of the signification of children’s access to collaboration with other children points to the importance of involving professionals from leisure time institutions and their pedagogic knowledge in the work of exceeding inequality. Therefore, we will emphasize the possibilities of professionals in leisure time institutions in relation to supporting the children’s possibilities of participation. We focus on their specific professional knowledge as different from, though related to the professional knowledge of teachers (Hence our insistence on the concept of leisure","author_count":2,"contributors":["Højholt, Charlotte","Røn Larsen, Maja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-562490"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-03","place":"Reykjavik, is","start":"2022-06-01","title":"Nordic Educational Research Association Conference 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Children s communities","Conduct of everyday life","Inequality","Schools"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"situated inequality in education and children s participation in social communities a task for professionals in leisure time institutions","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-562490","ids":["ruc-61d59612-51c7-4916-94ca-df104840a9b4"],"keyword":["Children's communities","Conduct of Everyday Life","Inequality","Schools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FFEF4E666213A1B97E24189A9D7E752E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-61d59612-51c7-4916-94ca-df104840a9b4"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Situated inequality in education and children’s participation in social communities : a task for professionals in leisure time institutions?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-562490","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Children are positioned unequally in relation to possibilities of participation in their lives across school and leisure time institutions. Often this production of inequality is understood as related to social inheritance and intergenerational reproduction of social family background. However, statistical and qualitative studies point out, that these relations are not automatic, causal and predictable. Inequality in school seems related to children’s access to social resources within schools, which again relates to concrete situated collaboration and conflicts among different participants here – teachers, parents, pedagogues and psychologists. In this paper, we present insight into social dynamics in the everyday life among both children and different professionals and illustrate how inequality is related to social situations and nexuses across children’s compound everyday life contexts – in order to understand how different professionals understandings and interventions interplay in relation to the children’s conduct of everyday life.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-569434"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-16","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2022-06-14","title":"9th Nordic-Baltic ISCAR 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Education","Inequality","Leisure time","Pedagogy","Situated inequality"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"situated inequality across school and leisure time changing practices relations and communities children s everyday lives in and across diverse contexts","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-569434","ids":["ruc-c844783b-55bd-4a1a-af4f-0039fb21dadc"],"keyword":["Education","Inequality","Leisure time","Pedagogy","situated inequality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-26510942232F1EE9BEF64B32A6FAEF76"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","4. Quality Education","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-c844783b-55bd-4a1a-af4f-0039fb21dadc"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Situated inequality across school and leisure time : Changing practices, relations and communities: Children’s everyday lives in and across diverse contexts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-569434","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
