Søren Thorgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-7059","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"simonÿpau","last":"Simonÿ","locid":"6c2dbf49-1a55-4aa3-a990-1549e39274dd","name":"Simonÿ, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1189-2967","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-d3e9395a-af48-4a0c-9ff4-a173f2b345d9","sdu-6c6e7f12-50d5-4265-acbd-4ef4848e3d8c"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Health behavior transformation in women living with chronic pain supported by occupational therapists","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.13-039467","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Copy-number aberrations (CNAs) are assessed using FISH analysis in diagnostics of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL), but CNAs can also be extrapolated from Illumina BeadChips developed for genome-wide methylation microarray screening. Increasing numbers of microarray data-sets are available from diagnostic samples, making it useful to assess the potential in CNA diagnostics. We benchmarked the limitations of CNA testing from two Illumina BeadChips (EPIC and 450k) and using two common packages for analysis (conumee and ChAMP) to FISH-based assessment of 11q, 13q, and 17p deletions in 202 CLL samples. Overall, the two packages predicted CNAs with similar accuracy regardless of the microarray type, but lower than FISH-based assessment. We showed that the bioinformatics analysis needs to be adjusted to the specific CNA, as no general settings were identified. Altogether, we were able to predict CNAs using methylation microarray data, however, with limited accuracy, making FISH-based assessment of deletions the superior diagnostic choice.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hussmann, Dianna","Starnawska, Anna","Kristensen, Louise","Daugaard, Iben","Cédile, Oriane","Nguyen, Vivi Quoc","Kjeldsen, Tina E","Hansen, Christine Søholm","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Kristensen, Thomas","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","Møller, Michael Boe","Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","Hansen, Lise Lotte","Wojdacz, Tomasz K"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013474"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wojdacz, Tomasz K"],"country":["Poland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Mount Sinai","Mount Sinai Health","Pomeranian Medical University","Pomeranian Medical University in Szczecin"],"keyword":["450k","CNA assessment","Chronic lymphocytic leukemia","Copy number aberration","EPIC","Methylation microarray"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"methylation microarray based detection of clinical copy number aberrations in cll benchmarked to standard fish analysis","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ygeno.2022.110510","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Harboefonden , Knud og Edith Eriksens Mindefond and Arvid Nilsson Fonden . The Graduate School of Health, Aarhus University , Denmark, funded the PhD fellowship for DH. T.K.W. was supported by the Maria Skłodowska-Cure fellowship CONFUND at Aarhus Institute of Advanced Studies , and the Programme “Polish Returns” from the Polish National Agency for Academic Exchange . A.S. was supported by the Lundbeck Foundation , Denmark."],"id":"S02-100.00-013474","identifier":[{"id":"85140607195","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36272495","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0bf6aed3-c9e2-4340-8e80-9acb3a6dd8da","sdu-40c90f81-e784-44b4-adb1-b4da1e987914"],"keyword":["450k","CNA assessment","Chronic lymphocytic leukemia","Copy-number aberration","EPIC","Methylation microarray"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D1FD5F42D64A3F47BE985692F707C00D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ygeno.2022.110510","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/212491879/1_s2.0_S0888754322002555_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022",