a03"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Influenza A virus in pigs and birds in Denmark","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-445388","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To explore [fluorine-18]-fluoro-2-deoxy-d-glucose positron-emission-tomography/computed tomography (18FDG-PET/CT) in patients where standard investigations were non-diagnostic. Methods: We reviewed medical records of previously healthy children who had 18FDG-PET/CT performed at Copenhagen University Hospital in 2015–2020 due to unexplained fever. Results: Thirty-five of 819 paediatric 18FDG-PET/CT were performed due to unexplained fever. The final diagnoses were malignancy (11%), infections (23%), inflammatory diseases (43%) and miscellaneous (26%). 18FDG-PET/CT was diagnostic in six cases with Takayasu's arteritis, tuberculosis, Langerhans cell histiocytosis and Ewing sarcoma. Sixteen cases had focal 18FDG-uptake, but 18FDG-PET/CT could only differentiate malignancy, infection and inflammation in three cases. In six cases with inflammatory diseases and no focal signs, PET/CT was normal except increased non-specific 18FDG-uptake in bone marrow and spleen in five cases. One case was false positive (suspicion of appendicitis) and two false negative (leukaemia and inflammatory disease). Conclusion: 18FDG-PET/CT was diagnostic, or contributed to the diagnosis, in several children with unexplained fever referred to a tertiary centre. Challenges comprised (i) only increased non-specific 18FDG-uptake in bone marrow and spleen in half of cases with inflammatory diseases, (ii) no differentiation between complicated infections, malignancy and inflammation in most cases with focal processes and (iii) a small risk of false positive and false negative results.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nygaard, Ulrikka","Larsen, Laerke Vinge","Vissing, Nadja Hawwa","von Linstow, Marie-Louise","Myrup, Charlotte","Berthelsen, Anne Kiil","Poulsen, Anja","Borgwardt, Lise"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-446259"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["FUO","PET CT","paediatric infectious diseases"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unexplained fever in children benefits and challenges of fdg pet ct","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.16503","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-446259","identifier":[{"id":"85135773573","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36210785","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-584ee7f8-b161-47c4-933d-e5e2f1586971"],"keyword":["FUO","PET-CT","paediatric infectious diseases","persistent fever"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AA67C6206BE6C96C94C810A833F56E44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/324127231/Acta_Paediatrica_2022_Nygaard_Unexplained_fever_in_children_Benefits_and_challenges_of_FDG_PET_CT.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/apa.16503","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ulrikka","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"43b2e239-ddc1-4676-a8db-0a0f23906813","name":"Nygaard, Ulrikka","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Laerke Vinge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Laerke Vinge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nadja Hawwa","key":"vissingpau","last":"Vissing","name":"Vissing, Nadja Hawwa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marie-Louise","key":"vonlinstowpau","last":"von Linstow","name":"von Linstow, Marie-Louise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte","key":"myruppau","last":"Myrup","name":"Myrup, Charlotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Kiil","key":"berthelsenpau","last":"Berthelsen","name":"Berthelsen, Anne Kiil","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anja","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, Anja","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise","key":"borgwardtpau","last":"Borgwardt","name":"Borgwardt, Lise","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36210785"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/apa.16503","issn":["08035253","08035326"],"issn_org":["08035253"],"issue":"11","journal":"Acta Paediatrica","pages":"2203-2209","status":"p","title":"Acta Paediatrica","title_org":"Acta Pædiatrica","volume":"111"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135773573"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-584ee7f8-b161-47c4-933d-e5e2f1586971"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unexplained fever in children — Benefits and challenges of FDG-PET/CT","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-446259","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Major geographical transmission of porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus (PRRSV) occurs via semen when a boar stud is infected. This happened in Denmark in 2019, providing an opportunity to compare previous experimental PRRSV boar studies with natural PRRSV-1 infection in boars. The aim of this study was to investigate the association between the presence of PRRSV RNA in serum, semen, testicles, and epididymis of boars naturally infected with PRRSV and to describe the histological lesions in the testes and epididymis combined with direct visualisation of PRRSV-infected cells by immunohistochemical staining (IHC). The exact timing of infection of each boar was not determined, but based on serology the boars were divided into two groups: acute and late infections. All boars included were sampled the same day. In this study, 35 boars and 10 healthy boars from another PRRSV-negative boar stud were included as histological controls. PRRSV RNA was found most often in serum (51%) and least frequently in semen (22%) and was more often detected in the reproductive tract in the acute phase of infection (p < 0.0001; RR: 2.58). Mononuclear cells and multinuclear giant cells were present in the adluminal compartment of the testis and epididymis in PRRSV-infected boars, but not in control boars (p < 0.05), which supports the hypothesis that macrophages are involved in the venereal spread of the virus.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pedersen, Kasper","Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Skade, Lotte","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-500756"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"virological and histopathological findings in boars naturally infected with porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus type 000000000001","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2022.874498","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-500756","identifier":[{"id":"35633676","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85130938343","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9130840","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b3b1881a-239d-4e71-9b87-a0edeec8998b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-610F121305491BD55BD8CAEDFC1C5664"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2022.874498","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/305712380/fmicb_13_874498.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["Danish Pig Research Centre, SEGES (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Sophie Amalie","key":"blirupplumpau","last":"Blirup-plum","locid":"54f7ba11-2529-4cf7-adb1-139dfa0e4b53","name":"Blirup-Plum, Sophie Amalie","name_org":"Blirup-plum, Sophie Amalie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"06d93bdc-8ddd-4561-8778-a8ffa2b5bd51","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte","key":"skadepau","last":"Skade","name":"Skade, Lotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik Elvang","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"20245e41-1eb4-4cfa-a2d6-e6851e101300","name":"Jensen, Henrik Elvang","orcid":"0000-0001-7277-7829","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35633676"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2022.874498","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"874498","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130938343"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b3b1881a-239d-4e71-9b87-a0edeec8998b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Virological and Histopathological Findings in Boars Naturally Infected With Porcine Reproductive and Respiratory Syndrome Virus Type 1","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-500756","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A systematic, prospective, passive monitoring of circulating subtypes of influenza A virus in Danish pigs wascarried out in 2021. The overall purpose of the monitoring was to identify which influenza virus subtypesand genotypes that circulated among Danish pigs.In 2021, a total of 2895 influenza A virus tests were performed on 857 submissions from 647 herdsregistered with different CHR no. In total, 453 (53 %) of the submissions from 377 different herds had atleast one positive sample. Submissions were distributed across the country. There were a higher number ofsubmissions during the winter, but influenza positive samples were detected all year round, with atendency to a higher positive proportion from September-December.Virus with an HA gene of pandemic H1N1pdm09 origin (H1pdm09) was detected in 189 submissions from164 herds registered with different CHR no. and thereby accounted for 42 % of the influenza A viruspositive submissions. The proportion of H1pdm09 is thereby significantly higher than last year where only29 % of the positive submission had an HA gene of H1N1pdm09 origin. In total, 312 influenza A viruspositive submissions were subtyped for both HA and NA. These analyzes showed that the most commonOvervågning af influenza A i svin, december 2022Side 7 af 31subtypes in Danish pigs in 2021 were H1avN2sw, H1pdm09N1av and H1N1pdm09. Similarly to last year, theprevalence of the H1pdm09N1av subtype increased and this subtype now represents 24 % of allsubmissions for which both HA and NA were subtyped. At the same time, the H1avN2sw subtype hasdecreased in prevalence, and was constituting only 54 % of all subtyped submissions. For the first time inDenmark, two human zoonotic infections with H1N1pdm09 and H1pdm09N1av viruses originating fromDanish swine, were documented. This emphasizes that viruses with a zoonotic potential are present in theDanish swine population. In addition, low cross-reaction to the human seasonal flu is expected as thegenetic and antigenic drift of the H1pdm09Nx viruses in swine is significant.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Krog, Jesper Schak","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-528054"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overvågning af influenza a virus i svin slutrapport 000000002021","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/338983808/Overvgning_af_influenza_A_i_svin_slutrapport_2021.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-528054","ids":["ku-e1446408-ce7a-4043-8e35-38e7cadc419b"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5713F38D7F49EC80CAD0E649D27F7A68"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/338983808/Overvgning_af_influenza_A_i_svin_slutrapport_2021.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"31","publisher":"Københavns Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e1446408-ce7a-4043-8e35-38e7cadc419b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Overvågning af influenza A virus i svin : Slutrapport 2021","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-528054","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Kjær, Lene Jung","Boklund, Anette","Larsen, Lars Erik","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Ward, Michael P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-719714"],"event":{"end":"2022-05-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2022-05-03","title":"ICAHS conference","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sydney"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"using national avian influenza data to predict spatial patterns in wild birds from denmark 000000002006 000000002020","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-719714","ids":["ku-2ec24467-d4b6-495c-bdcd-70918f79706e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-30EB09267B47EEFD70A041CB58490004"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Animal Welfare and Disease Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Jung","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"b93ddd14-b340-4550-b3cf-eb9473b0d716","name":"Kjær, Lene Jung","orcid":"0000-0001-9659-4672","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette","key":"boklundpau","last":"Boklund","locid":"b56cee2e-0320-4c3d-a360-6dc1f5b2ee67","name":"Boklund, Anette","orcid":"0000-0001-6359-3403","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michael P.","key":"wardpau","last":"Ward","name":"Ward, Michael P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2ec24467-d4b6-495c-bdcd-70918f79706e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Using national avian influenza data to predict spatial patterns in wild birds from Denmark, 2006-2020","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-719714","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Currently, no molecular biomarker indices are used in standard care to make treatment decisions at diagnosis of chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL). We used Infinium MethylationEPIC array data from diagnostic blood samples of 114 CLL patients and developed a procedure to stratify patients based on methylation signatures associated with mutation load of the IGHV gene. This procedure allowed us to predict the time to treatment with a hazard ratio (HR) of 8.34 (95% confidence interval [CI]: 4.54-15.30), as opposed to a HR of 4.35 (95% CI: 2.60-7.28) using IGHV mutation status. Detailed evaluation of 17 cases for which the two classification procedures gave discrepant results showed that these cases were incorrectly classified using IGHV status. Moreover, methylation-based classification stratified patients with different overall survival (HR=1.82; 95% CI: 1.07-3.09), which was not possible using IGHV status. Furthermore, we assessed the performance of the developed classification procedure using published HumanMethylation450 array data for 159 patients for whom information on time to treatment, overall survival and relapse was available. Despite 450K array methylation data not containing all the biomarkers used in our classification procedure, methylation signatures again stratified patients with significantly better accuracy than did IGHV mutation load regarding all available clinical outcomes. Thus, stratification using IGHV-associated methylation signatures may provide better prognostic power than IGHV mutation status.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Hussmann, Dianna","Starnawska, Anna","Kristensen, Louise","Daugaard, Iben","Thomsen, Astrid","Kjeldsen, Tina E","Hansen, Christine Søholm","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Dalsgaard Johansen, Karina","Ludvigsen, Maja","Kristensen, Thomas","Larsen, Thomas Stauffer","Møller, Michael Boe","Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","Hansen, Lise Lotte","Wojdacz, Tomasz K"],"cuid":["S02-099.29-030751"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wojdacz, Tomasz K"],"country":["Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pomeranian Medical University","Pomeranian Medical University in Szczecin"],"keyword":["Humans","Immunoglobulin Heavy Chains genetics","Leukemia Lymphocytic Chronic B Cell diagnosis","Methylation","Mutation","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-NP-LUND","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ighv associated methylation signatures more accurately predict clinical outcomes of chronic lymphocytic leukemia patients than ighv mutation load","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2021.278477","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.29-030751","identifier":[{"id":"85123163113","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34092057","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8968906","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-fb8eb304-9b04-4160-b930-6f27f47e59cc","sdu-f0572e67-e316-4ebe-ad3a-b3237425728c"],"keyword":["Humans","Immunoglobulin Heavy Chains/genetics","Leukemia, Lymphocytic, Chronic, B-Cell/diagnosis","Methylation","Mutation","Prognosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3224CF8FC9C90D6DBF2F32C9DE549AC3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2021.278477","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/201012518/10291_Article_Text_75597_2_10_20220329.pdf","version":"Publish