{"abstract":"Purpose: To evaluate the safety and feasibility of injecting allogeneic adipose-derived mesenchymal stem cells (ASCs) into the lacrimal gland (LG) as a treatment of aqueous deficient dry eye disease (ADDE). Methods: In this open-label, 5-visit clinical trial (baseline, treatment and weeks 1, 4 and 16) seven subjects with ADDE received one transconjunctival injection of allogeneic ASCs into the LG in one eye. The ASC product contained 22 million ASCs/ml and the injected volume was maximally 50% of the LG volume as determined on magnetic resonance imaging (MRI). Treatment related adverse events (AEs) were assessed at each visit (primary endpoint). Ocular Surface Disease Index (OSDI), tear osmolarity, tear film breakup time (TBUT), corneal staining (Oxford grade) and Schirmer's I test were assessed at each timepoint. Results: No AEs related to the study treatment were observed. Mean follow-up time was 126 days after treatment. The mean OSDI score decreased from 58.9 ± 20.6 at baseline to 34.1 ± 21.6 (p < 0.002). In the study eye mean tear osmolarity decreased from 312.9 ± 10.4 to 291.6 ± 10.9 mosm/l (p < 0.002), mean TBUT increased from 3.7 ± 1.5 to 7.1 ± 1.9 s (p < 0.002), mean Schirmer's I test increased from 4.6 ± 0.7 to 8.1 ± 3.1 mm/5 min (p < 0.03), while mean Oxford grade showed a trend towards a decrease from 2.4 ± 0.7 to 1.3 ± 1 (p < 0.10). Conclusion: Our trial suggests that injection of allogeneic ASCs into the LG is a safe and feasible treatment of severe ADDE. A randomized placebo-controlled trial aimed at elucidating the therapeutic effect of allogeneic ASCs in a larger patient cohort from our research group is currently underway.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Møller-Hansen, Michael","Larsen, Ann Cathrine","Toft, Peter Bjerre","Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","Schwartz, Camilla","Bruunsgaard, Helle","Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","Ekblond, Annette","Kastrup, Jens","Heegaard, Steffen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405319"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dry eye disease","Mesenchymal stem cells","Regenerative medicine","Stem cell therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"safety and feasibility of mesenchymal stem cell therapy in patients with aqueous deficient dry eye disease","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-405319","identifier":[{"id":"85096967228","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33253910","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-13ecd9d3-9e15-44d1-815d-a6439d5f9a60"],"keyword":["Dry eye disease","Mesenchymal stem cells","Regenerative medicine","Stem cell therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BEB066DDC07267DAAED76BC395521191"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"møllerhansenpau","last":"Møller-Hansen","locid":"191147e6-095b-48a6-9240-af4111b4a7a6","name":"Møller-Hansen, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ann Cathrine","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Ann Cathrine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Bjerre","key":"toftpau","last":"Toft","locid":"250fdb82-c343-47f2-8a2a-1675b9997059","name":"Toft, Peter Bjerre","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Duch","key":"lynggaardpau","last":"Lynggaard","locid":"48939833-8bab-4e03-82f4-c96cc9441aff","name":"Lynggaard, Charlotte Duch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Camilla","key":"schwartzpau","last":"Schwartz","name":"Schwartz, Camilla","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle","key":"bruunsgaardpau","last":"Bruunsgaard","locid":"f9d96093-0e5d-487b-91ef-4d0b9d5d72c2","name":"Bruunsgaard, Helle","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mandana","key":"haacksørensenpau","last":"Haack-Sørensen","name":"Haack-Sørensen, Mandana","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annette","key":"ekblondpau","last":"Ekblond","name":"Ekblond, Annette","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"kastruppau","last":"Kastrup","locid":"12c1241f-23da-492c-84b0-36691cb95255","name":"Kastrup, Jens","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"e1720fc3-b9d4-4664-8bcc-2394fd476fdd","name":"Heegaard, Steffen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33253910"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jtos.2020.11.013","issn":["15420124","19375913"],"issn_org":["15420124"],"journal":"Ocular Surface","pages":"43-52","status":"p","title":"Ocular Surface","title_org":"The Ocular Surface","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096967228"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-13ecd9d3-9e15-44d1-815d-a6439d5f9a60"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Safety and feasibility of mesenchymal stem cell therapy in patients with aqueous deficient dry eye disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405319","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In July 2019, a vaccine-derived recombinant Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus 1 strain (PRRSV-1) (Horsens strain) infected more than 40 Danish sow herds, resulting in severe losses. In the present study, the pathogenicity of the recombinant Horsens strain was assessed and compared to a reference PRRSV-1 strain using a well-characterized experimental model in young SPF pigs. Furthermore, the efficacies of three different PRRSV-1 MLV vaccines to protect pigs against challenge with the recombinant strain were assessed. Following challenge, the unvaccinated pigs challenged with the Horsens strain had significant increased viral load in serum compared to all other groups. No macroscopic changes were observed at necropsy, but tissue from the lungs and tonsils from almost all pigs were PRRSV-positive. The viral load in serum was lower in all vaccinated groups compared to the unvaccinated group challenged with the Horsens strain, and only small differences were seen among the vaccinated groups. The findings in the present study, combined with two other recent reports, indicate that this recombinant “Horsens” strain indeed is capable of inducing infection in growing pigs as well as in pregnant sows that is comparable to or even exceeding those induced by typical PRRSV-1, subtype 1 strains. However, absence of notable clinical signs and lack of significant macroscopic changes indicate that this strain is less virulent than previously characterized highly virulent PRRSV-1 strains.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Larsen, Lars Erik","Kristensen, Charlotte S.","Paboeuf, Frédéric","Renson, Patricia","Bourry, Olivier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434693"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["Agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l'alimentation, de l'environnement et du travail","All Global Affiliations"],"keyword":["PRRSV","Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus","Recombination","Swine","Vaccine efficacy","Vaccines"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"challenge of naïve and vaccinated pigs with a vaccine derived recombinant porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus 000000000001 strain horsens strain","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines9050417","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434693","identifier":[{"id":"33921958","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85105119231","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8143564","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4517f6d6-142c-431a-a8fd-3b570b112df4"],"keyword":["PRRSV","Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus","Recombination","Swine","Vaccine efficacy","Vaccines"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E6BB81EFC5BF3689A4522E8075A6CB9C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/262797766/vaccines_09_00417.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/vaccines9050417","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["Danish Pig Research Centre, SEGES (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l alimentation de l environnement et du travail","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Agence nationale de sécurité sanitaire de l'alimentation, de l'environnement et du travail","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lise K.","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"06d93bdc-8ddd-4561-8778-a8ffa2b5bd51","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","name_org":"Kvisgaard, Lise K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte S.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Frédéric","key":"paboeufpau","last":"Paboeuf","name":"Paboeuf, Frédéric","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Patricia","key":"rensonpau","last":"Renson","name":"Renson, Patricia","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Olivier","key":"bourrypau","last":"Bourry","name":"Bourry, Olivier","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33921958"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/vaccines9050417","issn":["2076393X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Vaccines","paperid":"417","status":"p","title":"Vaccines","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105119231"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]