d Medication (OptiNAM) for acutely admitted older patients : protocol for a randomized single-blinded controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.39-039569","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: A two-stage prosthesis exchange procedure has been the gold standard in surgical treatment of the chronically infected knee arthroplasty so far. This includes 2 surgeries/hospitalizations and an interim period of 2–3 months between surgeries with impaired health, functional status and quality of life of the patients. A one-stage exchange procedure holds many obvious advantages compared to the two-stage approach, but outcomes of a one-stage versus two-stage procedures have never been investigated in a randomized clinical trial. The purpose of this study is primarily to investigate time-adjusted differences in functional status of patients after one-stage versus two-stage revision. Secondary, to report time-adjusted differences in quality of life, complications (including re-revisions due to infection) and mortality. Methods: This study is a pragmatic, multi-center, randomized, non-inferiority trial comparing one-stage versus two-stage revision of the infected knee arthroplasty. Seven Danish hospitals are currently participating in the study, but additional hospitals can enter the study if adhering to protocol. Ninety-six patients will be included prospectively. Follow-up will be with PROM-questionnaires and clinical controls up to 10 years. The patients who are not able to participate in the randomized trial are followed in a parallel cohort study. PROM’s: Oxford Knee Score and EQ5D + EQ5D VAS questionnaires are completed preoperatively and sent out to the study participants at 6 weeks, 3, 6, 9, 12, 18 and 24 months as well as 5 and 10 years postoperatively. In addition a tailor made cost questionnaire on the non-treating hospital resource use, community health and social service use, travel costs, time off work and informal care are sent out. Discussion: If one of the two treatment alternatives is found superior in both domains of quality of life (both knee-specific and generic) and health economics, that treatment should be promoted. Other outcomes will open informed discussions about treatment strategies for periprosthetic knee infections. Trial registration: The randomized trial is registered on ClinicalTrials.gov with ID NCT03435679, initial release date January 31, 2018 and the cohort study is registered with ID NCT04427943, submitted January 8, 2020 and posted June 11, 2020.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","Odgaard, Anders","Fredborg, Charlotte","Schrøder, Henrik Morville","Emmeluth, Claus"],"cuid":["S03-096.74-024946"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["on behalf of the One-stage vs Two-stage Collaboration Group"],"corresponding_author":["Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"keyword":["Infection","Knee arthroplasty","One stage","PROM","Revision","Two stage"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"one stage versus two stage revision of the infected knee arthroplasty a randomized multicenter clinical trial study protocol","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-021-04044-8","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank all participating departments, and Region of Southern Denmark and Region Zealand for financial support. OPEN, Open Patient data Explorative Network, Odense University Hospital, Region of Southern Denmark has provided database management and statistical support for this study. Odense University Hospital, Region of Southern Denmark and Region Zealand has contributed with funding. Furthermore, a grant from the private fond Grosserer Chr. Andersen og hustru Ingeborg Ovidia Signe Andersen, født Schmidts Legat (foundation) has been obtained. The obtained funding is used to study coordination including salary to an allocated research nurse. All funding was non-commercial and with no influence on the study design and later reporting of the result from the study. In any case, the results will be published no matter whether they are positive, negative or inconclusive."],"id":"S03-096.74-024946","identifier":[{"id":"33579256","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85100979923","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7881574","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-a82fd212-c10d-4f67-a9d0-df48b1b9ccba","ku-a4dba329-2b94-4a02-99d8-5dea705d6fbd","sdu-0bd881ff-0a66-4f7a-b473-fb0618a17116"],"keyword":["Infection","Knee arthroplasty","One-stage","PROM","Revision","Two-stage"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-EB18791B17A7F464DF8CFC5AEA524EFB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/303682740/s12891_021_04044_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/179905032/s12891_021_04044_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12891-021-04044-8","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved, Slagelse og Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":5,"key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Regionshospitalet Horsens"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU"},{"affno":6,"key":"on behalf of the one stage vs two stage collaboration group","name":"on behalf of the One-stage vs Two-stage Collaboration Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Anders","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"33eeba1f-407c-4aa4-bf69-5efb12863f82","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Charlotte","key":"fredborgpau","last":"Fredborg","name":"Fredborg, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Morville","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","locid":"e123aeda-8b2e-44a9-b78f-34d1a4c942af","name":"Schrøder, Henrik Morville","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"emmeluthoth","last":"Emmeluth","locid":"46fc0375-0d39-4924-8ad4-b505de8b583f","name":"Emmeluth, Claus","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["33579256"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12891-021-04044-8","issn":["14712474"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","paperid":"175","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Musculoskeletal Disorders","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85100979923"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a82fd212-c10d-4f67-a9d0-df48b1b9ccba","ku-a4dba329-2b94-4a02-99d8-5dea705d6fbd","sdu-0bd881ff-0a66-4f7a-b473-fb0618a17116"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"One-stage versus two-stage revision of the infected knee arthroplasty - a randomized multicenter clinical trial study protocol","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.74-024946","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Acute and persistent pain after surgery is well described. However, no large-scale studies on immediate postoperative pain in the operating room (OR) exist, hindering potential areas of research to improve clinical outcomes. Thus, we aimed to describe the occurrence and severity of immediate postoperative pain in a large, unselected cohort. METHODS: This was a prospective cohort study, encompassing all procedures in 31 public hospitals in the Danish Realm, during a 5-day period including the weekend. Data on procedures and anesthesia were collected and the main outcome was occurrence of moderate or severe pain in the OR. Secondary outcomes included pain, sedation and nausea in the OR or during the first 15 min in the postanesthesia care unit (PACU) including relevant risk factors. Descriptive and logistic regression statistics were used. RESULTS: A total of 3675 procedures were included for analysis (87% inclusion rate). Moderate or severe pain occurred in 7.4% (95% CI 6.5% to 8.3%) of cases in the OR immediately after awakening, rising to 20.2% in the OR and/or PACU. Large intraprocedure and interprocedure variations occurred (0.0%-37.5%), and in 20% of cases with epidural-general anesthesia patients experienced moderate or severe pain. Independent risk factors were female sex, younger age, preoperative pain, daily opioid use and major surgical procedures. CONCLUSION: Moderate or severe pain in the immediate postoperative phase occurred in 20% of all cases with procedure and anesthesiological technique variations, suggesting a need for identification of relevant procedure-specific risk factors and development of preventive treatments. TRIAL REGISTRATION NUMBER: RoPR ID 43191.","author_count":62,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Mølgaard","Toft, Mette Helene","Awada, Hussein Nasser","Dirks, Jesper","Brandsborg, Birgitte","Rasmussen, Line Kirkegaard","Kirkegaard, Ellen","Hasfeldt-Hansen, Dorthe","Larsen, Thomas Egemose","Charalampidis, Georgios","Mørk, Emilie Louise Schjøtt","Rosager, Chirstine Linaa","Salam, Idress Ahmad","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Jørgensen, Marlene Kanstrup","Skjønnemand, Martin","Lund, Caterina Amanti","Schroder, Save","Sørensen, Johan Kløvgaard","Sølling, Christoffer","Hansen, Kristian Kraft","Rasmussen, Christina Kirkegaard","Steen, Nick Phaff","Nielsen, Anne Staal","Geisler, Anja","Køppen, Kasper Storm","Pælestik, Maria Bolther","Grøfte, Thorbjørn","Meyhoff, Christian Sylvest","Kroh, Charlotte Loumann","Christensen, Amalie Prien","Haugstvedt, Aleksander Fjeld","Hansen, Maria Aagaard","Nielsen, Christian Viggo","Dybdal, Bitten","Falcon, Lars","Hägi-Pedersen, Daniel","Jauho, Kristian","Wolsted, Henrik","Pedersen, Christian Alves Kohler","Sommer, Trine Nyboe","Kromberg, Laurits Schou","Kristensen, Danja Lykke","Svensson, Camilla Kara","Nielsen, Hans Fjeldsøe","Sørensen, Martin Kryspin","Jacobsen, Stig","Sundskard, Martin","Brahe, Nicole","Jakobsen, Karina","Jensen, Mette Skov","Odder, Lillian","Selter, Hansjörg","Mohr, Tróndur Høgnason","Jensen, Elin H","Jensen, Pernille Pia","Skjold, Christine","Aasvang, Eske Kvanner"],"cuid":["S04-099.89-008547"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Aasvang, Eske Kvanner"],"country":["Faroe Islands","Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dronning Ingrids Hospital","Dronning Ingrids Hospital, Nuuk","Landssjúkrahúsid Dronning Alexandrines Hospital","National Hospital of the Faroe Islands","Queen Ingrid's Hospital"],"keyword":["Acute pain","Pain","Pain Management","Postoperative"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-