{"abstract":"Medication-induced prolongation of the QT-interval (miQTP) can lead to cardiac arrhythmia. Our aim was to investigate the prevalence of forensic autopsy cases where fatal cardiac arrhythmia related to treatment with QT-prolonging medications (QT-PMs) could be suspected. We performed a cross-sectional study of 741 forensic autopsies undertaken at our institution in non-drug addicts aged 15 years or above from 2017 to 2019. We defined a high risk of miQTP by one detected QT-PM in a concentration above therapeutic level, or two or more detected QT-PMs in post mortem blood. We reviewed the autopsy reports from cases with a high miQTP-risk to identify cases with no other apparent cause of death. We discarded suicides and cases with lethal levels of QT-PMs. We identified 167 cases (22.5%) with high risk of miQTP, and discarded 36 suicides (4.9%) and 7 (0.9%) with lethal levels of QT-PMs. Apart from a high risk of miQTP, no other apparent explanation of the cause of death was present in seven (0.9%). In 18 cases (2.4%) with high miQTP-risk, the cause of death was primarily attributed to cardiac changes other than acute cardiovascular events. In conclusion, 22.5% had a high risk of miQTP, and fatal cardiac arrhythmia related to treatment with QT-PMs could be suspected in 0.9%. However, a genetic pro-arrhythmic background could not be excluded in our study. Furthermore, it is possible that QT-PMs could have played a role in some of the 2.4% of cases where the cause of death was mainly attributed to cardiac changes and the risk of miQTP was high.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ahmed, H.","Larsen, Maiken Kudahl","Hansen, M. R.","Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-022858"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, C. U.","Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj"],"keyword":["Antidepressants","Antiemetics","Antimycotics","Antipsychotic drugs","Antipsychotics","Cardiac arrhythmia","Guidelines","HOSPITAL CARDIAC ARREST","Interval","PROLONGATION","Risk","Torsades de pointes","Ventricular arrhythmias"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the role of qt prolonging medications in a forensic autopsy study from western denmark","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.forsciint.2021.110889","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-022858","identifier":[{"id":"000677701100005","type":"wos"},{"id":"85109451743","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34225211","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8bd2be24-2b26-4078-9e8d-ee3a10914151","sdu-3d901368-a5ce-48c8-b744-1510a83bd6a3"],"keyword":["ANTIPSYCHOTIC-DRUGS","Antidepressants","Antiemetics","Antimycotics","Antipsychotics","Cardiac arrhythmia","GUIDELINES","HOSPITAL CARDIAC-ARREST","INTERVAL","PROLONGATION","RISK","TORSADE-DE-POINTES","Torsades de pointes","VENTRICULAR-ARRHYTHMIAS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7029D65D36923AE37B4C459235A27DFD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.forsciint.2021.110889","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/184596469/1_s2.0_S0379073821002097_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/273849685/1_s2.0_S0379073821002097_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Forensic Medicine, Department of Forensic Medicine - Department of Forensic Medicine - Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology, Pharmacy and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"H.","key":"ahmedpau","last":"Ahmed","locid":"c069e275-4329-40f2-be1d-7769461c89cc","name":"Ahmed, H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M. K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"5dec5e73-3ad6-468f-8ee7-4fa887c20851","name":"Larsen, Maiken Kudahl","name_org":"Larsen, M. K.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M. R.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"58ab7b9c-6262-468d-91d6-247ef0076e29","name":"Hansen, Morten Rix","name_org":"Hansen, M. R.","orcid":"0000-0002-1582-7866","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C. U.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"d9de514e-16a5-468a-96aa-7dce1995a898","name":"Andersen, Charlotte Uggerhøj","name_org":"Andersen, C. U.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34225211"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.forsciint.2021.110889","issn":["03790738","18726283"],"issn_org":["03790738"],"journal":"Forensic Science International","paperid":"110889","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Forensic Science International","volume":"325"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85109451743"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8bd2be24-2b26-4078-9e8d-ee3a10914151","sdu-3d901368-a5ce-48c8-b744-1510a83bd6a3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The role of QT-prolonging medications in a forensic autopsy study from Western Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-022858","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Beginning in late 2017, highly pathogenic avian influenza (HPAI) H5N6 viruses caused outbreaks in wild birds and poultry in several European countries. H5N6 viruses were detected in 43 wild birds found dead throughout Denmark. Most of the Danish virus-positive dead birds were found in the period from February to April 2018. However, unlike the rest of Europe, sporadic HPAI H5N6-positive dead wild birds were detected in Denmark in July, August, September, and December 2018, with the last positive bird being found in January 2019. HPAI viruses were not detected in active surveillance of apparently healthy wild birds. In this study, we use full genome sequencing and phylogenetic analysis to investigate the wild bird HPAI H5N6 viruses found in Denmark. The Danish viruses were found to be closely related to those of contemporary HPAI H5N6 viruses detected in Europe. Their sequences formed two clusters indicating that at least two or more introductions of H5N6 into Denmark occurred. Notably, all viruses detected in the latter half of 2018 and in 2019 grouped into the same cluster. The H5N6 viruses appeared to have been maintained undetected in the autumn 2018.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Liang, Yuan","Krog, Jesper Schak","Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Holm, Elisabeth","Nielsen, Pernille Dahl","Hammer, Anne Sofie","Madsen, Jesper Johannes","Thorup, Kasper","Larsen, Lars Erik","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-034126"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane"],"keyword":["Birds","Disease Outbreaks","Europa","H5N6 subtype","Highly pathogenic avian influenza","Infectious disease outbreak","Influenza A virus","Phylogeny","Surveillance","WILD"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Danish Veterinary and Food Administration"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"molecular characterization of highly pathogenic avian influenza viruses h000000000005n000000000006 detected in denmark in 000000002018 000000002019","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v13061052","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This research was funded by The Danish Veterinary and Food Administration."],"id":"S02-100.00-034126","identifier":[{"id":"34199456","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85107011816","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8226499","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-43f71313-9de2-4ecd-abb1-8a219930abe9","ku-523ae191-2dbb-43b9-a3c3-89a1635490c0"],"keyword":["Birds","Disease outbreaks","Europa","H5N6 subtype","Highly pathogenic avian influenza","Infectious disease outbreak","Influenza A virus","Phylogeny","Surveillance","Wild"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AE0DCE14ED8BB8513BA95604679E25A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v13061052","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/264497580/viruses_13_01052.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273370124/viruses_13_01052.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nord