l, Charlotte Brandstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-9285-3099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Durita Lyngsø","key":"svartápau","last":"Svartá","locid":"7d14a946-3c39-479f-9e88-0b5c3061f8e5","name":"Svartá, Durita Lyngsø","orcid":"0000-0002-8931-8386","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","locid":"ef4a2fa7-9735-4b1e-a4fa-b1272def2cfc","name":"Bjerregaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7153-8447","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingelise","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"9c041339-f1ff-4dc1-ac52-077f3f6349c4","name":"Olesen, Ingelise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Viskum Lytken","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3ee738b1-09d1-4886-9ddf-67ca132997fe","name":"Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken","orcid":"0000-0002-6245-4222","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"52","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet. Statens Institut for Folkesundhed","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-eb8864b5-3a13-44d1-b409-5cffe573f289"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Kommunal sundhedsprofil - Kommuneqarfik Sermersooq : Befolkningsundersøgelsen i Grønland 2018","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-640671","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objectives This study aimed to investigate the process of a quasi-experimental stepped wedge clustered intervention trial which implemented workplace health literacy for reducing musculoskeletal pain among eldercare workers. Methods A central component of the intervention was structured communication sessions between employee and supervisor. We evaluated which challenges they addressed during the communication session, which actions they planned and how they rated the implementation of their own action plans. Three overall categories were used; organisation/management level, team level and individual level indicating in which organisational context the challenge appeared or the action was planned. For each overall category, a set of sub-categories were defined based on grounded theory and open coding. Results During 28 months, 2.497 sessions were registered. Among these, 2.919 challenges and 3.848 plans for action were identified. In 24% of the sessions no challenge was identified. Most frequent challenges concerned staffing (17%), organisation of tasks (15%) and team work (14%). Most frequently action plans concerned communication (18%), team-work (16%) and handling residents (14%). Half of the plans were solved at another level in the organisation than the challenge appeared. The highest implementation rate was found among actions planned on the individual level (52%), actions planned on team and management/organisational level were implemented at a lower rate (45% and 39%). Conclusions This study contributes to the discussion regarding what kind of work environment initiatives could be introduced to improve the work environment in the eldercare sector. The results underline the advantages in considering solutions to work environment and health challenges broadly at all levels in the organisation and the relevance of involving both the employee and the organisation/management in identifying and implementing solutions.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Munch, Pernille Kold","Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","Jørgensen, Marie Birk","Larsen, Anne Konring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-779867"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interventioner","Muskelskeletbesvær","Sosu"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Health Municipally of Copenhagen, Denmark."]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"which work environment challenges are top of mind among eldercare workers and how would they suggest to act upon them in everyday practice process evaluation of a workplace health literacy intervention","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apergo.2020.103265","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-779867","identifier":[{"id":"85090187379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["nfa-05cebc12-03d3-4864-83a6-3f45dabbc4df"],"keyword":["Interventioner","Muskelskeletbesvær","Sosu"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-065F3A6AF465C7E2EEEFAECA4FE0B00B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.apergo.2020.103265","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Musculoskeletal Disorders and Physical Workload"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Health Municipally of Copenhagen, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Kold","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","name":"Munch, Pernille Kold","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"180d2a5d-fe8e-4956-b192-48aed7083301","name":"Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1769-717X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Birk","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Marie Birk","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Konring","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Anne Konring","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.apergo.2020.103265","issn":["00036870","18729126"],"issn_org":["00036870"],"journal":"Applied Ergonomics","pages":"103265","publisher":"Elsevier Limited","status":"p","title":"Applied Ergonomics","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090187379"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-05cebc12-03d3-4864-83a6-3f45dabbc4df"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Which work environment challenges are top of mind among eldercare workers and how would they suggest to act upon them in everyday practice? Process evaluation of a workplace health literacy intervention","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-779867","year":"2021","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: As part of intervention feasibility evaluation before conducting a clinical trial, this study aimed to investigate perspectives of patients and clinicians involved in the occupational therapy lifestyle-oriented programme REVEAL(OT) [Redesign your EVEveryday Activities and Lifestyle with Occupational Therapy] which was added to multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment. Methods: We conducted three focus group interviews, two with eight voluntarily selected patients and one with four clinicians. Data were analysed using Braun & Clarke’s semantic data-driven analysis. Results: Patients reported satisfaction with the intervention and a greater acceptance of living with chronic pain through increased understanding of pain mechanisms, more effective daily planning and improved social interaction. Patients felt empowered to change lifestyle habits by restarting habitual interests, prioritizing joyful occupations for improved occupational balance, and lifestyle modifications. Contact to occupational therapists and peer support were important empowering factors for working with lifestyle goals. Patients and clinicians expressed their views on further improvement of the REVEAL(OT). Conclusions: Patients and clinicians found the lifestyle-oriented occupational therapy programme relevant as an add-on to the multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment. A need was expressed for a reduced information and treatment load and a higher degree of communication and cooperation among the clinicians involved in the intervention.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard","Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","Søndergaard, Jens","Mogensen, Vicki Oldenschläger","Larsen, Anette Enemark","Skou, Søren Thorgaard","Simonÿ, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-081.85-038775"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard"],"keyword":["health nutrition and quality of life"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility assessment of an occupational therapy lifestyle intervention added to multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment at a danish pain centre a qualitative evaluation from the perspectives of patients and clinicians","src":["kp","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17482631.2021.1949900","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.85-038775","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8276665","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34252015","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85111578834","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-42b599ee-9aae-4379-82ae-ae428e3df0c1","sdu-170907f4-2117-4a45-92f4-e7b399196abc"],"keyword":["health, nutrition and quality of life"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9A9F9AEE48EDEEEDAC8B9EA4127329C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17482631.2021.1949900","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/184284729/Feasibility_assessment_of_an_occupational_therapy_lifestyle_intervention_added_to_multidisciplinary_chronic_pain_treatment_at_a_Danish_pain_centre_a.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, User Perspectives and Community-based Interventions","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Næstved, Slagelse, Ringsted Hospitals (NSR), Research Unit of Physiotherapy and Occupational Therapy (Slagelse)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for sundhedsuddannelser - Dekan, Ergoterapeutuddannelsen","Sundhed for børn og voksne – Institut for Terapeut og Jordemoderuddannelser, Arbejdsliv - Bedre forebyggelse og behandling af skader og sygdomme der påvirker arbejdsevnen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Svetlana Solgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"8af11fa7-c3b5-4b92-b8c7-54cc4889b827","name":"Nielsen, Svetlana Solgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-3694-4236","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette Reffstrup","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"7b0b955e-4090-479a-8bef-6fd6ad983680","name":"Christensen, Jeanette Reffstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2412-5989","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"4829db0c-8486-4ad1-8e6b-d4f3dc56c386","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-1629-1864","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vicki Oldenschläger","key":"mogensenpau","last":"Mogensen","locid":"1b81a828-e7eb-4bad-9e54-f8f5697fc8e6","name":"Mogensen, Vicki Oldenschläger","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette Enemark","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e38cf8d3-cebc-42ce-a154-3c1b5a175cf5","name":"Larsen, Anette Enemark","orcid":"0000-0003-1395-4156","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Thorgaard","key":"skoupau","last":"Skou","locid":"656a59cf-32bc-4190-b072-4adf47d954c1","name":"Skou, Søren Thorgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4336-7059","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"simonÿpau","last":"Simonÿ","locid":"6c2dbf49-1a55-4aa3-a990-1549e39274dd","name":"Simonÿ, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1189-2967","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34252015"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17482631.2021.1949900","issn":["17482623","17482631"],"issn_org":["17482631"],"issue":"1","journal":"International Journal of Qualitative Studies on Health and Well-Being","paperid":"1949900","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Qualitative Studies on Health and Well-Being","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85111578834"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Universities","University Colleges","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-42b599ee-9aae-4379-82ae-ae428e3df0c1","sdu-170907f4-2117-4a45-92f4-e7b399196abc"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Feasibility assessment of an occupational therapy lifestyle intervention added to multidisciplinary chronic pain treatment at a Danish pain centre: a qualitative evaluation from the perspectives of patients and clinicians","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.85-038775","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: During the COVID-19 pandemic, decreasing rates of hospitalisations for cardiovascular disease raised concerns for undertreatment, particularly for vulnerable groups. We investigated how the initial COVID-19 public lockdown, impacted the risk of being hospitalised with a major cardiovascular event (MCE: myocardial infarction/stroke/heart failure) according to educational level. METHODS: We grouped all Danish residents according to educational attainment level (low, medium, high) and age (40-59, 60-69, ≥70 years). In each group, we calculated the age-standardised and sex standardised risk of MCE hospitalisation in the initial COVID-19 lockdown-period (13 March 2020-3 May 2020) and in the corresponding calendar period in 2019. We calculated age-standardised and sex-standardised risks to investigate whether the COVID-19 lockdown had a differential effect on MCE incidence according to educational level. RESULTS: In the period in 2019, 2700 Danish residents were hospitalised with MCE, compared with only 2290 during the lockdown. During lockdown, the risk of hospitalisation for MCE decreased among residents aged ≥70 with low education (risk difference (RD) -46.2 (-73.2; -19.2) per 100,000) or medium education (RD -23.2 (-50.8; 4.3) per 100 000), but not among residents with high education (RD 5.1 (-32.3; 42.5), per 100 000). The risk of hospitalisation for MCE did not decrease significantly for the younger age groups. CONCLUSIONS: The COVID-19 lockdown is associated with a reduced incidence for MCE, especially among low educated, elderly residents. This raises concern for undertreatment that without clinical awareness and action may widen the educational gap in cardiovascular morbidity and mortality.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Andersen, Julie","Strandberg-Larsen, Katrine","Gerds, Thomas","Gislason, Gunnar","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Blanche, Paul","Andersson, Charlotte","Køber, Lars","Fosbøl, Emil","Phelps, Matthew","Kragholm, Kristian","Andersen, Mikkel Porsborg","Østergaard, Lauge","Butt, Jawad","Schou, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-003624"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Julie"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Boston University"],"keyword":["Health Policy","Public health","Public health policy","Social inequalities","Socio economic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of major cardiovascular events according to educational level before and after the initial covid 000000000019 public lockdown a nationwide study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7868126/pdf/jech-2020-215133.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-003624","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7868126","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85112722558","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33542032","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-4a65e599-5ae5-4f70-aeaa-afcf015b8259","ku-cd351d39-9a84-4e81-9965-eb4b8648b70d"],"keyword":["health policy","public health","public health policy","social inequalities","socio-economic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3E666C8A4CD845B9AA6BC030FCDDAEE7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7868126/pdf/jech-2020-215133.pdf","version":"Published Ve