{"abstract":"Der er i 2020 gennemført en systematisk, prospektiv, passiv overvågning af cirkulerende influenza A virus subtyper i danske svin. Det overordnede formål med overvågningen var, at identificere hvilke influenza A virus subtyper og varianter, der cirkulerer blandt danske svin. Totalt blev der i 2020 iværksat undersøgelse for influenza A virus på 2512 prøver fordelt på 723 indsendelser fra 517 besætninger registreret med forskelligt CHR nummer. I alt havde 400 (55 %) af indsendelserne fra 315 forskellige besætninger minimum en positiv prøve. Indsendelserne fordelte sig over hele landet og over hele året. Der var flest indsendelser til undersøgelse i vinterhalvåret, men andelen af positive prøver var relativt ensartet over hele året. Alle influenzapositive prøver blev testet for HA-subtypen H1pdm09, og virus blev påvist i 115 indsendelser fra 91 besætninger registreret med forskelligt CHR nummer og udgjorde således 29 % af de influenza A virus positive indsendelser, hvilket er en højere procentdel end i 2019, hvor tallet lå på 20 %. I alt blev 216 influenzavirus positive indsendelser subtypet for både HA og NA. Tilsammen viste disse analyser, at de oftest påviste subtyper i danske svin i 2020 var H1avN2sw, H1pdm09N1av og H1N1pdm09. I år er der således sket en markant stigning i antallet af prøver, der testede positive for H1pdm09N1av. Samtidig sås et yderligere fald i antallet af prøver, der testede positive for ”avian-like” svine H1avN1av. I år blev der for første gang identificeret en hel human sæsoninfluenza virus i svin. Specielt for 2020 blev der også observeret en stigning af antallet af prøver, hvori der blev fundet flere influenzavirus i samme prøve","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Krog, Jesper Schak","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-416608"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"overvågning af influenza a virus i svin slutrapport 000000002020","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/280181526/SwIAV_overv_gning_slutrapport_2020.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-416608","ids":["ku-26ba71f4-5ec1-49d8-be5a-4c7cbc9fc184"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-51404A4CCDD44FA01203BA023A433077"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/280181526/SwIAV_overv_gning_slutrapport_2020.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"ed85c101-c8e6-403b-ba93-39e95e23e68d","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"28","publisher":"Københavns Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-26ba71f4-5ec1-49d8-be5a-4c7cbc9fc184"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Overvågning af influenza A virus i svin : Slutrapport 2020","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-416608","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: We explored teachers' emotional reactions to the COVID-19 pandemic, and the association between COVID-19 risk management and these emotional reactions. Methods: We used cross-sectional data from 2665 teachers working at public schools. Participants responded to a questionnaire in May 2020. The analyses were adjusted for sex, age, cohabitation, and region. Results: Knowledge about adequate test behavior and feeling secure regarding colleagues' actions to hinder spread of virus were associated with less frequent emotional reactions. Lack of access to personal protective equipment and exposure to infected pupils, parents or colleagues were associated with more frequent emotional reactions. Conclusion: Similar to other groups of frontline employees, teachers experience negative emotional reactions to the COVID-19 pandemic. Gaining knowledge about teachers' worries and fears during pandemics is an important first step enabling leaders and occupational health professionals to address these.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","Fuglsang, Nina Vibe","Larsen, Inge","Nilsson, Charlotte Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-421206"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Cross sectional","Health care workers","Mental health","Occupational health","Transmission","school teacher"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Union Teachers"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"covid 000000000019 risk management and emotional reactions to covid 000000000019 among school teachers in denmark results from the class study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8091902/pdf/joem-63-0357.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-421206","identifier":[{"id":"000680430200011","type":"wos"},{"id":"33928933","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85105218047","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8091902","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-2e9b85e4-2495-4fa4-b1d5-7d8a2be0413e"],"keyword":["COVID-19","HEALTH-CARE WORKERS","TRANSMISSION","cross-sectional","mental health","occupational health","school teacher"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-16912AF27924D0DA8DFF12C7FC866375"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8091902/pdf/joem-63-0357.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Union Teachers"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nabenielsenpau","last":"Nabe-Nielsen","locid":"266b247f-d127-46ae-a6ab-aa16c3f010b9","name":"Nabe-Nielsen, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0002-4298-1420","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Nina Vibe","key":"fuglsangpau","last":"Fuglsang","name":"Fuglsang, Nina Vibe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Inge","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte Juul","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"573fb3db-41df-4adf-86e6-e5b0c69a43ef","name":"Nilsson, Charlotte Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-3364-7412","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33928933"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/jom.0000000000002136","issn":["10762752","15365948"],"issn_org":["10762752"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Occupational and Environmental Medicine","pages":"357-362","status":"p","title":"Journal of Occupational and Environmental Medicine","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85105218047"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2e9b85e4-2495-4fa4-b1d5-7d8a2be0413e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"COVID-19 Risk Management and Emotional Reactions to COVID-19 Among School Teachers in Denmark Results From the CLASS Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-421206","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We investigated factors affecting avian influenza virus (AIV) detections in Danish wild birds using data from the passive and active AIV surveillance in wild birds from 2006-2020. We used this data and machine learning (ML) algorithms along with landscape and environmental variables to develop predictive models of AIV occurrence in Denmark. We furthermore assessed potential accessibility bias in the passive AIV surveillance data submitted by the public. The passive AIV surveillance data was biased regarding accessibility to areas compared to random locations within Denmark. ML models differed in their predictive power and were used to predict the risk of AIV presence throughout Denmark. Our results suggest that landscape variables may affect AIV presence and enabled us to create risk maps of AIV occurrence in Danish wild birds. This may aid future targeted surveillance efforts within Denmark.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kjær, Lene Jung","Boklund, Anette","Kirkeby, Carsten","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik","Halasa, Tariq","Ward, Michael P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-500925"],"event":{"end":"2021-03-26","place":"Online","start":"2021-03-24","title":"SVEPM Conference and Annual General Meeting 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sydney"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spatial patterns of avian influenza in wild birds from denmark 000000002006 000000002020","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-500925","ids":["ku-b3f0fc95-bbee-411b-99c1-720345b6c6d6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-19EB311414F04AAB4BAE387B88F2E729"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Animal Welfare and Disease Control"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene Jung","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"b93ddd14-b340-4550-b3cf-eb9473b0d716","name":"Kjær, Lene Jung","orcid":"0000-0001-9659-4672","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette Ella","key":"boklundpau","last":"Boklund","locid":"b56cee2e-0320-4c3d-a360-6dc1f5b2ee67","name":"Boklund, Anette","name_org":"Boklund, Anette Ella","orcid":"0000-0001-6359-3403","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"kirkebypau","last":"Kirkeby","locid":"ea24c9a4-7aa6-40f3-9afb-0af19f1e962d","name":"Kirkeby, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-9292-5526","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tariq","key":"halasapau","last":"Halasa","locid":"8eda71d3-00d4-4316-a46f-20be6613d7a7","name":"Halasa, Tariq","orcid":"0000-0003-1112-0254","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Michael P.","key":"wardpau","last":"Ward","name":"Ward, Michael P.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b3f0fc95-bbee-411b-99c1-720345b6c6d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spatial patterns of avian influenza in wild birds from Denmark, 2006-2020","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-500925","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Biased ligands that selectively confer activity in one pathway over another are pharmacologically important because biased signaling may reduce on-target side effects and improve drug efficacy. Here, we describe an N-terminal modification in the incretin hormone glucagon-like peptide (GLP-1) that alters the signaling capabilities of the GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R) by making it G protein biased over internalization but was originally designed to confer DPP-4 resistance and thereby prolong the half-life of GLP-1. Despite similar binding affinity, cAMP production, and calcium mobilization, substitution of a single amino acid (Ala8 to Val8) in the N-terminus of GLP-1(7-36)NH2 (GLP-1 Val8) severely impaired its ability to internalize GLP-1R compared to endogenous GLP-1. In-depth binding kinetics analyses revealed shorter residence time for GLP-1 Val8 as well as a slower observed association rate. Molecular dynamics (MD) displayed weaker and less interactions of GLP-1 Val8 with GLP-1R, as well as distinct conformational changes in the receptor compared to GLP-1. In vitro validation of the MD, by receptor alanine substitutions, confirmed stronger impairments of GLP-1 Val8-mediated signaling compared to GLP-1. In a perfused rat pancreas, acute stimulation with GLP-1 Val8 resulted in a lower insulin and somatostatin secretion compared to GLP-1. Our study illustrates that profound differences in molecular pharmacological properties, which are essential for the therapeutic targeting of the GLP-1 system, can be induced by subtle changes in the N-terminus of GLP-1. This information could facilitate the development of optimized GLP-1R agonists.","author_count":12,"contributors":["van der Velden, Wijnand J. C.","Smit, Florent Xavier","Christiansen, Charlotte Bayer","Møller, Thor C","Hjortø, Gertrud Malene","Larsen, Olav","Schiellerup, Sine P","Bräuner-Osborne, Hans","Holst, Jens Juul","Hartmann, Bolette","Frimurer, Thomas M.","Rosenkilde, Mette M."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-506001"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"glp 000000000001 val000000000008 a biased glp 000000000001r agonist with altered binding kinetics and impaired release of pancreatic hormones in rats","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7887852/pdf/pt0c00193.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-506001","identifier":[{"id":"85100239627","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000619803700023","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC7887852","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33615180","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-bc95527a-2656-4194-bc79-f4e4a789cb1c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF2441526AD120926BEAC51763A5E11E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7887852/pdf/pt0c00193.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Molecular and Translational Pharmacology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Wijnand J C","key":"vanderveldenpau","last":"van der Velden","locid":"af278015-4368-422b-9cfc-73594524e05b"