te Brandstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-9285-3099","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Durita Lyngsø","key":"svartápau","last":"Svartá","locid":"7d14a946-3c39-479f-9e88-0b5c3061f8e5","name":"Svartá, Durita Lyngsø","orcid":"0000-0002-8931-8386","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bjerregaardpau","last":"Bjerregaard","locid":"ef4a2fa7-9735-4b1e-a4fa-b1272def2cfc","name":"Bjerregaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7153-8447","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingelise","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"9c041339-f1ff-4dc1-ac52-077f3f6349c4","name":"Olesen, Ingelise","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina Viskum Lytken","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3ee738b1-09d1-4886-9ddf-67ca132997fe","name":"Larsen, Christina Viskum Lytken","orcid":"0000-0002-6245-4222","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"46","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet. Statens Institut for Folkesundhed","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c798e29d-0af3-4e7c-bfe3-188d66b51636"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Kommunal sundhedsprofil - Avannaata Kommunia : Befolkningsundersøgelsen i Grønland 2018","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-630397","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Cosmogenic exposure dating is one of the most widely used methods to constrain the deglaciation history of former glaciated areas. In Greenland, more than 1000 cosmogenic 10Be exposure ages (10Be ages) have been published within the last two decades. However, a recurring problem is that many of these studies have reported variable amounts of nuclide inheritance making the 10Be ages too old and difficult to assess without large datasets or independent age control. In this study, we test the accuracy of 10Be dating of Holocene moraines using independent age constraints from threshold lake records. In Kangerlussuaq, West Greenland, the 10Be ages of the Ørkendalen moraine system are highly clustered with a mean age of 6.8 ± 0.3 ka (no outliers). In contrast, the nearby Little Ice Age (LIA) moraine yields scattered 10Be ages ranging from 2.5 to 0.1 ka but with a mean of 0.18 ± 0.06 ka after excluding outliers which coincides with independent age constraints from threshold lakes and boulder kill dates. At Gletscherlukket, Southeast Greenland, the 10Be ages of the LIA moraine range from 10.2 to 1.6 ka with a mean of 1.9 ± 0.2 ka after excluding outliers. This is ~1.7 ka older than recorded in the proglacial threshold lakes and suggests that all samples from this site contain a significant amount of nuclide inheritance. Our results are consistent with other reports of skewed 10Be age distributions in LIA re-advance moraines and it probably reflects nuclide inheritance from exposure during the Holocene Thermal Maximum when the glaciers in Greenland were inside the LIA extent. In contrast, there is no evidence of nuclide inheritance in the Ørkendalen moraines, most likely because the glacial erosion was more intense prior to the formation of the moraines i.e. sometime between the advance phase during Last Glacial Maximum position and the subsequent lateglacial and Holocene deglaciation. Our results highlight a potential pitfall related to dating re-advance moraines using cosmogenic exposure dating and we recommend using a multi-method dating approach.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Larsen, Nicolaj K.","Søndergaard, Anne Sofie","Levy, Laura B.","Laursen, Charlotte H.","Bjørk, Anders A.","Kjeldsen, Kristian K.","Funder, Svend","Strunk, Astrid","Olsen, Jesper","Kjær, Kurt H."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-026826"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Nicolaj K."],"country":["Greenland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","California State Polytechnic University, Humboldt","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","Humboldt State University"],"keyword":["Cosmogenic exposure dating","Glacier fluctuations","Greenland","Little Ice Age","Moraines","Threshold lakes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cosmogenic nuclide inheritance in little ice age moraines a case study from greenland","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85107117382","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-026826","identifier":[{"id":"85107117382","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c2f1e159-72a3-4ad6-b488-9c16f7bb0e08","ku-4dc695d5-a1af-4fa5-b81c-810f628ae139"],"keyword":["Cosmogenic exposure dating","Glacier fluctuations","Greenland","Little Ice Age","Moraines","Threshold lakes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F3FF8AC0F9A4FD6ED67904AAAE96A345"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Geogenetics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Geoscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"humboldt state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Humboldt State University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"california state polytechnic university humboldt","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"California State Polytechnic University, Humboldt","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nicolaj K.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"e16a0d68-3720-4232-b4e5-e47ffa53a7c7","name":"Larsen, Nicolaj K.","orcid":"0000-0002-0117-1106","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Sofie","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"dfd36787-1a93-465b-82eb-9ac79f4cf73a","name":"Søndergaard, Anne Sofie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura B.","key":"levypau","last":"Levy","name":"Levy, Laura B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte H.","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"8011edcd-9fdf-405a-ace8-02c69dfdd80e","name":"Laursen, Charlotte H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders A.","key":"bjørkpau","last":"Bjørk","locid":"f2550d56-6b6b-4e84-b759-33415f1aaa9f","name":"Bjørk, Anders Anker","name_org":"Bjørk, Anders A.","orcid":"0000-0002-4919-792X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Kristian K.","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"f03cee74-a015-4d75-9ca1-40a2b5ffd493","name":"Kjeldsen, Kristian Kjellerup","name_org":"Kjeldsen, Kristian K.","orcid":"0000-0002-8557-5131","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend","key":"funderpau","last":"Funder","locid":"5c14b89c-0398-4357-9e06-3cb232635aa9","name":"Funder, Svend Visby","name_org":"Funder, Svend","orcid":"0000-0002-7636-0470","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"strunkpau","last":"Strunk","locid":"6e2187d7-ef06-46c7-a40d-c6de0254f9a5","name":"Strunk, Astrid","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"2e527ce1-e5f9-44c3-8896-acd476b303ea","name":"Olsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4445-5520","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kurt H.","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"edb4315d-1be7-426b-b2d9-a18bddc543b2","name":"Kjær, Kurt H.","orcid":"0000-0002-8871-5179","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.quageo.2021.101200","issn":["18711014"],"journal":"Quaternary Geochronology","paperid":"101200","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Quaternary Geochronology","volume":"65"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107117382"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c2f1e159-72a3-4ad6-b488-9c16f7bb0e08","ku-4dc695d5-a1af-4fa5-b81c-810f628ae139"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cosmogenic nuclide inheritance in Little Ice Age moraines - A case study from Greenland","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-026826","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Digital patient reported outcomes are used increasingly in daily care and treatment of inflammatory bowel disease. Their purpose includes increased focus on patient wellbeing, reduction in avoidable follow-up consultations and increased patient self-management. However, implementation issues occur and studies indicate patients may have concerns, particularly regarding having fewer face-to-face consultations. This study aims to explore patients’ perspectives of use and non-use of digital patient reported outcomes and to understand the mechanisms underpinning patient reluctance to engage with this health technology. Results: Sixteen patients with inflammatory bowel disease at a regional hospital in Denmark were interviewed about their experiences of, and perspectives on, digital patient reported outcomes. A certain level of eHealth literacy was found to be a fundamental condition for use, while other factors were barriers or facilitators for use of digital PROs. Patients’ main concerns were about potential consequences for their care and relationship with the clinic. Most patients in stable remission were satisfied with the hospital being a “life-line” if their symptoms worsened, and perceived digital patient reported outcomes to be an efficient tool to establish that “life-line”. Patients with severe symptoms and a high degree of emotional distress related to their disease valued the potential for digital patient reported outcomes to increase their clinicians’ focus on mental health and extra-intestinal symptoms. Conclusion: This study found that if patients had sufficient digital literacy, they perceived digital patient reported outcomes to be a useful replacement for face-to-face consultations. However, they were concerned about digital patient reported outcomes’ effect on the patient–clinician relationship and its ability to detect worsening of symptoms. These concerns may be mitigated by good patient–clinician relationships, and the option for patients to maintain direct telephone contact with their gastroenterology specialist.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Nielsen, Amalie Søgaard","Appel, Charlotte Weiling","Larsen, Birgit Furstrand","Kayser, Lars","Hanna, Lisa"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-030067"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Nielsen, Amalie Søgaard"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Deakin University"],"keyword":["Digital health","Digital patient reported outcomes","eHealth"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patient perspectives on digital patient reported outcomes in routine care of inflammatory bowel disease","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41687-021-00366-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-030067","identifier":[{"id":"85115192413","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34533682","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8448812","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-f032b178-aefe-45f6-9fa4-433f4fb544e7","ku-5c99fcb4-f404-4f05-a034-e6f8e3f8893e"],"keyword":["Digital health","Digital patient reported outcomes","eHealth"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3D33B4945F33DDEADCB5694096F6AAB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/280056159/Patient_perspectives_on_digital_patient_reported_outcomes_in_routine_care_of_inflammatory_bowel_disease.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41687-021-00366-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Health Services Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Diagnostisk Center, Universitetsklinik for Innovative Patientforløb, Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"deakin university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Deakin University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Amalie Søgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1e0e8e88-821d-4c48-a563-7afe883f8e9b","name":"Nielsen, Amalie Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-2884-3902","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte W.","key":"appelpau","last":"Appel","locid":"0d1db098-5494-4dd5-ad41-6c2d6a36a9e4","name":"Appel, Charlotte Weiling","name_org":"Appel, Charlotte W.","orcid":"0000-0003-0397-9739","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgit Furstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"2d816040-cec1-44f7-ac67-adf16438df62","name":"Larsen, Birgit Furstrand","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"kayserpau","last":"Kayser","locid":"94c6679f-d8da-419f-9bd0-186a97295257","name":"Kayser, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-0909-4088","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisa","key":"hannapau","last":"Hanna","name":"Hanna, Lisa","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34533682"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s41687-021-00366-2","issn":["25098020"],"journal":"Journal of Patient-Reported Outcomes","paperid":"92","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Journal of Patient-Reported Outcomes","title_org":"Journal of Patient Reported Outcomes","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85115192413"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f032b178-aefe-45f6-9fa4-433f4fb544e7","ku-5c99fcb4-f404-4f05-a034-e6f8e3f8893e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patient perspectives on digital patient reported outcomes in routine care of inflammatory bowel disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-030067","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aims: An in-depth understanding of the prognostic value of patient-reported outcomes (PRO) is essential to facilitate person-centred care in heart failure (HF). This study aimed to clarify the prognostic role of subjective mental and physical health status in patients with HF. Methods and results: Patients with HF were identified from the DenHeart Survey (n = 1499) and PRO data were obtained at hospital discharge, including the EuroQol five-dimensional questionnaire (EQ-5D), the HeartQoL, and the Hospital Anxiety and Depression Scale (HADS). Clinical baseline data were obtained from medical records and linked to nationwide registries with patient-level data on sociodemographics and healthcare contacts. Outcomes were all-cause and cardiovascular (CV) mortality, CV events, and HF hospitalization with 1- and 3-year follow-up. Analysing the PRO data on a continuous scale, a worse score in the following were associated with risk of all-cause and CV mortality after 1 year: the HeartQoL (adjusted hazard ratios (HRs) 1.91, 95% confidence interval (CI) 1.42-2.57 and 2.17, 95% CI 1.50-3.15, respectively), the EQ-5D (adjusted HRs 1.26, 95% CI 1.15-1.38 and 1.27, 95% CI 1.13-1.42, respectively), the HADS depression subscale (adjusted HRs 1.12, 95% CI 1.07-1.17 and 1.11, 95% CI 1.05-1.17, respectively), and the HADS anxiety subscale (adjusted HRs 1.08, 95% CI 1.03-1.13 and 1.09, 95% CI 1.04-1.15, respectively). Three-year results were overall in concordance with the 1-year results. A similar pattern was also observed for non-fatal outcomes. Conclusion: Health-related quality of life and symptoms of anxiety and depression at discharge were associated with all-cause and CV mortality at 1- and 3-year follow-up.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anne Ankerstjerne","Larsen, Signe Holm","Jensen, Martin","Berg, Selina Kikkenborg","Rasmussen, Trine Bernholdt","Borregaard, Britt","Thrysoee, Lars","Thorup, Charlotte Brun","Mols, Rikke Elmose","Wiggers, Henrik","Johnsen, Søren Paaske"],"cuid":["S03-093.74-697759"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Anne Ankerstjerne"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular events","Cardiovascular mortality","Heart failure","Heart failure hospitalization","Patient reported outcomes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prognostic impact of self reported health on clinical outcomes in patients with heart failure","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85109166907","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-093.74-697759","identifier":[{"id":"32232437","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85109166907","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8b3c41a7-df9e-45f3-9f48-d89a38c3883b","au-de55841d-90f8-46cd-b27a-20ca2df5278d","sdu-74ceab2d-e65a-45db-b1f8-8166d5e41676"],"keyword":["Cardiovascular events","Cardiovascular mortality","Heart failure","Heart failure hospitalization","Patient-reported outcomes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-118B10D4A544256E388D0EC02E96E902"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medic