{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Johansen, Stine Liv","Larsen, Malene Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-108331"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hvordan undersøger man børn og unges mediebrug","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dna","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://videnskab.dk/kultur-samfund/hvordan-undersoeger-man-boern-og-unges-mediebrug","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-108331","ids":["aau-c8d029e6-c7d1-44aa-9974-662b44b38ecd"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-187E3AB0D0410DEAA1E06158ED92FC7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://videnskab.dk/kultur-samfund/hvordan-undersoeger-man-boern-og-unges-mediebrug","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Mattering: Centre for Discourse & Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Liv","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Stine Liv","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["1903301X"],"issue":"2.7.2020","newspaper":"Videnskab.dk","status":"p","title":"Videnskab.dk","title_org":"Videnskab.dk [online]"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c8d029e6-c7d1-44aa-9974-662b44b38ecd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Hvordan undersøger man børn og unges mediebrug?","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-108331","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Into 2021, the cost per Watt of photovoltaics is now dominated by module infrastructure and area-related costs, which are mostly common to all the core photovoltaic technologies. Therefore, in order to further improve the photovoltaic cost metrics, the module efficiency is becoming a key aspect. Chalcogenide on silicon tandem solar cells have the potential to combine the higher efficiency of tandem cells with the low costs of the core Si and thin film chalcogenide technologies. Recently, our group demonstrated several protection strategies for achieving the direct growth of Cu2ZnSnS4 (CZTS) on Si, using a bottom Si cell based on Polycrystalline Silicon on Oxide (POLO) structures, including TiN-based diffusion barriers, SiN sacrificial protection layers and tuning of the polySi properties. In this contribution, we report on the generalization of our findings to other top cells from the chalcogenide family, by presenting a comparative study between CZTS, CuGaSe2 (CGSe) and AgInGaSe2 (AIGSe) tandems on Si fabricated in different institutes. We find that the compatibility of the different top cells with Si is largely determined by two aspects of the top cell: 1) the processing temperature, and 2) the Cu content of the absorber material. With its Cu content and high processing temperature (575 °C), CZTS was found to be the harshest of the three materials in terms of Si degradation, while the Cu-free AIGSe showed the least impact on Si. We reveal that the degradation occurs mostly through an increase in surface recombination at the polySi interfaces, associated with Cu contamination during the chalcogenide synthesis. As a result, the collection efficiency and open-circuit voltage (Voc) of the Si bottom cell deteriorate. By managing the impact on Si with the protection strategies mentioned, we were able to demonstrate a CZTS/Si tandem with 6.8% efficiency, the highest for a tandem of this kind. Additionally, we fabricated a CGSe/Si tandem with an open-circuit voltage of 1.3 V. Most importantly, in all cases the bottom Si cell achieves a Voc above 575 mV, which is the highest reported for any chalcogenide/Si tandem cell, highlighting the potential of our Si architecture for achieving high-efficiency tandem cells with top cells fabricated in harsh conditions. By overcoming the Si degradation hurdle, we suggest that the next challenge to advance this tandem concept lies in the realization of high-efficiency chalcogenide top cells on Si-based structures. With the current state of the art (i.e. single-junction results for high-bandgap chalcogenides), we identify a clear pathway for tandem efficiencies above 15%, and further improvements are possible depending on future advances in the top cell efficiencies","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hajijafarassar, Alireza","Martinho, Filipe Mesquita Alves","Saini, Nishant","Larsen, Jes","Engberg, Sara Lena Josefin","Canulescu, Stela","Stamate, Eugen","Schou, Jørgen","Platzer-Björkman, Charlotte","Vines, Lasse","Hansen, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319287"],"event":{"end":"2020-11-27","place":"Virtual event","start":"2020-11-26","title":"11<sup>th</sup> European Kesterite+ online workshop","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Martinho, Filipe Mesquita Alves"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["CZTS","Silicon","Tandem"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"enabling high efficiency chalcogenide si tandem solar cells a comparative study of different chalcogenide top cells on a thermally resilient si bottom cell","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235464046/Kesterite_workshop_2020_Filipe_abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319287","ids":["dtu-31842450-2d8a-4d46-bd87-1233ab88d23a"],"keyword":["AIGSe","CGSe","CZTS","Silicon","Tandem"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-260186ECD6CC116230F4C87212CF76B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/235464046/Kesterite_workshop_2020_Filipe_abstract.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization","Technical University of Denmark, National Centre for Nano Fabrication and Characterization, Nanofabrication, Plasma Aided Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alireza","key":"hajijafarassarpau","last":"Hajijafarassar","locid":"7fc8759f-8144-445a-8f3a-ce4d6c21492a","name":"Hajijafarassar, Alireza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Filipe Mesquita Alves","key":"martinhopau","last":"Martinho","locid":"cc345908-526d-4647-b36a-2949ff30b065","name":"Martinho, Filipe Mesquita Alves","orcid":"0000-0002-0616-3260","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nishant","key":"sainipau","last":"Saini","name":"Saini, Nishant","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jes","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Jes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Lena Josefin","key":"engbergpau","last":"Engberg","locid":"f096bb7e-e865-4481-8e41-cc870de06b02","name":"Engberg, Sara Lena Josefin","orcid":"0000-0002-1007-4092","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stela","key":"canulescupau","last":"Canulescu","locid":"baf98129-49b9-45a1-bce4-c53da0cf367e","name":"Canulescu, Stela","orcid":"0000-0003-3786-2598","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Eugen","key":"stamatepau","last":"Stamate","locid":"cdccdf75-364a-4cf1-929b-d85b45d73a7e","name":"Stamate, Eugen","orcid":"0000-0002-9649-2438","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"36386f68-83f0-4e02-8f17-bcd3a41ed971","name":"Schou, Jørgen","orcid":"0000-0002-8647-2679","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"platzerbjörkmanpau","last":"Platzer-Björkman","name":"Platzer-Björkman, Charlotte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"vinespau","last":"Vines","name":"Vines, Lasse","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"8d678857-a721-4f7f-9a33-1dadb7401ce4","name":"Hansen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-6090-8323","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-31842450-2d8a-4d46-bd87-1233ab88d23a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Enabling high-efficiency chalcogenide/Si tandem solar cells: a comparative study of different chalcogenide top cells on a thermally resilient Si bottom cell","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319287","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Seaweeds contain many valuable compounds that can be used in the food industry. Carrageenan is a polysaccharide which has been extracted from seaweed for centuries and is used as a texturizer in food and non-food products. However, seaweeds contain compounds other than carrageenan, such as proteins, which could also be extracted. This extraction should be done without compromising the industrial scale carrageenan extraction yield and quality. This study aimed at up-stream protein extraction from red seaweed Eucheuma denticulatum by using of an optimized enzyme-assisted extraction, including of an aqueous/enzymatic treatment followed by alkaline extraction, and then the commercial carrageenan extraction. The protein extraction efficiency of four enzymes was evaluated including Celluclast® 1.5L, Shearzyme® 500 L, Alcalase® 2.4 L FG and Viscozyme® L at a concentration of 0.0, 0.1, 0.2 and 0.4% (w/w). To avoid detrimental effects on carrageenan, all the experiments were performed at pH 7 at room temperature. The results showed that 0.2% w/w Alcalase® or Viscozyme® added individually achieved the highest protein extraction efficiencies (59 and 48%, respectively) at pH 7 and room temperature (p < 0.05). Determination of the most common carrageenan quality parameters indicated that using any of these enzymes had no negative effect on the carrageenan yield and quality.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Naseri, Alireza","Jacobsen, Charlotte","Sejberg, Jimmy J. P.","Pedersen, Tommy Ewi","Larsen, Jan","Hansen, Karin Meyer","Holdt, Susan Løvstad"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-320285"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Naseri, Alireza"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-CPK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-CPK","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","r