id":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anette","key":"boklundpau","last":"Boklund","locid":"b56cee2e-0320-4c3d-a360-6dc1f5b2ee67","name":"Boklund, Anette","orcid":"0000-0001-6359-3403","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tariq","key":"halasapau","last":"Halasa","locid":"8eda71d3-00d4-4316-a46f-20be6613d7a7","name":"Halasa, Tariq","orcid":"0000-0003-1112-0254","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wardpau","last":"Ward","name":"Ward, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"kirkebypau","last":"Kirkeby","locid":"ea24c9a4-7aa6-40f3-9afb-0af19f1e962d","name":"Kirkeby, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-9292-5526","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22541/au.160580354.45426969/v1","publisher":"Authorea","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab5cb1f7-2cf8-4314-b629-3b6612ce2ef0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Landscape and spatial patterns of avian influenza virus in Danish wild birds, 2006-2020","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-495806","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: In Denmark, quality-improvement initiatives aimed at providing a better colonoscopy service are few. The primary objective of this study was to improve colonoscopy quality at Aalborg University Hospital, Denmark, using structured training programmes. The secondary aim was to introduce a system for individual colonoscopist performance monitoring. METHODS: We conducted a colonoscopy-quality pilot study covering two major quality performance indicators: caecum intubation rate (CIR) and polyp detection rate (PDR). The pilot study was followed by colonoscopy training programmes offering experienced colonoscopists colonoscopy skills upgrading, polypectomy and train-the-trainers courses taught by English experts. Junior doctors completed a 20-day module-based colonoscopy-training programme. A regional individual colonoscopy quality-reporting system was developed as a supplementary file within the electronic health records. RESULTS: The CIR increased from 87.1% to 92.1% (p less-than 0.001) and the PDR from 33.7% to 41.7% (p less-than 0.001) in the course of the structured training programme. Multivariable analysis adjusting for patient sex, patient age and colonoscopy indication showed a significant increase in CIR (p less-than 0.001), but not in PDR (p = 0.19). The colonoscopy quality reporting system was introduced and now provides biannual feedback to all colonoscopists. CONCLUSIONS: Quality-improvement initiatives may lead to an improved CIR and possibly PDR. Nationwide training programmes and performance monitoring should be implemented to further improve and monitor colonoscopy quality. FUNDING: none. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not relevant.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Lasse","Bernstein, Inge","Lindorff-Larsen, Karen","Carlsen, Charlotte Green","Torp-Pedersen, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-083.60-006685"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Lasse"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improving colonoscopy quality through individualised training programmes","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/379602811/Pedersen_et_al._2020_Improving_colonoscopy_quality_through_individualised_training_programmes.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.60-006685","identifier":[{"id":"32741439","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85088908492","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-8a174a2a-fb77-4e4a-a119-d2423f82b7e4","au-0e9668f7-9857-446b-9622-74223dfdb9cc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-261BE137FCAEDC5B5E374FC84ADDA378"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/379602811/Pedersen_et_al._2020_Improving_colonoscopy_quality_through_individualised_training_programmes.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/dmj/improving-colonoscopy-quality-through-individualised-training-programmes","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Gastrointestinal Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Kirurgi og Kræftbehandling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, HE Centre, HE Centre - Centre for Health Sciences Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"2637b3fb-b84f-4ef6-8976-39b51dae9d40","name":"Pedersen, Lasse","orcid":"0000-0002-3299-1561","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Inge","key":"bernsteinpau","last":"Bernstein","locid":"fc5f604f-944f-4a7b-a98b-f5db5141174b","name":"Bernstein, Inge","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"lindorfflarsenpau","last":"Lindorff-Larsen","locid":"44148857-c2e8-4814-86a8-28c2b1951a63","name":"Lindorff-Larsen, Karen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Green","key":"carlsenpau","last":"Carlsen","locid":"c15e93b9-7b51-4d3b-9a42-fbf3aa255ad1","name":"Carlsen, Charlotte Green","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","locid":"5417d806-0578-4505-b3fe-68ae0359913e","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32741439"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["16039629"],"issue":"8","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A01200028","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Laegeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088908492"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8a174a2a-fb77-4e4a-a119-d2423f82b7e4","au-0e9668f7-9857-446b-9622-74223dfdb9cc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Improving colonoscopy quality through individualised training programmes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.60-006685","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus (PRRSV) is prevalent in Danish swine herds. In July 2019, PRRSV-1 was detected in a PRRSV-negative boar station and subsequently spread to more than 38 herds that had received semen from the boar station. Full genome sequencing revealed a sequence of 15.098 nucleotides. Phylogenetic analyses showed that the strain was a recombination between the Amervac strain (Unistrain PRRS vaccine; Hipra) and the 96V198 strain (Suvaxyn PRRS; Zoetis AH). The major parent was the 96V198 strain that spanned ORFs 1–2 and part of ORF 3 and the minor parent was the Amervac strain, which constituted the remaining part of the genome. The virus seems to be highly transmissible and has caused severe disease in infected herds despite a high level of genetic identity to the attenuated parent strains. The source of infection was presumable a neighbouring farm situated 5.8 km from the boar station.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Pedersen, Kasper","Stadejek, Tomasz","Trebbien, Ramona","Andresen, Lars Ole","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S02-098.58-036102"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Lars Erik"],"country":["Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Warsaw University of Life Sciences"],"keyword":["PRRSV","Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus","Recombination","Swine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a recombination between two type 000000000001 porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus prrsv 000000000001 vaccine strains has caused severe outbreaks in danish pigs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/tbed.13555","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-098.58-036102","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7540543","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85085524273","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32219985","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-9a265f21-6cc1-44ff-8567-f9e79c267b6d","ku-49a24e92-ff82-45cd-bf27-07176da7b424"],"keyword":["PRRSV","porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus","recombination","swine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-81B4851A93E8C6596E518DA0DCE6FBB5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/209337959/tbed.13555_1_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/252686033/tbed.13555.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/tbed.13555","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centre for Diagnostics DTU"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pl"