ogisk rapport for udbrud af HPAI H5N8 i slagtekylling opformeringsbesætning","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-251604","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Polte og gylte bidrog til introduktion af smitte med influenza i ti sobesætninger, og viruspositive polte betød en øget risiko for influenzavirus i farestalden i slutningen af karantæneperioden. Dette var uafhængigt af, om besætningen vaccinerede søer og polte imod influenza. Et øget fokus på smittebeskyttelse både til og fra karantænen samt korrekt og tidlig vaccination af polte og søer er vejen frem, hvis influenza skal under kontrol i din sobesætning.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Larsen, Inge","Krog, Jesper Schak","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-394777"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"derfor er influenza svær at håndtere resultater fra et ph d studium","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248502738/Notat_2009.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-394777","ids":["ku-022649e8-8ebd-4358-b42e-da6df63c33d8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BFF7C47601D220FB37D1704D53919EC5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://svineproduktion.dk/publikationer/kilder/notater/2020/2009","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248502738/Notat_2009.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpiapau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"3bc2c20c-771a-4d73-9424-e1173143a632","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensencharlottesonnepau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inge","key":"larseningepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"82b09bf9-73d5-4c71-a3c1-01e66b0e9ebe","name":"Larsen, Inge","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-2241","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogjesperschakpau","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"2009","journal":"SEGES Notat","status":"p","title":"SEGES Notat"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-022649e8-8ebd-4358-b42e-da6df63c33d8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"DERFOR ER INFLUENZA SVÆR AT HÅNDTERE : RESULTATER FRA ET PH.D.-STUDIUM","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394777","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this nation-wide cohort study we report the first long-term results of the association between having a atrial septal defects (ASD) on psychiatric disorders and use of psychotropic agents. Through population-based registries we included Danish individuals born before 1994 who received an ASD diagnosis between 1959and 2013. We used Cox proportional hazards regression and Fine and Grey competing risk regression to estimate the risk of receiving a psychiatric diagnosis and use of psychotropic medicine compared with a gender and age matched background population cohort. In 2,277 patients with a median follow-up from ASD diagnosis of 23.4 years (range 0.2 to 59.3 years) we found ASD patients to have a higher risk of psychiatric disorders (adjusted hazard ratio [HR]: 3.9; 95% confidence interval [CI] 3.4 to 4.5) compared with the comparison cohort and a cumulative incidence of using psychotropic agents 30 years after the ASD diagnosis of 47.4% (95% CI: 40.3 to 55.1) in the ASD patients and 25.5%, (95% CI: 23.5 to 27.8) in the comparison cohort. Diagnosis of the ASD before the age of 15 years (adjusted HR: 3.4; 95% confidence interval: 2.0 to 4.0) and surgical correction of the defect (HR: 1.5 (95% CI: 1.2 to 1.8), p <0.0001) had a higher risk than those with an ASD diagnosis after the age of 15 years and those with transcatheter closure of the defect. In conclusion, ASD patients had increased long-term risk of psychiatric disorder and use of psychotropic agents compared with a gender and age matched general population controls.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nyboe, Camilla","Udholm, Sebastian","Larsen, Signe Holm","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","Redington, Andrew","Hjortdal, Vibeke"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-029003"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Nyboe, Camilla"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of lifetime psychiatric morbidity in adults with atrial septal defect from a nation wide cohort","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85085334081","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-029003","identifier":[{"id":"32650900","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85085334081","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e14a74d0-3ce6-4348-af2d-a2eaadbcd13a","ku-8e5df15e-1aa4-4386-b0cd-c89fffe06a4a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-271DF05738042504C095D514212D4591"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cincinnati children s hospital medical center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cincinnati Children's Hospital Medical Center","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Cardiothoracic Surgery","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Camilla","key":"nyboepau","last":"Nyboe","locid":"357fc309-24af-440d-88c6-a052902392a0","name":"Nyboe, Camilla","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sebastian","key":"udholmpau","last":"Udholm","locid":"98f76ad9-df57-4c54-b3ba-7243356aa36b","name":"Udholm, Sebastian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Holm","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"77f9eb05-49b3-461b-bd54-9144084b12a0","name":"Larsen, Signe Holm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","locid":"1e308742-df61-47da-83ce-53d8a7c774c3","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","name_org":"Rask, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-7426-0353","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrew","key":"redingtonpau","last":"Redington","name":"Redington, Andrew","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Vibeke","key":"hjortdalpau","last":"Hjortdal","locid":"69607db8-0b14-4d01-95f0-c114bbc826ef","name":"Hjortdal, Vibeke Elisabeth","name_org":"Hjortdal, Vibeke","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32650900"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.amjcard.2020.04.047","issn":["00029149","18791913"],"issn_org":["00029149"],"journal":"American Journal of Cardiology","pages":"1-6","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Cardiology","title_org":"The American Journal of Cardiology","volume":"128"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085334081"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e14a74d0-3ce6-4348-af2d-a2eaadbcd13a","ku-8e5df15e-1aa4-4386-b0cd-c89fffe06a4a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of Lifetime Psychiatric Morbidity in Adults With Atrial Septal Defect (from a Nation-Wide Cohort)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-029003","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The degree of antigenic drift in swine influenza A viruses (swIAV) has historically been regarded as minimal compared to that of human influenza A virus strains. However, as surveillance activities on swIAV have increased, more isolates have been characterized, revealing a high level of genetic and antigenic differences even within the same swIAV lineage. The objective of this study was to investigate the level of genetic drift in one enzootically infected swine herd over one year. Nasal swabs were collected monthly from sows (n = 4) and piglets (n = 40) in the farrowing unit, and from weaners (n = 20) in the nursery. Virus from 1-4 animals were sequenced per month. Analyses of the sequences revealed that the hemagglutinin (HA) gene was the main target for genetic drift with a substitution rate of 7.6 × 10-3 substitutions/site/year and evidence of positive selection. The majority of the mutations occurred in the globular head of the HA protein and in antigenic sites. The phylogenetic tree of the HA sequences displayed a pectinate typology, where only a single lineage persists and forms the ancestor for subsequent lineages. This was most likely caused by repeated selection of a single immune-escape variant, which subsequently became the founder of the next wave of infections.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Larsen, Inge","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Krog, Jesper Schak","Wacheck, Silke","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-036029"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ceva Santé Animale"],"keyword":["Antigenic drift","Enzootic infections","Genetic drift","Hemagglutinin","Molecular clock","Selection","Sows","Substitution rate","Swine influenza A virus","immune escape variants"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"substantial antigenic drift in the hemagglutinin protein of swine influenza a viruses","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v12020248","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-036029","identifier":[{"id":"85080124532","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7077184","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32102230","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-96616371-0de1-4bbb-a774-f8aa1dfc0738","ku-4bca68c5-ce76-4504-a5c0-d66daec4b3db"],"keyword":["antigenic drift","enzootic infections","genetic drift","hemagglutinin","immune escape variants","molecular clock","selection","sows","substitution rate","swineinfluenza A virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6FE3D3466462542836F5F6E5BD6A820F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/244958071/viruses_12_00248_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/207382480/viruses_12_00248_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/v12020248","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centre for Diagnostics DTU","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"fr","key":"ceva santé animale","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ceva Santé Animale","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpiapau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"14d7fe91-822b-4f95-a07c-9479df41d8c5","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Gorm","key":"pedersenandersgormpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bb3513aa-fb20-46ef-ba14-9c150c929cf1","name":"Pedersen, Anders Gorm","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-8965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inge","key":"larseningepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"82b09bf9-73d5-4c71-a3c1-01e66b0e9ebe","name":"Larsen, Inge","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-2241","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensencharlottesonnepau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogjesperschakpau","last":"Krog","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Silke","key":"wachecksilkepau","last":"Wacheck","name":"Wacheck, Silke","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"135a9407-d29c-4508-8f79-978f5b295a15","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32102230"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/v12020248","issn":["19994915"],"issue":"2","journal":"Viruses","paperid":"248","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Viruses","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85080124532"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-96616371-0de1-4bbb-a774-f8aa1dfc0738","ku-4bca68c5-ce76-4504-a5c0-d66daec4b3db"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Substantial Antigenic Drift in the Hemagglutinin Protein of Swine Influenza A Viruses","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-036029","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Treatment with beta-blockers is currently recommended after myocardial infarction (MI). The evidence relies on trials conducted decades ago before implementation of revascularization and contemporary medical therapy or in trials enrolling patients with heart failure or reduced left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF ≤ 40%). Accordingly, the impact of beta-blockers on mortality and morbidity following acute MI in patients without reduced LVEF or heart failure is unclear. Methods/design: The Danish trial of beta-blocker treatment after myocardial infarction without reduced ejection fraction (DANBLOCK) is a prospective, randomized, controlled, open-label, non-blinded endpoint clinical trial designed to evaluate the efficacy of beta-blocker treatment in post-MI patients in the absence of reduced LVEF or heart failure. We will randomize 3570 patients will be randomized within 14 days of index MI to beta-blocker or control for a minimum of 2 years. The primary endpoint is a composite of all-cause mortality, recurrent MI, acute decompensated heart failure, unstable angina pectoris, or stroke. The primary composite endpoint will be assessed through locally reported and adjudicated endpoints supplemented by linkage to the Danish national registers. A number of secondary endpoints will be investigated including patient reported outcomes and cardiovascular mortality. Data from similar ongoing trials in Norway and Sweden will be pooled to perform an individual patient data meta-analysis. Discussion: DANBLOCK is a randomized clinical trial investigating the effect of long-term beta-blocker therapy after myocardial infarction in patients without heart failure and reduced LVEF. Results from the trial will add important scientific evidence to inform future clinical guidelines. Trial registration: Clinicaltrials.gov, NCT03778554. Registered on 19 December 2018. European Clinical Trials Database, 2018-002699-42, registered on 28 September 2018.","author_coun