{"abstract":"Reverse transcription real-time PCR (RT-qPCR) is one of several techniques used to determine the presence and level of infectious veterinary pathogens in diagnostic laboratories. Here we describe how automation of PCR reactions using integrated fluidic circuits (IFCs), an IFC controller MX and a Biomark HD instrument allows for the testing of 48 field samples with swine influenza for up to 48 different subtypes simultaneously in nanoliter volumes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Helene","Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-308385"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Helene"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subtyping of swine influenza using a high throughput real time pcr platform and a single microfluidics device","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85074404657","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-308385","identifier":[{"id":"85074404657","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31667759","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-0cad7188-9fd8-40a2-b746-522c7ce25ecb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F5BD8A1C8740495E180AAEFDDD78BEE5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical U