:"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085961865"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cb3a4de4-bdd0-49cb-9fdb-48e8f6b4b9dc","au-0614156b-a2c0-4741-8d9d-246492a23d0e","ku-65e1ef68-98b7-4f78-b688-37925d743acd","sdu-566c67c1-87eb-413a-9d2e-5d75456e53ec"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cohort Profile : The Copenhagen Child Cohort Study (CCC2000)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-098.64-009748","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: The demographic, economic and technological development in Denmark is bringing changes to the healthcare system, including shorter hospitalizations. An increasing number of patients are therefore being treated at home. Aim: The aim of this study was to examine the experience of being a patient at home. Methods: The study consists of 10 qualitative semi-structured interviews with patients receiving treatment at home. The interviews were analyzed based on Kvale and Brinkmann’s approach. Results: The findings are presented as four themes related to the patient’s perspective on receiving treatment at home: «The responsibility of the patient», «The requiring of courage,» «A sense of freedom» and «Feeling safe». Conclusion: The patients felt positive about receiving treatment at home, but the experience can be filled with dilemmas. However, this requires patients to be competent and responsible. Therefore, it is important that home treatment remains an individual choice.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jensen, Gitte Sylvester","Eckhardt, Michala","Skouenborg, Pernille Bak","Lyng Larsen, Karen","Højgaard, Kristina","Dybbro, Karina Løvendahl","Delmar, Charlotte","Hoeck, Bente"],"cuid":["S06-097.98-006229"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":"5+","continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","UiT The Arctic University of Norway","VID Specialized University"],"keyword":["Competencies","Health care system","Hverdagsliv","Omsorg","Patient perspective","Responsibility","Sygepleje","interviewundersøgelser"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC