ll,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-df907040-cd1e-4484-ad99-177c335d17f2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Social media insecurities in everyday life among young adults – an ethnography of anonymous Jodel disclosures","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-115050","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Respiratory and intestinal diseases in pigs can have significant negative influence on productivity and animal welfare. A wide range of real-time PCR (rtPCR) assays are used in our laboratory (National Veterinary Institute, Technical University of Denmark) for pathogen detection, and PCR analyses are performed on traditional rtPCR platforms in which a limited number of samples can be analyzed per day given limitations in equipment and personnel. To mitigate these restrictions, rtPCR assays have been optimized for the high-throughput rtPCR BioMark platform (Fluidigm). Using this platform, we developed a high-throughput detection system that can be used for simultaneous examination of 48 samples with detection specificity for 18 selected respiratory and enteric viral and bacterial pathogens of high importance to Danish pig production. The rtPCR assays were validated and optimized to run under the same reaction conditions using a BioMark 48.48 dynamic array (DA) integrated fluidic circuit chip, and the sensitivity and specificity were assessed by testing known positive samples. Performance of the 48.48DA was similar to traditional rtPCR analysis, and the specificity of the 48.48DA was high. Application of the high-throughput platform has resulted in a significant reduction in cost and working hours and has provided production herds with a new innovative service with the potential to facilitate the optimal choice of disease control strategies such as vaccination and treatment.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Krog, Jesper Schak","Skovgaard, Kerstin","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-312439"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Detection","High throughput","Real time PCR","Viruses"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of a high throughput real time pcr system for detection of enzootic pathogens in pigs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85075416666","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-312439","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7003221","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85075416666","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31752620","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1a2a2e39-a76b-4b56-8d14-b5fd2bdb80dc"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Detection","High-throughput","Porcine pathogens","Real-time PCR","Viruses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B29965446F89BD74249E66542417C267"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centre for Diagnostics DTU","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"4d2ddf87-a082-462e-86c4-567264391d29","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","orcid":"0000-0003-4948-9946","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kerstin","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c3c3868-b5a3-457b-8b97-9645ad03e405","name":"Skovgaard, Kerstin","orcid":"0000-0001-5663-4879","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31752620"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1040638719890863","issn":["10406387","19434936"],"issn_org":["10406387"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Veterinary Diagnostic Investigation","pages":"51-64","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Journal of Veterinary Diagnostic Investigation","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075416666"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1a2a2e39-a76b-4b56-8d14-b5fd2bdb80dc"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Development of a high-throughput real-time PCR system for detection of enzootic pathogens in pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-312439","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Infectious diseases are of great economic importance in commercial pig production, causing both clinical and subclinical disease, with influence on welfare, productivity, and antibiotic use. The causes of these diseases are often multifactorial and laboratory diagnostics are seldom routinely performed. The aim of the present study was to explore the benefits of monthly pathogen monitoring in nursery and finisher herds and to examine association between laboratory results and observed clinical signs, including coughing and diarrhoea. Three monthly samplings were conducted in three different age groups in six nursery and four finisher production units. For each unit, two pens were randomly selected in each age group and evaluated for coughing and diarrhoea events. Furthermore, faecal sock and oral fluid samples were collected in the selected pens and analysed for 18 respiratory and enteric viral and bacterial pathogens using the high-throughput real-time PCR BioMark HD platform (Fluidigm, South San Francisco, USA).  Results: In total, 174 pens were sampled in which eight coughing events and 77 diarrhoeic events were observed. The overall findings showed that swine influenza A virus, porcine circovirus 2, porcine cytomegalovirus, Brachyspira pilosicoli, Lawsonia intracellularis, Escherichia coli fimbria types F4 and F18 were found to be prevalent in several of the herds. Association between coughing events and the presence of swine influenza A virus, porcine cytomegalovirus (Cq ≤ 20) or a combination of these were found. Furthermore, an association between diarrhoeic events and the presence of L. intracellularis (Cq ≤ 24) or B. pilosicoli (Cq ≤ 26) was found.  Conclusions: The use of high-throughput real-time PCR analysis for continuous monitoring of pathogens and thereby dynamics of infections in a pig herd, provided the veterinarian and farmer with an objective knowledge on the distribution of pathogens in the herd. In addition, the use of a high-throughput method in combination with information about clinical signs, productivity, health status and antibiotic consumption, presents a new and innovative way of diagnosing and monitoring pig herds and even to a lower cost than the traditional method.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Kobberø, Maja","Kusk, Thomas K.","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Pedersen, Ken Steen","Kristensen, Charlotte S.","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360266"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård"],"keyword":["Diagnostics","Diarrhoea","Enteric bacteria","Enteric viruses","Monitoring","Respiratory viruses"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"objective pathogen monitoring in nursery and finisher pigs by monthly laboratory diagnostic testing","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-020-00161-3","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The study was funded by the Danish Pig Levy Fund."],"id":"S01-000.00-360266","identifier":[{"id":"32922832","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090957442","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7476771","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-ba4e6507-281f-43e8-9b97-30b4a96a9589"],"keyword":["Coughing","Diagnostics","Diarrhoea","Enteric bacteria","Enteric viruses","High-throughput real-time PCR","Monitoring","Respiratory bacteria","Respiratory viruses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C970756603699A7B612825E9AFE18EDA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws