{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Low plasma testosterone, either spontaneous or as a result of androgen deprivation therapy for prostate cancer, is associated with an increased risk of cardiovascular events. The underlying mechanism in humans is not understood. Experimental studies in mice have shown that castration facilitates atherogenesis and may increase signs of plaque vulnerability. Pigs used for translational atherosclerosis research have frequently been castrated for practical or commercial reasons, but the effect of castration on atherosclerosis has never been systematically evaluated in pigs. OBJECTIVE: To study the effect of castration on atherosclerotic plaque burden and type in genetically modified minipigs with hypercholesterolemia. METHODS: Newborn male Yucatan minipigs with transgenic overexpression of a human gain-of-function mutant of proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 were randomized to undergo orchiectomy (n = 8) or serve as controls (n = 6). Minipigs were started on high-fat diet at 3 months of age and the amount and composition of atherosclerotic lesions were analyzed at 12 months of age. Plasma lipid profiles and behavioral parameters were also assessed. RESULTS: Plasma lipids were slightly affected to a more atherogenic profile by orchiectomy, but atherosclerotic lesion size was unaltered in the LAD, thoracic aorta, abdominal aorta, and iliac arteries. The distribution of lesion types (xanthomas, pathological intimal thickening and fibroatheromas) were also not statistically different between groups in any of the examined vascular territories. The abdominal aorta developed the most advanced stages of disease with reproducible fibroatheroma formation, and here it was found that the area of necrotic core was significantly increased in orchiectomized pigs compared with controls. Orchiectomy also reduced aggressive behavior. CONCLUSIONS: Castration does not alter the burden of atherosclerosis in hypercholesterolemic Yucatan minipigs, but may increase necrotic core area in fibroatheromas.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Shim, Jeong Tangkjær","Schmidt, Nikolaj","Nogales, Paula","Larsen, Torben","Sørensen, Charlotte Brandt","Bentzon, Jacob Fog"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-208648"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro Nacional de Investigaciones Cardiovasculares (CNIC)"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of castration on atherosclerosis in yucatan minipigs with genetic hypercholesterolemia","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0234131","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-208648","identifier":[{"id":"85086008332","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32502216","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7274396","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-8b001ac8-e994-445e-977b-e769fcd793b4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8281147269A6C77B842777F43DA857C6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0234131","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"centro nacional de investigaciones cardiovasculares","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centro Nacional de Investigaciones Cardiovasculares (CNIC)","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeong T.","key":"shimpau","last":"Shim","locid":"d84f1f8a-0624-41e3-95ec-a4b0035d6891","name":"Shim, Jeong Tangkjær","name_org":"Shim, Jeong T.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikolaj","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"be862ebe-9ee7-46c4-9008-f429b129ff43","name":"Schmidt, Nikolaj","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Paula","key":"nogalespau","last":"Nogales","name":"Nogales, Paula","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Torben","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6eda720d-adf9-4bee-b02f-2d1a195cf8bf","name":"Larsen, Torben","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte B.","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"14bfd3d1-a9b2-4bc5-823b-233432e43cf3","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Brandt","name_org":"Sørensen, Charlotte B.","orcid":"0000-0002-4469-8696","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob F.","key":"bentzonpau","last":"Bentzon","locid":"b19cdb97-a953-43ff-ad51-19d0a680caed","name":"Bentzon, Jacob Fog","name_org":"Bentzon, Jacob F.","orcid":"0000-0002-3020-5002","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32502216"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0234131","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"6","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0234131","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086008332"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8b001ac8-e994-445e-977b-e769fcd793b4"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects of castration on atherosclerosis in Yucatan minipigs with genetic hypercholesterolemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-208648","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"In this study, a methane (CH4) mass balance was established for Hedeland landfill. CH4 generation rates were modelled using a multiphase first-order decay model (The Afvalzorg model) and determined at between 57 and 79 kg h−1. The CH4 emission rate was quantified at between 2 and 14 kg h−1, using the tracer gas dispersion method and the CH4 gas recovery efficiency was between 8 and 21%. At three places along the perimeter of the landfill, gas remediation systems have been installed to protect the residential houses from any risk of migrating landfill gas. About 0.76 kg h−1 of CH4 was extracted from these three remediation systems. Using a carbon mass balance for the lateral migrating landfill gas showed a fractional oxidation of about 78%, which corresponded to a CH4 flux of 3.5 kg h−1 from the three remediation systems, including the oxidised CH4. The total lateral CH4 flux (un-oxidised) from the total landfill perimeter was estimated at between 6.9 and 10.4 kg h−1. CH4 oxidation efficiency in the landfill cover soil, determined from stable carbon isotope analyses, was found to be between 12% and 92%. This resulted in an average CH4 oxidation rate of 32 kg h−1, using an average CH4 emission rate of 8 kg h−1. CH4 surface screenings and surface flux measurements supported the hypothesis that oxidation efficiency was in the higher range and that oxidation could close the CH4 mass balance.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fjelsted, Lotte","Christensen, A. G.","Larsen, J. E.","Kjeldsen, Peter","Scheutz, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-333175"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Fjelsted, Lotte"],"keyword":["Gas recovery","Horizontal landfill gas migration","Methane generation","Methane oxidation efficiencies","Oxidation in landfill cover soil","Tracer gas dispersion method"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NIRA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NIRA","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"closing the methane mass balance for an old closed danish landfill","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/219908771/Revised_manuscript_CLEAN.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work presented herein was funded by an industrial PhD project hosted by Niras A/S and The Technical University of Denmark (DTU). The PhD project was funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark (Project ref. no.: 4135-00011B ). The authors wish to thank ARGO for providing access to Hedeland landfill and all the data from previous investigations at the site. Appendix A"],"id":"S01-000.00-333175","identifier":[{"id":"31678804","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85074189986","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-600fcfec-60f3-48ef-8609-71edaa683433"],"keyword":["Gas recovery","Horizontal landfill gas migration","Methane generation","Methane oxidation efficiencies","Oxidation in landfill cover soil","Tracer gas dispersion method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-882D07F219A697EDE97F3F432EAC70C8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/219908771/Revised_manuscript_CLEAN.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Residual Resource Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"niras","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NIRA","l3nl":"NIRAS A/S","l3nn":"NIRAS","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NIRAS","namevar":["NIRAS A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NIRA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lotte","key":"fjelstedpau","last":"Fjelsted","locid":"66fc8252-3482-4d08-99ce-6f5ee964650f","name":"Fjelsted, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0002-2878-798X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A. G.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, A. G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J. E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, J. E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"49899b92-45e7-485d-88cb-faf95e4ac0d7","name":"Kjeldsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2738-9960","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"scheutzpau","last":"Scheutz","locid":"48fe2850-fdc6-4282-9b97-ac5773419e5c","name":"Scheutz, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-2218-5934","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31678804"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.wasman.2019.10.045","issn":["0956053X","18792456"],"issn_org":["0956053X"],"journal":"Waste Management","pages":"179-189","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Waste Management","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074189986"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","NIRAS A/S","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-600fcfec-60f3-48ef-8609-71edaa683433"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Closing the methane mass balance for an old closed Danish landfill","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-333175","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Information technologies (IT) are increasingly implemented in type 2 diabetes (T2D) treatment as a resource for remotely supported health care. However, possible pitfalls of introducing IT in health care are generally overlooked. Specifically, the effectiveness of IT to improve health care may depend on the user's readiness for health technology. Objective: We aim to investigate readiness for health technology in relation to mental well-being, sociodemographic, and disease-related characteristics among individuals with T2D. Methods: Individuals with T2D (aged ≥18 years) who had been referred to self-management education, exercise, diet counseling, smoking cessation, or alcohol counseling completed a questionnaire survey covering (1) background information, (2) the 5-item World Health Organization Well-Being Index (WHO-5), (3) receptiveness to IT use in physical activity, and (4) the Readiness and Enablement Index for Health Technology (READHY), constituted by dimensions related to self-management, social support, and eHealth literacy. Individuals were divided into profiles using cluster analysis based on their READHY scores. Outcomes included differences across profiles in mental well-being, sociodemographic, and disease-related characteristics. Results: Participants in the study were 155 individuals with T2D with a mean age of 60.2 (SD 10.7) years, 55.5% (86/155) of which were men and 44.5% (69/155) of which were women. Participants were stratified into 5 health technology readiness profiles based on the cluster analysis: Profile 1, high health technology readiness; Profile 2, medium health technology readiness; Profile 3, medium health technology readiness and high level of emotional distress; Profile 4, medium health technology readiness and low-to-medium eHealth literacy; Profile 5, low health technology readiness. No differences in sociodemographic and disease-related characteristics were observed across profiles; however, we identified 3 vulnerable subgroups of individuals: Profile 3 (21/155, 13.5%), younger individuals (mean age of 53.4 years, SD 8.9 years) with low mental well-being (mean 42.7, SD 14.7) and emotional distress (mean 1.69, SD 0.38); Profile 4 (20/155, 12.9%), older individuals (mean age 66.3 years, SD 9.0 years) with less IT use (50.0% used IT for communication) and low-to-medium eHealth literacy; and Profile 5 (36/155, 23.2%) with low mental well-being (mean 43.4, SD 20.1) and low readiness for health technology. Conclusions: Implementation of IT in health care of individuals with T2D should be based on comprehensive consideration of mental well-being, emotional distress, and readiness for health technology rather than sociodemographic and disease-related characteristics to identify the individuals in need of social support, self-management education, and extensive IT support. A one-size-fits-all approach to IT implementation in health care will potentially increase the risk of treatment failure among the most vulnerable individuals.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thorsen, Ida Kær","Rossen, Sine","Glümer, Charlotte","Midtgaard, Julie","Ried-Larsen, Mathias","Kayser, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543035"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Delivery of healthcare","Diabetes mellitus","Exercise","Healthcare Disparities","Mental health","Psychological distress","Socioeconomic Factors","Telemedicine","Type 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"health technology readiness profiles among danish individuals with type 000000000002 diabetes cross sectional study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/21195","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-543035","identifier":[{"id":"85091054850","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32930669","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7525399","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-faa63311-d3ff-4487-aa43-a7ea1aea3f6e"],"keyword":["Delivery of healthcare","Diabetes mellitus","Exercise","Healthcare disparities","Mental health","Psychological distress","Readiness for health technology","Socioeconomic factors","Telemedicine","Type 2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D02B73342EAE4DAECF3D4DB347797070"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/21195","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250375094/Health_Technology_Readiness_Profiles_Among_Danish_Individuals_With_Type_2_Diabetes.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Copenhagen Centre for Cancer and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Center for Diabetes, Municipality of Copenhagen","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Ida Kær","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","name":"Thorsen, Ida Kær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sine","key":"rossenpau","last":"Rossen","name":"Rossen, Sine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"glümerpau","last":"Glümer","name":"Glümer, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Julie","key":"midtgaardpau","last":"Midtgaard","locid":"9f64fbe5-60e9-49c3-bb06-7ec73d018a77","name":"Midtgaard, Julie","orcid":"0000-0003-2381-2127","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mathias","key":"riedlarsenpau","last":"Ried-Larsen","name":"Ried-Larsen, Mathias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"kayserpau","last":"Kayser","locid":"94c6679f-d8da-419f-9bd0-186a97295257","name":"Kayser, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-0909-4088","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32930669"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/21195","issn":["14388871","14394456"],"issn_org":["14394456"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","paperid":"e21195","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85091054850"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","copenhagen centre for cancer and health"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-faa63311-d3ff-4487-aa43-a7ea1aea3f6e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Health technology readiness profiles among danish individuals with type 2 diabetes : Cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-543035","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In March 2020, the World Health Organization elevated the coronavirus disease (COVID-19) epidemic to a pandemic and called for urgent and aggressive action worldwide. Public health experts have communicated clear and emphatic strategies to prevent the spread of COVID-19. Hygiene rules and social distancing practices have been implemented by entire populations, including 'stay-at-home' orders in many countries. The long-term health and economic consequences of the COVID-19 pandemic are not yet known. MAIN TEXT: During this time of crisis, some chiropractors made claims on social media that chiropractic treatment can prevent or impact COVID-19. The rationale for these claims is that spinal manipulation can impact the nervous system and thus improve immunity. These beliefs often stem from nineteenth-century chiropractic concepts. We are aware of no clinically relevant scientific evidence to support such statements. We explored the internet and social media to collect examples of misinformation from Europe, North America, Australia and New Zealand regarding the impact of chiropractic treatment on immune function. We discuss the potential harm resulting from these claims and explore the role of chiropractors, teaching institutions, accrediting agencies, and legislative bodies. CONCLUSIONS: Members of the chiropractic profession share a collective responsibility to act in the best interests of patients and public health. We hope that all chiropractic stakeholders will view the COVID-19 pandemic as a call to action to eliminate the unethical and potentially dangerous claims made by chiropractors who practise outside the boundaries of scientific evidence.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Axén, Iben","Bergström, Cecilia","Bronson, Marc","Côté, Pierre","Nim, Casper","Goncalves, Guillaume","Hébert, Jeffrey J","Hertel, Joakim Axel","Innes, Stanley","Larsen, Ole Kristoffer","Meyer, Anne-Laure","O'Neill, Søren","Perle, Stephen M","Weber, Kenneth A","Young, Kenneth J","Leboeuf-Yde, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586495"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Canada","Cyprus","France","Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institut Franco Européen de Chiropraxie","Karolinska Institute","Murdoch University","NEMUS Tønsberg Helseklinikk","Rutgers University–New Brunswick","Stanford University","Umeå University","University of Bridgeport","University of Central Lancashire - Cyprus","University of Ontario Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Chiropractors","Covid 19","Debate","Infodemic","Spinal manipulation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Evidence Based Chiropractic Network"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"misinformation chiropractic and the covid 000000000019 pandemic","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12998-020-00353-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586495","identifier":[{"id":"85096190413","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33208144","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7672412","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-2e769dfc-1700-406d-a118-850e0481955e"],"keyword":["Chiropractors","Covid-19","Debate","Infodemic","Professional traditionalism","Spinal manipulation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-12E7A59D2A3983C637FE8176934D0F27"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/175208018/s12998_020_00353_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12998-020-00353-2","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institute","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"umeå university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Umeå University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Evidence Based Chiropractic Network"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ca","key":"university of ontario institute of technology","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Ontario Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Sygehus Lillebælt, Forskningsenhed for Rygmedicin (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"fr","key":"institut franco européen de chiropraxie","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institut Franco Européen de Chiropraxie","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"us","key":"rutgers university new brunswick","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Rutgers University–New Brunswick","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"au","key":"murdoch university","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Murdoch University","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"no","key":"nemus tønsberg helseklinikk","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NEMUS Tønsberg Helseklinikk","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"us","key":"university of bridgeport","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Bridgeport","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"us","key":"stanford university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Stanford University","used":1},{"affno":"12","country":"cy","key":"university of central lancashire cyprus","loc":["Cyprus","Europe, EU"],"name":"University of Central Lancashire - Cyprus","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben","key":"axénpau","last":"Axén","name":"Axén, Iben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Cecilia","key":"bergströmpau","last":"Bergström","name":"Bergström, Cecilia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Marc","key":"bronsonpau","last":"Bronson","name":"Bronson, Marc","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierre","key":"côtépau","last":"Côté","name":"Côté, Pierre","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Casper Glissmann","key":"nimpau","last":"Nim","locid":"35229b19-b2da-4765-a846-e8e726738e9d","name":"Nim, Casper","name_org":"Nim, Casper Glissmann","orcid":"0000-0001-5845-2622","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Guillaume","key":"goncalvespau","last":"Goncalves","name":"Goncalves, Guillaume","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeffrey J","key":"hébertpau","last":"Hébert","name":"Hébert, Jeffrey J","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Joakim Axel","key":"hertelpau","last":"Hertel","name":"Hertel, Joakim Axel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Stanley","key":"innespau","last":"Innes","name":"Innes, Stanley","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Kristoffer","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"751989a4-f438-4a9a-b595-552cb6a6ed45","name":"Larsen, Ole Kristoffer","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Laure","key":"meyerpau","last":"Meyer","name":"Meyer, Anne-Laure","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"oneillpau","last":"O'Neill","locid":"1c5c1a7a-8e16-41c8-887f-d489cc82a998","name":"O'Neill, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-8064-7001","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Stephen M","key":"perlepau","last":"Perle","name":"Perle, Stephen M","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth A","key":"weberpau","last":"Weber","name":"Weber, Kenneth A","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"12","corresponding":null,"first":"Kenneth J","key":"youngpau","last":"Young","name":"Young, Kenneth J","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"leboeufydepau","last":"Leboeuf-Yde","locid":"21c15248-54d2-4267-a78f-ef73fc5a76a0","name":"Leboeuf-Yde, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1552-7772","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33208144"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12998-020-00353-2","issn":["2045709X"],"journal":"Chiropractic & Manual Therapies","paperid":"65","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Chiropractic & Manual Therapies","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85096190413"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2e769dfc-1700-406d-a118-850e0481955e"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Misinformation, chiropractic, and the COVID-19 pandemic","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-586495","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Can we color in the Altmetric donut by using a social media echo chamber, and does that manipulation lead to actual engagement with the work? Recently, a university professor told us every time she published she would tweet and re-tweet the DOI of her publication. To inflate her own Altmetric score she had created a series of artificial social media profiles “engaging” with her work. This peaked our curiosity and so we made a small-scale experiment. We encouraged our colleagues and the conference participants at LIBER 2019 to tweet and re-tweet the DOI of a letter to the editor describing our experiment published in LIBER Quarterly. The interest in our experiment spiraled out beyond our usual network. For every tweet we increased our score. But no matter how much we tried we did not manage to make it spread to other SoMe platforms than twitter and our donut has remained blue (the color of tweets). We tried again and again to obtain scores from Youtube, Google+, various blogs, but had no success. Our overall theoretical framework for this work is Roger’s diffusion of innovations theory. We will use this theory to explain both the success (many tweets) and the failures (on other platforms) of our experiment. Our poster is richly illustrated with maps how the DOI was tweeted and retweeted and examples of SoMe platforms where we were less successful and all of it set within the framework of our theoretical approach.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dorch, Bertil","Deutz, Daniella Bayle","Wien, Charlotte","Drongstrup, Dorte","Vlachos, Evgenios","Larsen, Asger Væring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760103"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"singing the donut blues creating a some echo chamber to boost the scores on altmetric","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-760103","ids":["ku-8a4138c0-da8f-4013-a430-0530f3c89b3c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6CE152F8614309CE048237279E1F49EF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, DARK"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Bertil F.","key":"dorchpau","last":"Dorch","locid":"c058289c-b917-464f-838c-4b8d9e1a69f7","name":"Dorch, Bertil","name_org":"Dorch, Bertil F.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniella Bayle","key":"deutzpau","last":"Deutz","name":"Deutz, Daniella Bayle","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"wienpau","last":"Wien","name":"Wien, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorte","key":"drongstruppau","last":"Drongstrup","name":"Drongstrup, Dorte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Evgenios","key":"vlachospau","last":"Vlachos","name":"Vlachos, Evgenios","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Asger Væring","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3465b5e-1b9d-4c08-9fc3-9a9dfa287b40","name":"Larsen, Asger Væring","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-2637","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-8a4138c0-da8f-4013-a430-0530f3c89b3c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Singing the donut blues: Creating a SoMe echo chamber to boost the scores on Altmetric","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-760103","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: To measure the sustainable improvements in the work environment, a flexible and highly responsive tool is needed that will give important focus to the implementation process. A digital checklist was developed, in collaboration with key stakeholders, to document the implementation of changes in eldercare sector workplaces. Objective: This paper describes the study protocol of a dissemination study that aims to examine when, why and how the digital checklist is spread to the Danish eldercare sector following a national campaign targeting particularly nursing homes and home care. Methods: This prospective observational study will use quantitative data from; Google Analytics and describing use of the checklist as documented website engagement, a survey among members in the largest union in the sector, information from a Central Business Register and monitoring of campaign activities. The evaluation will be guided by the five elements of the RE-AIM framework; Reach, Effectiveness, Adoption, Implementation, and Maintenance. Results: The study was approved in June 2016 and began in October 2018. The campaign that is the foundation for the evaluation began in 2017 and ended in 2018. However, the webpage where we collect data is still running. Results are expected in late 2019. Conclusions: This protocol provides a working example of how to evaluate dissemination of a checklist to improve implementation of work environment initiatives in the eldercare sector in Denmark. To our knowledge, the implementation in a national-wide Danish work environment has not been previously undertaken. Given that the checklist is sector-specific for work environment initiatives, and developed through systematic collaboration between research and practice, it is likely to have high utility and impact, however the proposed evaluation will determine this. This study will advance dissemination research and in particular the evaluation of the impact of these types of studies. Finally, this study advances the field through digital tools that can be used for evaluation of dissemination efforts (e.g. google analytics associated with website) in the context of a rigorous research design activity.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","Højberg, Helene","Larsen, Anne Konring","Munch, Pernille Kold","Osborne, Richard","Kwak, Lydia","Jensen, Irene","Linnan, Laura","Jørgensen, Marie Birk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-780455"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Institute of Environmental Medicine (IMM), Karolinska Institute, Stockholm, Sweden.","Institute of Environmental Medicine, Karolinska Institute, Stockholm, Sweden.","Swinburne University of Technology","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill"],"keyword":["IkkepåBFI listen","Internationalartikel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Health Municipally of Copenhagen, Denmark."]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation and dissemination of a checklist to improve implementation of work environment initiatives in the eldercare sector protocol for a prospective observational study","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/16039","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-780455","identifier":[{"id":"85096203000","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["nfa-42fca8cf-2e41-437c-98f9-ced18823c206"],"keyword":["IkkepåBFI-listen","Internationalartikel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8945909F1C9028D3EFF6EEEEB4188B4E"],"oa_link":