}
{"abstract":"In this work, we developed a novel approach combining bioinformatics, testing of functionality and bottom-up proteomics to obtain peptide emulsifiers from potato side-streams. This is a significant advancement in the process to obtain emulsifier peptides and it is applicable to any type of protein. Our results indicated that structure at the interface is the major determining factor of the emulsifying activity of peptide emulsifiers. Fish oil-in-water emulsions with high physical stability were stabilized with peptides to be predicted to have facial amphiphilicity: (i) peptides with predominantly α-helix conformation at the interface and having 18–29 amino acids, and (ii) peptides with predominantly β-strand conformation at the interface and having 13–15 amino acids. In addition, high physically stable emulsions were obtained with peptides that were predicted to have axial hydrophobic/hydrophilic regions. Peptides containing the sequence FCLKVGV showed high in vitro antioxidant activity and led to emulsions with high oxidative stability. Peptide-level proteomics data and sequence analysis revealed the feasibility to obtain the potent emulsifier peptides found in this study (e.g. γ-1) by trypsin-based hydrolysis of different side streams in the potato industry.","author_count":10,"contributors":["García Moreno, Pedro Jesús","Gregersen Echers, Simon","Nedamani, Elham","Olsen, Tobias Hegelund","Marcatili, Paolo","Overgaard, Michael Toft","Andersen, Mogens Larsen","Hansen, Egon Bech","Jacobsen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S03-098.64-000572"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["García Moreno, Pedro Jesús"],"country":["Spain"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Granada"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of emulsifier potato peptides by bioinformatics application to omega 000000000003 delivery emulsions and release from potato industry side streams","src":["aau","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-57229-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.64-000572","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6971092","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85078291287","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31959786","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-0adff025-3a0b-48c2-a1da-dbc5ea5c04bf","dtu-b771ace5-8d23-46c1-a472-bf128bb9e4da","ku-e243acf3-4582-4a55-aea1-082898bcdb16"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-E465B004BFCB0E379FACD61C18E939B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/204814937/s41598_019_57229_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/235856345/Identification_of_emulsifier_potato_peptides_by_bioinformatics.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/400806644/s41598_019_57229_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-019-57229-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of