{"abstract":"Food allergy affects a small but significant number of children and adults. Food allergy is responsible for considerable morbidity and is the commonest cause of anaphylaxis in children. One of the aims of the European Union funded \"Integrated Approaches to Food Allergen and Allergy Risk Management\" (iFAAM) project was to improve our understanding of the best way to prevent the development of food allergy. Groups within the project worked on integrating the current prevention evidence base as well as generating new data to move our understanding forward. This paper from the iFAAM project is a unique addition to the literature on this topic as it not only outlines the recently published randomised controlled trials (as have previous reviews) but it also summarises two iFAAM-associated project workshops. These workshops focused on how we may be able to use dietary strategies in early life to prevent the development of food allergy and summarises the range of opinions amongst experts in this controversial area.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Roberts, G.","Grimshaw, K.","Beyer, K. Kirsten","Boyle, R.","Lack, G.","Austin, M.","Garcia-Larsen, V.","Grabenhenrich, L.","Halken, S.","Keil, T.","Madsen, Charlotte Bernhard","Regent, L.","Schnadt, S.","Szajewska, H.","van Ree, R.","Mills, E N C"],"cuid":["S02-098.76-033604"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Roberts, G.","Roberts, Graham"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Poland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anaphylaxis UK","Charité - University Medicine Berlin","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Deutscher Allergie‐ und Asthmabund","German Allergy and Asthma Association","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Imperial College London","Johns Hopkins Bloomberg School of Public Health","Johns Hopkins University","Medical University of Warsaw","St. Mary's Hospital","The Anaphylaxis Campaign","University Hospital Southampton NHS Foundation Trust","University of Amsterdam","University of Manchester","University of Southampton"],"keyword":["Diet","Food allergy","Nutrition","Prevention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can dietary strategies in early life prevent childhood food allergy a report from two ifaam workshops","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/196062838/Roberts_2019_psot_print_Can_dietary_strategies_in_early_life_prevent_childhood_food_allergy_A_report_from_two_iFAAM_workshops_002_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This report was generated as part of the EU iFAAM project: Integrated Approaches to Food Allergen and Allergy Risk Management (Grant Agreement No. 312147) and an iFAAM workshop held at the UK Food Standards Agency. We would like to acknowledge the assistance of the UK Food Standards Agency in hosting the workshop. Liz Kendall and Erin Oliver from the Food Standards Agency and Rachel Elsom from Public Health England were observers at the workshop. We would also like to acknowledge the support of ILSI in arranging the second workshop."],"id":"S02-098.76-033604","identifier":[{"id":"85075459645","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31631412","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-2e3b9aa1-9410-4d3f-b284-785d2c980bc6","sdu-2a0f17e4-9a13-4513-aae7-8d0962a8ed9a"],"keyword":["diet","food allergy","nutrition","prevention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-