},{"affno":"4","first":"Charlotte","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","name":"Kjærgaard, Charlotte","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Brian H.","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"64eabb36-abe3-4db4-82a3-10ca891e1872","name":"Jacobsen, Brian H.","orcid":"0000-0002-0025-4399","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Esben","key":"aukenpau","last":"Auken","name":"Auken, Esben","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anker Lajer","key":"højbergpau","last":"Højberg","name":"Højberg, Anker Lajer","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Stefan","key":"schaperpau","last":"Schaper","name":"Schaper, Stefan","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"2020/11","pages":"38","publisher":"Danmarks og Grønlands Geologiske Undersøgelse","repno":"Danmarks og Grønlands Geologiske Undersøgelse Rapport, 2020/11","series":"Danmarks og Grønlands Geologiske Undersøgelse Rapport","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-50f67f0b-b6ed-4427-a5fa-4189980e3a89"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Danish review on advances in assessing : N retention in the subsurface in relation to future targeted N-regulation of agriculture","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-441777","year":"2019","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Through a focus on conflicts, the aim of this paper is to discuss theoretical challenges in conceptualizing the dialectic relationship between historical conditions and situated interplay in concrete everyday practice. We argue that the concept of conflict can help us move beyond the tendency within psychology to regard history and situated practice, structure and activity, and so-called micro and macro processes apart – and to regard social life as unambiguous or as governed through hegemony. A situated study about conflictuality illustrates both societal conflicts about the school and how children in school deal with quite unequal conditions when it comes to handling the conflictuality of school life. Analyses of coordination and conflicts between the parties (children, parents, teachers, psychologists, etc.) elucidate the connections between intersubjective means of making things work in everyday practice, and historical struggles relating to the school as a societal institution. To understand processes of reproducing and transgressing inequality in school, we therefore need concepts that enables us to understand these processes as both historically AND as politicalprocesses driven by intersubjectivity related to specific possibilities and dilemmas – what we call politics of everyday life. From a social practice perspective we discuss how to grasp the ways persons constitute the conditions for the acting of each other in a situated interplay in which, together, they deal with common historical problems.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Højholt, Charlotte","Røn Larsen, Maja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-563770"],"event":{"end":"2019-08-23","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2019-08-19","title":"18th Conference of the International Society for Theoretical Psychology: Measured Lives - Theoretical Psychology in an Era of Acceleration","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"situated inequality and politics of everyday life","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-563770","ids":["ruc-742d66c6-5063-4c1b-b8d0-51ee76961b1d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-82A63D7A000A8B764A2EFA6E1D560C76"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-742d66c6-5063-4c1b-b8d0-51ee76961b1d"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Situated Inequality and Politics of Everyday Life","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-563770","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
