{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Røn Larsen, Maja","Højholt, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-562117"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"konflikter om børns skoleliv et forskningsprojekt på tværs","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-562117","ids":["ruc-5bfba096-e05e-44f0-a14e-7f88a9453a57"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1E931DE89EC22FEE88CDF18289D43392"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, Subject, Technology and Social Practice","Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology, The Danish Centre for Research in Early Childhood Education and Care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Maja","key":"rønlarsenpau","last":"Røn Larsen","locid":"43249523-b160-4888-8421-4a606d27561a","name":"Røn Larsen, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1413-6059","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"højholtpau","last":"Højholt","locid":"e1ae7eb0-773c-4cc6-84ac-4868fa79025a","name":"Højholt, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0601-0456","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["0906690X","19030002"],"issn_org":["19030002"],"issue":"2","journal":"Pædagogisk Psykologisk Tidsskrift","pages":"3-13","status":"p","title":"Pædagogisk Psykologisk Tidsskrift","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-5bfba096-e05e-44f0-a14e-7f88a9453a57"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Konflikter om børns skoleliv : et forskningsprojekt på tværs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-562117","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Is it possible to manipulate the Altmetric score by using a social media echo chamber? Recently we came across something that triggered our curiosity. A university professor told us that she had created a series of social media profiles to inflate her Altmetric scores. Whenever publishing she herself would tweet and re-tweet the DOI of the publication and in this way enhance her own Altmetric performance. Following this, we made a small scale experiment. We encouraged our colleagues to tweet and re-tweet the DOI of a publication and found to our surprise that interest in this article spiraled out beyond our usual network, making a relatively inferior piece of work skyrocket towards the top 5% of all research outputs scored by Altmetric. To examine the pliability of altmetric scores in a structured way, we will write an editorial in a scientific journal encouraging readers to share the DOI of the editorial on various social media platforms. We will track the effect of this engineered social engagement on the Altmetric donut over time. We will then use this altmetric engagement pattern as a baseline for our next experiment, examining the effect of a social media echo chamber. We will create a new DOI with no text behind it on Zenodo and a series of artificial profiles mimicking the exact patterns identified in the first experiment. We will see to what extent we can attain equal or even higher altmetric scores. Finally, we will track whether the DOI has had actual social engagement or has only been mentioned within our echo chamber.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Deutz, Daniella Bayle","Vlachos, Evgenios","Drongstrup, Dorte","Larsen, Asger Væring","Dorch, Bertil F.","Wien, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-603601"],"event":{"end":"2019-10-10","place":"Stirling, gb","start":"2019-10-09","title":"6:AM Altmetrics Conference","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Deutz, Daniella Bayle"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coloring in the altmetric donut","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154884015/Coloring_in_the_Donut_9_October_2019_DB_Deutz.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-603601","ids":["sdu-6a5da7ad-73eb-4830-815e-28dc2e133238"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-249F901B2E240FBF8D41634EF0DE7CD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/154884015/Coloring_in_the_Donut_9_October_2019_DB_Deutz.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Central Administration, The University Library of Southern Denmark, Forsknings- og analyseafdeling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniella Bayle","key":"deutzpau","last":"Deutz","locid":"0cb11e5a-a77e-4373-9b4d-1c30e830aaad","name":"Deutz, Daniella Bayle","orcid":"0000-0001-7230-6031","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Evgenios","key":"vlachospau","last":"Vlachos","locid":"498d5f74-7d1b-4ec7-86fa-42df0ee32146","name":"Vlachos, Evgenios","orcid":"0000-0001-8235-0423","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"drongstruppau","last":"Drongstrup","locid":"107fd236-3b34-45ab-8fa8-c46521f9390a","name":"Drongstrup, Dorte","orcid":"0000-0002-2541-3819","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Væring","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fd7856d4-9391-4ae2-9349-f9181309b577","name":"Larsen, Asger Væring","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-2637","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bertil F.","key":"dorchpau","last":"Dorch","locid":"da82eabd-45cb-46bf-b322-b68bb5f0294d","name":"Dorch, Bertil F.","orcid":"0000-0003-2594-6778","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"wienpau","last":"Wien","locid":"277f8354-05c4-44a4-b3b9-df9d557c9028","name":"Wien, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-3257-2084","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6a5da7ad-73eb-4830-815e-28dc2e133238"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Coloring in the Altmetric Donut","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-603601","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A virus (IAV) is a highly contagious pathogen in pigs. Swine IAV (swIAV) infection causes respiratory disease and is thereby a challenge for animal health, animal welfare and the production economy. In Europe, the most widespread strategy for controlling swIAV is implementation of sow vaccination programs, to secure delivery of protective maternally derived antibodies (MDAs) to the newborn piglets. In this study we report a unique case, where a persistently swIAV (A/sw/Denmark/P5U4/2016(H1N1)) infected herd experienced an acute outbreak with a new swIAV subtype (A/sw/Denmark/HB4280U1/2017(H1N2)) and subsequently decided to implement a mass sow vaccination program. Clinical registrations, nasal swabs and blood samples were collected from four different batches of pigs before and after vaccination. Virus isolation, sequencing of the virus strain and hemagglutinin inhibition (HI) tests were performed on samples collected before and during the outbreak and after implementation of mass sow vaccination. After implementation of the sow mass vaccination, the time of infection was delayed and the viral load significantly decreased. An increased number of pigs, however, tested positive at two consecutive sampling times indicating prolonged shedding. In addition, a significantly smaller proportion of the 10–12 weeks old pigs were seropositive by the end of the study, indicating an impaired induction of antibodies against swIAV in the presence of MDAs. Sequencing of the herd strains revealed major differences in the hemagglutinin gene of the strain isolated before- and during the acute outbreak despite that, the two strains belonged to the same HA lineage. The HI tests confirmed a limited degree of cross-reaction between the two strains. Furthermore, the sequencing results of the hemagglutinin gene obtained before and after implementation of mass sow vaccination revealed an increased substitution rate and an increase in positively selected sites in the globular head of the hemagglutinin after vaccination.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Larsen, Inge","Krog, Jesper Schak","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S02-086.36-033003"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Ryt-Hansen, Pia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acute influenza a virus outbreak in an enzootic infected sow herd impact on viral dynamics genetic and antigenic variability and effect of maternally derived antibodies and vaccination","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0224854","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.36-033003","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6855628","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85075070759","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31725751","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-130f0baf-9d8a-4a31-aa17-381c44cb7fd3","ku-deb9806a-1871-4879-aa44-dc057e0a7674"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F0D237CA977CF88FA3CA5141197A913C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0224854","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/230847632/journal.pone.0224854.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/198178784/in_an_enzootic_infected_sow_herd_Impact_on_viral_dynamics_genetic_and_antigenic_variability_and_effect_of_maternally_derived_antibodies_and_vaccination.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Production, Nutrition and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pia","key":"rythansenpiapau","last":"Ryt-Hansen","locid":"14d7fe91-822b-4f95-a07c-9479df41d8c5","name":"Ryt-Hansen, Pia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Gorm","key":"pedersenandersgormpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bb3513aa-fb20-46ef-ba14-9c150c929cf1","name":"Pedersen, Anders Gorm","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-8965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Inge","key":"larseningepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"82b09bf9-73d5-4c71-a3c1-01e66b0e9ebe","name":"Larsen, Inge","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-2241","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogjesperschakpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensencharlottesonnepau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31725751"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0224854","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"11","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0224854","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075070759"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-130f0baf-9d8a-4a31-aa17-381c44cb7fd3","ku-deb9806a-1871-4879-aa44-dc057e0a7674"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Acute Influenza A virus outbreak in an enzootic infected sow herd: Impact on viral dynamics, genetic and antigenic variability and effect of maternally derived antibodies and vaccination","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.36-033003","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: MED13L-related intellectual disability is characterized by moderate intellectual disability (ID), speech impairment, and dysmorphic facial features. We present 8 patients with MED13L-related intellectual disability and review the literature for phenotypical and genetic aspects of previously described patients. MATERIALS AND METHODS: In the search for genetic aberrations in individuals with ID, two of the patients were identified by chromosomal microarray analysis, and five by exome sequencing. One of the individuals, suspected of MED13L-related intellectual disability, based on clinical features, was identified by Sanger sequencing. RESULTS: All 8 individuals had de novo MED13L aberrations, including two intragenic microdeletions, two frameshift, three nonsense variants, and one missense variant. Phenotypically, they all had intellectual disability, speech and motor delay, and features of the mouth (open mouth appearance, macroglossia, and/or macrostomia). Two individuals were diagnosed with autism, and one had autistic features. One had complex congenital heart defect, and one had persistent foramen ovale. The literature was reviewed with respect to clinical and dysmorphic features, and genetic aberrations. CONCLUSIONS: Even if most clinical features of MED13L-related intellectual disability are rather non-specific, the syndrome may be suspected in some individuals based on the association of developmental delay, speech impairment, bulbous nasal tip, and macroglossia, macrostomia, or open mouth appearance.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Tørring, Pernille Mathiesen","Larsen, Martin Jakob","Brasch-Andersen, Charlotte","Krogh, Lotte Nylandsted","Kibæk, Maria","Laulund, Lone","Illum, Niels","Dunkhase-Heinl, Ulrike","Wiesener, Antje","Popp, Bernt","Marangi, Giuseppe","Hjortshøj, Tina Duelund","Ek, Jakob","Vogel, Ida","Becher, Naja","Roos, Laura","Zollino, Marcella","Fagerberg, Christina Ringmann"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-023485"],"filters":{"