"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael","key":"borrepau","last":"Borre","locid":"f0a95cf0-1ff2-4308-991f-749123c14ba5","name":"Borre, Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Klaus","key":"brassopau","last":"Brasso","locid":"59b1e9f4-7fb8-4172-a372-7c1388821f78","name":"Brasso, Klaus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Signe Benzon","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Signe Benzon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1 6","first":"Susanne Oksbjerg","key":"daltonpau","last":"Dalton","locid":"84d10468-fe5d-4cc7-952f-1d89d961390f","name":"Dalton, Susanne Oksbjerg","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"3cb2ae19-c1b9-4dad-9928-adbd1c51b4b7","name":"Nørgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5891","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anton","key":"pottegårdpau","last":"Pottegård","locid":"addfc2c1-4fc9-44cd-8087-bce3bc986652","name":"Pottegård, Anton","orcid":"0000-0001-9314-5679","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"hallaspau","last":"Hallas","locid":"1fc2d4e1-080d-4c53-bd96-63186af28ae9","name":"Hallas, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-8097-8708","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Toft","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"4d49d93a-4913-4223-ba59-272e717a845d","name":"Sørensen, Henrik Toft","orcid":"0000-0003-4299-7040","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"e0c48e7a-dd83-4611-a29d-82dbb474b355","name":"Friis, Søren","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30831581"],"pub":{"doi":"10.7326/m17-3085","issn":["00034819","0570183X"],"issn_org":["00034819"],"issue":"7","journal":"Annals of Internal Medicine","pages":"443-452","publisher":"American College of Physicians","status":"p","title":"Annals of Internal Medicine","volume":"170"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85063916988"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-709c1523-6e62-49fc-bde9-41149ef90330","ku-555fe786-f103-4e98-b978-4f038e7118db","sdu-48d7fefa-ee56-41a5-8cf6-e6b163a184f0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Use of Low-Dose Aspirin and Mortality After Prostate Cancer Diagnosis : A Nationwide Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.91-020915","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Subsurface flow wetlands with a woodchip-based biofilter are known to act as effective measures in mitigating site-specific nutrient losses in agricultural drainage. To optimize operation, the combined effect of water temperature, hydraulic residence time (HRT), and filter design is fundamental. This 2-yr study evaluated a combination of three flow designs and two woodchips mixtures at a test facility receiving agricultural drainage discharge from a 78-ha catchment. The biofilter test facility consisted of six independent parallel-constructed wetlands (CW1-CW6), with two types of filter mixtures and three different hydraulic designs (horizontal, vertical upward, and vertical downward flow). Horizontal CWs performed best with an annual removal of total N (TN) amounting to 53 to 54% of the load, corresponding to a daily removal of 2.16 to 2.32 g N m-3 d-1. Removal by the vertical CWs amounted to 38 to 60% of the TN load or 1.19 to 2.31 g N m-3 d-1. Despite low temperatures and HRT down to 3 h, all CWs functioned well in winter with 20 to 30% N removal. In contrast, during summer when the hydraulic load was low and HRT was up to >96 h, N removal was ∼100%, and the reduction sequence proceeded with sulfate reduction and formation of H2S. Statistical analysis and model development revealed that the percentage removal of both TN and nitrate N was mostly dependent on water temperature and HRT, explaining 81.7 to 91.1 and 83.5 to 89.5% of the variation, respectively.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hoffmann, Carl Christian","Larsen, Søren Erik","Kjærgaard, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-244647"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hoffmann, Carl Christian"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nitrogen removal in woodchip based biofilters of variable designs treating agricultural drainage discharges","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2134/jeq2018.12.0442","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-244647","identifier":[{"id":"85074480045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c9dc4896-cb05-4b11-8368-08a26a13cf3d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F39B00649836ECF312212E842B8673DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2134/jeq2018.12.0442","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/194188329/jeq2018.12.0442.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Catchment Science and Environmental Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl Christian","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","locid":"353a0760-7b7a-4348-9f47-7df140234554","name":"Hoffmann, Carl Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-9162","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"kjaergaardpau","last":"Kjaergaard","locid":"b3be00f6-c690-4933-946a-9ab606926cdd","name":"Kjærgaard, Charlotte","name_org":"Kjaergaard, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2134/jeq2018.12.0442","issn":["00472425","15372537"],"issn_org":["00472425"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Environmental Quality","pages":"1881-1889","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Environmental Quality","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074480045"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c9dc4896-cb05-4b11-8368-08a26a13cf3d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Nitrogen removal in woodchip-based biofilters of variable designs treating agricultural drainage discharges","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-244647","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"An unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV)-mounted thermal infrared (TIR) camera’s ability to delineate landfill gas (LFG) emission hotspots was evaluated in a field test at two Danish landfills (Hedeland landfill and Audebo landfill). At both sites, a test area of 100 m2 was established and divided into about 100 measuring points. The relationship between LFG emissions and soil surface temperatures were investigated through four to five measuring campaigns, in order to cover different atmospheric conditions along with increasing, decreasing and stable barometric pressure. For each measuring campaign, a TIR image of the test area was obtained followed by the measurement of methane (CH4) and carbon dioxide (CO2) emissions at each measuring point, using a static flux chamber. At the same time, soil temperatures measured on the surface, at 5 cm and 10 cm depths, were registered. At the Hedeland landfill, no relationship was found between LFG emissions and surface temperatures. In addition, CH4 emissions were very limited, on average 0.92–4.52 g CH4 m−2 d−1, and only measureable on the two days with decreasing barometric pressure. TIR images from Hedeland did not show any significant temperature differences in the test area. At the Audebo landfill, an area with slightly higher surface temperatures was found in the TIR images, and the same pattern with slightly higher temperatures was found at a depth of 10 cm. The main LFG emissions were found in the area with the higher surface temperatures. LFG emissions at Audebo were influenced significantly by changes in barometric pressure, and the average CH4 emissions varied between 111 g m−2 d−1 and 314 g m−2 d−1, depending on whether the barometric pressure gradient had increased or decreased, respectively. The temperature differences observed in the TIR images from both landfills were limited to between 0.7 °C and 1.2 °C. The minimum observable CH4 emission for the TIR camera to identify an emission hotspot was 150 g CH4 m−2 d−1 from an area of more than 1 m2.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Fjelsted, Lotte","Christensen, A. G.","Larsen, J. E.","Kjeldsen, Peter","Scheutz, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-314316"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Fjelsted, Lotte"],"keyword":["Drone","IR","Landfill gas","Remote sensing","Surface flux","UAS"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NIRA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NIRA","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of a landfill methane emission screening method using an unmanned aerial vehicle mounted thermal infrared camera a field study","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/148570839/Revised_version_of_Paper_on_thermography_of_LFG_emissions_Clean.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-314316","identifier":[{"id":"85047467429","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29853253","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-20cb36bf-d43e-433e-9636-2246183a5052"],"keyword":["Drone","IR","Landfill gas","Remote sensing","Surface flux","UAS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6457B4759A5A34F69A3E931F9E7F65AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/148570839/Revised_version_of_Paper_on_thermography_of_LFG_emissions_Clean.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Residual Resource Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"niras","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NIRA","l3nl":"NIRAS A/S","l3nn":"NIRAS","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NIRAS","namevar":["NIRAS A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NIRA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte","key":"fjelstedpau","last":"Fjelsted","locid":"66fc8252-3482-4d08-99ce-6f5ee964650f","name":"Fjelsted, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0002-2878-798X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"A. G.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, A. G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J. E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, J. E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"49899b92-45e7-485d-88cb-faf95e4ac0d7","name":"Kjeldsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2738-9960","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"scheutzpau","last":"Scheutz","locid":"48fe2850-fdc6-4282-9b97-ac5773419e5c","name":"Scheutz, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-2218-5934","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29853253"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.wasman.2018.05.031","issn":["0956053X","18792456"],"issn_org":["0956053X"],"journal":"Waste Management","pages":"893-904","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Waste Management","volume":"87"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047467429"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","NIRAS A/S","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-20cb36bf-d43e-433e-9636-2246183a5052"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Assessment of a landfill methane emission screening method using an unmanned aerial vehicle mounted thermal infrared camera – A field study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-314316","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"An S-methylated analogue of tropodithietic acid (TDA, 1), methyl troposulfenin (2), was isolated from the marine alphaproteobacterium Phaeobacter inhibens. The structure was elucidated by NMR and HRMS. Its inhibitory effect against the fish pathogen Vibrio anguillarum was 4-fold to 100-fold lower than that of the known antibacterial compound TDA. Methyl troposulfenin lacks the acidic proton of TDA, indicating that the methylation turns the potent antibacterial TDA into an inactive compound, and thereby, this analysis supports the proposed mode of action of TDA.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Phippen, Christopher","Jørgensen, Cecilie M.","Bentzon-Tilia, Mikkel","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","Gram, Lone","Sonnenschein, Eva C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350594"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sonnenschein, Eva C."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"isolation of methyl troposulfenin from phaeobacter inhibens","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/183857168/Phippen_MeTDA_Stucture_paper_resubmission_190404.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350594","identifier":[{"id":"30978024","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85066127058","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9a5e5a8d-cf30-471c-9ba6-501744c733f6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E2C81A808822F1884C3FE242C0AB38A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/183857168/Phippen_MeTDA_Stucture_paper_resubmission_190404.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"