["09069577"],"newspaper":"Sundhedsplejersken","status":"p","title":"Sundhedsplejersken"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c603b327-df08-41b5-b8d4-cfb888fc89d4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Sociale medier og trivsel i ungdomslivet : Hvordan kan sundhedsplejersker gå i dialog med børn og unge om deres online hverdagsliv?","type":"Newspaper Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107523","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Most towns and places have their own character and identity, and the architectural heritage is often a carrier of this identity in local communities. Many of these are today challenged by changes in demography and production, where the original buildings are abandoned in order to meet new needs within agriculture, industry and housing (Hansen 2013). The result is that the heritage buildings are in decay and demolished, while new more functional buildings are being built, leading to a loss of history and cultural heritage. A solution to this problem could be to promote adaptive reuse of the historic buildings, which will be both more sustainable and preserve a part of the place identity and history. This is both difficult and costly compared with building new, and it can seem more rational to demolish them and build new according to modern and industrialized construction methods. The Aarhus School of Architecture entered into a partnership with Faaborg-Midtfyn Municipality to develop a method and conduct a pilot project. The task of the demonstration project is to develop and construct a housing project in an existing factory building from 1905 in the small Danish town Ryslinge, which will be able to compete with corresponding conventional housing construction.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Buthke, Jan","Ostenfeld Pedersen, Simon","Larsen, Niels Martin","Bundgaard, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-125468"],"event":{"end":"2019-07-26","place":"Lisbon, pt","start":"2019-07-24","title":"ICSA2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Architecture","Arkitektur","Modularisation","Modularisering","Transformation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-ART"],"level3":{"ART":["DI-ART-AAA","DI-ART-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-ART-AAA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transformation of architectural heritage through adaptive modular systems","src":["arka"],"src-code":["DI-ART-AAA"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-125468","ids":["arka-bf33c60a-7758-4b97-a5b0-33b4cd3a3d08"],"keyword":["No","architecture","arkitektur","modularisation","modularisering","transformation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E2604545591BF39F3FD2B9CBA7D88423"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aarhus school of architecture","l2":"DI-ART","l2n":"Artistic Higher Education Institutions","l3":"DI-ART-AAA","l3nn":"Aarhus School of Architecture","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Aarhus School of Architecture","namevar":["Aarhus School of Architecture"],"nora_code":"DI-ART-AAA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"buthkepau","last":"Buthke","locid":"1adb9019-e266-4102-ba97-81805412321f","name":"Buthke, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon","key":"ostenfeldpedersenpau","last":"Ostenfeld Pedersen","locid":"a1565931-9ae1-4d91-9b93-434c7c435eb3","name":"Ostenfeld Pedersen, Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ca21b870-556a-4ab4-903d-8e82d9005449","name":"Larsen, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0003-1479-4350","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"bundgaardpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"ed512640-7a78-4298-bcc6-6fc8782baf9c","name":"Bundgaard, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arka-bf33c60a-7758-4b97-a5b0-33b4cd3a3d08"],"src":["Aarhus School of Architecture"],"title":"Transformation of architectural heritage through adaptive modular systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-125468","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Adipokines secreted from white adipose tissue play a role in metabolic crosstalk and homeostasis, whereas the brown adipose secretome is less explored. We performed high-sensitivity mass-spectrometry-based proteomics on the cell media of human adipocytes derived from the supraclavicular brown adipose and from the subcutaneous white adipose depots of adult humans. We identified 471 potentially secreted proteins covering interesting categories such as hormones, growth factors, extracellular matrix proteins, and proteins of the complement system, which were differentially regulated between brown and white adipocytes. A total of 101 proteins were exclusively quantified in brown adipocytes, and among these was ependymin-related protein 1 (EPDR1). EPDR1 was detected in human plasma, and functional studies suggested a role for EPDR1 in thermogenic determination during adipogenesis. In conclusion, we report substantial differences between the secretomes of brown and white human adipocytes and identify novel candidate batokines that can be important regulators of human metabolism.","author_count":24,"contributors":["Deshmukh, Atul S.","Peijs, Lone","Beaudry, Jacqueline L","Jespersen, Naja Z","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Ma, Tao","Brunner, Andreas D","Larsen, Therese J.","Bayarri-Olmos, Rafael","Prabhakar, Bhargav Saligram","Helgstrand, Charlotte","Severinsen, Mai C.","Holst, Birgitte","Kjaer, Andreas","Tang-Christensen, Mads","Sanfridson, Annika","Garred, Peter","Privé, Gilbert G","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Gerhart-Hines, Zachary","Nielsen, Søren","Drucker, Daniel J","Mann, Matthias","Scheele, Camilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-496096"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"proteomics based comparative mapping of the secretomes of human brown and white adipocytes reveals epdr000000000001 as a novel batokine","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2018/08/30/402867.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-496096","identifier":[{"id":"85074164870","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31668873","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-abe0ec28-0d16-450d-93ec-efd9f939d9cc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4F387153042789211C68E4E4266EF37C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://www.biorxiv.org/content/biorxiv/early/2018/08/30/402867.full.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Zierath Group","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Protein Research, Proteomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Atul S","key":"deshmukhatulspau","last":"Deshmukh","locid":"ec9031a8-0215-4c06-ba88-f66863916df9","name":"Deshmukh, Atul S.","name_org":"Deshmukh, Atul S","orcid":"0000-0002-2278-1843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lone","key":"peijslonepau","last":"Peijs","locid":"01a2f323-97c7-4180-a9c0-3ef47964ff7b","name":"Peijs, Lone","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacqueline L","key":"beaudryjacquelinelpau","last":"Beaudry","name":"Beaudry, Jacqueline L","rank