st":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01066854","19023715"],"issn_org":["01066854"],"issue":"11","journal":"Dansk Veterinærtidsskrift","pages":"47-47","publisher":"Den Danske Dyrlægeforening","status":"p","title":"Dansk Veterinærtidsskrift","title_org":"Dansk Veterinaertidsskrift"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0b350032-739e-45f9-92ea-8caa95fd8ad3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Højpatogen fugleinfluenza med subtypen H5N6 er forblevet i Danmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-307967","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Avian influenza virus (AIV) subtypes H5 and H7 can infect poultry causing low pathogenicity (LP) AI, but these LPAIVs may mutate to highly pathogenic AIV in chickens or turkeys causing high mortality, hence H5/H7 subtypes demand statutory intervention. Serological surveillance in the European Union provides evidence of H5/H7 AIV exposure in apparently healthy poultry. To identify the most sensitive screening method as the first step in an algorithm to provide evidence of H5/H7 AIV infection, the standard approach of H5/H7 antibody testing by haemagglutination inhibition (HI) was compared with an ELISA, which detects antibodies to all subtypes. Sera (n = 1055) from 74 commercial chicken flocks were tested by both methods. A Bayesian approach served to estimate diagnostic test sensitivities and specificities, without assuming any 'gold standard'. Sensitivity and specificity of the ELISA was 97% and 99.8%, and for H5/H7 HI 43% and 99.8%, respectively, although H5/H7 HI sensitivity varied considerably between infected flocks. ELISA therefore provides superior sensitivity for the screening of chicken flocks as part of an algorithm, which subsequently utilises H5/H7 HI to identify infection by these two subtypes. With the calculated sensitivity and specificity, testing nine sera per flock is sufficient to detect a flock seroprevalence of 30% with 95% probability.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Arnold, M E","Slomka, M J","Breed, A C","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Pritz-Verschuren, S","Venema-Kemper, S","Bouwstra, R J","Trebbien, Ramona","Zohari, S","Ceeraz, V","Larsen, Lars Erik","Manvell, R J","Koch, G","Brown, I H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334404"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Slomka, M J"],"country":["Netherlands","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Animal & Plant Health Agency","National Veterinary Institute","Wageningen Bioveterinary Research"],"keyword":["Bayesian"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation of elisa and haemagglutination inhibition as screening tests in serosurveillance for h000000000005 h000000000007 avian influenza in commercial chicken flocks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0950268817002898","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334404","identifier":[{"id":"29325601","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85048056136","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-641c231a-b417-4d2f-b5ae-8e1f98057dec"],"keyword":["AIV (avian influenza virus)","Bayesian","ELISA (enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay)","H5/H7 AIV surveillance","HI (haemagglutination inhibition)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-03975EBEDC804B2D358BB49B8C7060E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1017/S0950268817002898","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/142463241/evaluation_of_elisa_and_haemagglutination_inhibition_as_screening_tests_in_serosurveillance_for_h5h7_avian_influenza_in_commercial_chicken_flocks.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"animal plant health agency","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Animal & Plant Health Agency","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"wageningen bioveterinary research","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Wageningen Bioveterinary Research","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"national veterinary institute","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"National Veterinary Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M E","key":"arnoldpau","last":"Arnold","name":"Arnold, M E","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M J","key":"slomkapau","last":"Slomka","name":"Slomka, M J","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A C","key":"breedpau","last":"Breed","name":"Breed, A C","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"pritzverschurenpau","last":"Pritz-Verschuren","name":"Pritz-Verschuren, S","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"venemakemperpau","last":"Venema-Kemper","name":"Venema-Kemper, S","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"R J","key":"bouwstrapau","last":"Bouwstra","name":"Bouwstra, R J","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","locid":"f5a78ced-77e8-4da1-950c-9c1992eac344","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"S","key":"zoharipau","last":"Zohari","name":"Zohari, S","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"V","key":"ceerazpau","last":"Ceeraz","name":"Ceeraz, V","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L E","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, L E","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R J","key":"manvellpau","last":"Manvell","name":"Manvell, R J","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"G","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","name":"Koch, G","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"I H","key":"brownpau","last":"Brown","name":"Brown, I H","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29325601"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0950268817002898","issn":["09502688","14694409"],"issn_org":["09502688"],"journal":"Epidemiology and Infection","pages":"1-8","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Epidemiology and Infection"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048056136"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-641c231a-b417-4d2f-b5ae-8e1f98057dec"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Evaluation of ELISA and haemagglutination inhibition as screening tests in serosurveillance for H5/H7 avian influenza in commercial chicken flocks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334404","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we investigate the planning of operating rooms at Rigshospitalet, a large Danish hospital. Each operation must be assigned to a specific operating room and also be scheduled for a specific time while taking into account clinical guidelines. Both elective and emergency operations are included, such that the elective operations are planned while still taking potential emergency operations into consideration. Furthermore, the duration of each operation is uncertain. The aim is to construct robust operating room schedules that minimise overtime work and release unused capacity. Due to the uncertainty associated with arrival of emergency patients and also the duration of each operation, a deterministic model is not suitable for this problem. Therefore, we develop a stochastic model where operation duration can vary and where the arrivals of emergency patients are unknown. The stochastic model is computationally heavy, so two mixed integer programming based heuristics denoted 2-Step Relax-and-Fix and All Open Relax-and-Fix are developed to solve the problem. The computational study is based on an extensive dataset compromising 304 days. The heuristics give good results with half of the operating rooms having less than 8 min of overtime work. To test the robustness of the solutions we carry out a simulated implementation of the operation plans. The simulation shows that the heuristic solutions are fairly robust. In general, results show a clear potential for implementing the method for planning and scheduling of operating rooms at Rigshospitalet.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kroer, Line Ravnskjær","Foverskov, Karoline","Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Hansen, Aske Skouboe","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-378503"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Jesper"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"planning and scheduling operating rooms for elective and emergency surgeries with uncertain duration","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150862536/MELJU_1_s2.0_S2211692317300188_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-378503","identifier":[{"id":"85045836717","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f725dbea-1080-438b-a562-150d2eba2954"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-03C2AB034301CD792FA9140E59A0B71B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150862536/MELJU_1_s2.0_S2211692317300188_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Ravnskjær","key":"kroerpau","last":"Kroer","name":"Kroer, Line Ravnskjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karoline","key":"foverskovpau","last":"Foverskov","name":"Foverskov, Karoline","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aske Skouboe","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"18f81523-2d28-483e-9428-7f115bc2c75d","name":"Hansen, Aske Skouboe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.orhc.2018.03.006","issn":["22116923"],"journal":"Operations Research for Health Care","pages":"107-119","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Operations Research for Health Care","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85045836717"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-f725dbea-1080-438b-a562-150d2eba2954"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Planning and scheduling operating rooms for elective and emergency surgeries with uncertain duration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-378503","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Michelsen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-445960"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Beat","Det Humanistiske Fakultet","Flowradio","Jazz","Listener Surveys","Lytterundersøgelser","Music radio","Musikradio","Radiosymfoniorkestret","The National Symphony Orchestra"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beatmusikkens indtog","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-445960","ids":["ku-57d6a08e-6429-4475-a8a3-5dd699885364"],"keyword":["Beat","Det Humanistiske Fakultet","Flowradio","Listener Surveys","Lytterundersøgelser","Music radio","Radiosymfoniorkestret","The National Symphony Orchestra","jazz","musikradio"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BF544A18C9E3C12472E293DAFCDEDCA9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Arts and Cultural Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"michelsenpau","last":"Michelsen","locid":"6687b104-47d2-45df-bb71-20e1e9c5b001","name":"Michelsen, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"michelsenpedh","last":"Michelsen","name":"Michelsen, Morten","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Iben","key":"havepedh","last":"Have","name":"Have, Iben","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anja Mølle","key":"lindelofpedh","last":"Lindelof","name":"Lindelof, Anja Mølle","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"rørdamlarsenpedh","last":"Rørdam Larsen","name":"Rørdam Larsen, Charlotte","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"smithsivertsenpedh","last":"Smith-Sivertsen","name":"Smith-Sivertsen, Henrik","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788771843781"],"pages":"86-90","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus Universitetsforlag","status":"p","subtitle":"Danmarks Radio og musikken","title":"Stil nu ind ..."},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-57d6a08e-6429-4475-a8a3-5dd699885364"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beatmusikkens indtog","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-445960","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The intra-islet theory states that glucagon secretion is suppressed when insulin secretion is stimulated, but glucagon's role in intra-islet paracrine regulation is controversial. This study investigated intra-islet functions of glucagon in mice. We examined glucagon-induced insulin secretion using isolated perfused pancreata from wild-type, GLP-1 receptor (GLP-1R) knockout, diphtheria toxin-induced proglucagon knockdown, β cell-specific glucagon receptor (Gcgr) knockout, and global Gcgr knockout (Gcgr −/−) mice. We found that glucagon stimulates insulin secretion through both Gcgr and GLP-1R. Moreover, loss of either Gcgr or GLP-1R does not change insulin responses, whereas combined blockage of both receptors significantly reduces insulin secretion. Active GLP-1 is identified in pancreatic perfusate from Gcgr −/− but not wild-type mice, suggesting that β cell GLP-1R activation results predominantly from glucagon action. Our results suggest that combined activity of glucagon and GLP-1 receptors is essential for β cell secretory responses, emphasizing a role for paracrine intra-islet glucagon actions to maintain appropriate insulin secretion. Glucose-stimulated insulin secretion can be regulated by glucagon and GLP-1 receptors on paracrine β-cells. Svendsen et al. find that complete blockade of glucagon signaling in islets severely limits insulin secretion but establish that paracrine glucagon signaling involves both the glucagon and GLP-1 receptors.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Svendsen, Berit","Larsen, Olav","Gabe, Maria Buur Nordskov","Christiansen, Charlotte Bayer","Rosenkilde, Mette M","Drucker, Daniel J","Holst, Jens Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-467351"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Toronto"],"keyword":["GLP 1 receptor","Glucagon","Glucagon receptor","Intra islet communication","Perfused mouse pancreas","exendin 9 39"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insulin secretion depends on intra islet glucagon signaling","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2018.10.018","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-467351","identifier":[{"id":"30380405","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85055086764","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7b6bd9cb-f73b-417b-a7a6-4f12b6d33420"],"keyword":["GLP-1 receptor","Intra-islet communication","exendin(9-39)","glucagon","glucagon receptor","perfused mouse pancreas"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88BCBD14C5E1C4A8397206585EFFBCA7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209460301/PIIS2211124718315948.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.celrep.2018.10.018","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Novo Nordisk Foundation Center for Basic Metabolic Research, Juul Holst Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of toronto","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Toronto","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Berit","key":"svendsenpau"