{"abstract":"Background Many factors can influence the occurrence of neonatal diarrhoea in piglets. Currently, well-known pathogens such as enterotoxigenic Escherichia coli and Clostridium perfringens type C appear to play a minor role in development of disease. Other infectious pathogens may be involved. In this study, we aimed to investigate the presence of selected infectious pathogens in neonatal piglets with clinical and pathological signs of enteric disease. The association between rotavirus A, Enterococcus hirae, Clostridium difficile and Clostridium perfringens type A/C and diarrhoea was investigated in a case control study on piglet level. The possible role of E. coli virulence factors was investigated in a multistep-procedure using herd-pools of E.coli isolates to screen for their presence. Results Rotavirus A was detected more often in cases (25%) than in controls (6%) (P < 0.001). The detection rate of Enterococcus hirae, Clostridium difficile and C. perfringens type A positive for beta2 genes was the same in the two groups of piglets. C. perfringens type C was not detected in the study. Investigations on E. coli virulence factors showed a high prevalence of EAST1 toxin genes (55% of tested case piglets were positive) and AIDA-1 adhesin genes (63% of toxin positive case piglets were positive) in case piglets. Conclusions Detection of rotavirus A was statistically significantly associated with neonatal piglet diarrhoea. An aetiologic role of E. coli carrying virulence factors EAST1 and AIDA-1 needs further investigation as the study points out these two factors as possible causative factors in neonatal diarrhoea. Detection of E.hirae, C.difficile and C. perfringens type A carrying beta 2 genes was not associated with neonatal piglet diarrhoea. However, the study suggested that massive overgrowth by E. hirae could be part of the pathogenesis in some cases of neonatal diarrhoea.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kongsted, Hanne","Pedersen, Karl","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik","Pedersen, Ken Steen","Jorsal, Sven Erik","Bækbo, Poul"],"cuid":["S02-094.95-024358"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Kongsted, Hanne"],"keyword":["AIDA 1","Beta 2","C difficile","C perfringens type a","E coli virulence factors","EAST1","Enterococcus hirae","Neonatal diarrhoea","Piglets","Rotavirus A"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-SEGES"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-SEGES","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diarrhoea in neonatal piglets a case control study on microbiological findings","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-018-0094-5","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-094.95-024358","identifier":[{"id":"PMC6120089","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85057101938","type":"scopus"},{"id":"30186621","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-9fc7f9c1-bc70-4d0f-b078-2c1ebfe56cab","dtu-06386a88-aa36-4917-a516-a73ea77120e2"],"keyword":["AIDA-1","Beta 2","C. difficile","C. perfringens type a","E. coli virulence factors","EAST1","Enterococcus hirae","Neonatal diarrhoea","Piglets","Rotavirus a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-61EE4E1482473599748E42611BC2E963"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/154188403/s40813_018_0094_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/134727807/s40813_018_0094_5.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s40813-018-0094-5","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences, Department of Animal and Veterinary Sciences - ANIS Welfare"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Bacteriology & Parasitology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"seges innovation","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-SEGES","l3nn":"SEGES Innovation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SEGES Innovation","namevar":["SEGES"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-SEGES","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hanne","key":"kongstedhannepau","last":"Kongsted","locid":"30a5921a-546d-4672-838a-acee578f33ac","name":"Kongsted, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0001-6811-5881","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karl","key":"pedersenkarlpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d1138736-2a78-423a-9950-0ce651434ec7","name":"Pedersen, Karl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagercharlottekristianepau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenkensteenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sven Erik","key":"jorsalsveneriklindpau","last":"Jorsal","locid":"4787cc8c-02f9-41fb-84de-11c1c8b680e3","name":"Jorsal, Sven Erik Lind","name_org":"Jorsal, Sven Erik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Poul","key":"bækbopoulpau","last":"Bækbo","name":"Bækbo, Poul","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30186621"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s40813-018-0094-5","issn":["20555660"],"journal":"Porcine Health Management","paperid":"17","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Porcine Health Management","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85057101938"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9fc7f9c1-bc70-4d0f-b078-2c1ebfe56cab","dtu-06386a88-aa36-4917-a516-a73ea77120e2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Diarrhoea in neonatal piglets: a case control study on microbiological findings","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.95-024358","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Aim: We investigated whether DNA methylation regulates expression of LPL and PI3K complex genes in chronic lymphocytic leukemia (CLL) and evaluated the prognostic significance of LPL promoter methylation in CLL patients. Patients & methods: Methylation of LPL promoter was assessed in 112 patients using methylation-sensitive high-resolution melting (MS-HRM).Results: Patients with a fully or heterogeneously methylated LPL promoter had significantly longer median time to treatment (p < 0.001) and 75% lower (hazard ratio: 0.25; 95% CI: 0.15-0.42; p < 0.001) risk of requirement for treatment as opposed to patients with nonmethylated promoter. Multivariate modeling confirmed independent prognostic value of these findings. Conclusion: Chronic lymphocytic leukemia patients with a fully or heterogeneously methylated LPL gene promoter display indolent disease course and acquisition of heterogeneous methylation of LPL promoter is insufficient to induce gene expression.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Daugaard, Iben","Hussmann, Dianna","Kristensen, Louise","Kristensen, Thomas","Kjeldsen, Tina E","Nyvold, Charlotte G","Larsen, Thomas S","Møller, Michael B","Hansen, Lise Lotte","Wojdacz, Tomasz K"],"cuid":["S02-099.88-024365"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Biomarker","CLL","Chronic lymphocytic leukemia","MS HRM","Treatment","heterogeneous methylation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic lymphocytic leukemia patients with heterogeneously or fully methylated lpl promotor display longer time to treatment","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"a