{"abstract":"A biosynthetic gene cluster of the fungal xanthone heterodimer neosartorin (1) was discovered in Aspergillus novofumigatus, and its biosynthesis was investigated by a series of gene-deletion experiments. The results indicate that the two monomeric units of 1 are synthesized by the same set of enzymes, with chrysophanol (5) as a common precursor. Furthermore, the P450 monooxygenase NsrP for the heterodimerization was discovered, which also accepts non-native substrates to afford novel xanthone dimers.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Matsuda, Yudai","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-340991"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic characterization of neosartorin biosynthesis provides insight into heterodimeric natural product generation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85056346243","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-340991","identifier":[{"id":"30394754","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85056346243","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-7a0da493-8ea6-424d-aa57-49686a6b0fc6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3D746E4232258D394F75A7F21BA094E8"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yudai","key":"matsudapau","last":"Matsuda","locid":"c04a466b-918c-42ea-8968-9fc97637023d","name":"Matsuda, Yudai","orcid":"0000-0001-5650-4732","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Held","key":"gotfredsenpau","last":"Gotfredsen","locid":"1cf4df84-2d0e-4693-bf47-e9932e3bf0e3","name":"Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","orcid":"0000-0002-7386-119X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30394754"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.orglett.8b03123","issn":["15237052","15237060"],"issn_org":["15237060"],"issue":"22","journal":"Organic Letters","pages":"7194-7200","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Organic Letters","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056346243"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7a0da493-8ea6-424d-aa57-49686a6b0fc6"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Genetic Characterization of Neosartorin Biosynthesis Provides Insight into Heterodimeric Natural Product Generation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-340991","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Based on the due date of a pregnant woman Danish Health Authority guidelines prescribe time windows for when the woman should have midwife consultations. A principle of continuity of care means that each woman should preferably see the same midwife at every consultation. For the first consultation pregnant women are assigned an arbitrary free time slot belonging to a specific midwife. In turn, this midwife is expected to have consultations with this woman in specific weeks according to authority guidelines. This random assignment of pregnant women to midwives means that each midwife has a very unbalanced workload and that there is an imbalance between the workloads of different midwifes within each week. The aim of this work is to devise a method for assigning and scheduling midwife consultations that results in a balanced workload for each midwife and among the midwives while making sure consultation guidelines are respected. We present a mathematical model for this problem and through simulation of the historical flow of pregnant women show that using this model would have significantly reduced workload imbalances, even when including a further restriction not currently adhered to. The model is too demanding to be implemented at the hospital. Therefore, we develop an assignment tool based on full enumeration for one pregnant woman at a time. Simulations show that this approach can still reduce workload imbalances considerably. The tool, which has now been implemented at the hospital, is also used to test the workload impact of continuity of care.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Græse, Line","Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-362271"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assignment of pregnant women to midwives","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-362271","ids":["dtu-c1127839-1523-4ad3-8b46-1717cc2e18b7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-987A2167632331418DA677EFC91F55A5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"græsepau","last":"Græse","name":"Græse, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"36","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c1127839-1523-4ad3-8b46-1717cc2e18b7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Assignment of Pregnant Women to Midwives","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-362271","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
