{"abstract":"This chapter throws light on the development of a participatory inquiry for learning and knowledge building based on roleplaying. The practice described here is aimed at develop competences in dialogue, relational awareness, critical self-reflexivity and collaboration among the employees and leaders working in an institution. It is carried out and described from within the movement, often referred to as the dialogical turn (Flecha et al. 2003) or the relational turn (Donati 2011). The practice is rooted in a constructionist stance and inspired by action research and arts-based research. I present an example of my work with a specific project, which took place in a 24-hour care center for neglected adolescents between the ages of 12-18. It went on for a period of one and a half years. The adolescents were forced to live at the institution because they had been removed from their parents due to social and psychological problems. During their childhood they had often experienced serious breaches of trust in their relationships with other people.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hersted, Lone"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094552"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"doing relational research through roleplaying","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.routledge.com/Relational-Research-and-Organisation-Studies/Madsen-Madsen-Larsen-Larsen-Hersted-Hersted-Rasmussen-Rasmussen/p/book/9780815394150","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094552","ids":["aau-99723210-dd81-4fba-bd66-e16fe07891ba"],"keyword":["Roleplaying, reflecting team, dialogic process, collaborative learning, organizational learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E59AF593FB2E7D691E5B48769D0F4CAB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Processer og Læring i Organisationer (Learning)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone","key":"herstedpau","last":"Hersted","locid":"ec8fb75d-cbe5-44e9-b4a1-e5dcbe418de3","name":"Hersted, Lone","orcid":"0000-0003-0934-1170","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Øland","key":"madsenpedh","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Charlotte Øland","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette Vinther","key":"larsenpedh","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Mette Vinther","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Lone","key":"herstedpedh","last":"Hersted","name":"Hersted, Lone","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen Gulddahl","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jørgen Gulddahl","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9780429507557"],"isbn":["9780815394150"],"pages":"117-141","publisher":"Routledge","series":"Routledge Series in Management, Organizations and Society","status":"p","title":"Relational Research and Organisation Studies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-99723210-dd81-4fba-bd66-e16fe07891ba"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Doing relational research through roleplaying","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094552","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: New training modalities such as simulation are widely accepted in radiology; however, development of effective simulation-based training programs is challenging. They are often unstructured and based on convenience or coincidence. The study objective was to perform a nationwide needs assessment to identify and prioritize technical procedures that should be included in a simulation-based curriculum. Methods: A needs assessment using the Delphi method was completed among 91 key leaders in radiology. Round 1 identified technical procedures that radiologists should learn. Round 2 explored frequency of procedure, number of radiologists performing the procedure, risk and/or discomfort for patients, and feasibility for simulation. Round 3 was elimination and prioritization of procedures. Results: Response rates were 67 %, 70 % and 66 %, respectively. In Round 1, 22 technical procedures were included. Round 2 resulted in pre-prioritization of procedures. In round 3, 13 procedures were included in the final prioritized list. The three highly prioritized procedures were ultrasound-guided (US) histological biopsy and fine-needle aspiration, US-guided needle puncture and catheter drainage, and basic abdominal ultrasound. Conclusion: A needs assessment identified and prioritized 13 technical procedures to include in a simulation-based curriculum. The list may be used as guide for development of training programs. Key Points: • Simulation-based training can supplement training on patients in radiology.• Development of simulation-based training should follow a structured approach.• The CAMES Needs Assessment Formula explores needs for simulation training.• A national Delphi study identified and prioritized procedures suitable for simulation training.• The prioritized list serves as guide for development of courses in radiology.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nayahangan, Leizl Joy","Nielsen, Kristina Rue","Albrecht-Beste, Elisabeth","Bachmann Nielsen, Michael","Paltved, Charlotte","Lindorff-Larsen, Karen","Nielsen, Bjørn Ulrik","Konge, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121001"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical Competence","Computer Simulation","Curriculum","Delphi Technique","Denmark","Education Medical Graduate methods","Humans","Journal Article","Needs Assessment","Needs Assessment organization administration","Patient Simulation","Radiology","Radiology education","Simulation Training","Ultrasonography Interventional standards","Ultrasonography standards"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Copenhagen Academy for Medical Education and Simulation, The Capital Region of Denmark, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determining procedures for simulation based training in radiology a nationwide needs assessment","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85040245358&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121001","identifier":[{"id":"29318426","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85040245358","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f4103f67-8f4e-4eb2-8083-1fd2384e0774"],"keyword":["Clinical Competence","Computer Simulation","Curriculum","Delphi technique","Denmark","Education, Medical, Graduate/methods","Humans","Journal Article","Needs Assessment/organization & administration","Needs assessment","Patient Simulation","Radiology","Radiology/education","Simulation training","Ultrasonography, Interventional/standards","Ultrasonography/standards"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-7-89AFB4D508