{"abstract":"Mængden af PCV2-virus i poolede serumprøver kan anvendes til at finde grise med meget PCV2-virus, hvorimod mængden af PCV2-virus i spyt og fæces er velegnede til at vurdere tilstedeværelsen af eller tidspunktet for en begyndende PCV2-infektion. Der er ikke god overensstemmelse mellem PCV2-niveauerne (mængden af virus i blodet) i blod (serum) og spyt opsamlet ved rebtest eller fæces opsamlet ved sokkeprøver. Det viser resultater fra et veterinært speciale udarbejdet på DTU Veterinærinstituttet i samarbejde med KU SUND, MSD Animal Health og SEGES Svineproduktion. Resultaterne betyder, at PCV2-niveauet i serum ikke kan udledes fra måling af PCV2-niveauet i spyt eller fæces. Rebtesten og sokkeprøverne vil dog kunne anvendes til at screene for forekomst af PCV2 i besætningen. Ved vurdering af PCV2-niveauet i en poolet serumprøve er det vigtigt at holde sig for øje, at enkelte grise med et højt PCV2-niveau vil kunne forårsage et højt PCV2-niveau i den poolede serumprøve. Studiet inkluderede 34 stier ligeligt fordelt på to aldersgrupper (14-15 uger og 18-19 uger) i én slagtesvinebesætning. I hver sti blev der udtaget én rebtest til opsamling af spyt, én sokkeprøve til opsamling af fæces samt blodprøver fra alle grise i stien. I laboratoriet på DTU blev der udfærdiget to serumpools. Den ene pool bestod af serum fra alle grisene i stien, og den anden pool inkluderede kun serum fra grise, som tyggede i rebet under opsamlingen af spytprøven. Alle individuelle dyrs PCV2-niveau i serum blev tillige undersøgt i syv tilfældigt udvalgte stier. Resultaterne viste, at der ikke var god overensstemmelse mellem PCV2-niveauerne i de forskellige prøvematerialer. Ydermere viste analyser af de individuelle serumprøver, at enkelte dyr med et højt PCV2-niveau kan forårsage et højt PCV2-niveau i en poolet serumprøve, idet kun enkelte grise havde PCV2-niveauer lige så højt som PCV-niveauet i den poolede serumprøve fra alle grise i stien. Anbefalingen er derfor, at der anvendes serumpools, når formålet er at bestemme, om der findes grise med et højt PCV2-niveau. Når formålet er at identificere, om infektionen er til stede i besætningen eller bestemme, hvornår infektionen starter, er spyt eller sokkeprøver derimod også velegnede. På nuværende tidspunkt er der mere viden om tolkningen af PCV2-niveau i serum end i spyt og fæces fra sokkeprøver.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Neumann, Katrine","Buse, Katja Strøm","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Nielsen, Gitte Blach","Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","Larsen, Lars Erik","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-335649"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"påvisning af pcv000000000002 notat nr 000000001807","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/146794458/Notat_1807_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-335649","ids":["dtu-680e9264-786e-4850-a9ad-7a10e8e458a7"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BED9CA9D15B5185C2DEC513F06592366"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/146794458/Notat_1807_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://svineproduktion.dk/publikationer/kilder/notater/2018/1807","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["MSD Animal Health Nordic"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"danish agriculture food council","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-AAF","l3nl":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","l3nn":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","namevar":["Danish Agriculture and Food Council"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-AAF","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine","key":"neumannkatrinepau","last":"Neumann","name":"Neumann, Katrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katja Strøm","key":"busekatjastrømpau","last":"Buse","name":"Buse, Katja Strøm","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagercharlottekristianepau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gitte Blach","key":"nielsengitteblachpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Gitte Blach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Saxmose","key":"nielsensørensaxmosepau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Søren Saxmose","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensencharlottesonnepau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"4","publisher":"SEGES Svineproduktion","status":"p","volume":"2018"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Danish Agriculture & Food Council","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","msd animal health nordic"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-680e9264-786e-4850-a9ad-7a10e8e458a7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Påvisning af PCV2 : Notat nr 1807","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-335649","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A viruses (IAVs) are important human and animal pathogens with high impact on human and animal health. In Denmark, a passive surveillance program for IAV in pigs has been performed since 2011, where screening tests and subsequent subtyping are performed by reverse transcription quantitative real-time PCR (RT-qPCR). A disadvantage of the current subtyping system is that several assays are needed to cover the wide range of circulating subtypes, which makes the system expensive and time-consuming. Therefore, the aim of the present study was to develop a high-throughput method, which could improve surveillance of swine influenza viruses (swIAVs) and lower the costs of virus subtyping. Twelve qPCR assays specific for various hemagglutinin and neuraminidase gene lineages relevant for swIAV and six assays specific for the internal genes of IAV were developed and optimized for the high-throughput qPCR platform BioMark (Fluidigm). The qPCR assays were validated and optimized to run under the same reaction conditions using a 48.48 dynamic array (48.48DA). The sensitivity and specificity was assessed by testing virus isolates and field samples with known subtypes. The results revealed a performance of the swIAV 48.48DA similar to conventional real-time analysis, and furthermore, the specificity of swIAV 48.48DA was very high and without cross reactions between the assays. This high-throughput system provides a cost-effective alternative for subtyping of swIAVs.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Krog, Jesper Schak","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Skovgaard, Kerstin","Harder, Timm C.","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343071"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subtyping of swine influenza viruses using a high throughput real time pcr platform","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2018.00165","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343071","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5972299","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85047566938","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29872645","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-80e2e604-f6ab-4ec1-bfae-f40dbb037975"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A076B087B9829B8F0A4E2C00042EE87D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fcimb.2018.00165","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/148758521/Goecke_2018_Subtyping_of_swine_influenza_viruse.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"friedrich loeffler institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"4d2ddf87-a082-462e-86c4-567264391d29","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","orcid":"0000-0003-4948-9946","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kerstin","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c3c3868-b5a3-457b-8b97-9645ad03e405","name":"Skovgaard, Kerstin","orcid":"0000-0001-5663-4879","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Timm C.","key":"harderpau","last":"Harder","name":"Harder, Timm C.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Ø.","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","name_org":"Breum, Solvej Ø.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars E.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E.","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29872645"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fcimb.2018.00165","issn":["22352988"],"journal":"Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology","paperid":"165","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","publisher_org":"Frontiers Media S.A.","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Cellular and Infection Microbiology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85047566938"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-80e2e604-f6ab-4ec1-bfae-f40dbb037975"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Subtyping of Swine Influenza Viruses Using a High-Throughput Real-Time PCR Platform","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343071","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Novofumigatonin (1), isolated from the fungus Aspergillus novofumigatus, is a heavily oxygenated meroterpenoid containing a unique orthoester moiety. Despite the wide distribution of orthoesters in nature and their biological importance, little is known about the biogenesis of orthoesters. Here we show the elucidation of the biosynthetic pathway of 1 and the identification of key enzymes for the orthoester formation by a series of CRISPR-Cas9-based gene-deletion experiments and in vivo and in vitro reconstitutions of the biosynthesis. The novofumigatonin pathway involves endoperoxy compounds as key precursors for the orthoester synthesis, in which the Fe(II)/α-ketoglutarate-dependent enzyme NvfI performs the endoperoxidation. NvfE, the enzyme catalyzing the orthoester synthesis, is an Fe(II)-dependent, but cosubstrate-free, endoperoxide isomerase, despite the fact that NvfE shares sequence homology with the known Fe(II)/α-ketoglutarate-dependent dioxygenases. NvfE thus belongs to a class of enzymes that gained an isomerase activity by losing the α-ketoglutarate-binding ability.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Matsuda, Yudai","Bai, Tongxuan","Phippen, Christopher","Nødvig, Christina Spuur","Kjærbølling, Inge","Vesth, Tammi Camilla","Andersen, Mikael Rørdam","Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Abe, Ikuro","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-354270"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"country":["Japan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tokyo City University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"novofumigatonin biosynthesis involves a non heme iron dependent endoperoxide isomerase for orthoester formation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04983-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-354270","identifier":[{"id":"29968715","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85049511618","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6030086","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-a679dde7-29b8-44f8-9cd0-4904ad9b9a0b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E127BCB2ADA02F6307432290FB5471D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/150817407/s41467_018_04983_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-04983-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Biotechnology and Biomedicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"jp","key":"tokyo city university","loc":["Japan","Asia, East","OECD"],"name":"Tokyo City University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yudai","key":"matsudapau","last":"Matsuda","locid":"c04a466b-918c-42ea-8968-9fc97637023d","name":"Matsuda, Yudai","orcid":"0000-0001-5650-4732","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tongxuan","key":"baipau","last":"Bai","name":"Bai, Tongxuan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christopher B. W.","key":"phippenpau","last":"Phippen","locid":"395b4fe2-4c7c-4bb2-b2da-eac308e463aa","name":"Phippen, Christop