te Brandt","key":"sørensencharlottebrandtpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"14bfd3d1-a9b2-4bc5-823b-233432e43cf3","name":"Sørensen, Charlotte Brandt","orcid":"0000-0002-4469-8696","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30062172"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jacbts.2017.06.004","issn":["2452302X"],"issue":"5","journal":"JACC: Basic to Translational Science","pages":"591-600","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"JACC: Basic to Translational Science","title_org":"JACC: Basic to translational science","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042148702"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-26f6d550-083e-470e-bc41-ac22fd927e38","dtu-f6640060-bc9d-450c-95a2-24901023646a","ku-90709418-18fb-4095-a438-4df8d102d6b5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Apolipoprotein E Deficiency Increases Remnant Lipoproteins and Accelerates Progressive Atherosclerosis, But Not Xanthoma Formation, in Gene-Modified Minipigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-088.14-666129","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES AND BACKGROUND: Practical skills training in vascular surgery is facing challenges because of an increased number of endovascular procedures and fewer open procedures, as well as a move away from the traditional principle of \"learning by doing.\" This change has established simulation as a cornerstone in providing trainees with the necessary skills and competences. However, the development of simulation based programs often evolves based on available resources and equipment, reflecting convenience rather than a systematic educational plan. The objective of the present study was to perform a national needs assessment to identify the technical procedures that should be integrated in a simulation based curriculum. DESIGN AND METHODS: A national needs assessment using a Delphi process was initiated by engaging 33 predefined key persons in vascular surgery. Round 1 was a brainstorming phase to identify technical procedures that vascular surgeons should learn. Round 2 was a survey that used a needs assessment formula to explore the frequency of procedures, the number of surgeons performing each procedure, risk and/or discomfort, and feasibility for simulation based training. Round 3 involved elimination and ranking of procedures. RESULTS: The response rate for round 1 was 70%, with 36 procedures identified. Round 2 had a 76% response rate and resulted in a preliminary prioritised list after exploring the need for simulation based training. Round 3 had an 85% response rate; 17 procedures were eliminated, resulting in a final prioritised list of 19 technical procedures. CONCLUSION: A national needs assessment using a standardised Delphi method identified a list of procedures that are highly suitable and may provide the basis for future simulation based training programs for vascular surgeons in training.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Nayahangan, Leizl Joy","Konge, Lars","Schroeder, T V","Paltved, Charlotte","Lindorff-Larsen, Karen","Eiberg, J P","Nielsen, B U"],"cuid":["S04-099.98-009135"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Curriculum","Curriculum development","Delphi Technique","Denmark","Education Medical Graduate","Health Services Needs and Demand","High fidelity simulation training","Humans","Journal Article","Needs Assessment","Simulation","Simulation based education","Vascular Surgical Procedures","Vascular surgery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Copenhagen Academy for Medical Education and Simulation, The Capital Region of Denmark, Copenhagen, Denmark; Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, University of Copenhagen, Copenhagen, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a national needs assessment to identify technical procedures in vascular surgery for simulation based training","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85014087899","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-099.98-009135","identifier":[{"id":"28258884","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85014087899","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000400034700015","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-bd4d11fd-128f-4e1a-ad4d-b461da8d3dc1","au-68074857-3796-4999-bc5a-745ad50c88ae","ku-656b6b40-e87d-46e0-810f-72dc79d0fb80","sdu-0c225bf6-b0a1-4353-bb80-5b524fc90ba2"],"keyword":["Curriculum","Curriculum development","Delphi Technique","Denmark","Education, Medical, Graduate","Health Services Needs and Demand","High Fidelity Simulation Training","Humans","Journal Article","Needs Assessment","Simulation