Kristian Fog","orcid":"0000-0002-5848-0911","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28805711"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/md15080253","issn":["16603397"],"issue":"8","journal":"Marine Drugs","paperid":"253","publisher":"Multidisciplinary Digital Publishing Institute (MDPI)","status":"p","title":"Marine Drugs","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85029638733"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c8c8d537-1cc6-4bd1-bb47-8d71cc04e32e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A Dereplication and Bioguided Discovery Approach to Reveal New Compounds from a Marine-Derived Fungus Stilbella fimetaria","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-364540","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND/AIMS: Congenital hyperinsulinism (CHI) is a heterogeneous disease most frequently caused by KATP-channel (ABCC8 and KCNJ11) mutations, with neonatal or later onset, variable severity, and with focal or diffuse pancreatic involvement as the two major histological types. CHI confers a high risk of neurological impairment; however, sparsely studied in larger patient series. We assessed the neurodevelopmental outcome in children with CHI at follow-up in a mixed international cohort. METHODS: In two hyperinsulinism expert centers, 75 CHI patients were included (Russian, n = 33, referred non-Scandinavian, treated in Denmark n = 27, Scandinavian, n = 15). Hospital files were reviewed. At follow-up, neurodevelopmental impairment and neurodevelopmental, cognitive and motor function scores were assessed. RESULTS: Median (range) age at follow-up was 3.7 years (3.3 months-18.2 years). Neurodevelopmental impairment was seen in 35 (47%). Impairment was associated with abnormal brain magnetic resonance imaging (MRI); odds ratio (OR) (95% CI) 15.0 (3.0-74.3), p = 0.001; lowest recorded blood glucose ≤1 mmol/L; OR 3.8 (1.3-11.3), p = 0.015, being non-Scandinavian patient, OR 3.8 (1.2-11.9), p = 0.023; and treatment delay from first symptom to expert center >5 days; OR 4.0 (1.0-16.6), trend p = 0.05. In multivariate analysis (n = 31) for early predictors with exclusion of brain MRI, treatment delay from first symptom to expert center >5 days conferred a significantly increased risk of neurodevelopment impairment, adjusted OR (aOR) 15.6 (1.6-146.7), p = 0.016, while lowest blood glucose ≤1 mmol/L had a trend toward increased risk, aOR 3.5 (1.1-14.3), p = 0.058. No associations for early vs. late disease onset, KATP-channel mutations, disease severity, focal vs. diffuse disease, or age at follow-up were seen in uni- or multivariate analysis. CONCLUSION: Not only very low blood glucose, but also insufficient treatment as expressed by delay until expert center hospitalization, increased the risk of neurodevelopmental impairment. This novel finding calls for improvements in spread of knowledge about CHI among health-care personnel and rapid contact with an expert CHI center on suspicion of CHI.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov","Melikyan, Maria","Globa, Evgenia","Shcherderkina, Inna","Portner, Fani Juel","Larsen, Anna Marie","Filipsen, Karen","Brusgaard, Klaus","Christiansen, Charlotte Dahl","Hansen, Lars Kjærsgaard","Christesen, Henrik Thybo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-619665"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU"],"country":["Russia","Ukraine"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pediatric Endocrinology, Ukrainian Centre of Endocrine Surgery,","Russian Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Congenital hyperinsulinism","Hypoglycemia","Neurodevelopmental impairment","Neurological outcome","Treatment delay"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Pediatric, Endocrinology Scientific Centre, Moscow, Russia."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"both low blood glucose and insufficient treatment confer risk of neurodevelopmental impairment in congenital hyperinsulinism a multinational cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2017.00156","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-619665","identifier":[{"id":"28740482","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85025434167","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5502348","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-a2596165-dfc6-47f1-b984-694215bdd7ed"],"keyword":["Congenital hyperinsulinism","Hypoglycemia","Neurodevelopmental impairment","Neurological outcome","Treatment delay"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2C016AA0F569748480BC34E4AD93C187"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fendo.2017.00156","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/125528780/Both_Low_Blood_Glucose_and_Insufficient_Treatment_Confer_Risk_of_Neurodevelopmental_Impairment_in_Congenital_Hyperinsulinism.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Paediatrics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ru","key":"russian academy of sciences","loc":["Russia","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Russian Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ua","key":"pediatric endocrinology ukrainian centre of endocrine surgery","loc":["Ukraine","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"Pediatric Endocrinology, Ukrainian Centre of Endocrine Surgery,","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pediatric, Endocrinology Scientific Centre, Moscow, Russia."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annett Helleskov","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"5e6d18d0-56bd-4173-808e-7be947059c9f","name":"Rasmussen, Annett Helleskov","orcid":"0000-0001-7122-4114","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"melikyanpau","last":"Melikyan","name":"Melikyan, Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Evgenia","key":"globapau","last":"Globa","name":"Globa, Evgenia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Inna","key":"shcherderkinapau","last":"Shcherderkina","name":"Shcherderkina, Inna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fani","key":"poertnerpau","last":"Poertner","locid":"b7d41fc4-a537-438d-9fde-ca7724e330e4","name":"Portner, Fani Juel","name_org":"Poertner, Fani","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna-Maria","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"99ee0494-b5ab-4375-85b0-5898a75acadf","name":"Larsen, Anna Marie","name_org":"Larsen, Anna-Maria","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"filipsenpau","last":"Filipsen","locid":"9b300892-e301-4ae3-89b0-b50f137bfed1","name":"Filipsen, Karen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Klaus","key":"brusgaardpau","last":"Brusgaard","locid":"81205519-e2e8-445f-9c7d-d74c189a9ab5","name":"Brusgaard, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0002-2096-4988","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"dahlchristiansenpau","last":"Dahl Christiansen","locid":"62f0dced-525d-459c-9d95-5452d65095c6","name":"Christiansen, Charlotte Dahl","name_org":"Dahl Christiansen, Charlotte","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Kjaersgaard","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"79b933b7-6119-448d-9632-9789032b4ab5","name":"Hansen, Lars Kjærsgaard","name_org":"Hansen, Lars Kjaersgaard","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Boye Thybo","key":"christesenpau","last":"Christesen","locid":"c8317e72-7a09-4c80-81e9-b69855b68e8f","name":"Christesen, Henrik Thybo","name_org":"Christesen, Henrik Boye Thybo","orcid":"0000-0001-5330-6853","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28740482"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fendo.2017.00156","issn":["16642392"],"issue":"JUL","journal":"Frontiers in Endocrinology","paperid":"156","publisher":"Frontiers Media","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Endocrinology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025434167"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a2596165-dfc6-47f1-b984-694215bdd7ed"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Both Low Blood Glucose and Insufficient Treatment Confer Risk of Neurodevelopmental Impairment in Congenital Hyperinsulinism : A Multinational Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-619665","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This study describes the Danish publication award system (BFI), investigates whether its built-in incentives have had an effect on publication behavior at the University of Southern Denmark, and discusses the possible future implications on researcher incentives should universities wish to measure BFI on the individual level. We analyzed publication data from the university CRIS system (Pure) and from SciVal. Several studies indicate that co-authored scholarly journal articles attract more citations than single author articles. The reason for this are not clear, however, research collaboration across institutions and countries is commonly accepted in the research community and among university managements as one way of increasing the researcher’s and institution’s reputation and impact. The BFI system is designed to award scholarly publication activity at Danish universities, especially publication in international journals of high status. However, we find that the built-in incentives leave the researcher and his or her institution with a dilemma: If the researchers optimize their performance by forming author groups with external collaborators, the optimal way of doing so for the researchers is not the optimal way seen from the perspective of the university. Our analysis shows that the typical article has 6.5 authors, two of which are internal, and that this has remained stable since the introduction of the BFI. However, there is variation across the disciplines. While ‘the Arts and Humanities’ and ‘the Social Sciences’ seem to compose author groups in a way which does not optimize the performance of the institution, both ‘Health’ and ‘the Natural Sciences’ seem to optimize according to criteria other than those specified in the BFI.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Wien, Charlotte","Dorch, Bertil F.","Larsen, Asger Væring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-628377"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bibliometrics","Citations","Information science"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contradicting incentives for research collaboration","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124677274/Wien_ea2017a.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-628377","identifier":[{"id":"85019709403","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c06c00d8-fc31-4d04-9c6b-cb8cb169f9e3"],"keyword":["Bibliometrics","Citations","Information science"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D122CD5F90031C5CF68E2308FC96D09"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/124677274/Wien_ea2017a.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Central Administration, The University Library of Southern Denmark, Forsknings- og analyseafdeling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"wienpau","last":"Wien","locid":"277f8354-05c4-44a4-b3b9-df9d557c9028","name":"Wien, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-3257-2084","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bertil F.","key":"dorchpau","last":"Dorch","locid":"da82eabd-45cb-46bf-b322-b68bb5f0294d","name":"Dorch, Bertil F.","orcid":"0000-0003-2594-6778","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Væring","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fd7856d4-9391-4ae2-9349-f9181309b577","name":"Larsen, Asger Væring","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-2637","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s11192-017-2412-0","issn":["01389130","15882861"],"issn_org":["01389130"],"issue":"2","journal":"Scientometrics","pages":"903-915","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Scientometrics","volume":"112"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019709403"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c06c00d8-fc31-4d04-9c6b-cb8cb169f9e3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Contradicting Incentives for Research Collaboration","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-628377","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"According to regulation (EC) No 854/2004 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 29 April 2004 laying down specific rules for the organisation of official controls on products of animal origin intended for human consumption. classification of production areas for live bivalve mollusks etc.3and the associated sampling plan are required to be based on so-called ‘sanitary surveys’. A sanitary survey is an assessment of the interactions between potential sources of microbial pollution, climate conditions and oceanography in the area. The EU Commission guidance for making a sanitary survey formed the basis for this report. However, in certain cases, the Danish practice for microbiological sampling frequency and classification made previously on the basis of this, as described in ‘muslingebekendtgørelsen’ is summarized in Appendix 13. The report covers production areas P1, P2, P3 and P4 within Nissum Broads. These production areas coincide currently with the algae monitoring area A1. For editorial reasons, the production areas are regarded under one term as ‘Nissum Broads’, acknowledging that the four production areas only include a proportion of Nissum Broards. The covered production areas within Nissum Broads are marked as A1 on the maps in this report. The report recommends a microbiological sampling plan consisting of recommended selected sampling points and sampling frequencies for individual production areas. It is further discussed whether merging of production areas into fewer production areas could be considered in the future. This merge would then reduce the number of sampling points, without compromising food safety. The report is supported by public available data from monitoring of microbiological contamination in Nissum Broads, where the concentration of E. coli is determined in samples of mussels, etc. taken at different sampling points within each area. The report points to the most precautionary fixed sampling points for future monitoring In summary, the sanitary survey of Nissum Broads identifies an area that in general is a microbial homogeneous, stable and microbiologically clean area, and only rare occurrences of critical microbial contamination were found.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Martin Mørk","Jakobsen, Hans","Göke, Cordula","Hendriksen, Niels Bohse","Koefoed Rømer, Jonas","Mohn, Christian","Schultz, Anna Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-089.66-015500"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["E coli","Fiskeri","Mikrobiologisk forurening","Muslinger","Nissum Bredning","Sanitary survey","Toskallede bløddyr"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sanitary survey rapport 000000000002 nissum bredning","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dce2.au.dk/pub/TR100.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.66-015500","ids":["au-27d0db7a-8c08-424e-9d19-e0fee0e926c7","dtu-73044824-a4df-4ee3-9894-2bb85f2fa282"],"keyword":["E. coli","Nissum Bredning","Toskallede bløddyrw","fiskeri","mikrobiologisk forurening","muslinger","sanitary survey","toskallede bløddyr"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-0061B2206F043D6DF63249FFC2E8FBB0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dce2.au.dk/pub/TR100.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Diversity and Experimental Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Microbial Food Safety"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Mørk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d24cdbff-3543-4170-b95f-c315ce7477bb","name":"Larsen, Martin Mørk","orcid":"0000-0003-4331-8548","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"115e2890-be07-49a8-a340-d271dd22ac2b","name":"Jakobsen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0001-9590-2362","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cordula","key":"gökepau","last":"Göke","locid":"203ca293-fd97-4b16-8eba-24b61d042e20","name":"Göke, Cordula","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bohse","key":"hendriksenpau","last":"Hendriksen","locid":"50fd9962-24ef-4560-9838-1bb6da39e607","name":"Hendriksen, Niels Bohse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"koefoedrømerpau","last":"Koefoed Rømer","locid":"02a85068-d9f1-4a76-a2f6-b5751937ada4","name":"Koefoed Rømer, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8895-2529","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"mohnpau","last":"Mohn","locid":"3249f637-7852-40ab-b6ac-1b8670bcd9c9","name":"Mohn, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-4331-1365","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna Charlotte","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"3a3d5130-acf6-4846-93e3-f3b891d83e60","name":"Schultz, Anna Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1484-9120","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"100","pages":"112","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Teknisk rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 100","series":"Teknisk rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-27d0db7a-8c08-424e-9d19-e0fee0e926c7","dtu-73044824-a4df-4ee3-9894-2bb85f2fa282"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Sanitary survey rapport 2: Nissum Bredning","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.66-015500","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The amount of animal manure used in modern agriculture is increasing due to the increase in global animal production. Pig slurry is known to contain zoonotic bacteria such as E. coli, Salmonella spp. and Campylobacter spp., and viruses such as hepatitis E virus and group A rotavirus. Coliform bacteria, present in manure, have previously been shown to leach into tile drains. This poses a potential threat to aquatic environments and may also influence the quality of drinking water. As knowledge is especially scarce about the fate of viruses when applied to fields in natural settings, this project sets out to investigate the leaching potential of six different microorganisms: E. coli and Enterococcus spp. (detected by colony assay), somatic coliphages (using plaque assays), and hepatitis E virus, porcine circovirus type 2, and group A rotavirus (by real-time polymerase chain reaction). All six microorganisms leached through the soil entering the tile drains situated at 1-m depth the first day following pig slurry application. The leaching pattern of group A rotavirus differed substantially from the pattern for somatic coliphages, which are otherwise used as indicators for virus contamination. Furthermore, group A rotavirus was detected in monitoring wells at 3.5-m depth up to 2 months after pig slurry application. The detection of viral genomic material in drainage water and shallow groundwater signifies a potential hazard to human health that needs to be investigated further, as water reservoirs used for recreational use and drinking water are potentially contaminated with zoonotic pathogens.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Krog, J S","Forslund, A","Larsen, L E","Dalsgaard, A.","Kjaer, J.","Olsen, Preben","Schultz, A. C."],"cuid":["S03-098.21-014031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Agriculture","Groundwater monitoring","Health","Pathogen","Solute transport"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"leaching of viruses and other microorganisms naturally occurring in pig slurry to tile drains on a well structured loamy field in denmark","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10040-016-1530-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.21-014031","identifier":[{"id":"85011630027","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-13ddebe2-35fd-4af0-b2cd-0e4513c4eb44","dtu-f29bf606-9611-43c3-8e55-e4d102095f3c","ku-493aad34-82ed-4333-8c79-1a06e1d1b1cb"],"keyword":["Agriculture","Groundwater monitoring","Health","Pathogen","Solute transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-51960862CDE531760E1EEAB039047323"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/179667930/10.1007_2Fs10040_016_1530_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10040-016-1530-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/134462801/10.1007_2Fs10040_016_1530_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Food Safety and Zoonoses"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"geus geological survey of denmark and greenland","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-GEUS","l3nn":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"GEUS Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","namevar":["Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-GEUS","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology, Department of Agroecology - Soil Physics and Hydropedology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anita","key":"forslundpau","last":"Forslund","locid":"50e7ab83-b763-4eed-a70e-31d5fe24f3b1","name":"Forslund, Anita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3