ewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8c411fa7-bf90-48b2-b026-c0e39bc938e0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Is Lumbosacral Plexus Block an Effective and Safe Alternative as Surgical Anesthesia for Total Hip Replacement?","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-209343","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we explore tramp ship routing and scheduling. Tramp ships operate much like taxies following the available demand. Tramp operators can determine some of their demand in advance by entering into long-term contracts and then try to maximise profits from optional voyages found in the spot market. Routing and scheduling a tramp fleet to best utilise fleet capacity according to current demand is therefore an ongoing and complicated problem. Here we add further complexity to the routing and scheduling problem by incorporating voyage separation requirements that enforce a minimum time spread between some voyages. The incorporation of these separation requirements helps balance the conflicting objectives of maximising profit for the tramp operator and minimising inventory costs for the charterer, since these costs increase if similar voyages are not performed with some separation in time. We have developed a new and exact branch-and-price procedure for this problem. We use a dynamic programming algorithm to generate columns and describe a time window branching scheme used to enforce the voyage separation requirements which we relax in the master problem. Computational results show that our algorithm in general finds optimal solutions very quickly and performs much faster compared to an earlier a priori path generation method. Finally, we compare our method to an earlier adaptive large neighbourhood search heuristic and find that on similar-sized instances our approach generally uses less time to find the optimal solution than the adaptive large neighbourhood search method uses to find a heuristic solution.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Lusby, Richard Martin","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-327394"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exact algorithms","Maritime transport","Optimization","Scheduling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tramp ship routing and scheduling with voyage separation requirements","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/133955432/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-327394","identifier":[{"id":"85019004841","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-4cb2011e-23e9-4560-8653-8d9aad00a70e"],"keyword":["Exact algorithms","Maritime transport","Optimization","Scheduling","Spread requirement"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-527A2CF1DE3EB4F237D18913F40C7D28"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/133955432/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science, Operations Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard Martin","key":"lusbypau","last":"Lusby","locid":"51599544-7991-404d-b9a7-ec2f5ad4824b","name":"Lusby, Richard Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-8652-6219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00291-017-0480-4","issn":["01716468","14366304"],"issn_org":["01716468"],"issue":"4","journal":"OR Spectrum - Quantitative Approaches in Management","pages":"913-943","publisher":"Springer Verlag","status":"p","title":"OR Spectrum - Quantitative Approaches in Management","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019004841"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-4cb2011e-23e9-4560-8653-8d9aad00a70e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tramp ship routing and scheduling with voyage separation requirements","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-327394","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Hansen, Mette Sif","Krog, Jesper Schak","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Chriél, Mariann","Larsen, Lars Erik","Kokotovic, Branko"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334396"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Mink"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lungebetændelse hos mink med ansamlinger af mononukleære inflammationsceller","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/130796216/DTU1.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334396","ids":["dtu-6413636d-6a1a-41cb-a512-1afbf3d29494"],"keyword":["mink","non-suppurative pneumonia"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1A718995DE4B14491EAEF8273A3DEFB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/130796216/DTU1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Sif","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"5d04b165-7fc1-46cf-88f7-35be695b954c","name":"Hansen, Mette Sif","orcid":"0000-0002-8132-8475","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mariann","key":"chriélpau","last":"Chriél","locid":"1a5d6261-6bd2-4940-baab-5d5fcc3c0f7c","name":"Chriél, Mariann","orcid":"0000-0001-5306-4495","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Branko","key":"kokotovicpau","last":"Kokotovic","locid":"0bd94224-b86f-40a5-9bb1-3c8215d8a2e5","name":"Kokotovic, Branko","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"113-119","place":"Aarhus N","publisher":"Kopenhagen Fur","status":"p","title":"Faglig årsberetning 2016 : Kopenhagen Fur"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6413636d-6a1a-41cb-a512-1afbf3d29494"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Lungebetændelse hos mink med ansamlinger af mononukleære inflammationsceller","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334396","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"De senere år er der i flere tilfælde fundet influenzavirus i mink med kompliceret og dødelig lungebetændelse. I Danmark rekvireres undersøgelse for influenzavirus imidlertid kun sjældent i forbindelse med diagnostiske indsendelser fra syge mink. Derfor undersøges der i reglen kun for influenzavirus, hvis der opstår mistanke om influenza ved obduktionen, eller hvis der er alvorlige langvarige udbrud. For at kunne iværksætte foranstaltninger, der begrænser forekomsten af influenza hos mink, er det nødvendigt at kende udbredelsen af influenzavirus blandt farmede mink i Danmark. Formålet med denne undersøgelse var at gennemføre en systematisk overvågning af forekomsten af influenzavirus i lungerne fra mink indsendt til diagnostisk undersøgelse på DTU Veterinærinstituttet uanset årsag. Der blev indsamlet materiale i 2016 i perioden fra sommer til pelsning og desuden indgik mink anvendt til et minkobduktionskursus, samt vilde mink. Der blev påvist influenza A virus i mink fra otte farme. Genetiske analyser indikerede, at disse virus stammede fra både danske svin og mennesker. For at forebygge udbrud af influenza i farmede mink anbefales det, at undgå kontakt mellem mink og influenzasyge personer, samt sikre at minkfoder indeholdende biprodukter fra slagtesvin er varmebehandlet eller inaktiveret på anden vis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Krog, Jesper Schak","Larsen, Gitte","Chriél, Mariann","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-367343"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane"],"keyword":["Influenza A virus","Mink"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mink kan også have influenza","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/146465068/Mink_kan_ogs_have_influenza.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-367343","ids":["dtu-d213c907-c28f-4db4-aff3-75aaaec5c5be"],"keyword":["Influenza A virus","Mink","Zoonose"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3F5E7F3C008760D8011279A3B715A7FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/146465068/Mink_kan_ogs_have_influenza.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagercharlottekristianepau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogjesperschakpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"larsengittepau","last":"Larsen","locid":"ea426e5f-93bd-48f5-a3c8-e5f8004413a7","name":"Larsen, Gitte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mariann","key":"chriélmariannpau","last":"Chriél","locid":"1a5d6261-6bd2-4940-baab-5d5fcc3c0f7c","name":"Chriél, Mariann","orcid":"0000-0001-5306-4495","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["24459437"],"journal":"Faglig Årsberetning","pages":"102-105","publisher":"Kopenhagen Fur","status":"p","title":"Faglig Årsberetning","volume":"2017"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d213c907-c28f-4db4-aff3-75aaaec5c5be"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Mink kan også have influenza","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-367343","year":"2017","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To examine the association between retinal vessel diameters and retinopathy in participants with and without type 2 diabetes in a Danish population-based cohort. METHODS: The study included 878 persons aged 30 to 60 years from the Inter99 Eye Study. Retinopathy was defined as a presence of one or more retinal hemorrhages or one or more microaneurysms. Vessel diameters were expressed as central retinal artery equivalent diameter (CRAE) and central retinal vein equivalent diameter (CRVE). Multiple linear regression analyses were performed. RESULTS: Among participants with diabetes, CRAE was 6.3 µm (CI 95%: 1.0 to 11.6, p = 0.020) wider and CRVE was 7.9 µm (CI 95%: 0.7 to 15.2, p = 0.030) wider in those with retinopathy compared to those without retinopathy, after adjusting for age, gender, HbA1c, blood pressure, smoking, serum total and HDL cholesterol. In all participants, CRAE increased with presence of retinopathy (p = 0.005) and with smoking (p = 0.001), and CRAE decreased with hypertension (p < 0.001), high HDL cholesterol (p = 0.016) and age (p < 0.001). Central retinal vein equivalent diameter increased with presence of retinopathy (p = 0.022) and with smoking (p < 0.001), and decreased with higher HDL cholesterol (p < 0.001) and age (p = 0.015). Female gender was associated with wider CRVE (p = 0.029). CONCLUSIONS: Wider retinal vessel diameters were associated with the presence of retinopathy in participants with diabetes, but not in participants without diabetes. The associations between retinal vessel diameters and known retinopathy risk factors were confirmed. These results suggest that information obtained by non-invasive imaging of the interior of the eye can contribute to a better understanding of systemic disease processes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Drobnjak, Dragana","Munch, Inger Christine","Glümer, Charlotte","Færch, Kristine","Kessel, Line","Larsen, Michael","Veiby, Nina C B B"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-402425"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"relationship between retinal vessel diameters and retinopathy in the inter000000000099 eye study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcte.2017.03.002","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-402425","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5651334","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29067255","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85017166938","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-0f1a97b9-a533-4b0b-96eb-0898b6967fef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B10904E89DE53905A7BB4531532652DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/194637362/1_s2.0_S2214623717300029.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcte.2017.03.002","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Dragana","key":"drobnjakpau","last":"Drobnjak","name":"Drobnjak, Dragana","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","locid":"a1af1ee5-c4b4-44d8-a7af-b7c1ce0882ac","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"glümerpau","last":"Glümer","name":"Glümer, Charlotte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kristine","key":"færchpau","last":"Færch","name":"Færch, Kristine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","locid":"3201472a-2f23-417e-bd01-a7950e2ff370","name":"Kessel, Line","orcid":"0000-0002-9375-1510","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nina C B B","key":"veibypau","last":"Veiby","name":"Veiby, Nina C B B","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29067255"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcte.2017.03.002","issn":["22146237"],"journal":"Journal of Clinical and Translational Endocrinology","pages":"22-28","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical and Translational Endocrinology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017166938"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0f1a97b9-a533-4b0b-96eb-0898b6967fef"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Relationship between retinal vessel diameters and retinopathy in the Inter99 Eye Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-402425","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: General health promoting campaigns are often not targeted at the people who need them the most. Web- and app-based tools are a new way to reach, motivate, and help people with poor health status. OBJECTIVE: The aim of our study was to test a Web- and mobile app-based tool (\"SoSu-life\") on employees in the social welfare and health care sector in Denmark. METHODS: A randomized controlled trial was carried out as a workplace intervention. The tool was designed to help users make healthy lifestyle changes such as losing weight, exercise more, and quit smoking. A team competition between the participating workplaces took place during the first 16 weeks of the intervention. Twenty nursing homes for elderly people in 6 municipalities in Denmark participated in the study. The employees at the nursing homes were randomized either 1:1 or 2:1 on a municipality level to use the SoSu-life tool or to serve as a control group with no intervention. All participants underwent baseline measurements including body weight, waist circumference, body fat percentage, blood pressure, and blood cholesterol level and they filled in a questionnaire covering various aspects of health. The participants were measured again after 16 and 38 weeks. RESULTS: A total of 566 (SoSu-life: n=355, control: n=211) participants were included in the study. At 16 weeks there were 369 participants still in the study (SoSu-life: n=227, control: n=142) and 269 participants completed the 38 week intervention (SoSu-life: n=152, control: n=117). At 38 weeks, the SoSu-life group had a larger decrease in body weight (-1.01 kg, P=.03), body fat percentage (-0.8%, P=.03), and waist circumference (-1.8 cm, P=.007) compared with the control group. CONCLUSIONS: The SoSu-life Web- and app-based tool had a modest yet beneficial effect on body weight and body fat percentage in the health care sector staff. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinicaltrials.gov NCT02438059; http://clinicaltrials.gov/ct2/show/NCT02438059 (Archived by WebCite at http://www.webcitation.org/6i6y4p2AS).","author_count":3,"contributors":["Balk-Møller, Nina Charlotte","Poulsen, Sanne Kellebjerg","Larsen, Thomas Meinert"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-466466"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of a nine month web and app based workplace intervention to promote healthy lifestyle and weight loss for employees in the social welfare and health care sector a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/jmir.6196","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-466466","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5404146","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28396303","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85018724956","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-79fd7f5a-9caf-4492-81f7-369fc9f3de82"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CA974AA1FDE42A3DF3B74B95981E95AC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/jmir.6196","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/184673357/Balk_M_ller_et_al_Journal_of_Medical_Internet_Research_2017_Vol_19_4_e108.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nina Charlotte","key":"balkmøllerpau","last":"Balk-Møller","locid":"84d79d17-8272-4ed8-855c-504511d901b8","name":"Balk-Møller, Nina Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-8457-2916","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sanne Kellebjerg","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"789e64f3-7deb-45c2-8f4b-5b8695aee785","name":"Poulsen, Sanne Kellebjerg","orcid":"0000-0003-4897-3955","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Meinert","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"be620f10-2a0e-430c-94d1-5246c8ef122a","name":"Larsen, Thomas Meinert","orcid":"0000-0001-7621-3131","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28396303"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/jmir.6196","issn":["14388871","14394456"],"issn_org":["14394456"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","paperid":"e108","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018724956"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-79fd7f5a-9caf-4492-81f7-369fc9f3de82"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of a nine-month web- and app-based workplace intervention to promote healthy lifestyle and weight loss for employees in the social welfare and health care sector : A randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466466","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"According to the Regulation for food products of animal origin (Europa Parlamentets og Rådets Forordning (EF) Nr. 854), microbiological classification of production areas for live bivalve mollusks etc.3 and the associated sampling plan are required to be based on a so-called ‘sanitary surveys’. A sanitary survey is an assessment of the interactions between potential sources of microbial pollution, climate conditions and oceanography in the area. The EU Commission guidance for making a sanitary survey formed the basis for this report. However, in certain cases, the Danish practice for microbiological sampling frequency and classification made previously on the basis of this, as described in ‘muslingebekendtgørelsen’ is summarized in Appendix 13. The report covers production areas (P)16, P33, P34, P35, P36, P37, P38 and P39 in Løgstør Broads. These production areas coincide currently with the algae area A6. For editorial reasons, the production areas are regarded under one term “Løgstør Broads’, knowing that the production areas also include other bordering geographical areas. The covered production areas within Løgstør Broads are marked as A6 The report recommends a microbiological sampling plan consisting of recommended selected sampling points and sampling frequencies for individual production areas. It is further discussed whether merging of production areas into fewer production areas could be considered in the future. This merge would then reduce the number of sampling points, without compromising food safety. The report is supported by public assessible data from monitoring of microbiological contamination in Løgstør Broads, where the concentration of E. coli is determined in samples of mussels, etc. taken at fixed sampling points. The Danish monitoring of production areas for live bivalve mollusks offers generally a solid set of historical data of E. coli concentrations in clams etc. collected from the positions where mussels have been harvested in the past in Løgstør Broads. The key data set used is the classification of production areas based on samples taken during the past 10 years (2007-2016). Within this data set, 99.2 % of a total of 908 samples contain E. coli A level (<230 E. coli/100 g), and 0 % of a total of 350 samples contain Salmonella. In summary, the sanitary survey of Løgstør Broads identifies an area that in general is a microbial homogeneous, stable and microbiologically clean area, and only rare occurrence of critical microbial contamination were found.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Martin Mørk","Jakobsen, Hans","Göke, Cordula","Hendriksen, Niels Bohse","Koefoed Rømer, Jonas","Mohn, Christian","Schultz, Anna Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-086.21-029216"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["E coli","Fiskeri","Løgstør Bredning","Mikrobiologisk forurening","Muslinger","Sanitary survey","Toskallede bløddyr"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sanitary survey af produktionsområder i løgstør bredning","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dce2.au.dk/pub/TR99.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.21-029216","ids":["au-e47523f8-2daf-4aa3-8b83-71cc44f0ca56","dtu-7b82dbe5-734a-4691-b2ca-c3dd1ed2a391"],"keyword":["E. Coli","Fiskeri","Løgstør Bredning","Mikrobiologisk forurening","Muslinger","Sanitary survey","Toskallede bløddyr"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-3D9D66C67E3DB6C434ADFE754F6A82B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dce2.au.dk/pub/TR99.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Diversity and Experimental Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Microbial Food Safety"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Mørk","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d24cdbff-3543-4170-b95f-c315ce7477bb","name":"Larsen, Martin Mørk","orcid":"0000-0003-4331-8548","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"115e2890-be07-49a8-a340-d271dd22ac2b","name":"Jakobsen, Hans","orcid":"0000-0001-9590-2362","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cordula","key":"gökepau","last":"Göke","locid":"203ca293-fd97-4b16-8eba-24b61d042e20","name":"Göke, Cordula","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Bohse","key":"hendriksenpau","last":"Hendriksen","locid":"50fd9962-24ef-4560-9838-1bb6da39e607","name":"Hendriksen, Niels Bohse","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"koefoedrømerpau","last":"Koefoed Rømer","locid":"02a85068-d9f1-4a76-a2f6-b5751937ada4","name":"Koefoed Rømer, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-8895-2529","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"mohnpau","last":"Mohn","locid":"3249f637-7852-40ab-b6ac-1b8670bcd9c9","name":"Mohn, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-4331-1365","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna Charlotte","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"3a3d5130-acf6-4846-93e3-f3b891d83e60","name":"Schultz, Anna Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1484-9120","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"99","pages":"128","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","repno":"Teknisk rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi, No. 99","series":"Teknisk rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-e47523f8-2daf-4aa3-8b83-71cc44f0ca56","dtu-7b82dbe5-734a-4691-b2ca-c3dd1ed2a391"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Sanitary survey af produktionsområder i Løgstør Bredning","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.21-029216","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Denne sanitary survey vurderer de potentielle mikrobiologiske forureningskilder, der kan have betydning for muslingeproduktionen i Venø Bugt, Venø Sund, Kås Bredning, Salling Sund, Lysen Bredning, Dråby Vig og Fur Sund (produktionsområderne 5-9 og 12-15). Det undersøgte område er underopdelt i en række produktionsområder, der er vurderet hver for sig. Bakterien E. coli er anvendt som indikator for mikrobiologisk forurening. I en række appendikser er der beskrevet potentielle kilder til mikrobiologisk forurening og muligheden for spredning eller nedbrydning af eventuel forurening ud fra de fysiske forhold i området. Hvert appendiks afsluttes med en kort konklusion. Datagrundlaget for rapporten er offentligt tilgængelige data og omfatter statistiske kilder for spildevand, husdyr og landbrug m.m. i tilgrænsende kommuner samt muslingefiskeriets egenkontrol og myndighedernes verifikation af denne. Det konkluderes i rapporten, at det undersøgte område generelt er karakteriseret ved lave forekomster af E. coli, med kun få observationer af E. coli i kritiske koncentrationer. Rapporten indeholder forslag til en prøvetagningsplan, som tager udgangspunkt i EU’s retningslinjer for overvågning af mikrobiologisk forurening af muslinger m.m","author_count":7,"contributors":["Larsen, Martin Mørk","Jakobsen, Hans","Göke, Cordula","Hendriksen, Niels Bohse","Koefoed Rømer, Jonas","Mohn, Christian","Schultz, Anna Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-092.55-016376"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Dråby Vig","E coli","Fiskeri","Fur Sund","Kås Bredring","Lysen Bredning","Mikrobiologisk forurening","Muslinger","Salling Sund","Sanitary survey","Toskallede bløddyr","Venø Bugt","Venø Sund"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sanitary survey rapport 000000000003 venø bugt kås og salling","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139329767/TR104.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.55-016376","ids":["au-3376846e-3c11-4c78-bb3e-adba1fd5e620","dtu-41165042-4046-483e-95c7-6c37433f7e52"],"keyword":["Dråby Vig","E. coli","Fur Sund","Kås Bredring","Lysen Bredning","Salling Sund","Venø Bugt","Venø Sund","fiskeri","mikrobiologisk forurening","muslinger","sanitary survey","toskallede bløddyr"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-2D1ED2978888D0496774920C22A49D8B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/139329767/TR104.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dce2.au.dk/pub/TR104.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Diversity and Experimental Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute, Research Group for Microbial Food Safety"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin Mørk","key":"larsenpau