{"abstract":"This report describes a triple-reassortant influenza A virus with a HA that resembles H3 of human seasonal influenza from 2004 to 2005, N2 from influenza A virus already established in swine, and the internal gene cassette from A(H1N1)pdm09 has spread in Danish pig herds. The virus has been detected in several Danish pig herds during the last 2-3 years and may possess a challenge for human as well as animal health.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Krog, Jesper Schak","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Michael Albin","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-305612"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Case report","H1N1pdm09","H3N2","Influenza A virus","Zoonosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"triple reassortant influenza a virus with h000000000003 of human seasonal origin na of swine origin and internal a h000000000001n000000000001 pandemic 000000002009 genes is established in danish pigs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132188706/Krog_et_al_2017_Influenza_and_Other_Respiratory_Viruses_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-305612","identifier":[{"id":"28245096","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85017098832","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5410721","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-037505e0-98f6-49cd-9191-d5065ed988f8"],"keyword":["H1N1pdm09","H3N2","case report","influenza A virus","zoonosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3532AD0BF075B3B69BE465F39245B6CC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/132188706/Krog_et_al_2017_Influenza_and_Other_Respiratory_Viruses_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Merial Norden A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogjesperschakpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagercharlottekristianepau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Albin","key":"larsenmichaelalbinpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Michael Albin","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenlarserikpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28245096"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/irv.12451","issn":["17502640","17502659"],"issn_org":["17502640"],"issue":"3","journal":"Influenza and Other Respiratory Viruses","pages":"298-303","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Influenza and Other Respiratory Viruses","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85017098832"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","merial norden a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-037505e0-98f6-49cd-9191-d5065ed988f8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Triple-reassortant influenza A virus with H3 of human seasonal origin, NA of swine origin, and internal A(H1N1) pandemic 2009 genes is established in Danish pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-305612","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This presentation addresses a tramp routing and scheduling problem. Tramp ships operate like taxies by following the available demand, as opposed to liner ships that operate like busses on a fixed route network according to a published timetable. Tramp operators determine some of the demand in advance by ensuring long-term contracts. The rest of the demand comes from optional voyages found in the spot market. Routing and scheduling a tramp feet to best utilize feet capacity according to the current demand is therefore an ongoing and complicated problem. We add further complexity by incorporating voyage separation requirements that enforce a minimum time spread between some voyages. We developed a new and exact Branch-and-Price procedure for this problem. A dynamic programming algorithm generates columns, while a novel time window branching scheme is used to enforce the voyage separation requirements. Computational results show that the algorithm finds optimal solutions very quickly for the vast majority of test instances. We compare the results with two earlier published methods and show that our Branch-and-Price approach outperforms both an a priori path generation method and an Adaptive Large Neighbourhood Search heuristic.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Jesper","Lusby, Richard Martin","Vilhelmsen, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313282"],"event":{"end":"2017-07-21","place":"Québec City, ca","start":"2017-07-17","title":"IFORS 2017","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tramp ship routing and scheduling with voyage separation requirements","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-313282","ids":["dtu-1d2cee6e-b770-4dba-aa15-36de67983c51"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E71A6A269DD6F09C1D13D563706B822A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science, Operations Research","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Transport DTU"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard Martin","key":"lusbypau","last":"Lusby","locid":"51599544-7991-404d-b9a7-ec2f5ad4824b","name":"Lusby, Richard Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-8652-6219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1d2cee6e-b770-4dba-aa15-36de67983c51"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tramp ship routing and scheduling with voyage separation requirements","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313282","year":"2017","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Studies from Eastern European countries proved that porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus Type 1 (PRRSV-1) harbours high genetic diversity and that genetically divergent subtypes 2-4 circulate in this area. In the present study, we compared the pathogenicity of two different PRRSV-1 subtype 2 strains and a strain representing PRRSV-1 subtype 1. Four groups of 8-week-old specific pathogen free pigs were either infected with subtype 2 strain ILI6, subtype 2 strain or BOR59, subtype 1 strain 18794, or mock inoculated. The most pronounced clinical signs were observed in pigs infected with BOR59. Pigs from both subtype 2 strain infected groups exhibited significantly elevated mean body temperatures on DPI 2 compared to the other two groups, the difference remaining significant up to DPI 13 for the BOR59 group, only. The pigs in the latter group also displayed significantly highest levels of early viremia together with the most rapid APP response. Overall, the results indicated that BOR59 strain can be considered a highly pathogenic strain, similarly to subtype 3 strains Lena and SU1-bel, while the virulence of the other subtype 2 strain ILI6 was intermediate between BOR59 and subtype 1 strain.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Stadejek, Tomasz","Larsen, Lars Erik","Podgórska, Katarzyna","Bøtner, Anette","Botti, Sara","Dolka, Izabella","Fabisiak, Michał","Heegaard, Peter M. H.","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Huć, Tomasz","Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Sapierzyński, Rafał","Nielsen, Jens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334250"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Veterinary Research Institute","Parco Technologico Padano","Warsaw University of Life Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pathogenicity of three genetically diverse strains of prrsv type 000000000001 in specific pathogen free pigs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85019770214","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334250","identifier":[{"id":"85019770214","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28554869","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-63a5003d-0234-48ec-a941-367065f2e231"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E0B266B7E53266D00E32B6F0B47AF731"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"pl","key":"warsaw university of life sciences","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Warsaw University of Life Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pl","key":"national veterinary research institute","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"National Veterinary Research Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"it","key":"parco technologico padano","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Parco Technologico Padano","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasz","key":"stadejekpau","last":"Stadejek","name":"Stadejek, Tomasz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars E","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","name_org":"Larsen, Lars E","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Katarzyna","key":"podgórskapau","last":"Podgórska","name":"Podgórska, Katarzyna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anette","key":"bøtnerpau","last":"Bøtner","locid":"70ad6406-3b8c-4e50-95f5-b0f448fc69ea","name":"Bøtner, Anette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"bottipau","last":"Botti","name":"Botti, Sara","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Izabella","key":"dolkapau","last":"Dolka","name":"Dolka, Izabella","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michał","key":"fabisiakpau","last":"Fabisiak","name":"Fabisiak, Michał","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Mikael Helweg","key":"heegaardpau","last":"Heegaard","locid":"f15c1dfb-4275-4369-9b2b-2af936d2e0e6","name":"Heegaard, Peter M. H.","name_org":"Heegaard, Peter Mikael Helweg","orcid":"0000-0003-4506-4932","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tomasz","key":"hućpau","last":"Huć","name":"Huć, Tomasz","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"58ce239f-6c30-44e0-ab54-f017a1821425","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafał","key":"sapierzyńskipau","last":"Sapierzyński","name":"Sapierzyński, Rafał","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"34511f38-e2d9-41d2-a82f-1044f16d784c","name":"Nielsen, Jens","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28554869"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.vetmic.2017.05.011","issn":["03781135","18732542"],"issn_org":["03781135"],"journal":"Veterinary Microbiology","pages":"13-19","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Veterinary Microbiology","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019770214"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-63a5003d-0234-48ec-a941-367065f2e231"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Pathogenicity of three genetically diverse strains of PRRSV Type 1 in specific pathogen free pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334250","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Sludge treatment reed bed (STRB) systems combine dewatering, stabilisation and long-term storage of sludge. The main objective of this study was to investigate how substance concentrations change in the sludge residue during treatment and to conduct substance flow analyses covering the flow of substances in an STRB system over a 12-year treatment period, followed by three months' post-treatment in a stockpile area (SPA). Samples of sludge, reject water and sludge residue of different ages were collected at two Danish STRB system facilities and analysed for content of relevant substances. Concentrations of carbon and nitrogen in the sludge residue residing in an STRB system changed as a function of treatment time, mainly due to mineralisation; only a negligible part was lost to reject water. Considering metals and phosphorus, the main share was accumulated in the sludge residue; only minor fractions were lost to mineralisation or reject water. Post-treatment in an SPA resulted in an increase in dry matter content from 24% to 32%. After treatment, the concentrations of heavy metals (lead, cadmium, nickel, zinc, copper and chromium) in the sludge residue met the threshold values stated by the Danish Environmental Protection Agency and the EU.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Julie Dam","Nielsen, Steen M","Scheutz, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334776"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Heavy metals","Nitrogen","Phosphorus","Sewage sludge"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-WSP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-WSP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of a danish sludge treatment reed bed system and a stockpile area using substance flow analysis","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85034660066","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334776","identifier":[{"id":"85034660066","type":"scopus"},{"id":"wst_2017_348","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29144287","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-6550ac25-c016-46ed-97fb-9cd03261196f"],"keyword":["fertiliser quality","heavy metals","nitrogen","phosphorus","sewage sludge","sludge residue"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D8AE5B9F26948AF0F807BB3DD692223"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Residual Resource Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"wsp danmark","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-WSP","l3nl":"WSP Danmark A/S","l3nn":"WSP Danmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"WSP Danmark","namevar":["Orbicon"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-WSP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Julie Dam","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"96983a7c-0a55-45a8-a10e-759b599e33a3","name":"Larsen, Julie Dam","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen M","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Steen M","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"scheutzpau","last":"Scheutz","locid":"48fe2850-fdc6-4282-9b97-ac5773419e5c","name":"Scheutz, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-2218-5934","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29144287"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2166/wst.2017.348","issn":["02731223","19969732"],"issn_org":["02731223"],"issue":"9","journal":"Water Science and Technology","pages":"2291-2303","publisher":"IWA Publishing","status":"p","title":"Water Science and Technology","volume":"76"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85034660066"],"sdg":["2. Zero Hunger","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","WSP Danmark A/S"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6550ac25-c016-46ed-97fb-9cd03261196f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Assessment of a Danish sludge treatment reed bed system and a stockpile area, using substance flow analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334776","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Introduction. Swine influenza is a respiratory disease caused by multiple subtypes of influenza A virus (IAV). The genome of IAV consists of 8 segments and subtype classification is based on the surface glycoproteins hemagglutinin (HA) and neuraminidase (NA). In Denmark, the influenza screening test and subsequent subtyping is performed by real time RT-PCR (RT-qPCR) but several assays are needed to cover the wide range of circulating subtypes which is expensive,resource and time demanding. To mitigate these restrictions the high-throughput qPCR platform BioMark (Fluidigm) has been explored. The BioMark platform uses less sample and reagent volume compared to standard qPCR platforms and allows for up to 9,216 parallel reactions on one chip. Materials and methods. A total of 14 PCR assays specific for the different subtypes of HA and NA genes relevant for swine influenza and 6 assays specific for the internal genes of IAV were validated and optimised to run under identical reaction conditions and assembled on a dynamic array chip (Fluidigm). Results. The sensitivity and specificity of the chip was assessed by testing cell culture isolates and field samples with known subtypes (based on sequencing). The results revealed that the performance of the dynamic chip was similar to conventional real time analysis. Discussion and conclusion. Application of the chip for subtyping of swine influenza has resulted in a significant reduction in time, cost and working hours. Thereby, it is possible to offer diagnostic services with reduced price and turnover time which will facilitate choice of vaccines and by that lead to reduction of antibiotic used.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","Krog, Jesper Schak","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Skovgaard, Kerstin","Harder, T.","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-343066"],"event":{"end":"2017-05-05","place":"Prague, cz","start":"2017-05-03","title":"9th European Symposium of Porcine Health Management (ESPHM 2017)","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"subtyping of swine influenza viruses using a high throughput real time pcr platform","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/140539921/ESPHM2017_Proceedings_SIV_Fluidigm_chip.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-343066","ids":["dtu-80e09bd3-04ae-4ec7-ae79-317a79a86a10"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E49A5B3F532313BFBBC841441668D5C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/140539921/ESPHM2017_Proceedings_SIV_Fluidigm_chip.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division for Diagnostics & Scientific Advice, Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"friedrich loeffler institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicole Bakkegård","key":"goeckepau","last":"Goecke","locid":"4d2ddf87-a082-462e-86c4-567264391d29","name":"Goecke, Nicole Bakkegård","orcid":"0000-0003-4948-9946","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kerstin","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"2c3c3868-b5a3-457b-8b97-9645ad03e405","name":"Skovgaard, Kerstin","orcid":"0000-0001-5663-4879","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"T.","key":"harderpau","last":"Harder","name":"Harder, T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-80e09bd3-04ae-4ec7-ae79-317a79a86a10"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Subtyping of swine influenza viruses using a high-throughput real time PCR platform","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-343066","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: An increasing number of Web- and app-based tools for health promotion are being developed at the moment. The ambition is generally to reach out to a larger part of the population and to help users improve their lifestyle and develop healthier habits, and thereby improve their health status. However, the positive effects are generally modest. To understand why the effects are modest, further investigation into the participants' experiences and the social aspects of using Web- and app-based health promotion tools is needed. OBJECTIVE: The objectives of this study were to investigate the motivation behind taking part in and using a Web- and app-based health promotion tool (SoSu-life) at the workplace and to explore the participants' experiences with using the tool. METHODS: Qualitative interviews with 26 participants who participated in a 38-week randomized controlled trial of a workplace Web- and app-based tool for health promotion were conducted. Data were supplemented with tracking the frequency of use. The basic features of the tool investigated in the trial were self-reporting of diet and exercise, personalized feedback, suggestions for activities and programs, practical tips and tricks, and a series of social features designed to support and build interactions among the participants at the workplace. RESULTS: The respondents reported typically one of the two reasons for signing up to participate in the study: either a personal wish to attain some health benefits or the more social reason that participants did not want to miss out on the social interaction with colleagues. Peer pressure from colleagues had made some participants to sign up even though they did not believe they had an unhealthy behavior. Of the total of 355 participants in the intervention group, 203 (57.2%) left the intervention before it ended. Of the remaining participants, most did not use the tool after the competition at the end of the initial 16-week period. The actual number of active users of the tool throughout the whole intervention period was low; however, the participants reported that lifestyle habits became a topic of conversation. CONCLUSIONS: A tool that addresses group interactions at workplaces appears to initiate peer pressure, which helped recruitment for participation. However, active participation was low. A social change was indicated, allowing for more interaction among colleagues around healthy lifestyle issues. Future and more long-term studies are needed to determine whether such social changes could lead to sustained improvements of health.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Balk-Møller, Nina Charlotte","Larsen, Thomas Meinert","Holm, Lotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417644"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Health promotion","Internet","Qualitative Research","Smartphone","Weight Reduction Programs","Workplace","eHealth"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"experiences from a web and app based workplace health promotion intervention among employees in the social and health care sector based on use data and qualitative interviews","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/jmir.7278","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-417644","identifier":[{"id":"PMC5668633","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85044072084","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29051133","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2881b03b-7e93-4b7b-9fe5-9fe4ac1303f1"],"keyword":["Health promotion","Internet","Qualitative research","Smartphone","Weight reduction programs","Workplace","eHealth"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7C91CADAD89023C9C6B472B7FF44197F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/184877508/Balk_Moeller_et_al_Journal_of_Medical_Internet_Research_2017_Vol_19_10_e350.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2196/jmir.7278","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Nina Charlotte","key":"balkmøllerpau","last":"Balk-Møller","locid":"84d79d17-8272-4ed8-855c-504511d901b8","name":"Balk-Møller, Nina Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-8457-2916","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Meinert","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"be620f10-2a0e-430c-94d1-5246c8ef122a","name":"Larsen, Thomas Meinert","orcid":"0000-0001-7621-3131","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lotte","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"fbaa1305-c82c-40fa-a115-031c135c8a40","name":"Holm, Lotte","orcid":"0000-0003-0667-7779","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29051133"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2196/jmir.7278","issn":["14388871","14394456"],"issn_org":["14394456"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","paperid":"e350","status":"p","title":"Journal of Medical Internet Research","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044072084"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2881b03b-7e93-4b7b-9fe5-9fe4ac1303f1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Experiences from a web- and app-based workplace health promotion intervention among employees in the social and health care sector based on use-data and qualitative interviews","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-417644","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
