{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Wisborg, Julie Riisom","Larsen, Asger Væring","Drachen, Thea Marie","Wien, Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-081.82-756284"],"event":{"end":"2017-11-10","place":"Helsinki, fi","start":"2017-11-09","title":"22nd Nordic Workshop on Bibliometrics and Research Policy","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a phd is a phd is a phd or on potential differences in publication patterns among industrial and conventional phd students","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129091838/PHD_POSTER.PDF","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.82-756284","ids":["ku-d2074fec-0421-408a-be60-f50fc90ea479","sdu-1f127bb5-f777-4d22-83df-2e938b74e97a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-C0F19EAE4753EB52E22DD463FAB044EB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129091838/PHD_POSTER.PDF","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, SAM-RES, Dean's Office - Faculty of Business and Social Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, External Centres, Det Kgl. Bibliotek - Universitetsbibliotekarens ledelsessekretariat"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Riisom","key":"wisborgpau","last":"Wisborg","locid":"01cad256-8449-4654-8e36-cb99c88ca233","name":"Wisborg, Julie Riisom","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Væring","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fd7856d4-9391-4ae2-9349-f9181309b577","name":"Larsen, Asger Væring","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-2637","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thea Marie","key":"drachenpau","last":"Drachen","locid":"299fab63-abe6-4f40-9658-fa7a11619ee7","name":"Drachen, Thea Marie","orcid":"0000-0003-4760-5536","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"wienpau","last":"Wien","locid":"277f8354-05c4-44a4-b3b9-df9d557c9028","name":"Wien, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-3257-2084","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d2074fec-0421-408a-be60-f50fc90ea479","sdu-1f127bb5-f777-4d22-83df-2e938b74e97a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A PhD is a PhD is a PhD - or? : On potential differences in publication patterns among industrial and conventional PhD students","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.82-756284","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: To identify patterns of multimorbidity in the general population and examine how these patterns are related to socio-demographic factors and health-related quality of life. STUDY DESIGN AND SETTING: We used latent class analysis to identify subgroups with statistically distinct and clinically meaningful disease patterns in a nationally representative sample of Danish adults (N = 162,283) aged 16+ years. The analysis was based on 15 chronic diseases. RESULTS: Seven classes with different disease patterns were identified: a class with no or only a single chronic condition (59% of the population) labeled \"1) Relatively Healthy\" and six classes with a very high prevalence of multimorbidity labeled; \"2) Hypertension\" (14%); \"3) Musculoskeletal Disorders\" (10%); \"4) Headache-Mental Disorders\" (7%); \"5) Asthma-Allergy\" (6%); \"6) Complex Cardiometabolic Disorders\" (3%); and \"7) Complex Respiratory Disorders\" (2%). Female gender was associated with an increased likelihood of belonging to any of the six multimorbidity classes except for class 2 (Hypertension). Low educational attainment predicted membership of all of the multimorbidity classes except for class 5 (Asthma-Allergy). Marked differences in health-related quality of life between the seven latent classes were found. Poor health-related quality of life was highly associated with membership of class 6 (Complex Cardiometabolic Disorders) and class 7 (Complex Respiratory Disorders). Despite different disease patterns, these two classes had nearly identical profiles in relation to health-related quality of life. CONCLUSION: The results clearly support that diseases tend to compound and interact, which suggests that a differentiated public health and treatment approach towards multimorbidity is needed.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Finn Breinholt","Pedersen, Marie Hauge","Friis, Karina","Glümer, Charlotte","Lasgaard, Mathias"],"cuid":["S02-089.26-029278"],"filters":{"add