{"abstract":"The Danish Bibliometric Research Indicator (BFI) is part of the performance-based model for the distribution of a special pool of baseline funding for universities and public research institutions in Denmark. BFI rewards the research publications published in the most recognized scientific journals, and gives a bonus for publications done through inter-institutionary collaboration. Credits given to universities are fractionalized between the participating universities. So far credits are not assigned to the individual authors but only to their institutions. However, it turns out that research collaboration is associated with a higher number of citations than single authorship which may present the author with two opposing incentives for research collaboration.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dorch, Bertil F.","Wien, Charlotte","Larsen, Asger Væring"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-639781"],"event":{"end":"2016-11-04","place":"København, dk","start":"2016-11-03","title":"21st Nordic Workshop on Bibliometrics and Research Policy","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bibliometri","Publishing"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opposing incentives for collaboration","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121419839/image.jpg","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-639781","ids":["sdu-e887cdc6-e025-489d-a736-3adb9514d0c1"],"keyword":["bibliometri","publishing"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0A44DE273B231286A43F7BA7BDEAFDE6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121419839/image.jpg","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Central Administration","SDU, Central Administration, The University Library of Southern Denmark, University Library of Southern Denmark. General Office"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bertil F.","key":"dorchpau","last":"Dorch","locid":"da82eabd-45cb-46bf-b322-b68bb5f0294d","name":"Dorch, Bertil F.","orcid":"0000-0003-2594-6778","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte","key":"wienpau","last":"Wien","locid":"277f8354-05c4-44a4-b3b9-df9d557c9028","name":"Wien, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0002-3257-2084","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger Væring","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fd7856d4-9391-4ae2-9349-f9181309b577","name":"Larsen, Asger Væring","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-2637","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e887cdc6-e025-489d-a736-3adb9514d0c1"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Opposing incentives for collaboration","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-639781","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"In late February 2014, unusually high numbers of wild birds, thick-billed murre (Uria lomvia), were found dead at the coast of South Greenland. To investigate the cause of death, 45 birds were submitted for laboratory examinations in Denmark. Avian influenza viruses (AIVs) with subtypes H11N2 and low pathogenic (LP) H5N1 were detected in some of the birds. Characterization of the viruses by full-genome sequencing revealed that all the gene segments belonged to the North American lineage of AIVs. The seemingly sparse and mixed subtype occurrence of LP AIVs in these birds, in addition to an emaciated appearance of birds, suggests that the murre die-off was not due to infection with AIV, but could be the mere cause of sparse food availability or stormy weather. Here we present the first characterization of AIVs isolated in Greenland, and our results support the idea that wild birds in Greenland may be involved in the movement of AIV between North America and Europe.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Hartby, Christina Marie","Krog, Jesper Schak","Merkel, Flemming Ravn","Holm, Elisabeth","Larsen, Lars Erik","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane"],"cuid":["S02-097.46-023115"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Brünnich s guillemot","Greenland","H5N1","Thick billed murre","Uria lomvia"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"first characterization of avian influenza viruses from greenland 000000002014","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84987748125","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.46-023115","identifier":[{"id":"84987748125","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27309071","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-8f3861f0-2cb6-4c8e-948b-f0f8ecc7e149","dtu-1f85a97e-595a-43ef-9d4e-70bb5209cefd"],"keyword":["Brünnich's guillemot","Greenland","H11N2","H5N1","Intercontinental exchange of influenza virus","Low pathogenic avian influenza virus","Thick-billed murre","Uria lomvia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-4A02CD30080B1BEFF70F0C53C3A7A70A"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christina Marie","key":"hartbypau","last":"Hartby","locid":"91d05451-70ef-459e-8781-4fa025583e88","name":"Hartby, Christina Marie","orcid":"0000-0003-2852-970X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"merkelpau","last":"Merkel","locid":"7ebb69f4-00b0-438d-ae73-5305d25780ec","name":"Merkel, Flemming Ravn","name_org":"Merkel, Flemmin