{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The first Danish Report Card on Physical Activity (PA) for Children and Youth describes Denmark's efforts in promoting and facilitating PA and PA opportunities for children and youth. METHODS: The report card relies primarily on a synthesis of the best available research and policy strategies identified by the Report Card Research Committee consisting of a wide presentation of researchers and experts within PA health behaviors and policy development. The work was coordinated by Research and Innovation Centre for Human Movement and Learning situated at the University of Southern Denmark and the University College Lillebaelt. Nine PA indicators were graded using the Active Healthy Kids Canada Report Card development process. RESULTS: Grades from A (highest) to F (lowest) varied in Denmark as follows: 1) Overall Physical Activity (D+), 2) Organized Sport Participation (A), 3) Active Play (INC; incomplete), 4) Active Transportation (B), 5) Sedentary Behaviors (INC), 6) Family and Peers (INC), 7) School (B), 8) Community and the Built Environment (B+), and 9) Government strategies and investments (A-). CONCLUSIONS: A large proportion of children in Denmark do not meet the recommendations for PA despite the favorable investments and intensions from the government to create good facilities and promote PA.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Larsen, Lisbeth Runge","Troelsen, Jens","Kirkegaard, Kasper Lund","Riiskjær, Søren","Krølner, Rikke","Østergaard, Lars","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Møller, Niels Christian","Christensen, Bjørn Friis Neerfeldt","Jensen, Jens-Ole","Østergård, Charlotte","Skovgaard, Thomas"],"cuid":["S04-095.32-039420"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"keyword":["Child health","Health communication","Knowledge translation","schools courses and institutions"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"OT":["Danmarks Idrætsforbund"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"results from denmark s 000000002016 report card on physical activity for children and youth","src":["kp","sdu","ucl","via"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1123/jpah.2016-0403","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-095.32-039420","identifier":[{"id":"27848735","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84998655065","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["kp-ca6a8d17-884b-4ab7-ac50-b00ebfa33da3","sdu-7d0eea50-97d5-4f40-a7eb-d075b9ddccf1","ucl-ca6a8d17-884b-4ab7-ac50-b00ebfa33da3","via-ca6a8d17-884b-4ab7-ac50-b00ebfa33da3"],"keyword":["Child health","Health communication","Knowledge translation","schools, courses and institutions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-EC6BF80CB766F1E3AC03E3CEBFC212A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.kp.dk/ws/files/48536952/jpah.2016_0403.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1123/jpah.2016-0403","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.via.dk/ws/files/48536952/jpah.2016_0403.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://ucviden.ucl.dk/ws/files/48536952/jpah.2016_0403.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"nam