 University of Southern Denmark","UCL University College","VIA University College"],"title":"Results From Denmark's 2016 Report Card on Physical Activity for Children and Youth","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.32-039420","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this paper is to explore how paradoxes unfold in management practices and how moments of relational dialogic, self-reflexive learning can transform these paradoxes into new understandings of the complexities of organizing and management. We work with paradox, not as a label but a lens arising from equivocality and ambiguous organizational interpretations. We therefore apply perspective on organizing that acknowledge the super complex processes of organising and approach research from a becoming perspective. The research findings presented in this paper explores from whit-in the movement from spectator to practitioner in an organizational change process. We focus on moments of dialogue in our research that reach beyond the hegemony of organizational life, inviting new ways of going on, change, differing voices and polyfoni. The focus on moments of dialogue represents a way for us to explore ‘the flux of reality from within’ with the managers. We therefore draw on Bakhtin’s ideas regarding ongoing centripetal (monologic) and centrifugal (dialogic) forces of language and aim to demonstrate how working with language and the awareness of the embodied embedded practices at the same time both constitutes and reconstruct organizational paradoxes.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Madsen, Charlotte Øland","Schulze, Pernille","Larsen, Mette Vinther"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-069220"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-18","place":"Corfu, gr","start":"2016-06-16","title":"Eight Symposium on Process Organization Studies","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ledelse","Paradokser","Praksisforskning"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"paradoxes in practice","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/245958513/PROS_2016_Madsen_Schulze_Larsen.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-069220","ids":["aau-424555a4-dbd6-460f-8e8f-6315449c332c"],"keyword":["Paradokser","ledelse","praksisforskning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DC67B98F42188280DE5B01E7E047FB12"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/245958513/PROS_2016_Madsen_Schulze_Larsen.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Centre for Learning in Organisations","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Øland","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"22026f1a-b034-403c-90cb-f6bc643a2f49","name":"Madsen, Charlotte Øland","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pernille","key":"schulzepau","last":"Schulze","locid":"b5b3aeb9-5cfa-4898-a827-4b9af90ff87d","name":"Schulze, Pernille","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Vinther","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0de85dc7-1bbc-4121-81f7-05c927f84a51","name":"Larsen, Mette Vinther","orcid":"0000-0002-4966-8090","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-424555a4-dbd6-460f-8e8f-6315449c332c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Paradoxes in Practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-069220","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Most studies of polytrauma examined highly mixed patient groups. The objective of the present study was to report the development of patient-reported quality of life (QOL), in a patient group with musculoskeletal polytrauma, excluding patients with major thoracic, abdominal, and brain injuries. MATERIALS AND METHODS: The study design was a 1-year cohort follow-up study. Recordings of injury severity were measured with the ISS and NISS. Patient-reported QOL was measured with the questionnaires Eq5d-5L and SF-36 and compared to age-matched reference populations. Moreover, patients return to work status was measured. Data were collected prospectively at discharge, 3, 6, and 12 months. RESULTS: 53 patients were included. The mean age was 42.3 years, ranging from 17 to 78 years. Twelve months after trauma admission, the mean Eq5d-5L index was 0.601 (95 % CI 0.546-0.657). A progressive increasing Eq5d-5L index and SF-36 PCS was observed between the discharge and the 12-month follow-up (p < 0.001). The development in QOL from 6 to 12 months almost shows identically scores. Throughout the study period, patients reported significant worse QOL compared with the established reference population. 32 % of patients have resumed earlier employment status at 1-year follow-up. CONCLUSIONS: Throughout the 12-month observational period, patients reported worse QOL compared to the age-matched reference population. The development of QOL from 6- to 12-month time points almost showed identically scores with only little improvement. At the end of 1-year follow-up, 32 % of patients had resumed prior employment status.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Peter","Gøthgen, Charlotte Buch","Rasmussen, Sten","Iyer, Annika Brigitte","Elsøe, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-088261"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"one year development of qol following orthopaedic polytrauma a prospective observational cohort study of 000000000053 patients","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-088261","identifier":[{"id":"84981186332","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27501705","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000386067900008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-834d86ef-6fb2-4c5b-89af-55cae16490a1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F573459939BBF9A9FDE273E63D32E4C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Fysio- og Ergoterapi [Klinik Akut]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"21210203-656b-4b12-81cf-5f838dd57e33","name":"Larsen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-8094-4463","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Buch","key":"gøthgenpau","last":"Gøthgen","locid":"ac2b98c1-0262-408d-927d-c938cfc59f10","name":"Gøthgen, Charlotte Buch","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"05d1d595-13be-4295-8ad1-8d29206859c8","name":"Rasmussen, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-8664-352X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annika Brigitte","key":"iyerpau","last":"Iyer","locid":"e99a8c7a-2b15-4d5d-80d0-343a85da4c33","name":"Iyer, Annika Brigitte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rasmus","key":"elsoepau","last":"Elsoe","locid":"d76bd066-40d4-4fcb-b264-ce8421d08fdf","name":"Elsøe, Rasmus","name_org":"Elsoe, Rasmus","orcid":"0000-0001-5781-5604","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27501705"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00402-016-2550-5","issn":["09368051","14343916"],"issn_org":["09368051"],"issue":"11","journal":"Archives of Orthopaedic and Trauma Surgery","pages":"1539-1546","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Archives of Orthopaedic and Trauma Surgery","volume":"136"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84981186332"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-834d86ef-6fb2-4c5b-89af-55cae16490a1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"One-year development of QOL following orthopaedic polytrauma : a prospective observational cohort study of 53 patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-088261","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
