":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788741266428"],"isbn":["9788741264301"],"pages":"250","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-2ac8bda4-8b0a-4098-b748-aca5dfe48da7","via-2ac8bda4-8b0a-4098-b748-aca5dfe48da7"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","VIA University College"],"title":"Samskabelse og socialt entreprenørskab : en casebaseret grundbog til professionsuddannelserne","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-038650","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Auditory verbal hallucinations (AVH) are common during development and may arise due to dysregulation in top-down processing of sensory input. This study was designed to examine the frequency and correlates of speech illusions measured using the White Noise (WN) task in children from the general population. Associations between speech illusions and putative risk factors for psychotic disorder and negative affect were examined. METHOD: A total of 1486 children aged 11-12 years of the Copenhagen Child Cohort 2000 were examined with the WN task. Psychotic experiences and negative affect were determined using the Kiddie-SADS-PL. Register data described family history of mental disorders. Exaggerated Theory of Mind functioning (hyper-ToM) was measured by the ToM Storybook Frederik. RESULTS: A total of 145 (10%) children experienced speech illusions (hearing speech in the absence of speech stimuli), of which 102 (70%) experienced illusions perceived by the child as positive or negative (affectively salient). Experiencing hallucinations during the last month was associated with affectively salient speech illusions in the WN task [general cognitive ability: adjusted odds ratio (aOR) 2.01, 95% confidence interval (CI) 1.03-3.93]. Negative affect, both last month and lifetime, was also associated with affectively salient speech illusions (aOR 2.01, 95% CI 1.05-3.83 and aOR 1.79, 95% CI 1.11-2.89, respectively). Speech illusions were not associated with delusions, hyper-ToM or family history of mental disorders. CONCLUSIONS: Speech illusions were elicited in typically developing children in a WN-test paradigm, and point to an affective pathway to AVH mediated by dysregulation in top-down processing of sensory input.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rimvall, M K","Clemmensen, L","Munkholm, A","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","Skovgaard, A M","Simons, C J P","van Os, J","Jeppesen, P"],"cuid":["S03-097.77-014220"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Maastricht University"],"keyword":["Child","Denmark","Experimental design","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease epidemiology","Hallucinations epidemiology","Humans","Illusions physiology","Journal Article","Male","Preadolescence","Psychosis","Psychotic Disorders epidemiology","Psychotic experiences","Registries","Speech Perception physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introducing the white noise task in childhood associations between speech illusions and psychosis vulnerability","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84979255157","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.77-014220","identifier":[{"id":"27444712","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000385358000005","type":"wos"},{"id":"84979255157","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-167c2f7e-f104-4484-a23b-4d1bc56a0806","ku-a50d207e-1244-4e9e-9d91-7198eddfef58","sdu-9f2d8ad1-d38f-42ba-81a4-e0c8afa6c82d"],"keyword":["Child","Denmark","Experimental design","Female","Genetic Predisposition to Disease/epidemiology","Hallucinations/epidemiology","Humans","Illusions/physiology","Journal Article","Male","Psychotic Disorders/epidemiology","Registries","Speech Perception/physiology","preadolescence","psychosis","psychotic experiences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-86C9D2B93FBD504BE6F8F958AF6E5ED1"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Mental Health Services CPH"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Social Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Psychatric Hospital for Children and Adolescents","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinic for Functional Disorder","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Psychiatric Hospital for Children and Adolescents"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"maastricht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Maastricht University","used":1},{"affno":5,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Department of Health and Social Context"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M K","key":"rimvallpau","last":"Rimvall","name":"Rimvall, M K","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Lars","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"9807a75d-5c56-489c-a259-033c56295527","name":"Clemmensen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-1750-4649","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Anja","key":"munkholmpau","last":"Munkholm","locid":"c7a4259b-f80c-4067-97c3-1261d32bd5ce","name":"Munkholm, Anja","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Ulrikka","key":"raskpau","last":"Rask","locid":"1e308742-df61-47da-83ce-53d8a7c774c3","name":"Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","orcid":"0000-0002-7426-0353","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janne","key":"tidselbaklarsenpau","last":"Tidselbak Larsen","locid":"5e35426b-5cd7-438a-a11a-bfd44f63fbdf","name":"Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","name_org":"Tidselbak Larsen, Janne","orcid":"0000-0002-0385-1017","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J.T.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, J.T.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A. M.","key":"skovgaardpau","last":"Skovgaard","locid":"f1e6d144-f7de-4477-a60c-3046ccb9ca8d","name":"Skovgaard, Anne Mette","name_org":"Skovgaard, A. M.","orcid":"0000-0002-8793-8303","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"C J P","key":"simonspau","last":"Simons","name":"Simons, C J P","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"J","key":"vanospau","last":"van Os","name":"van Os, J","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"P.","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"2a1a09ff-cac8-4162-ab6f-ff07e9d1656f","name":"Jeppesen, Pia","name_org":"Jeppesen, P.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27444712"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/s0033291716001112","issn":["00332917","14698978"],"issn_org":["00332917"],"issue":"13","journal":"Psychological Medicine","pages":"2731-2740","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","title":"Psychological Medicine","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979255157"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-167c2f7e-f104-4484-a23b-4d1bc56a0806","ku-a50d207e-1244-4e9e-9d91-7198eddfef58","sdu-9f2d8ad1-d38f-42ba-81a4-e0c8afa6c82d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Introducing the White Noise task in childhood : associations between speech illusions and psychosis vulnerability","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.77-014220","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Little systematic evidence is available on potential gender differences in patients with an implantable cardioverter defibrillator (ICD) from a real-world cohort. We designed the DEFIB-WOMEN (The Utilization of Implantable Cardioverter DEFIBrillator Therapy in the Treatment of Heart Disease: Clinical and Psychological outcomes in WOMEN) study to examine gender differences on (1) patient-reported outcomes (PROs), (2) procedure- and device-related complications, and (3) ventricular tachyarrhythmia and mortality. This presents the study design and baseline characteristics of the cohort. METHODS: DEFIB-WOMEN is a national, multicenter, prospective, observational study. First-time implanted patients are asked to complete PROs at several time points. Information on baseline and follow-up characteristics are captured from patients' medical records, purpose-designed questions, and the Danish national registers. The DEFIB-WOMEN cohort is composed of 1,790 (19% women; 343/1,790) patients implanted between June 2010 and April 2013. RESULTS: Women and men differed on several demographic and clinical baseline characteristics, including on the prescription of β-blockers, statins, angiotensin-converting enzyme inhibitors, and psychotropic agents. Although women generally had a healthier clinical profile, they reported significantly more symptoms of anxiety and depression and ICD concerns (fear of shock) as compared to men. These differences were not only statistically significant but also clinically relevant, with the magnitude of the differences in anxiety and ICD concerns being 0.44 and 0.42, respectively, as indicated by Cohen's effect size index. CONCLUSIONS: These preliminary results indicate that women with an ICD experience particularly more anxiety and ICD concerns as compared to men at the time of implant. Future results of DEFIB-WOMEN will show whether these gender differences persist and whether there are also gender differences in complications and survival.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Pedersen, Susanne S","Nielsen, Jens Cosedis","Riahi, Sam","Haarbo, Jens","VidebAEk, Regitze","Larsen, Mogens Lytken","Skov, Ole","Knudsen, Charlotte","Johansen, Jens Brock"],"cuid":["S03-097.96-010856"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corpau":["DEFIB-WOMEN Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Susanne S."],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam"],"keyword":["Complications","Gender differences","Implantable cardioverter defibrillator","Mortality","Patient reported outcomes","Ventricular tachyarrhythmia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study design and cohort description of defib women a national danish study in patients with an icd","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84994791379","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-097.96-010856","identifier":[{"id":"27566441","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000389147000012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84994791379","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e34a5116-a201-4444-9508-5cdc60601c71","au-390aa2a0-c996-45d2-b0b6-040461bc45e9","sdu-4c0e6902-65bf-4ee6-b4ce-cb528eb5a285"],"keyword":["complications","gender differences","implantable cardioverter defibrillator","mortality","patient-reported outcomes","ventricular tachyarrhythmia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-C6F11C4A31540FE71D40A62CE3B0DC0C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Psychology, INSIDE","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Department of Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"erasmus university medical center rotterdam","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Erasmus University Medical Center Rotterdam","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospi