"l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Department of Educational Psychology, The Danish University of Education"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jette","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","name":"Kofoed, Jette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"SMID's årsmøde 2016"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4e9d358f-7b22-4538-81c2-ccee7e4d2be5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"A snap of intimacy : Photo-sharing practices among youth on social media","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-072834","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The purpose of this article is to explore what can be learned about management learning when social poetics is used as a perspective to make sense of how seven leaders, during a year-long top leader competence development course, constructed meaning with each other, with consultants and with researchers about what leading in ‘Cullinan ways’ means. The article is based on a relational constructionism perspective, and we bring in two aspects of social poetics – the notion of metaphors and engaging in reflexive critique – to present and discuss how the understanding and use of the concept ‘Cullinany’ continually changed and was reworked based on the conversations the seven leaders had with each other. The purpose of this presentation is to initiate a discussion about how formal management learning programmes can be understood (and possibly also designed) from a perspective in which the ontological and social poetic aspects of language are assigned primacy","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Mette Vinther","Madsen, Charlotte Øland"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-073640"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Management learning","Relationel ledelse","Social poetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring how social poetics can be used to understand processes of management learning","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-073640","identifier":[{"id":"84992034587","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000389917200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-513c06df-f9ec-4945-b77a-1a8d610c67e4"],"keyword":["management learning","relationel ledelse","relfeksivitet","social poetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ECEBA6C1D2214E6CDD296F4E9A577A13"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities, Department of Learning and Philosophy, Centre for Learning in Organisations","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Business and Management, Firms, Innovation and Relations Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette Vinther","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"0de85dc7-1bbc-4121-81f7-05c927f84a51","name":"Larsen, Mette Vinther","orcid":"0000-0002-4966-8090","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Øland","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"22026f1a-b034-403c-90cb-f6bc643a2f49","name":"Madsen, Charlotte Øland","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1350507616644551","issn":["13505076","14617307"],"issn_org":["13505076"],"issue":"5","journal":"Management Learning","pages":"489-505","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Management Learning","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84992034587"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-513c06df-f9ec-4945-b77a-1a8d610c67e4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Exploring how social poetics can be used to understand processes of management learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=si