{"abstract":"Four new yanuthone analogs (1–4) were isolated from the filamentous fungus Aspergillus niger. The structures of the new compounds were elucidated on the basis of UHPLC-DAD-HRMS data and one-dimensional and two-dimensional NMR spectroscopy. Labeling studies with 13C8-6-methylsalicylic acid identified three class I yanuthones originating from the polyketide 6-methylsalicylic acid (yanuthone K, L and M (1–3)) and a class II yanuthone, which was named yanuthone X2 (4). The four new compounds were tested toward the pathogenic yeast Candida albicans and all displayed antifungal activity. Yanuthone X2 represents the first example of a bioactive class II yanuthone, demonstrating the pharmaceutical potential of this class.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Petersen, Lene Maj","Holm, Dorte Koefoed","Knudsen, Peter Boldsen","Nielsen, Kristian Fog","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-380521"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterization of four new antifungal yanuthones from i aspergillus niger i","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:10.1038/ja.2014.130","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-380521","identifier":[{"id":"84925595851","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fdd64aec-094f-4323-98f4-fff62de2d269"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2E01B962B5D26CC67624CD12885BF2FD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/doi:10.1038/ja.2014.130","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemistry, Organic Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lene Maj","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"7a1c5a02-7eb8-40e3-a1ec-621fb3c37652","name":"Petersen, Lene Maj","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Dorte Koefoed","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"aedc7b19-7dd8-4af4-a8cc-5a73f5783c91","name":"Holm, Dorte Koefoed","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Boldsen","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"991df7f2-a085-49ce-a926-da127ba3b28b","name":"Knudsen, Peter Boldsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Fog","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d2067ee9-e48c-4cf4-ac8f-ee775d8aff5a","name":"Nielsen, Kristian Fog","orcid":"0000-0002-5848-0911","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Held","key":"gotfredsenpau","last":"Gotfredsen","locid":"1cf4df84-2d0e-4693-bf47-e9932e3bf0e3","name":"Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","orcid":"0000-0002-7386-119X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe Hasbro","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"dec3038b-f004-4c96-84a1-52825e1c0ce8","name":"Mortensen, Uffe Hasbro","orcid":"0000-0002-7794-7273","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ja.2014.130","issn":["00218820","03682781"],"issn_org":["00218820"],"journal":"The Journal of Antibiotics","pages":"201-205","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Antibiotics","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925595851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fdd64aec-094f-4323-98f4-fff62de2d269"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Characterization of four new antifungal yanuthones from<i> Aspergillus niger</i>","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-380521","year":"2015","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Assessment of myocardial longitudinal function has proved to be a sensitive marker of deteriorating myocardial function in aortic stenosis, demonstrated by both color Doppler tissue imaging and recently by two-dimensional speckle-tracking echocardiography. The aim of this study was to compare velocity (color Doppler tissue imaging) and deformation (two-dimensional speckle-tracking echocardiography) in relation to global and regional longitudinal function in asymptomatic and severe symptomatic aortic stenosis. METHODS: In a cross-sectional design, 231 patients with aortic stenosis were divided into four groups: asymptomatic moderate aortic stenosis (aortic valve area, 1.0-1.5 cm(2); n = 38), asymptomatic severe aortic stenosis (aortic valve area < 1.0 cm(2); n = 66), and symptomatic severe aortic stenosis with preserved (n = 68) and reduced (<50%) left ventricular ejection fraction (n = 59). RESULTS: Among all global (peak systolic s', diastolic e' and a', longitudinal displacement, and global longitudinal strain and strain rate) and regional longitudinal (basal, middle, and apical longitudinal strain and strain rate) parameters, only diastolic e', longitudinal displacement, and basal longitudinal strain (BLS) remained significantly associated with symptomatic status, independent of age, gender, heart rate, aortic valve area, stroke volume index, left ventricular mass index, left atrial volume index, and tricuspid annular systolic plane excursion. Furthermore, in a model with the aforementioned parameters, including e', longitudinal displacement, and BLS, only BLS remained significantly associated with symptomatic status in the entire study population (BLS per one-unit decrease: odds ratio, 1.23; 95% CI, 1.04-1.46; P = .017). Furthermore, patients with BLS < 13% were more likely to be symptomatic (odds ratio, 4.97; 95% CI, 2.6-9.4; P < .001), and no patients with asymptomatic severe aortic stenosis with BLS ≥ 13% were admitted with myocardial infarction or heart failure during follow-up of 1,462 days. CONCLUSIONS: Among the many echocardiographic measures of longitudinal velocity and deformation, BLS has the strongest association with symptomatic status in aortic stenosis, and BLS < 13% is related to adverse outcomes in severe asymptomatic aortic stenosis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Carstensen, Helle Gervig","Larsen, Linnea Hornbech","Hassager, Christian","Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","Dalsgaard, Morten","Kristensen, Charlotte Burup","Jensen, Jan Skov","Mogelvang, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-404471"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tissue velocities and myocardial deformation in asymptomatic and symptomatic aortic stenosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-404471","identifier":[{"id":"25944424","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84938548824","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-128dc676-cd81-4462-b806-98eb973d247e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6DC3399147DD2B8B6B50F80A1A2508B7"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Helle Gervig","key":"carstensenpau","last":"Carstensen","name":"Carstensen, Helle Gervig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Linnea Hornbech","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Linnea Hornbech","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"49196e5d-0f61-44b2-a6b9-cd6c5f8f3bc2","name":"Hassager, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1199-0981","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus Fuglsang","key":"kofoedpau","last":"Kofoed","locid":"ec141562-c77f-498d-af6e-db9e08a4e895","name":"Kofoed, Klaus Fuglsang","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","name":"Dalsgaard, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte Burup","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Burup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jan Skov","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"e29024e8-87d0-4edb-a304-f0b6393488a4","name":"Jensen, Jan Skov","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"mogelvangpau","last":"Mogelvang","name":"Mogelvang, Rasmus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25944424"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.echo.2015.03.013","issn":["08947317","10976795"],"issn_org":["08947317"],"issue":"8","journal":"Journal of the American Society of Echocardiography","pages":"969-80","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Society of Echocardiography","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938548824"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-128dc676-cd81-4462-b806-98eb973d247e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tissue Velocities and Myocardial Deformation in Asymptomatic and Symptomatic Aortic Stenosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-404471","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Herein we describe the first structure-activity relationship study of the broad-range iGluR antagonist (2S,3R)-3-(3-carboxyphenyl)pyrrolidine-2-carboxylic acid (1) by exploring the pharmacological effect of substituents in the 4, 4', or 5' positions and the bioisosteric substitution of the distal carboxylic acid for a phosphonic acid moiety. Of particular interest is a hydroxyl group in the 4' position 2a which induced a preference in binding affinity for homomeric GluK3 over GluK1 (Ki = 0.87 and 4.8 μM, respectively). Two X-ray structures of ligand binding domains were obtained: 2e in GluA2-LBD and 2f in GluK1-LBD, both at 1.9 Å resolution. Compound 2e induces a D1-D2 domain opening in GluA2-LBD of 17.3-18.8° and 2f a domain opening in GluK1-LBD of 17.0-17.5° relative to the structures with glutamate. The pyrrolidine-2-carboxylate moiety of 2e and 2f shows a similar binding mode as kainate. The 3-carboxyphenyl ring of 2e and 2f forms contacts comparable to those of the distal carboxylate in kainate.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Krogsgaard-Larsen, Niels","Storgaard, Morten","Møller, Charlotte","Demmer, Charles S","Hansen, Jeanette","Han, Liwei","Monrad, Rune N","Nielsen, Birgitte","Tapken, Daniel","Pickering, Darryl S","Kastrup, Jette Sandholm","Frydenvang, Karla","Bunch, Lennart"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-543444"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structure activity relationship study of ionotropic glutamate receptor antagonist 000000000002s 000000000003r 000000000003 000000000003 carboxyphenyl pyrrolidine 000000000002 carboxylic acid","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-543444","identifier"