-Henrik","name_org":"Winsløw, Jan-Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jan-Henrik","key":"winsløvpau","last":"Winsløv","name":"Winsløv, Jan-Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan-Henrik","key":"winsloevpau","last":"Winsloev","name":"Winsloev, Jan-Henrik","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"langhoffpau","last":"Langhoff","name":"Langhoff, Charlotte","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"mühlmannpau","last":"Mühlmann","name":"Mühlmann, Charlotte","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"muehlmannpau","last":"Muehlmann","name":"Muehlmann, Charlotte","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Merete","key":"nordentoftpau","last":"Nordentoft","locid":"6d0fe19c-7c81-463b-8bc8-822d71584b69","name":"Nordentoft, Merete","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26359612"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2215-0366(14)00083-2","issn":["22150366","22150374"],"issn_org":["22150366"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Lancet Psychiatry","pages":"49-58","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Psychiatry","title_org":"Lancet Psychiatry","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920830695"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","børne- og ungdomspsykiatri","institut for klinisk medicin - hjertemedicinsk afdeling b, sks"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-48d65267-c7a4-45b6-a253-1c797a41e2a3","ku-e4961f3e-5ac2-48c2-8568-510b32a49415","sdu-61b67062-2c88-4f3c-9661-3f8edad5cb57"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Short-term and long-term effects of psychosocial therapy for people after deliberate self-harm : a register-based, nationwide multicentre study using propensity score matching","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-097.17-003540","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Psychotic experiences (PE) in individuals of the general population are hypothesized to mark the early expression of the pathology underlying psychosis. This notion of PE as an intermediate phenotype is based on the premise that PE share genetic liability with psychosis. We examined whether PE in childhood was predicted by a family history of mental disorder with psychosis rather than a family history of nonpsychotic mental disorder and whether this association differed by severity of PE. The study examined data on 1632 children from a general population birth cohort assessed at age 11-12 years by use of a semistructured interview covering 22 psychotic symptoms. The Danish national registers were linked to describe the complete family history of hospital-based psychiatric diagnoses. Uni- and multivariable logistic regressions were used to test whether a family history of any mental disorder with psychosis, or of nonpsychotic mental disorder, vs no diagnoses was associated with increased risk of PE in offspring (hierarchical exposure variable). The occurrence of PE in offspring was significantly associated with a history of psychosis among the first-degree relatives (adjusted relative risk [RR] = 3.29, 95% CI: 1.82-5.93). The risk increased for combined hallucinations and delusions (adjusted RR = 5.90, 95% CI: 2.64-13.16). A history of nonpsychotic mental disorders in first-degree relatives did not contribute to the risk of PE in offspring nor did any mental disorder among second-degree relatives. Our findings support the notion of PE as a vulnerability marker of transdiagnostic psychosis. The effect of psychosis in first-degree relatives may operate through shared genetic and environmental factors.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jeppesen, Pia","Larsen, Janne Tidselbak","Clemmensen, Lars","Munkholm, Anja","Rimvall, Martin Kristian","Rask, Charlotte Ulrikka","van Os, Jim","Petersen, Liselotte","Skovgaard, Anne Mette"],"cuid":["S03-098.83-024694"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's College London","Maastricht University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the ccc000000002000 birth cohort study of register based family history of mental disorders and psychotic experiences in offspring","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/schbul/sbu167","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-098.83-024694","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4535626","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84943141249","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25452427","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a43d72e4-275d-449d-8f7b-ec93112fa910","ku-875c2f9e-913b-4e31-890f-7118d955b8de","sdu-c90e4de2-bba7-4a78-9efe-16225eb9bfc7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-EB5F60049D35C4E1FE18C2B54D7D6C0F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/schbul/sbu167","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_cod