{"abstract":"A tramp ship operator typically has some contracted cargoes that must be carried and seeks to maximize prot by carrying optional cargoes. Hence, tramp ships operate much like taxies following available cargoes and not according to a fixed route network and itinerary as liner ships. Marine fuel is referred to as bunker and bunker costs constitute a significant part of the daily operating costs. There can be great variations in bunker prices across bunker ports so it is important to carefully plan bunkering for each ship. As ships operate 24 hours a day, they must refuel during operations. Therefore, route and schedule decisions affect the options for bunkering. Current practice is, however, to separate the two planning problems by first constructing fleet schedules and then plan bunkering for these fixed schedules. In this paper we explore the effects of integrating bunker planning in the routing and scheduling phase and present a mixed integer programming formulation for the integrated problem of optimally routing, scheduling and bunkering a tramp fleet. Aside from the integration of bunker, this model also extends standard tramp formulations by using load dependent costs, speed and bunker consumption. We devise a solution method based on column generation with a dynamic programming algorithm to generate columns. The method is heuristic mainly due to a discretization of the continuous bunker purchase variables. We show that the integrated planning approach can increase prots and that the decision of which cargoes to carry and on which ships is affected by the bunker integration and by changes in the bunker prices.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Lusby, Richard Martin","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-346859"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bunkering","Column generation","Routing","Scheduling","Tramp shipping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tramp ship routing and scheduling with integrated bunker optimization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152316871/bunker_paper_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-346859","identifier":[{"id":"84913596380","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8db75ced-6b7c-49f1-a053-6220a1eb4d6c"],"keyword":["Bunkering","Column Generation","Routing","Scheduling","Tramp Shipping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9AA42C7708C1C76FF3D7000F44436025"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152316871/bunker_paper_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard Martin","key":"lusbypau","last":"Lusby","locid":"51599544-7991-404d-b9a7-ec2f5ad4824b","name":"Lusby, Richard Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-8652-6219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s13676-013-0039-8","issn":["21924376","21924384"],"issn_org":["21924376"],"issue":"2","journal":"EURO Journal on Transportation and Logistics","pages":"143-175","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"EURO Journal on Transportation and Logistics","title_org":"EURO Journal of Transportation and Logistics","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84913596380"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8db75ced-6b7c-49f1-a053-6220a1eb4d6c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Tramp ship routing and scheduling with integrated bunker optimization","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-346859","year":"2014","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Swine influenza is a respiratory disease caused by multiple subtypes of influenza A virus. Swine influenza virus (SIV) is enzootic in swine populations in Europe, Asia, North and South America. The influenza A virus genome consist of eight distinct gene segments and SIV subtypes are defined by the combination of the gene segments hemagglutinin (HA) and neuraminidase (NA). In most European countries, the avian-like (av)H1N1, the 2009 pandemic variant (H1N1pdm09), H1N2 and H3N2 subtypes have constituted the dominating SIV subtypes during recent years. In Denmark, the H1N2 subtype is a reassortant between avH1N1 and H3N2 which is different from the dominating European H1N2 subtype (1). The prevalence of the H1N1pdm09 virus in swine has increased since 2009 in some countries including Denmark. Here we present the results of the national passive surveillance program on influenza in swine performed from 2009-13.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars Erik","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Trebbien, Ramona","Krog, Jesper Schak","Breum, Solvej Østergaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-352798"],"event":{"end":"2014-06-11","place":"Cancun, mx","start":"2014-06-08","title":"23rd IPVS Congress","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surveillance programs in denmark has revealed the circulation of novel reassortant influenza a viruses in swine","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/103604880/SIV_abstract_IPVS2014.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-352798","ids":["dtu-a19ec7b7-cb8c-47a8-aa53-6a7c3bec4379"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5032A0CA575681CED8AAFFD203C27E1C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/103604880/SIV_abstract_IPVS2014.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","locid":"f5a78ced-77e8-4da1-950c-9c1992eac344","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 23rd IPVS Congress"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a19ec7b7-cb8c-47a8-aa53-6a7c3bec4379"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Surveillance programs in Denmark has revealed the circulation of novel reassortant influenza A viruses in swine","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352798","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Subhi, Yousif","Henningsen, Gitte","Larsen, Charlotte T.","Sørensen, Mette Sejer","Sørensen, Torben Lykke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-450172"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"foveal morphology affects self perceived visual function and treatment response in age related macular degeneration a cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0091227","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-450172","identifier":[{"id":"24618706","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3949984","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84897494784","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5ec71cc1-4d19-4fdb-bc5f-5cdb63af6852"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F7372215A3F12A045E55A9D511419C03"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0091227","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Yousif","key":"subhiyousifpau","last":"Subhi","name":"Subhi, Yousif","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gitte","key":"henningsengittepau","last":"Henningsen","name":"Henningsen, Gitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte T.","key":"larsencharlottetpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Charlotte T.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette Sejer","key":"sørensenmettesejerpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Mette Sejer","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben Lykke","key":"sørensentorbenlykkepau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"550703c3-9c07-4138-81f1-36460e23efb9","name":"Sørensen, Torben Lykke","orcid":"0000-0002-6790-0199","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24618706"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0091227","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"3","journal":"PLOS ONE","pages":"1-12","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84897494784"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5ec71cc1-4d19-4fdb-bc5f-5cdb63af6852"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Foveal morphology affects self-perceived visual function and treatment response in age-related macular degeneration. A cohort study.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-450172","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In patients undergoing coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI), the standard post procedure regime includes immobilization and bed rest despite the use of vascular closure devices. AIM: In the Mobilization after Coronary Angiography or Percutaneous Coronary Intervention (MOBS) study we compared bleeding complications after cardiac catheterization with femoral artery access after mobilization immediately off the angiographic table or standard care with1 hour (MOBS I after a diagnostic angiogram) or 2 hours of bed rest before mobilization (MOBS II after PCI). METHODS: Bleeding complications were defined as major (requiring surgery of the femoral artery, transfusion or increased hospital stay) and minor (hematoma <5 × 5 cm(2), oozing from the puncture site or minor bleeding that could be compressed manually). RESULTS: In the MOBS I cohort (100 patients were mobilized immediately and 100 patients followed standard care) no major bleeding complications were seen. In the immediate mobilization group 2.0% experienced minor bleeding compared to 4.0% in the standard care group (p=0.41). In the MOBS II cohort after PCI (158 patients were mobilized immediately and 161 patients followed standard care), major bleeding complication rates did not differ significantly between the two groups: immediate mobilization group 26.6% vs. standard care group 28.0%, p=0.78. The majority of bleeding complications were due to oozing: immediate mobilization group 22.8% vs. standard care group 20.5%, p=0.62. CONCLUSIONS: Immediate mobilization after a coronary angiogram or PCI with the femoral access site closed by the closure device AngioSeal was not associated with increased bleeding risk compared to standard care with bed rest.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Ellen Nyholm","Hansen, Charlotte Bak","Thayssen, Per","Jensen, Lisette Okkels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-623737"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Ellen Nyholm"],"keyword":["Closure device","Complications","Mobilization","Percutaneous Coronary Intervention"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"immediate mobilization after coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention following hemostasis with the angioseal vascular closure device the mobs study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1474515113516702","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-623737","identifier":[{"id":"24336239","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84907220889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b05f60d6-ac7d-4590-baaf-2d6e8542c42d"],"keyword":["Closure device","complications","mobilization","percutaneous coronary intervention"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28FDCA04068FFD907895951590C7BDC4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/1474515113516702","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Cardiology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellen Nyholm","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"f7fc0455-3f55-491c-9f98-e111de0a68b3","name":"Larsen, Ellen Nyholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Bak","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Charlotte Bak","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"thayssenpau","last":"Thayssen","name":"Thayssen, Per","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette Okkels","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24336239"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1474515113516702","issn":["14745151","18731953"],"issn_org":["14745151"],"issue":"5","journal":"European Journal of Cardiovascular Nursing","pages":"466-472","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Cardiovascular Nursing","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907220889"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b05f60d6-ac7d-4590-baaf-2d6e8542c42d"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Immediate mobilization after coronary angiography or percutaneous coronary intervention following hemostasis with the AngioSeal vascular closure device (the MOBS study)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-623737","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Artiklerne i dette seriehæfte kunne kaldes en slags midtvejsrapporter som udtryk for, hvor de tre UCN-projektgrupper og de to ph.d. studerende er nået til efter ca. et år, hvor samtlige projektdeltagere har haft daglig undervisning på deres uddannelse ’ved siden af’. Overskriften for gruppe ets arbejde hedder; ”Virkelighedsnær undervisning med digitale medier.” Gruppe tos tema er: ” Studiestøttende undervisning.” og gruppe tre arbejder med: ”Læring i og med praksis i det reelle og det virtuelle rum.” Gruppe ets artikel sætter fokus på anvendelsen af digitale medier til at fremme studerendes motivation for læring med det formål, at de studerende skal kunne anvende det lærte i en senere praksis. Begrebet motivation gøres til genstand for en nærmere analyse og sættes i forhold til muligheder og begrænsninger ved forskellige former for teknologimedieret læring. Gruppe to sætter sig i artiklen ”Virkelighedsnær undervisning med digitale medier” for at undersøge, hvad der skal til for at understøtte studerendes studieaktiviteter uden for campus, og retter blikket mod studerende på radiografuddannelsen ved UCN og studerende på kandidatuddannelsen i socialt arbejde ved AAU ud fra en formodning om, at der er eksplicitte udfordringer på begge disse uddannelser, hvad angår studerendes studieaktiviteter uden for campus. Gruppe tre bidrager med to artikler, hvor den første sætter sig for at afklare den teoretiske grundlag for gruppens arbejde med de videregående uddannelsers praksisrelation, herunder de studerendes forhold til deres praksis, forstået ved begrebet professionel identitet. I de indledende studier trækkes der bl.a. på teorier om professioner, identitet, læring, teknologi, digitale habitater og peer tutoring. Den anden artikel beskriver de metodiske overvejelser, den praktiske udførelse og empiriske analyse vedrørende et forsøg, der afvikledes i slutningen af studieåret 2013/14. Forsøget byggede på den antagelse, at erfaringerne fra den professionelle identitetsdannelse i et praktikophold på en videregående uddannelse kan videregives til andre, og forsøget havde til hensigt at undersøge, om dette kunne understøttes i et digitalt habitat. Med udgangspunkt i sit ph.d.-projekt bidrager Line Helverskov Horn foruden til de to artikler fra gruppe tre også med sin egen vinkel på undervisning og studier med digitale medier i form af artiklen om professionel identitet i professionsuddannelserne. Line ser på vilkårene for at støtte udvikling af professionel identitet i lyset af de muligheder og perspektiver, som informations- og kommunikationsteknologi (IKT) åbner for. Også Thomas Kjærgaard tager udgangspunkt i sit ph.d.-projekt og afslutter seriehæftet med sin artikel: ”Fra digitale drømme - til digitale strømme.” Thomas stiller spørgsmålet om, hvordan man udnytter teknologier i undervisningen på professionshøjskoler. Teknologierne er allerede i undervisningsrummet, og det drejer sig om at få klarhed over hvad teknologierne bidrager med, og hvilke kompetencer det kræver at udnytte teknologiernes affordans. Derudover sættes fokus på, hvordan man med teknologi bliver en mere læringskompetent (dvs. får gode strategier for læring) studerende.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Nielsen, Annegrethe","Pedersen, Annette","Jensen, Charlotte Heigaard","Wahl, Christian","Staugaard, Hans Jørgen","Lukassen, Niels Bech","Falk, Lars","Horn, Line Helverskov","Jensen, Louise Bach","Larsen, Louise Landbo","Gudiksen, Maria Boel Klok","Dau, Susanne","Kjærgaard, Thomas","Knudsen, Torben Broe","Gro-Nielsen, Brit"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-652556"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Blended learning","Digital dannelse","Digital kommunikation","Digitale medier","E læring","Undervisningsteknologi","digitalt studiemiljø","e læringsaktiviteter","eLearning","undervisningspraksis","virtuel læring"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCN"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCN"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"just duit status og perspektiver fra et igangværende forsknings og udviklingsprojekt i ucn","src":["ucn"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCN"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-652556","ids":["ucn-ec286097-c713-459d-aed1-dafc1493044b"],"keyword":["blended learning","digital dannelse","digital kommunikation","digitale medier","digitalt studiemiljø","e-læring","e-læringsaktiviteter","e-værktøjer","elearning","undervisningspraksis","undervisningsteknologi","virtuel læring","virtuel, virtuelle netværk, e-learning, IT-støttet læring, refleksion,"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-BF5437BB554AA95100C5EE0AF9CDE439"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucn university college of northern denmark","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCN","l3nl":"University College of Northern Denmark","l3nn":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCN University College of Northern Denmark","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen UCN, UCN Direktion, UCN Velfærd, Jordemoderuddannelsen"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annegrethe","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"83e758c2-337e-4133-b1a3-78ce812af57f","name":"Nielsen, Annegrethe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"dc321c0b-ba7e-40c3-adf6-fe7bf82ddbdb","name":"Pedersen, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-7267-2856","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Heigaard","key":"jensenped","last":"Jensen","locid":"dc9d437a-4aaa-4443-b3d8-630376295985","name":"Jensen, Charlotte Heigaard","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"wahlpau","last":"Wahl","locid":"2fcb136b-fcca-431f-ba