locid":"cf82626c-41b3-42c5-b289-42b5f2dc6f1f","name":"Hasager, Charlotte Bay","orcid":"0000-0002-2124-5651","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"WenZhong","key":"shenwenzhongpedh","last":"Shen","name":"Shen, WenZhong","rank":20,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2013 International Conference on aerodynamics of Offshore Wind Energy Systems and wakes (ICOWES2013)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a8989c73-2b21-4ad5-a2d9-6d8afecd2d86"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Benchmarking of wind farm scale wake models in the EERA - DTOC project","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-354905","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Both Type 1 and Type 2 PRRS viruses are circulating among Danish pigs. The first appearance of Type 1 PRRSV in Denmark was in 1992 whereas the Type 2 PRRSV was introduced in 1996 after the use of a live attenuated vaccine that reverted to virulence. Since then, vaccination to control the disease for both PRRSV genotypes has been widely used in Denmark and it is therefore highly relevant to monitor the diversity of currently circulating PRRSV strains. Only subtype 1 of the Type 1 PRRSV strains and vaccine-like Type 2 PRRSV strains were previously detected in Denmark, however, only few Danish PRRSV strains were sequenced. Denmark exports more than 50.000 living pigs each month. A portion of these pigs inevitably harbor PRRSV. Thus, the diversity of PRRSV in Denmark is of interest to other countries besides Denmark. The main objective of the present study was to close the gap in knowledge on the genetic diversity of currently circulating PRRSV stains in Danish pigs by sequencing ORF5 and ORF7 of approximately 41 Type 1 and 50 Type 2 strains isolated between 2003 and 2013. Furthermore, full genome analysis was performed on nine Type 1 and nine Type 2 selected strains. The preliminary assessment of the results showed that the Type 1 strains all belonged to subtype 1. Based on the ORF5 sequences, the Danish Type 1 viruses clustered into two groups. These two groups shared 84 % to 92 % and 94 % to 99% nucleotide identity to the Lelystad virus, respectively. The sequenced Type 2 viruses showed a significant higher level of identity in that the ORF5 sequences were 94 - >99 % identical at the nucleotide level. Most of the Type 2 viruses, shared high level of identity to the VR2332 vaccine strain (Ingelvac MLV), but a few more diverse isolates were also identified, including strains with interesting deletions in NSP2 and other genes. The full genome sequences of Danish strains showed an overall nucleotide identity of 88-98% (Type 1) and 94 % to >99 % (Type 2). The impact of these results will be discussed.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","Brar, Manreetpal Singh","Leung, Frederick Chi-Ching","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-370319"],"event":{"end":"2013-05-22","place":"Beijing, cn","start":"2013-05-20","title":"International Porcine Reproductive and Respiratory Syndrome Symposium (PRRS 2013)","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["Hong Kong"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Hong Kong"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the diversity of porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus type 000000000001 and 000000000002 in denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/55237625/prod11369865018746.The_diversity_of_PRRSV_Type_1_and_Type_2_in_Denmark.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-370319","ids":["dtu-dbcbe5aa-d453-41f0-ae4a-fb7eee0c75b2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E595463138EA22F4213ACC44C315C845"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/55237625/prod11369865018746.The_diversity_of_PRRSV_Type_1_and_Type_2_in_Denmark.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"danish agriculture food council","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-AAF","l3nl":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","l3nn":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","namevar":["Danish Agriculture and Food Council"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-AAF","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"hk","key":"the university of hong kong","loc":["Hong Kong","Asia, East"],"name":"The University of Hong Kong","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"58ce239f-6c30-44e0-ab54-f017a1821425","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sonne","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, Charlotte Sonne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Manreetpal Singh","key":"brarpau","last":"Brar","name":"Brar, Manreetpal Singh","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederick Chi-Ching","key":"leungpau","last":"Leung","name":"Leung, Frederick Chi-Ching","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Danish Agriculture & Food Council","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-dbcbe5aa-d453-41f0-ae4a-fb7eee0c75b2"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The diversity of Porcine Reproductive and Respiratory Syndrome Virus Type 1 and 2 in Denmark","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-370319","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Postweaning multisystemic wasting syndrome (PMWS) is a worldwide spread condition that affects pigs in nursery and/or fattening units, and is considered to have a severe economic impact on swine production. The main clinical sign of PMWS is wasting, but can also include pallor of the skin, icterus, respiratory distress and diarrhoea. The main essential infectious agent for PMWS development is porcinecircovirus type 2 (PCV2), but the exact cause of PMWS is still unclear.PCV2 is present in most pig herds, but the occurrence of PMWS is more sporadic, and it is been difficult to reproduce PMWS by inoculating PCV2 alone. However, studies where co-infections have been applied have been more successful. Based on this, we modeled PMWS development based on longitudinal data on antibodies and PMWS status from herds in Denmark and Spain, where presence of a range of pathogens were considered as explanatory variables in the form of maternal immunity and the occurrence of seroconversion against the considered pathogens. However, maternal immunity could not be measured from mother animals due to cross fostering, no time points for seroconversion was available, and no case/control status could be assigned as PMWS do not have an ‘infectious period’ after which animals may be assigned control status. The talk will concentrate on the framework in which this was handled, which may be translated to similar settings for similar studies. We found that seroconversion towards PCV2 and Lawsonia intracellularis had a significant impact on PMWS in the Danish data, but it appears that the effect is positive, in the sense that seroconverted animals were less likely to develop PMWS. A number of maternal immunities also significantly affected PMWS development. Furthermore it was uncovered that most of these effects would not have been detected if pathogens were considered by themselves and not simultaneously.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Grau-Roma, L.","Stockmarr, Anders","Kristensen, C. S.","Enøe, Claes","López-Soria, S.","Nofrarías, M.","Bille-Hansen, Vivi","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Sibila, M.","Jorsal, Sven Erik Lind","Fraile, L.","Baekbo, P.","Vigre, H.","Segalés, J.","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373444"],"event":{"end":"2013-03-20","place":"Hangzhou, cn","start":"2013-03-18","title":"BIT’s 5th World Congress of Vaccine","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pmws development in pigs from affected farms in spain and denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/53801394/prod11364940429509.WCV_Abstract_Anders_Stockmarr.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-373444","ids":["dtu-e65c7b30-06d4-4a79-8999-ac26e71b8c8e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-75713D1CCDA663D018A575ED63FD868E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/53801394/prod11364940429509.WCV_Abstract_Anders_Stockmarr.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Statistics and Data Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"grauromapau","last":"Grau-Roma","name":"Grau-Roma, L.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"stockmarrpau","last":"Stockmarr","locid":"f8ce8f15-f38a-4f99-a8c6-08b0cd7b0f6a","name":"Stockmarr, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8681-2370","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"C. S.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, C. S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claes","key":"enøepau","last":"Enøe","locid":"fac77991-1382-4a1b-83d4-58af7681c006","name":"Enøe, Claes","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"lópezsoriapau","last":"López-Soria","name":"López-Soria, S.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"nofraríaspau","last":"Nofrarías","name":"Nofrarías, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vivi","key":"billehansenpau","last":"Bille-Hansen","locid":"3ac4b70b-8324-43f3-bf7a-c0c5a8275522","name":"Bille-Hansen, Vivi","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"sibilapau","last":"Sibila","name":"Sibila, M.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sven Erik Lind","key":"jorsalpau","last":"Jorsal","locid":"4787cc8c-02f9-41fb-84de-11c1c8b680e3","name":"Jorsal, Sven Erik Lind","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"frailepau","last":"Fraile","name":"Fraile, L.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"baekbopau","last":"Baekbo","name":"Baekbo, P.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"H.","key":"vigrepau","last":"Vigre","name":"Vigre, H.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"segaléspau","last":"Segalés","name":"Segalés, J.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"BIT’s 5th World Congress of Vaccine"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e65c7b30-06d4-4a79-8999-ac26e71b8c8e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"PMWS Development in Pigs from Affected Farms in Spain and Denmark","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373444","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The high level of diversity among PRRS viruses makes it very important to monitor the overall genetic variations in relation to the sensitivity of diagnostic tests and vaccination efficacy, but only few full genome sequences of PRRSV strains isolated in Europe have been made public available. In the present study, fast and robust methods for long range RT-PCR amplification and subsequent next generation sequencing (NGS) of PRRSV Type 1 and Type 2 viruses were developed and validated on nine Type 1 and nine Type 2 PRRSV viruses. The methods were shown to generate robust and reliable sequences both on primary material and cell culture adapted viruses and the protocols were shown to perform well on all three NGS platforms tested (Roche 454 FLX, Illumina HiSeq 2000, and Ion Torrent PGM™ Sequencer). To complete the sequences at the 5’ end, 5’ Rapid Amplification of cDNA Ends (5’ RACE) was conducted followed by cycle sequencing of clones. The genome lengths were determined to be 14,876-15,098 and 15,342-15,408 nucleotides long for the Type 1 and Type 2 strains, respectively. These methods will greatly facilitate the generation of more complete genome PRRSV sequences globally which in turn may lead to identification of markers of virulence and improve our understanding of PRRSV evolution and pathogenesis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Fahnøe, Ulrik","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Ait-Ali, Tahar","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-374248"],"event":{"end":"2013-05-22","place":"Beijing, cn","start":"2013-05-20","title":"International Porcine Reproductive and Respiratory Syndrome Symposium (PRRS 2013)","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast and robust methods for full genome sequencing of porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus prrsv type 000000000001 and type 000000000002","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/55237527/prod11369864828911.Fast_and_robust_methods_for_full_genome_sequencing_of_Porcine_Reproductive_and_Respiratory_Syndrome_Virus.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-374248","identifier":[{"id":"84882998892","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e8ed9799-bf28-4792-9aeb-72cb2d96a559"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-CB805682B6CB668BAE54DC5897E001A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/55237527/prod11369864828911.Fast_and_robust_methods_for_full_genome_sequencing_of_Porcine_Reproductive_and_Respiratory_Syndrome_Virus.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"58ce239f-6c30-44e0-ab54-f017a1821425","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","rank":1,"