{"abstract":"PRRSV is a positive-sense RNA virus with a high degree of genetic variability among isolates. For diagnostic sensitivity and vaccine design it is essential to monitor PRRSV genetic diversity. However, to date only a few full genome sequences of PRRSV isolates have been made publicly available. In the present study, fast and robust methods for long range RT-PCR amplification and subsequent next generation sequencing (NGS) were developed and validated on nine Type 1 and nine Type 2 PRRSV viruses. The methods generated robust and reliable sequences both on primary material and cell culture adapted viruses and the protocols performed well on all three NGS platforms tested (Roche 454 FLX, Illumina HiSeq2000, and Ion Torrent PGM™ Sequencer). These methods will greatly facilitate the generation of more full genome PRRSV sequences globally.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Fahnøe, Ulrik","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Ait-Ali, Tahar","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-313436"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Full genome sequencing","Next generation sequencing","PRRSV"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a fast and robust method for full genome sequencing of porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus prrsv type 000000000001 and type 000000000002","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58394459/1_s2.0_S0166093413002735_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-313436","identifier":[{"id":"84882998892","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23891870","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-1db2f5eb-9810-4f96-a1db-a4741adbd8c1"],"keyword":["Full genome sequencing","Illumina HiSeq2000","Ion Torrent PGM sequencer","Next generation sequencing","PRRSV","Roche 454 FLX"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7D92D3C925AD23EEACF767AE8ED4D596"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58394459/1_s2.0_S0166093413002735_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jviromet.2013.07.019","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"58ce239f-6c30-44e0-ab54-f017a1821425","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"fahnøepau","last":"Fahnøe","locid":"409de6f2-ff5a-4623-8c2e-4bb18ee9c505","name":"Fahnøe, Ulrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tahar","key":"aitalipau","last":"Ait-Ali","name":"Ait-Ali, Tahar","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23891870"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jviromet.2013.07.019","issn":["01660934","18790984"],"issn_org":["01660934"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Virological Methods","pages":"697-705","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Virological Methods","volume":"193"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882998892"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1db2f5eb-9810-4f96-a1db-a4741adbd8c1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A fast and robust method for full genome sequencing of Porcine Reproductive and Respiratory Syndrome Virus (PRRSV) Type 1 and Type 2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-313436","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The transmission of wave energy passing an offshore wind farm is studied. Three effects that can change the wave field are analysed, which is the A) energy dissipation due to drag resistance, B) wave reflection/diffraction from structures, and C) the effect of a modified wind field inside and on the lee side of the wind farm. The drag dissipation, A), is quantified by a quadratic resistance law. The effect of B) is parameterised based on 1st order potential theory. A method to find the amount of reflected and transmitted wave energy is developed based on the panel method WAMIT™ and a radiation condition at infinity. From airborne and Satellite SAR (Synthetic Aperture Radar) a model has been derived for the change of the water surface friction C) inside and on the lee side of the offshore wind farm. The effects have been implemented in a spectral wind wave model,MIKE21 SW, and a parametric study to compare the 3 different processes has been carried out. The method to study reflection/diffraction can be used for any type of offshore structure, vessel or a number of structures, as long as the assumptions for the use of potential wave theory are valid, and the effect of the modified wind field on the water surface friction is known. © 2013 Elsevier B.V. All rights reserved.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christensen, Erik Damgaard","Johnson, Martin","Sørensen, Ole Rene","Hasager, Charlotte Bay","Badger, Merete","Larsen, Søren Ejling"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334584"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Offshore wind farm","Radiation condition","Wave energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transmission of wave energy through an offshore wind turbine farm","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.coastaleng.2013.08.004","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334584","identifier":[{"id":"84883637530","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-64ac2339-287b-4306-8222-9912eda29288"],"keyword":["Offshore wind farm","Radiation condition","Spectral wind wave model","Wave energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D56A1E68B25D3AD2BF2318B5DCE9D653"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.coastaleng.2013.08.004","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Coastal and Maritime Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Damgaard","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"c2692ef3-b38f-4a15-8662-446ba0db8cc5","name":"Christensen, Erik Damgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-5225-5828","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"johnsonpau","last":"Johnson","name":"Johnson, Martin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Rene","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Ole Rene","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Bay","key":"hasagerpau","last":"Hasager","locid":"cf82626c-41b3-42c5-b289-42b5f2dc6f1f","name":"Hasager, Charlotte Bay","orcid":"0000-0002-2124-5651","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merete","key":"badgerpau","last":"Badger","locid":"0493bb98-dd30-4b8d-8540-c3889c8a4e55","name":"Badger, Merete","orcid":"0000-0002-2072-8619","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Ejling","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"6fc30efb-9800-4fe7-ba37-bee5bf5243f3","name":"Larsen, Søren Ejling","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.coastaleng.2013.08.004","issn":["03783839","18727379"],"issn_org":["03783839"],"journal":"Coastal Engineering","pages":"25-46","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Coastal Engineering","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84883637530"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-64ac2339-287b-4306-8222-9912eda29288"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Transmission of wave energy through an offshore wind turbine farm","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334584","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A novel reassortant influenza A virus, H1avN2hu, has been found in Danish swine. The virus contains an H1 gene similar to the hemagglutinin (HA) gene of H1N1 avian-like swine viruses and an N2 gene most closely related to the neuraminidase (NA) gene of human H3N2 viruses from the mid-1990s.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Trebbien, Ramona","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351571"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influenza a virus with a human like n000000000002 gene is circulating in pigs","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58572104/Genome_Announc._2013_Breum_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351571","identifier":[{"id":"24051313","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3778196","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84998693238","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9d96499c-6c3d-4429-b341-b2a82b6f455e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-21245ED99EA67659819DFBFA223951C5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58572104/Genome_Announc._2013_Breum_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/genomeA.00712-13","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","locid":"f5a78ced-77e8-4da1-950c-9c1992eac344","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24051313"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/genomea.00712-13","issn":["21698287"],"issue":"5","journal":"Genome Announcements","paperid":"e00712-13","status":"p","title":"Genome Announcements","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84998693238"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-9d96499c-6c3d-4429-b341-b2a82b6f455e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Influenza A Virus with a Human-Like N2 Gene Is Circulating in Pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-351571","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Influenza A virus has been endemic in Danish swine for the last 30 years, with H1N1 and H1N2 being the dominating subtypes. The purpose of this study was to investigate the genetic and antigenic evolution of the influenza viruses found in Danish swine during the last 10 years. A total of 78 samples were isolated in MDCK cells, RNA extracted and the hemagglutinin and neuraminidase genes full length sequenced. In addition, the isolates were tested in hemagglutination inhibition (HI) tests against a panel of known antisera raised against a range of European swine influenza virus isolates. Phylogenetic analysis of the HA and NA genes revealed continuous evolutionary drift as expected for RNA viruses with low mutational selection pressure. Estimated selection pressures indicated that more purifying and less diversifying selection controlled the H1 evolution. The mean rates of synonymous and non-synonymous substitutions for H1, N1 and N2 were found to be in agreement with previously observed values for Eurasian swine lineages. Calculation of possible glycosylation sites in the hemagglutinin gene revealed that the H1N2 and H1N1 subtypes had three well conserved glycosylation sites in common. The results of the HI tests were analysed by antigenic cartography to quantify the antigenic relationship between the virus isolates. The antigenic cartography map showed that most of the Danish viruses were antigenic very similar, with only a few outliers. In conclusion, this study provided an important contribution to the complex epidemiology of circulating swine influenza virus in Denmark and indicates that vaccine development targeted against Danish H1N1 and H1N2 need only to include few components for the induction of cross protection against the predominant strains. The study was supported by grants from “European surveillance network for influenza in pigs (ESNIP) 3” (http://www.esnip3.eu) and The Danish Veterinary and Food Administration.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fobian, Kristina","Kirk, Isa Kristina","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Lewis, Nicola","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-360589"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-19","place":"Oxford, gb","start":"2013-09-17","title":"Influenza2013","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Phylogeny","Swine influenza"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic and antigenic characterization of influenza a virus circulating in danish swine during the past decade","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/59173128/Oxford2013ver2_abstract.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-360589","ids":["dtu-bb6d8652-b928-4c49-80de-0b6de29ac65c"],"keyword":["Antigenic cartography","Phylogeny","Swine influenza"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C7EAAD6AB4FF0B3CC06BC8AA817879F8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/59173128/Oxford2013ver2_abstract.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristina","key":"fobianpau","last":"Fobian","locid":"5b336c5a-55d3-493e-ad84-7c0738a3dcb1","name":"Fobian, Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Isa Kristina","key":"kirkpau","last":"Kirk","locid":"adf1bfe6-93e6-43ef-afe1-26d21dd2ea6d","name":"Kirk, Isa Kristina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicola","key":"lewispau","last":"Lewis","name":"Lewis, Nicola","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bb6d8652-b928-4c49-80de-0b6de29ac65c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Genetic and antigenic characterization of influenza A virus circulating in Danish swine during the past decade","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-360589","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Lusby, Richard Martin","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-379982"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-27","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2013-09-25","title":"4th International Conference on Computational Logistics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the tank allocation problem in bulk shipping","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58834981/The_Tank_Allocation_Problem.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-379982","ids":["dtu-fbf31ed8-9ed4-44b5-b594-2bbea8aceb5c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-70CC734754BCE1FFDA94E039B84B57CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/58834981/The_Tank_Allocation_Problem.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard Martin","key":"lusbypau","last":"Lusby","locid":"51599544-7991-404d-b9a7-ec2f5ad4824b","name":"Lusby, Richard Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-8652-6219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-fbf31ed8-9ed4-44b5-b594-2bbea8aceb5c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"The Tank Allocation Problem in Bulk Shipping","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-379982","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Lack of animal models with human-like size and pathology hampers translational research in atherosclerosis. Mouse models are missing central features of human atherosclerosis and are too small for intravascular procedures and imaging. Modeling the disease in minipigs may overcome these limitations, but it has proven difficult to induce rapid atherosclerosis in normal pigs by high-fat feeding alone, and genetically modified models similar to those created in mice are not available. D374Y gain-of-function mutations in the proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 (PCSK9) gene cause severe autosomal dominant hypercholesterolemia and accelerates atherosclerosis in humans. Using Sleeping Beauty DNA transposition and cloning by somatic cell nuclear transfer, we created Yucatan minipigs with liver-specific expression of human D374Y-PCSK9. D374Y-PCSK9 transgenic pigs displayed reduced hepatic low-density lipoprotein (LDL) receptor levels, impaired LDL clearance, severe hypercholesterolemia, and spontaneous development of progressive atherosclerotic lesions that could be visualized by noninvasive imaging. This model should prove useful for several types of translational research in atherosclerosis.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Al-Mashhadi, Rozh","Sørensen, Charlotte Brandt","Kragh, Peter M","Christoffersen, Christina","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Tolbod, Lars Poulsen","Thim, Troels","Du, Yutao","Li, Juan","Liu, Ying","Moldt, Brian","Schmidt, Mette","Vajta, Gabor","Larsen, Torben","Purup, Stig","Bolund, Lars","Nielsen, Lars B","Callesen, Henrik","Falk, Erling","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm","Bentzon, Jacob Fog"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animals","Animals Genetically Modified","Atherosclerosis","Cloning Organism","DNA","Disease Models Animal","Female","Humans","Hypercholesterolemia","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Liver","Male","Mutation","Phenotype","Proprotein Convertases","RNA Messenger","Receptors LDL","Serine Endopeptidases","Swine","Swine Miniature","Transgenes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"familial hypercholesterolemia and atherosclerosis in cloned minipigs created by dna transposition of a human pcsk000000000009 gain of function mutant","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.3004853","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-016031","identifier":[{"id":"23283366","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84872013355","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-2f185926-017c-443b-a910-76c0809855af","ku-6e4a5a4b-0648-4523-807f-9bb08921f747"],"keyword":["Animals","Animals, Genetically Modified","Atherosclerosis","Cloning, Organism","DNA","Disease Models, Animal","Female","Humans","Hypercholesterolemia","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Liver","Male","Mutation","Phenotype","Proprotein Convertases","RNA, Messenger","Receptors, LDL","Serine Endopeptidases","Swine","Swine, Miniature","Transgenes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FBB2D726AB69E848804C02549A72D74F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1126/scitranslmed.3004853","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)","Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, He