{"abstract":"The purpose of this study was to identify and characterize fungal natural products (NPs) with in vitro bioactivity towards leukemia cells. We based our screening on a combined analytical and bio-guided approach of LC-DAD-HRMS dereplication, explorative solid-phase extraction (E-SPE), and a co-culture platform of CLL and stromal cells. A total of 289 fungal extracts were screened and we tracked the activity to single compounds in seven of the most active extracts. The novel ophiobolin U was isolated together with the known ophiobolins C, H, K as well as 6-epiophiobolins G, K and N from three fungal strains in the Aspergillus section Usti. Ophiobolins A, B, C and K displayed bioactivity towards leukemia cells with induction of apoptosis at nanomolar concentrations. The remaining ophiobolins were mainly inactive or only slightly active at micromolar concentrations. Dereplication of those ophiobolin derivatives possessing different activity in combination with structural analysis allowed a correlation of the chemical structure and conformation with the extent of bioactivity, identifying the hydroxy group at C3 and an aldehyde at C21, as well as the A/B-cis ring structure, as indispensible for the strong activity of the ophiobolins. The known compounds penicillic acid, viridicatumtoxin, calbistrin A, brefeldin A, emestrin A, and neosolaniol monoacetate were identified from the extracts and also found generally cytotoxic.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bladt, Tanja Thorskov","Dürr, Claudia","Knudsen, Peter Boldsen","Kildgaard, Sara","Frisvad, Jens Christian","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Seiffert, Martina","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-315580"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Cancer Research Center"],"keyword":["Chemistry"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bio activity and dereplication based discovery of ophiobolins and other fungal secondary metabolites targeting leukemia cells","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/66138709/molecules_18_14629.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-315580","identifier":[{"id":"84890946411","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24287995","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-2502a390-3f50-417f-bc74-9571ffa8a702"],"keyword":["Chemistry"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51CC10FE4B6CCD794CF7FE622C70DB35"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/molecules181214629","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/66138709/molecules_18_14629.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Natural Product Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"german cancer research center","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"German Cancer Research Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tanja Thorskov","key":"bladtpau","last":"Bladt","locid":"f3901515-2083-40bb-a1e7-4ef23deb7e31","name":"Bladt, Tanja Thorskov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claudia","key":"dürrpau","last":"Dürr","name":"Dürr, Claudia","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Boldsen","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"991df7f2-a085-49ce-a926-da127ba3b28b","name":"Knudsen, Peter Boldsen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"kildgaardpau","last":"Kildgaard","locid":"e2aa7e75-5e6d-4dac-9b3f-c84affe68992","name":"Kildgaard, Sara","orcid":"0000-0003-3761-0382","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Christian","key":"frisvadpau","last":"Frisvad","locid":"b2d4f948-9e1c-4f8c-9c02-05588bfa21b9","name":"Frisvad, Jens Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-0573-4340","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Held","key":"gotfredsenpau","last":"Gotfredsen","locid":"1cf4df84-2d0e-4693-bf47-e9932e3bf0e3","name":"Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","orcid":"0000-0002-7386-119X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martina","key":"seiffertpau","last":"Seiffert","name":"Seiffert, Martina","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24287995"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/molecules181214629","issn":["14203049","14315157"],"issn_org":["14203049"],"issue":"12","journal":"Molecules","pages":"14629-14650","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Molecules","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84890946411"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2502a390-3f50-417f-bc74-9571ffa8a702"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Bio-Activity and Dereplication-Based Discovery of Ophiobolins and Other Fungal Secondary Metabolites Targeting Leukemia Cells","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-315580","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"A tramp ship operator typically has some contracted cargoes that must be carried and seeks to maximize pro_t by carrying optional cargoes. Hence, tramp ships operate much like taxies following available cargoes and not according to a _xed route network and itinerary as liner ships. Marine fuel is referred to as bunker fuel or simply bunker and bunker costs constitute a signi_cant part of the daily operating costs. There can be great variations in bunker prices across bunker ports so it is important to carefully plan bunkering for each ship. As ships operate 24 hours a day, they must refuel during operations. Therefore, route and schedule decisions a_ect the options for bunkering. Current practice is, however, to separate the two planning problems by first constructing fleet schedules and then plan bunkering for these fixed schedules. In this paper we explore the effects of integrating bunker planning in the routing and scheduling phase and present a mixed integer programming formulation for the integrated problem of optimally routing, scheduling and bunkering a tramp fleet. Aside from the integration of bunker, this model also extends standard tramp formulations by using load dependent costs, speed and bunker consumption. We devise a solution method based on column generation with a dynamic programming algorithm to generate columns. The method is heuristic mainly due to a discretization of the continuous bunker purchase variables. We show that the integrated planning approach can increase pro?ts and that the decision of which cargoes to carry and on which ships is affected by the bunker integration and by changes in the bunker prices.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","Lusby, Richard Martin","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-321540"],"event":{"end":"2013-09-06","place":"Rotterdam, nl","start":"2013-09-03","title":"OR 2013 - International Conference on Operations Research","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"routing and scheduling in tramp shipping integrating bunker optimization","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152316903/Routing_and_Scheduling123.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-321540","ids":["dtu-39194bdf-287c-4407-8f83-2fb9bfb6fbe8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F480373D222D64861BFCC554514FE958"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/152316903/Routing_and_Scheduling123.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering, Management Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"vilhelmsenpau","last":"Vilhelmsen","locid":"6ceebc69-a38c-4b56-9070-23135aa491c6","name":"Vilhelmsen, Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0001-8260-6791","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard Martin","key":"lusbypau","last":"Lusby","locid":"51599544-7991-404d-b9a7-ec2f5ad4824b","name":"Lusby, Richard Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-8652-6219","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-39194bdf-287c-4407-8f83-2fb9bfb6fbe8"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Routing and Scheduling in Tramp Shipping - Integrating Bunker Optimization","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-321540","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
