{"abstract":"Introduction Real-time PCR tests have been developed to detect and quantify Porcine Circovirus type 2 (PCV2) and Lawsonia intracellularis in pigs’ faeces. Pooling of individual faecal samples is often used to reduce the costs of diagnostic testing. The objective of this study was to determine the association between quantities of PCV2 and L. intracellularis in pooled faecal samples and diarrhoea in pigs. Materials and Methods Forty individual faecal samples were collected from grower (>10weeks) pigs on five farms in Denmark. Each pig was described as having diarrhoea +/-. Eighteen individual “diarrhoea” and 18 “non-diarrhoea” samples were randomly selected from each farm. Six “diarrhoea” and six “non-diarrhoea” pooled samples were made by combining three individual “diarrhoea/non-diarrhoea” samples. Individual and pooled samples were tested using real-time PCR specific for PCV2 and L. intracellularis. The associations between diarrhoea (+/-) and pooled faecal PCV2 and L. intracellularis quantity were analysed using logistic regression (Stata/IC 11.1). Results Low quantities of L. intracellularis were detected in six non-diarrhoeic pigs. There was no association between PCV2 or L. intracellularis quantity in pooled faecal samples and diarrhoea (p>0.05). However, when moderate/massive categories for L. intracellularis were combined, there was a tendency toward significance (OR=4.9; 95%CI 0.9 26.0). Conclusions PCV2 was not associated with diarrhoea in pigs on the five farms studied. Our results suggest that the quantity of L. intracellularis in pooled faecal samples may reflect diarrhoea status, however further research in this area is required. Subclinically-affected pigs shed low quantities of L. intracellularis.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Holyoake, Patricia K.","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik","Pedersen, Ken S.","Johansen, Markku","Stege, Helle","Moore, Karen","Ståhl, Marie","Angen, Øystein","Nielsen, Jens Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-304934"],"event":{"end":"2012-04-27","place":"Bruges, be","start":"2012-04-25","title":"4th European Symposium of Porcine Health Management","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Primary Industries, Queensland"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Danish Pig Production"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real time pcr testing for porcine circovirus type 000000000002 and lawsonia intracellularis to assess diarrhoea status","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6484106/ESPHMabstract2.doc","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-304934","ids":["dtu-01625f4e-81d7-4017-a0fa-8feea59cbb6a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A214576DD8016ECEF3D38CEE3F19A13F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.esphm2012.be/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6484106/ESPHMabstract2.doc","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"department of primary industries queensland","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"Department of Primary Industries, Queensland","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division of Veterinary Diagnostics and Research","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division of Veterinary Diagnostics and Research, Section for Veterinary Diagnostics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Pig Production"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Patricia K.","key":"holyoakepau","last":"Holyoake","name":"Holyoake, Patricia K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ken S.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Ken S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Markku","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Markku","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle","key":"stegepau","last":"Stege","name":"Stege, Helle","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"moorepau","last":"Moore","name":"Moore, Karen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"ståhlpau","last":"Ståhl","locid":"08fe2834-3786-49f0-971b-b33bd7098652","name":"Ståhl, Marie","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Øystein","key":"angenpau","last":"Angen","locid":"f852fd28-a6ec-441e-b6a8-65b5970c86d4","name":"Angen, Øystein","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-01625f4e-81d7-4017-a0fa-8feea59cbb6a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Real-time PCR testing for Porcine Circovirus Type 2 and Lawsonia intracellularis to assess diarrhoea status","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-304934","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Influenza in mink (Neovison vison) is assumed to be rare, but outbreaks have previously been reported in farmed mink. The first report was from Swedish mink farms in 1984 and the second was reported from Canadian mink farms. In 2009, influenza A of the subtype H3N2 was detected in several Danish mink farms with respiratory symptoms. Full-genome sequencing showed that the virus was a human/swine reassortant, with the H and N gene most related to human H3N2 viruses circulating in 2005. The remaining 6 genes were most closely related to H1N2 influenza viruses circulating in Danish swine. This virus had not previously been described in swine, mink nor humans. PCRs assays specifically targeting the new reassortant were developed and used to screen influenza positive samples from humans and swine in Denmark with negative results. Thus, there was no evidence that this virus had spread to humans or was circulating in Danish pigs. In 2010 and 2011, influenza virus was again diagnosed in diseased mink in a few farms. The genetic typing showed that the virus was similar to the pandemic H1N1 virus circulating in humans and swine. The H3N2 virus was not detected in 2010 and 2011. Taken together, these findings indicate that mink is highly susceptible for influenza A virus of human and swine origin and may therefore act as a potential host/reservoir for influenza A viruses.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars Erik","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Trebbien, Ramona","Bradstad, Karolina","Nielsen, Lars Peter","Chriél, Mariann","Jensen, Trine Hammer","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Handberg, Kurt","Jørgensen, Poul Henrik","Harslund, Jakob le Fèvre","Rangstrup-Christensen, Lena","Pedersen, Bjarne","Hammer, Anne Sofie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-306432"],"event":{"end":"2012-08-24","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2012-08-21","title":"10th International Scientific Congress in fur animal production (IFASA 2012)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Holstebro Veterinary Clinic"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outbreaks of influenza a virus in farmed mink neovison vison in denmark molecular characterization of the involved viruses","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51541212/prod21357491693004.IFASA2012_mink_influenza_Molekyl_r_lael_rev111220.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-306432","ids":["dtu-062d6c78-1a7c-474b-a2cc-d6da027e165b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BD26B1E0F85BD4D6563B23A13C90B2CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51541212/prod21357491693004.IFASA2012_mink_influenza_Molekyl_r_lael_rev111220.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","ke