{"abstract":"Background The objective of this study was to investigate the association between average daily gain and the number of Lawsonia intracellularis bacteria in faeces of growing pigs with different levels of diarrhoea. Methods A longitudinal field study (n?=?150 pigs) was performed in a Danish herd from day 29 to 47 post weaning. Every third day all pigs were weighed, subjected to a clinical examination and faecal samples were obtained. Faecal samples were subjected to dry matter determination and absolute quantification by PCR for L. intracellularis and porcine circovirus type 2 (PCV2). Association between average daily gain, faecal dry matter content, numbers of L. intracellularis bacteria and PCV2 genome copies in faeces was investigated in a multilevel mixed-effects linear model. Results Increasing numbers of L. intracellularis log10 bacteria/g faeces were significantly associated with decreasing average daily gain (P?<?0.001). The association was decreasing with increasing faecal dry matter content (P?<?0.01). The number of PCV2 log10 copies/g faeces was not significantly associated with average daily gain of the pigs (P?>?0.5). Conclusion The results suggest a potential application of a PCR quantifying L. intracellularis in growing pigs. Faecal dry matter content must be taken into consideration in interpretation of such test results.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Ken Steen","Skrubel, Rikke","Stege, Helle","Angen, Øystein","Ståhl, Marie","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik","Nielsen, Jens Peter"],"cuid":["S02-096.56-036492"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Lawsonia intracellularis","Pig","Porcine circovirus type 2","Quantitative PCR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between avaerage daily gain faecal dry matter content and concentration of em lawsonia intracellularis em in faeces","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51541445/1751_0147_54_58.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-096.56-036492","identifier":[{"id":"84866558480","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3533900","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23013807","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-ac201fb9-452c-4aa7-9572-2d700b4e94c1","ku-509e2d78-9419-418f-9b59-b0610ef74475"],"keyword":["Lawsonia intracellularis","Pig","Porcine circovirus type 2","Quantitative PCR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-D5D4E805E22336670B3659E5B92C4BE2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.actavetscand.com/content/54/1/58","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1751-0147-54-58","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51541445/1751_0147_54_58.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Large Animal Sciences, Production & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Bacteriology, Pathology and Parasitology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rikke","key":"skrubelpau","last":"Skrubel","locid":"7f2db8d7-e77e-494b-ad40-d00db3c48125","name":"Skrubel, Rikke","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helle","key":"stegepau","last":"Stege","locid":"fcd35d18-c0ae-4328-95f3-f912e648c498","name":"Stege, Helle","orcid":"0000-0003-3033-4207","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Øystein","key":"angenpau","last":"Angen","locid":"f852fd28-a6ec-441e-b6a8-65b5970c86d4","name":"Angen, Øystein","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Marie","key":"ståhlpau","last":"Ståhl","locid":"08fe2834-3786-49f0-971b-b33bd7098652","name":"Ståhl, Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e550301c-f89e-4a8b-bf34-e6fc3b76ff37","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23013807"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1751-0147-54-58","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","pages":"58","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","title_org":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica (Online)","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866558480"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ac201fb9-452c-4aa7-9572-2d700b4e94c1","ku-509e2d78-9419-418f-9b59-b0610ef74475"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between avaerage daily gain, faecal dry matter content and concentration of <em>Lawsonia intracellularis </em>in faeces","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.56-036492","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Spread of pig slurry as an organic fertilizer is commonly used in Danish agriculture. The slurry is spread untreated so pathogens able to survive in slurry tanks will be widely distributed in the environment. The objective of this study was to examine if hepatitis E virus (HEV), which is known to be excreted in faeces from pigs, will be transported through the soil and into the drainage system of a field due to precipitation or will be retained in the soil matrix. Water from the drainage system is not treated before it is discharged into larger water reservoirs (lake, fjords, streams), and hence could present a risk for virus transmission to wildlife and shellfish. We tested the presence of HEV in water drained from a test field where slurry from a Danish pig farm had been applied and in mussels from different regions in Denmark with fields in close proximity. Methods: Slurry from a Danish pig farm was spread on a tile-drained field of loamy soil. Water that arrived at the drainage system located 1 m below surface was collected over a time period of 4 month. Samples were collected on a weekly basis and when water flow in the drainage system exceeded a certain threshold (an event). In addition, samples of water collected from wells located along the field and groundwater. Archived mussels from different regions in Denmark were included in the study. Virus was concentrated from water using Poly Ethylene Glycol precipitation and virus from the digestive tissue of the mussels was extracted sing proteinase K treatment. Subsequently, viral genomic RNA, from both water and mussels, was purified using the NucliSENS miniMAG system and detection and quantification of HEV and mengovirus (used as process control) were performed by real time RT-PCR. Results: Water samples representing a total of 14 events were tested. HEV was detected in the first event following spread of pig slurry. In agreement with this, the weekly sample of this period also tested positive. HEV was not found in any of the subsequent water samples. Of the 70 blue mussel samples, that mainly originated from fjords, none tested positive. Conclusion: HEV is regarded as a zoonotic virus with pigs as the primary reservoir. The pathway to humans and other mammals is unclear. Here we show that under Danish conditions, spread of pig slurry can cause viral contamination of water reservoirs, making HEV accessible to the population and wildlife. This indicates a possible route of HEV transmission from pigs to other reservoirs. We also show that retention in soil matrix is at a minimum as HEV was detected at first rainfall after application of pig slurry. The viability of the viruses found in this study is still unclear since HEV cannot be cultivated in cells. We did not find any HEV positive mussel samples indicating that the release of HEV from fields is not a concern for shellfish production.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Krog, Jesper Schak","Forslund, Anita","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Larsen, Lars Erik","Schultz, Anna Charlotte"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-036891"],"event":{"end":"2012-09-07","place":"Madrid, es","start":"2012-09-04","title":"9th International Congress of Veterinary Virology","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spread of hepatitis e virus from pig slurry to the water environment","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51540781/prod21357336377645.Abstract_ESVV.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-036891","ids":["dtu-bd822d5f-ac7b-412a-8297-e7b884273475","ku-62a317f8-11de-4d3d-a03e-ad52898e5dd1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-128636934AAEC434C8E438D24D1AB7BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51540781/prod21357336377645.Abstract_ESVV.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper Schak","key":"krogpau","last":"Krog","locid":"1e238a71-3075-4303-91fe-3cedb620123d","name":"Krog, Jesper Schak","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anita","key":"forslundpau","last":"Forslund","locid":"13c0cf01-c30b-4f91-8415-4143daf93980","name":"Forslund, Anita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna Charlotte","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"3a3d5130-acf6-4846-93e3-f3b891d83e60","name":"Schultz, Anna Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-1484-9120","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["2. Zero Hunger","3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bd822d5f-ac7b-412a-8297-e7b884273475","ku-62a317f8-11de-4d3d-a03e-ad52898e5dd1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Spread of Hepatitis E virus from pig slurry to the water environment","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-036891","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Hvorfor bruger børn og unge sociale netværkssider? Hvordan ser et venskab ud på internettet? Hvad betyder brugen af nye sociale medier for børn og unges identitet? Og hvordan forholder de sig til de risici, som uomtvisteligt også er en del af den sociale mediekultur? Dette kapitel indeholder en grundig introduktion til, hvordan danske børn og unge anvender sociale netværkssider som en del af deres hverdagsliv til at vedligeholde sociale relationer og konstruere identitet. Kapitlet starter med at definere, hvad sociale medier og sociale netværkssi- der er, og hvordan den historiske udvikling har været. Herefter skal vi se på, hvordan børn og unge selv begrunder deres brug af sociale netværkssider, og hvilke motiver der ligger bag deres mange timer foran skærmen. Dernæst sætter kapitlet fokus på børn og unges venskaber på sociale netværkssider, hvad der karakteriserer et venskab i dag, og hvordan børn og unge dyrker de sociale relationer. Dette leder over i en diskussion af identitetsbegrebet og de praksisser, der er forbundet med selvfremstilling på sociale netværks- sider. Kapitlet afsluttes med en inddragelse af risiciperspektiver og børn og unges egen stillingstagen hertil.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Malene Charlotte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118314"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"børn unge og sociale netværkssider hvad ved vi","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-118314","ids":["aau-eaee485b-9d2f-4d1e-a580-3652cdf7c9fc"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-48336F50ACD14558554B49DF98827859"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, E-learning lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Charlotte","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"cc0033d3-6794-4e0c-b451-939e05f9a1ee","name":"Larsen, Malene Charlotte","orcid":"0000-0003-4821-5855","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","isbn":["9788790833800"],"pages":"13-70","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Systime Academic","status":"p","title":"Sociale netværkssider som tekst og kontekst","volume":"1."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-eaee485b-9d2f-4d1e-a580-3652cdf7c9fc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Børn, unge og sociale netværkssider. Hvad ved vi?","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-118314","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
