{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Audet, Joachim","Hoffmann, Carl Christian","Baattrup-Pedersen, Annette","Elsgaard, Lars","Kjærgaard, Charlotte","Larsen, Søren Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-214729"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-21","place":"dk","start":"2012-06-17","title":"Society of Wetland Scientists meeting European","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"greenhouse gas emissions in riparian wetlands","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-214729","ids":["au-95d9155f-4995-4cd1-9d41-a733ee1f998a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8BC8CD36C9B186F7A194C43281846806"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Lake Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"audetpau","last":"Audet","locid":"51de9f19-0692-434b-b884-12147bf58637","name":"Audet, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0001-5839-8793","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl Christian","key":"hoffmannpau","last":"Hoffmann","locid":"353a0760-7b7a-4348-9f47-7df140234554","name":"Hoffmann, Carl Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-9162","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Annette","key":"baattruppedersenpau","last":"Baattrup-Pedersen","locid":"e4f5886d-70a8-4174-a224-b21d0dfc8689","name":"Baattrup-Pedersen, Annette","orcid":"0000-0002-3118-344X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elsgaardpau","last":"Elsgaard","locid":"61694e4f-57ee-44c7-8821-c3d2590ff4e0","name":"Elsgaard, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0058-7609","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"b3be00f6-c690-4933-946a-9ab606926cdd","name":"Kjærgaard, Charlotte","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"fc89ca38-79d9-4781-a6b1-8394e722b334","name":"Larsen, Søren Erik","orcid":"0000-0001-8428-2065","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-95d9155f-4995-4cd1-9d41-a733ee1f998a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Greenhouse gas emissions in riparian wetlands","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-214729","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Commercials offer the opportunity for intergenerational memory and impinge on cultural memory. TV commercials for foodstuffs often make reference to past times as a way of authenticating products. This is frequently achieved using visual cues, but in this paper I would like to demonstrate how such references to the past and ‘the good old days’ can be achieved through sounds. In particular, I will look at commercials for Danish non-dairy spreads, especially for OMA margarine. These commercials are notable in that they contain a melody and a slogan – ‘Say the name: OMA margarine’ – that have basically remained the same for 70 years. Together these identifiers make OMA an interesting Danish case to study. With reference to Ann Rigney’s memorial practices or mechanisms, the study aims to demonstrate how the auditory aspects of Danish margarine commercials for frying tend to be limited in variety: in general, the soundtracks of margarine commercials seem to merge into one, they are somewhat alike. The OMA commercials are no exception, but the OMA melody makes a distinction. In general the soundtracks of OMA margarine commercials (and the use of melody) seem to have shifted from using a predominantly semantic causal soundtrack to tracks using aesthetic and musicalised elements which are supposed to arouse more sensuous feelings in the consumers.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Larsen, Charlotte Rørdam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-239709"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recycling sounds in commercials interchanges between past and present in danish margarine commercials 000000001936 000000002000","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.soundeffects.dk/article/view/5184/5430","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-239709","ids":["au-c16d68d2-8562-4b98-9e81-2eed40e65c29"],"keyword":["commercials, recycling music, nostalgia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E136589C25E2F3FF6377062467B8DCC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.soundeffects.dk/article/view/5184/5430","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Musicology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Rørdam","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"4e604018-2471-4a68-a18b-0ae187425b3d","name":"Larsen, Charlotte Rørdam","orcid":"0000-0002-5465-0338","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["1904500X"],"journal":"SoundEffect","pages":"22-43","publisher":"Aarhus University","status":"p","title":"SoundEffect","volume":"2/1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c16d68d2-8562-4b98-9e81-2eed40e65c29"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Recycling Sounds in Commercials : Interchanges between past and present in Danish margarine commercials 1936-2000","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-239709","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome (PRRS) has for nearly 3 decades been economically one of the most important swine diseases. Despite intensive research focus, many unanswered questions remain regarding the pathogenesis of PRRSV. In situ hybridization (ISH) is generally considered a more useful diagnostic tool than immunohystochemistry (IHC) and may be helpful in further research ofpathogenesis. ISH is able to detect virus in non-progressive stages therefore the length of successful detection after infection is expected. It is not widely used, however, because of problems with specificity of the oligonucleotide probe due to the pronounced diversity of the PRRSV genome. The aim of the present study was to evaluate a PRRSV specific ISH protocol, Three, non-overlapping PRRSV specific 20 nucleotides , DIG labeled oligonucleotide probes were designed targeting the ORF7 region. The probes were specific designed to recognize PRRSV Type I isolates only. A total of 19 positive PRRSV paraffin blocks from different organs and infected with different strains were tested as well as a negative control. All samples were simultaneously tested by IHC using different anti-PRRSV monoclonal antibodies. Five experiments of ISH were performed, using a pool of 1 nmol of each of the three oligonucleotide probes with two different prehybridization temperature (105°C and 80°C) and time (5 and 10 min), using 0.5 nmol of each of the probes separately with prehybridization on 105°C during 5 min. Positive signals were detected in alveolar macrophages in lungs, in hystiocytes in lymph nodes, Payer patches and tonsils, in macrophages, on inflamed area in ileum and in glomerular cells. 58 EuroPRRS2012 Budapest, Hungary ISH showed better sensitivity than IHC while there was an obvious discrepancy between sensitivity among the probes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Novosel, Dinko","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Larsen, Lars Erik","Boye, Mette","Jensen, Tim Kåre","Jungi