{"abstract":"Purpose: Retinal vascular lesions such as microaneurysms and haemorrhages, while typical of diabetic retinopathy, are also seen in subjects without diabetes where they are associated with elevated cardiovascular mortality. In theory, these lesions could be a consequence of past hyperglycaemia. We examined the prevalence and risk factors for retinopathy, including lens fluorescence, a biomarker of cumulative life-time glycaemia in adults without diabetes. Methods: Cross-sectional population-based study of 711 subjects without diabetes (WHO 1999 criteria) aged 30-60 years, including oral glucose tolerance testing, clinical and laboratory examinations, non-invasive ocular lens fluorometry and seven-field fundus photography. Results: Retinopathy was present in 8.3% (CI(95) 6.3-10.3%) of subjects. Higher systolic blood pressure (SBP) (p = 0.032), increasing body mass index (BMI) (p = 0.014) and wider waist circumference (p = 0.014) were significantly associated with retinopathy after adjusting for age and sex. Retinopathy was not significantly related to long-term, short-term or current glycaemia (lens fluorescence, HbA(1c) , fasting plasma glucose). In the multivariate analysis, the odds ratio (OR) for retinopathy in subjects with SBP =160 mmHg compared to subjects with SBP","author_count":6,"contributors":["Munch, Inger Christine","Kessel, Line","Borch-Johnsen, Knut","Glümer, Charlotte","Lund-Andersen, Henrik","Larsen, Michael"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809885"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microvascular retinopathy in subjects without diabetes the inter000000000099 eye study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1755-3768.2011.2148.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809885","identifier":[{"id":"21470389","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84868200453","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5f1b82d7-1454-492f-8dfb-7fdbc1923eae"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-447C586B1CF0262EE2F1E8E349E2526C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1755-3768.2011.2148.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Section of Neurology, Psychiatry and Sensory Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Inger Christine","key":"munchpau","last":"Munch","name":"Munch, Inger Christine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Line","key":"kesselpau","last":"Kessel","name":"Kessel, Line","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Knut","key":"borchjohnsenpau","last":"Borch-Johnsen","name":"Borch-Johnsen, Knut","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Charlotte","key":"glümerpau","last":"Glümer","name":"Glümer, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"lundandersenpau","last":"Lund-Andersen","name":"Lund-Andersen, Henrik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1d460214-c0db-4a15-a3a5-360c73746ed4","name":"Larsen, Michael","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21470389"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1755-3768.2011.2148.x","issn":["1755375X","17553768"],"issn_org":["1755375X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Ophthalmologica","pages":"613-9","status":"p","title":"Acta Ophthalmologica","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84868200453"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5f1b82d7-1454-492f-8dfb-7fdbc1923eae"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Microvascular retinopathy in subjects without diabetes : the Inter99 Eye Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809885","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Oral fluid testing has been suggested as an alternative diagnostic approach for surveillance of pathogens in swine herds3. In Denmark oral fluid has been used for detection of PCV22 and swine veterinarians are eager to use it for diagnosis of other pathogens. The aim of the present study was to evaluate the diagnostic performance of oral fluid testing for PRRSV by PCR under Danish conditions. Materials and Methods Five herds with PRRS positive nursery pigs were selected for sampling by convenience. Oral fluid and blood samples were collected from each of 10 pens in each of the 5 herds. Oral fluid was collected by providing 1 cotton rope in each selected pen for 30 minutes. Blood samples from 5 systematic randomly selected pigs in each pen were taken and the separated serum was pooled penwise. Different purification methods were tested in order to decrease the content of PCR inhibitors in the RNA extract of oral fluid. QIAamp Viral RNA Mini Kit (QIAGEN) was selected for purification of RNA from oral fluid and serum. Purified RNA was tested for PRRSV by real-time RT-PCR by a modified previously published assay1. Overall agreement, diagnostic sensitivity and diagnostic specificity were calculated in order to evaluate the performance of oral fluid as test material in comparison with penwise pooled sera. PCR results from serum samples were considered as gold standard. Results The detection of PRRSV in oral fluid and pooled serum is shown in figure 1 and 100% agreement was observed at the herd level. Pen level agreement between oral fluid and pooled serum samples for detection of PRRSV in the 50 pens is displayed in table 1. Overall agreement was 68%. The diagnostic sensitivity of oral fluid testing was 0.75 (95% CI= 0.55-0.89) and the diagnostic specificity of oral fluid testing was 0.95 (95% CI= 0.77-1.0). Figure 1. Herd level detection of PRRSV based on samples from 50 pens Table 1. 2x2 table of PRRSV real-time RT-PCR results, when testing pooled serum samples and oral fluid samples from 50 pens Conclusions and Discussion Agreement between oral fluid and serum testing at herd and pen level was promising. The present results indicate that oral fluid testing for PRRSV at pen level has a high diagnostic specificity and a somewhat lower, but acceptable diagnostic sensitivity. These findings suggest that oral fluid testing using the real-time RT-PCR procedure established in this study is applicable for PRRS surveillance and diagnosis under Danish conditions.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Heiselberg, P. R.","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Pedersen, Ken Steen","Nielsen, Jens Peter","Kristensen, C. S.","Breum, S. Ø.","Larsen, L. E."],"cuid":["S02-080.67-033439"],"event":{"end":"2012-06-13","place":"Jeju, kr","start":"2012-06-10","title":"22nd International Pig Veterinary Society Congress","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-PR-ALL"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-AAF","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pcr diagnosis of prrs virus in oral fluids from weaned danish pigs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7931568/IPVS_2012_prh.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-080.67-033439","ids":["dtu-2634e3be-4e14-47cc-97a2-76206c6d1a78","ku-7a3b8923-14e1-428c-bdf5-2611b059838b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-9FA0B707B81AACC29DF503B60DA8A5CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/7931568/IPVS_2012_prh.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.ipvs2012.kr/main.html","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division of Veterinary Diagnostics and Research","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Division of Veterinary Diagnostics and Research, Section for Veterinary Diagnostics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Large Animal Sciences, Production & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish agriculture food council","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-AAF","l3nl":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","l3nn":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Agriculture & Food Council","namevar":["Danish Agriculture and Food Council"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-AAF","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ken Steen","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"e7e2a10f-e368-4635-9481-f23e58c80aa8","name":"Pedersen, Ken Steen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jens Peter","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"e550301c-f89e-4a8b-bf34-e6fc3b76ff37","name":"Nielsen, Jens Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"C. S.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","name":"Kristensen, C. S.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"1013","status":"p","subtitle":"22nd International Pig Veterinary Society Congress","title":"IPVS 2012 Korea","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Danish Agriculture & Food Council","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2634e3be-4e14-47cc-97a2-76206c6d1a78","ku-7a3b8923-14e1-428c-bdf5-2611b059838b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PCR diagnosis of PRRS virus in oral fluids from weaned Danish pigs","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.67-033439","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Background Hemorrhagic pneumonia is a disease of farmed mink (Neovison vison) caused by Pseudomonas aeruginosa. The disease is highly seasonal in Danish mink with outbreaks occurring almost exclusively in the autumn. Human respiratory syncytial virus (RSV) has been shown to augment infection with P. aeruginosa in mice and to promote adhesion of P. aeruginosa to human respiratory cells. Findings We tested 50 lung specimens from mink with hemorrhagic pneumonia for bovine RSV by reverse transcriptase polymerase chain reaction (PCR) and for human RSV by a commercial real-time PCR. RSV was not found. Conclusions This study indicates that human and bovine RSV is not a major co-factor for development of hemorrhagic pneumonia in Danish mink.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Salomonsen, Charlotte Mark","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Larsen, Lars Erik","Jakobsen, Jeanette","Høiby, Niels","Hammer, Anne Sofie"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-033234"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Hemorrhagic pneumonia","Mink","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Respiratory syncytial virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"investigation of the presence of human or bovine respiratory syncytial virus in the lungs of mink em neovison vison em with hemorrhagic pneumonia due to em pseudomonas aeruginosa em","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51527137/1751_0147_54_70.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-033234","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3533935","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23181342","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84869870290","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1dd00e22-0d13-4ba4-9b98-4816ebea1ee0","ku-b14d998a-982b-4702-909f-88d5caaac9ba"],"keyword":["Hemorrhagic pneumonia","Mink","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Respiratory syncytial virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-53A0071995F840D95198C51B72EE361F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/1751-0147-54-70","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/46071649/1751_0147_54_70.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51527137/1751_0147_54_70.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Division of Poultry, Fish and Fur Animals"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Pathobiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Mark","key":"salomonsenpau","last":"Salomonsen","locid":"4a30d7ed-aaf8-4326-b5b6-8b24a3886723","name":"Salomonsen, Charlotte Mark","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","name":"Jakobsen, Jeanette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels","key":"høibypau","last":"Høiby","name":"Høiby, Niels","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Sofie","key":"hammerpau","last":"Hammer","locid":"78af063d-b05f-4a2b-b040-024f5c0cbcab","name":"Hammer, Anne Sofie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23181342"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/1751-0147-54-70","issn":["0044605X","17510147"],"issn_org":["0044605X"],"issue":"70","journal":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica","title_org":"Acta Veterinaria Scandinavica (Online)","volume":"54"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84869870290"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-1dd00e22-0d13-4ba4-9b98-4816ebea1ee0","ku-b14d998a-982b-4702-909f-88d5caaac9ba"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Investigation of the presence of human or bovine respiratory syncytial virus in the lungs of mink (Neovison vison) with hemorrhagic pneumonia due to Pseudomonas aeruginosa","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-033234","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"In Denmark and Greenland, extensive surveillance of avian influenza (AI) viruses in wild bird populations has been conducted from 2007 through 2010. In Denmark, the surveillance consisted of passive surveillance of wild birds found dead or sick across Denmark and active surveillance of apparently healthy live birds in waterfowl reservoirs and along migratory flyways, birds living in proximity to domestic poultry, and hunted game birds. Dead birds were sampled by oropharyngeal swabbing. Healthy live wild birds were captured with nets, traps, or by hand and were sampled by swabbing of the oropharyngeal and cloacal tracts, or swabs were collected from fresh fecal droppings. Hunted game birds were delivered to game-handling establishments, where each bird was sampled by oropharyngeal and cloacal swabbing. During the 2007–10 period, a total of 11,055 wild birds were sampled in Denmark, of which 396 were birds that were found dead. In Greenland, samples were collected mainly from fecal droppings in breeding areas. Samples from 3555 live and apparently healthy wild birds were tested. All swab samples were tested by pan-influenza reverse transcriptase–PCR (RT-PCR), and the positive samples were further tested by H5/H7 specific RT-PCRs. H5/H7-positive samples were subjected to hemagglutination cleavage site sequencing for pathotyping. In addition, all RT-PCR–positive samples were subjected to virus isolation, and the virus isolates were subsequently subtyped. In Denmark, low pathogenic (LP) H5 viruses were detected throughout the period, in addition to a few LPAI H7 and several other subtypes. In Greenland, very few samples were positive for AI. None of them were found to be of the H5 or H7 subtypes by RT-PCR. Isolation of these viruses in eggs was unsuccessful; thus, they were not subtyped further. The findings did, however, demonstrate the presence of LPAI viruses in Greenland. For several water bird species overwintering in North America and northwest Europe, respectively, Greenland constitutes a common breeding area. This raises the possibility that viruses could be transmitted to North America via Greenland and vice versa. In Denmark, the screenings for AI showed LPAI viruses to be naturally occurring in the wild bird population, particularly in waterfowl. The occurrence of AI viruses in the wild bird population may pose a risk for AI infections in Danish poultry.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Trebbien, Ramona","Handberg, Kurt J.","Therkildsen, Ole Roland","Madsen, Jesper Johannes","Thorup, Kasper","Baroch, John A.","DeLiberto, Thomas J.","Larsen, Lars Erik","Jørgensen, Poul Henrik"],"cuid":["S03-084.85-023648"],"event":{"end":"2012-04-04","place":"London, gb","start":"2012-04-01","title":"8th International Symposium on Avian Influenza","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","United States Department of Agriculture"],"keyword":["Avian influenza virus","Denmark","Greenland","Surveillance","Wild birds"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surveillance for avian influenza viruses in wild birds in denmark and greenland 000000002007 000000000010","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1637/10190-041012-ResNote.1","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-084.85-023648","identifier":[{"id":"23402125","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000313136200029","type":"wos"},{"id":"84871963311","t