{"abstract":"Porcine reproductive and respiratory syndrome virus (PRRSV) belongs to the Arteriviridae family and is the cause of significant respiratory and reproductive disease in swine worldwide. Strains of PRRSV are divided into two genotypes: type 1 and type 2, also referred to as EU and US type, respectively, due to their geographical origin. In Denmark the type 1 virus was first recognized in 1992, and since 1996 both types of PRRSV are widely spread. Approximately 50 % of the herds are seropositive for PRRSV antibodies against either or both types of PRRSV. In November 2010, a severe case of PRRSV with high mortality rate in piglets occurred in Northern Jutland. PRRSV type 2 was detected by real-time RT-PCR in lung tissue from 10 days old piglets. The outbreak was treated by extensive vaccination with Ingelvac® PRRS MLV and strict management procedures. 6 weeks later, the mortality of liveborn piglets had dropped to normal levels. From week 6 until week 14 after the initial outbreak, up to 75 % of fetuses were born as mummified. PCV2 and PPV have not been detected in the fetuses. 15 weeks after the initial outbreak, the number of liveborn piglets and the mortality until weaning was back to normal. Total losses of piglets until weaning for the 15 week period were about 50 %. Losses in the nursery and finisher barn are still substantial 15 weeks after the initial outbreak. Sequencing of ORF5 and ORF7 confirmed the type of PRRSV to be type 2, and revealed distinct nucleotide differences compared to other Danish PRRSV type 2 sequences in the ORF5 region. We speculate that the virus causing this outbreak is more pathogenic than previously recognized Danish PRRSV type 2 strains.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","Rathkjen, P. H.","Breum, Solvej Østergaard","Trebbien, Ramona","Larsen, Lars Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331340"],"event":{"end":"2011-06-09","place":"Acme, us","start":"2011-06-04","title":"12th International Nidovirus Symposium","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"prrsv outbreak with high mortality in northern part of denmark","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51540673/prod21357335347942.AbstractNido2011_01032011ckhj_final.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331340","ids":["dtu-59ffb872-3282-4854-9414-52e3849489e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-C60B3CF25BC5BF0546514198E0FCAD6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/51540673/prod21357335347942.AbstractNido2011_01032011ckhj_final.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Boehringer Ingelheim Danmark A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lise Kirstine","key":"kvisgaardpau","last":"Kvisgaard","locid":"58ce239f-6c30-44e0-ab54-f017a1821425","name":"Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Kristiane","key":"hjulsagerpau","last":"Hjulsager","locid":"6c1511ef-8211-4653-8c81-cd55b7f63f64","name":"Hjulsager, Charlotte Kristiane","orcid":"0000-0001-7557-8876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"P. H.","key":"rathkjenpau","last":"Rathkjen","name":"Rathkjen, P. H.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Solvej Østergaard","key":"breumpau","last":"Breum","locid":"ef91abed-bcb7-4427-b534-982cec892366","name":"Breum, Solvej Østergaard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ramona","key":"trebbienpau","last":"Trebbien","locid":"f5a78ced-77e8-4da1-950c-9c1992eac344","name":"Trebbien, Ramona","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Erik","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"09c2a33d-b353-44de-a850-f3c7dec879cb","name":"Larsen, Lars Erik","orcid":"0000-0003-0730-5555","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","boehringer ingelheim danmark a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-59ffb872-3282-4854-9414-52e3849489e1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"PRRSV outbreak with high mortality in northern part of Denmark","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-331340","year":"2011","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Ocean winds in the Baltic Sea are expected to power many wind farms in the coming years. This study examines satellite Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) images from Envisat ASAR for mapping wind resources with high spatial resolution. Around 900 collocated pairs of wind speed from SAR wind maps and from 10 meteorological masts, established specifically for wind energy in the study area, are compared. The statistical results comparing in situ wind speed and SAR-based wind speed show a root mean square error of 1.17 m s−1, bias of −0.25 m s−1, standard deviation of 1.88 m s−1 and correlation coefficient of R2 0.783. Wind directions from a global atmospheric model, interpolated in time and space, are used as input to the geophysical model function CMOD-5 for SAR wind retrieval. Wind directions compared to mast observations show a root mean square error of 6.29° with a bias of 7.75°, standard deviation of 20.11° and R2 of 0.950. The scale and shape parameters, A and k, respectively, from the Weibull probability density function are compared at only one available mast and the results deviate ~2% for A but ~16% for k. Maps of A and k, and wind power density based on more than 1000 satellite images show wind power density values to range from 300 to 800 W m−2 for the 14 existing and 42 planned wind farms.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hasager, Charlotte Bay","Badger, Merete","Peña, Alfredo","Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","Bingöl, Ferhat"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334207"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Vindenergi","Vindkraftmeteorologi","Wind energy","Wind power meteorology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sar based wind resource statistics in the baltic sea","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5237421/Hasager_article.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334207","identifier":[{"id":"80051889744","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-637ef97d-eaf5-4fd5-be98-06d82b2adf0a"],"keyword":["Vindenergi","Vindkraftmeteorologi","Wind Energy","Wind power meteorology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE87BBB8253CE94191425611E7441FC1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5237421/Hasager_article.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/2072-4292/3/1/117/","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/rs3010117","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Wind Energy Division","Technical University of Denmark, Risø National Laboratory for Sustainable Energy, Wind Energy Division, Meteorology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Bay","key":"hasagerpau","last":"Hasager","locid":"cf82626c-41b3-42c5-b289-42b5f2dc6f1f","name":"Hasager, Charlotte Bay","orcid":"0000-0002-2124-5651","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Merete","key":"badgerpau","last":"Badger","locid":"0493bb98-dd30-4b8d-8540-c3889c8a4e55","name":"Badger, Merete","orcid":"0000-0002-2072-8619","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"penadiazpau","last":"Pena Diaz","locid":"2292abbf-9c66-4504-a423-128432556c8c","name":"Peña, Alfredo","name_org":"Pena Diaz, Alfredo","orcid":"0000-0002-7900-9651","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xiaoli Guo","key":"larsénpau","last":"Larsén","locid":"b4f442ea-5cb6-4979-b106-e210895b35d8","name":"Larsén, Xiaoli Guo","orcid":"0000-0001-8696-0720","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ferhat","key":"bingölpau","last":"Bingöl","locid":"fb9b7f1e-f17b-46f3-b60b-128ee8c63392","name":"Bingöl, Ferhat","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/rs3010117","issn":["20724292"],"issue":"1","journal":"Remote Sensing","pages":"117-144","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Remote Sensing","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80051889744"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-637ef97d-eaf5-4fd5-be98-06d82b2adf0a"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"SAR-based Wind Resource Statistics in the Baltic Sea","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334207","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
