","publisher":"Dansk Psykologisk Forlag","status":"p","subtitle":"samarbejde på tværs","title":"Børn i vanskeligheder"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-04d252d4-6c6c-4854-9fd0-955fd54d1d95"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Visitationsprocesser - som betingelse for at arbejde med børn i vanskeligheder","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-556339","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Quantitative PCR (qPCR) for detection of fusion transcripts and overexpressed genes is a promising tool for following minimal residual disease (MRD) in patients with hematological malignancies. Its widespread clinical use has to some extent been hampered by differences in data analysis and presentation that complicate multicenter clinical trials. To address these issues, we designed a highly flexible MRD-reporting software program, in which data from various qPCR platforms can be imported, processed, and presented in a uniform manner to generate intuitively understandable reports. The software was tested in a two-step quality control (QC) study; the first step involved eight centers, whose previous experience with the software ranged from none to extensive. The participants received cDNA from consecutive samples from a BCR-ABL+ chronic myeloid leukemia (CML) patient and an acute myeloid leukemia (AML) patient with both CBFβ-MYH11 and WT1 target genes, they conducted qPCR on their respective hardware platforms and generated a series of reports with pre-defined features. In step two, five centers used the software to report BCR-ABL+ MRD in a harmonized manner, applying their recently obtained CML international scale conversion factors. The QC study demonstrated that this MRD-reporting software is suitable for efficient handling of qPCR data, generation of MRD reports and harmonization of MRD data.Leukemia advance online publication, 15 April 2011; doi:10.1038/leu.2011.69.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Ostergaard, Mette","Nyvold, Charlotte Guldborg","Jovanovic, J V","Andersen, M T","Kairisto, V","Morgan, Y G","Tobal, K","Pallisgaard, Niels","Ozbek, U","Pfeifer, H","Schnittger, S","Grubach, Lykke","Larsen, J K","Grimwade, D","Hokland, Peter"],"cuid":["S02-098.56-022120"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["DNA Complementary","DNA Neoplasm","Database Management Systems","Databases Genetic","Europe","Humans","Information Services","Leukemia Myelogenous Chronic BCR ABL Positive","Leukemia Myeloid Acute","Neoplasm Residual","Oncogene Proteins Fusion","Quality control","Reproducibility of Results","Research Report","Reverse Transcriptase Polymerase Chain Reaction","Translational Medical Research"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development of standardized approaches to reporting of minimal residual disease data using a reporting software package designed within the european leukemianet","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/leu.2011.69","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-098.56-022120","identifier":[{"id":"21494256","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79960212330","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-8179e272-0e6f-4efe-aebe-fb4a8c996161","sdu-2ef16d43-a633-4140-84a6-db0a12b46e9d"],"keyword":["DNA, Complementary","DNA, Neoplasm","Database Management Systems","Databases, Genetic","Europe","Genes, Wilms Tumor","Humans","Information Services","Leukemia, Myelogenous, Chronic, BCR-ABL Positive","Leukemia, Myeloid, Acute","Neoplasm, Residual","Oncogene Proteins, Fusion","Quality Control","Reproducibility of Results","Research Report","Reverse Transcriptase Polymerase Chain Reaction","Translational Medical Research"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E8DA16B7642DCF43116B36BDC07363F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/leu.2011.69","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinical Biochemistry, HEM"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Biochemistry and Immunology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M","key":"ostergaardpau","last":"Ostergaard","locid":"6fe22191-331e-449f-a1b4-19e2f2157623","name":"Ostergaard, Mette","name_org":"Ostergaard, M","orcid":"0000-0002-0620-6910","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"M","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","name":"Østergaard, M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Guldborg","key":"nyvoldpau","last":"Nyvold","locid":"ff577c47-d55d-436b-bdd9-1ed87d6538ba","name":"Nyvold, Charlotte Gu