{"abstract":"During a global research expedition, more than five hundred marine bacterial strains capable of inhibiting the growth of pathogenic bacteria were collected. The purpose of the present study was to determine if these marine bacteria are also a source of compounds that interfere with the agr quorum sensing system that controls virulence gene expression in Staphylococcus aureus. Using a gene reporter fusion bioassay, we recorded agr interference as enhanced expression of spa, encoding Protein A, concomitantly with reduced expression of hla, encoding α-hemolysin, and rnaIII encoding RNAIII, the effector molecule of agr. A marine Photobacterium produced compounds interfering with agr in S. aureus strain 8325-4, and bioassay-guided fractionation of crude extracts led to the isolation of two novel cyclodepsipeptides, designated solonamide A and B. Northern blot analysis confirmed the agr interfering activity of pure solonamides in both S. aureus strain 8325-4 and the highly virulent, community-acquired strain USA300 (CA-MRSA). To our knowledge, this is the first report of inhibitors of the agr system by a marine bacterium.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Månsson, Maria","Nielsen, Anita","Kjærulff, Louise","Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","Wietz, Matthias","Ingmer, Hanne","Gram, Lone","Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-036542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inhibition of virulence gene expression in em staphylococcus aureus em by novel depsipeptides from a marine em photobacterium em","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6309618/prod21323336324627.M_nsson-etal_2011MarDrugs_solonamide.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-036542","identifier":[{"id":"80053311236","type":"scopus"},{"id":"22363239","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3280567","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-ae662566-35c2-490a-b412-bd4556642c39","ku-77cc6718-1d43-49df-8639-e51a05af533c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B17C3862917F14C022473AA2A1E60CD6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/md9122537","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/6309618/prod21323336324627.M_nsson-etal_2011MarDrugs_solonamide.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Center for Microbial Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Life Sciences, Department of Veterinary Disease Biology, Section of Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"månssonpau","last":"Månsson","locid":"b544bec6-c495-4e6d-8b22-b1a749699479","name":"Månsson, Maria","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anita","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise","key":"kjærulffpau","last":"Kjærulff","locid":"840d3acf-77d5-4323-84ed-14a6ff8aabfc","name":"Kjærulff, Louise","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Charlotte Held","key":"gotfredsenpau","last":"Gotfredsen","locid":"1cf4df84-2d0e-4693-bf47-e9932e3bf0e3","name":"Gotfredsen, Charlotte Held","orcid":"0000-0002-7386-119X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthias","key":"wietzpau","last":"Wietz","locid":"f8928597-cfad-401a-84d2-07faf1cbbda3","name":"Wietz, Matthias","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Hanne","key":"ingmerpau","last":"Ingmer","locid":"abe2cd31-84e7-4f06-81a3-33e08bf93b8f","name":"Ingmer, Hanne","orcid":"0000-0002-8350-5631","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lone","key":"grampau","last":"Gram","locid":"9fabd1ae-e28f-4a5d-8456-7a075b4aa34e","name":"Gram, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-1076-5723","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Ostenfeld","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"bd958d52-71b6-4720-b30a-cc9305633b43","name":"Larsen, Thomas Ostenfeld","orcid":"0000-0002-3362-5707","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22363239"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/md9122537","issn":["16603397"],"issue":"12","journal":"Marine Drugs","pages":"2537-2552","status":"p","title":"Marine Drugs","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80053311236"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ae662566-35c2-490a-b412-bd4556642c39","ku-77cc6718-1d43-49df-8639-e51a05af533c"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Inhibition of Virulence Gene Expression in Staphylococcus aureus by Novel Depsipeptides from a Marine Photobacterium","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-036542","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To determine transfusion rates, risk factors for transfusion and the prevalence of unexpected red blood cell alloantibodies in women undergoing hysterectomy for benign disease. In addition, we aimed to evaluate the necessity of the pretransfusion testing for red blood cell alloantibodies. DESIGN: Retrospective cohort study. SETTING: The Danish Hysterectomy Database and a regional computerized blood bank register. POPULATION: The 4 181 hysterectomies in 2004 reported to the Hysterectomy Database. The blood bank registers 2 603 hysterectomies performed between 1997 and 2005. METHODS: From the hysterectomy database, information about indications for the hysterectomy, surgical procedures, re-operations, number of blood transfusions, and demographic, descriptive and clinical characteristics were extracted. Urgency of the transfusion episodes was evaluated by a retrospective review of the patients' medical records. From the regional blood bank register, results of the screening for red blood cell alloantibodies were extracted. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES: Transfusion rates, prevalence of unexpected red blood cell alloantibodies. RESULTS: In all, 242 women (5.8%) received blood transfusions, but only 32 of the 4 181 women (0.77%) were urgently transfused. Re-operations were frequently associated with urgent blood transfusions. Nine of the 2 603 women from the regional register (0.35%) had newly detected, clinically significant red blood cell alloantibodies. CONCLUSIONS: The risk of a hemolytic transfusion reaction was estimated to be less than 1 in 17 000 hysterectomies (upper confidence limit) if the routine pretransfusion test were to be omitted. We suggest that reconsideration of the necessity for routine preoperative pretransfusion testing for women undergoing hysterectomy for benign disease is indicated.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Thoestesen, Lisbeth M","Rasmussen, Kjeld L","Lauszus, Finn Friis","Hansen, Charlotte T","Titlestad, Kjell E","Larsen, Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-149227"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Blood Banks","Blood Transfusion","Databases Factual","Denmark","Erythrocytes","Female","Hemolysis","Humans","Hysterectomy","Isoantibodies","Medical Records","Middle Aged","Prevalence","Registries","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transfusion rate and prevalence of unexpected red blood cell alloantibodies in women undergoing hysterectomy for benign disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79956207711","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-149227","identifier":[{"id":"79956207711","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21370997","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-22aeb7cd-db32-4f9f-945a-14dd1ed9d1ce"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Blood Banks","Blood Transfusion","Databases, Factual","Denmark","Erythrocytes","Female","Hemolysis","Humans","Hysterectomy","Isoantibodies","Medical Records","Middle Aged","Prevalence","Registries","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-B295DFCBBFE752CFBEE63839E2595885"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Gynækologisk/Obstetrisk afd., Herning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first